// Multilevel Master Listening — Part 5
window.LISTENING_L5=[{"n":1,"title":"Part of an interview with a woman who works in retail management","dur":518.03425,"x":[{"ps":44.47,"en":101.57,"c":"You hear part of an interview with a woman who works in retail management."},{"ps":203.03,"en":269.05,"c":"You overhear a woman telling a friend a story about a swan."},{"ps":380.73,"en":436.96,"c":"You hear part of an interview with Bruce Loder, a successful businessman who's talking about his early life."}],"items":[{"q":"How does the woman feel now about her first job in retailing?","qu":"Ayol savdodagi birinchi ishi haqida hozir qanday fikrda?","o":["Pleased by the way she handled staff.","Confident that it gave her a good start.","Relaxed about the mistakes she made."],"ou":["Xodimlar bilan munosabatidan mamnun.","U yaxshi boshlanish berganiga ishonchi komil.","Qilgan xatolari uni bezovta qilmaydi."],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":56.47,"en":64.93,"si":4,"ev":"Every week you would see the sales figures for your product and then act on that… It was a good grounding.","uz":"Har hafta mahsulotingiz savdo ko'rsatkichlarini ko'rib, shunga qarab harakat qilardingiz… Bu yaxshi poydevor bo'ldi.","why":"\"A good grounding\" = yaxshi boshlanish (B). A va C — tuzoq: u xodimlar bilan xato qilganini va hozir uyalishini aytadi.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the woman advised to do next?","qu":"Ayolga keyin nima qilish maslahat beriladi?","o":["Reflect on her skills.","Volunteer for extra work.","Discuss her situation with her boss."],"ou":["O'z ko'nikmalari haqida o'ylab ko'rish.","Qo'shimcha ishga ixtiyoriy kirishish.","Vaziyatini rahbari bilan muhokama qilish."],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":86.78,"en":94.56,"si":11,"ev":"I think you need to work out skills you can offer, emphasizing your selling points.","uz":"O'ylaymanki, avval qanday ko'nikmalarni taklif qila olishingizni aniqlab olishingiz kerak.","why":"\"Work out skills you can offer\" = ko'nikmalari haqida o'ylab ko'rish (A). Rahbarga borish (C) — aksincha, \"before you rush off to see your line manager\".","hl":null},{"q":"What problem did the woman have with the swan?","qu":"Ayolning oqqush bilan qanday muammosi bo'ldi?","o":["She misunderstood its intentions.","She underestimated the speed of its approach.","She failed to realise the consequences of disturbing it."],"ou":["Uning niyatini noto'g'ri tushundi.","Uning qanchalik tez yaqinlashishini kam baholadi.","Uni bezovta qilish oqibatlarini anglamadi."],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":234.71,"en":239.39,"si":21,"ev":"I guess we'd gone too close to the nest. I'd never have done that if I'd known what would happen.","uz":"Uyaga juda yaqin borib qolgan ekanmiz. Nima bo'lishini bilganimda, hech qachon bunday qilmasdim.","why":"U oqqushni bezovta qilish oqibatini bilmagan (C). Tezligi (B) eshitiladi, lekin muammo — bu emas.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the man's reaction to the story?","qu":"Erkak hikoyaga qanday munosabat bildiradi?","o":["He feels he would have handled the situation better.","He is unconvinced by the woman's version of events.","He fails to see quite how serious the problem was."],"ou":["U vaziyatni yaxshiroq hal qilgan bo'lardi deb o'ylaydi.","Ayolning voqeani aytib berishiga ishonmaydi.","Muammo qanchalik jiddiy bo'lganini to'liq tushunmaydi."],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":259.77,"en":269.05,"si":27,"ev":"Still, I'm sure he wouldn't have hurt you. — Are you kidding? Swans can be really aggressive at nesting times.","uz":"Baribir u sizga ziyon yetkazmasdi deb o'ylayman. — Hazillashyapsizmi? Oqqushlar uya qurish paytida juda tajovuzkor bo'ladi.","why":"Erkak xavf qanchalik jiddiy bo'lganini tushunmaydi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"Why did Bruce decide to give up the idea of studying art?","qu":"Bruce nega san'at o'qish fikridan voz kechdi?","o":["He failed to gain a place at art college.","He became tired of doing representational art.","He was persuaded that he could not realise his ambition."],"ou":["San'at kollejiga kira olmadi.","Tasviriy (realistik) san'atdan zerikdi.","Orzusiga erisha olmasligiga ishontirishdi."],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":391.58,"en":410.53,"si":32,"ev":"All the college tutors said, \"Forget representational art…\" And you believed them? I did. That was my biggest mistake.","uz":"Barcha kollej o'qituvchilari: \"Tasviriy san'atni unuting…\" deyishdi. Ularga ishondingizmi? Ha. Bu eng katta xatoim bo'ldi.","why":"Uni orzusiga erisha olmasligiga ishontirishgan (C). A — tuzoq: uchta kollej uni qabul qilgan.","hl":null},{"q":"What was his father's reaction to Bruce's decision?","qu":"Otasi Brucening qaroriga qanday munosabatda bo'ldi?","o":["He was anxious to discuss alternative employment options.","He was angry that a good opportunity had been wasted.","He was dismissive of the advantages of higher education."],"ou":["Boshqa ish variantlarini muhokama qilishni xohladi.","Yaxshi imkoniyat boy berilganidan jahli chiqdi.","Oliy ta'lim afzalliklarini mensimadi."],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":411.06,"en":427.84,"si":33,"ev":"His face was white with rage. He said, \"You could have made something of going to college. You won't get another chance.\"","uz":"Uning yuzi g'azabdan oqarib ketdi: \"Kollejda o'qib, biror narsaga erishishing mumkin edi. Boshqa imkoniyating bo'lmaydi.\"","why":"G'azab + boy berilgan imkoniyat = B. Otasi boshqa ish variantlarini muhokama qilmadi — darhol zavodda ish taklif qildi.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":44.47,"e":44.47,"t":"Extract One — You hear part of an interview with a woman who works in retail management."},{"s":44.47,"e":45.5,"t":"So Fiona"},{"s":46.2,"e":49.95,"t":"Can you tell me about how you started in fashion retailing? Yes, of course."},{"s":50.39,"e":55.71,"t":"After I finished university, I took a job with a big high street chain. I was an assistant manager."},{"s":56.47,"e":63.23,"t":"Every week you would see the sales figures for your product and then act on that by placing repeat orders or putting a new style in."},{"s":63.83,"e":64.93,"t":"It was a good grounding."},{"s":65.37,"e":70.94,"t":"However, most of the staff had been there years and I think I did make mistakes in my dealings with them."},{"s":71.67,"e":73.63,"t":"blush now to think of my time there."},{"s":74.23,"e":77.15,"t":"I then moved on after five years to my present job."},{"s":77.75,"e":82.11,"t":"And now you're thinking of moving up the ladder. How do you see yourself in 10 years time?"},{"s":82.68,"e":85.15,"t":"I would eventually like to be in senior management."},{"s":86.78,"e":94.56,"t":"Before you rush off to see your line manager, I think you need to work out skills you can offer, emphasizing your selling points, showing them what you can do."},{"s":95.38,"e":98.46,"t":"Also, have you been going the extra mile to get things done?"},{"s":98.94,"e":101.57,"t":"or doing more than what is asked of you recently."},{"k":"h","s":203.03,"e":203.03,"t":"Extract Two — You overhear a woman telling a friend a story about a swan."},{"s":203.03,"e":210.37,"t":"So what happened last weekend? Well, we were taking our boat along the river when we passed a pair of swans with a nest nearby."},{"s":211.13,"e":215.23,"t":"One swan just carried on feeding, but the other one, the male, I think."},{"s":215.7,"e":221.21,"t":"decided to come and investigate. Oh fantastic! I've never seen a swan's nest close up."},{"s":221.78,"e":223.13,"t":"I expect he was hungry."},{"s":223.93,"e":229.12,"t":"Well, actually it was immediately obvious from his body language that he had other things on his mind."},{"s":229.75,"e":234.14,"t":"He was flapping his wings really hard and approaching at incredible speed."},{"s":234.71,"e":236.86,"t":"I guess we'd gone too close to the nest."},{"s":237.34,"e":239.39,"t":"I'd never have done that if I'd known what would"},{"s":239.9,"e":241.79,"t":"Gosh, amazing."},{"s":242.33,"e":245.25,"t":"I've never heard of swans behaving like that before."},{"s":245.94,"e":255.65,"t":"So what did you do? Row like mad? Well, we got out onto the bank but he followed us up and then stood between us and the boat for about an hour."},{"s":256.09,"e":259.2,"t":"We just couldn't frighten him away. No, I suppose not."},{"s":259.77,"e":269.05,"t":"Still, I'm sure he wouldn't have hurt you. Are you kidding? You should have seen the way he moved. Swans can be really aggressive at nesting times. Hmm."},{"k":"h","s":380.73,"e":380.73,"t":"Extract Three — You hear part of an interview with Bruce Loder, a successful businessman who's talking about his early life."},{"s":380.73,"e":384.99,"t":"Bruce, at school you discovered you had a natural talent for art."},{"s":385.75,"e":387.93,"t":"Yes, I inherited my dad's gift for drawing."},{"s":388.38,"e":391.13,"t":"I wanted to do representational art, paint portraits,"},{"s":391.58,"e":410.53,"t":"But every college I went to, and there were three who accepted me, all the college tutors said, \"Forget representational art. Get a single lens reflex 33mm camera, hit the shutter, crash, there's your picture.\" Not even Rembrandt could get that accuracy, so it's not worth it. And you believed them? I did. That was my biggest mistake. I haven't picked up a paintbrush since."},{"s":411.06,"e":427.84,"t":"How did your father react when you told him you weren't going to art college? His face was white with rage. He said, \"Right, that's it. You could have made something of going to college. You won't get another chance. Now I've got a perfectly good job for you on the factory floor. You start this week, take it or leave it.\""},{"s":428.31,"e":429.15,"t":"I said no."},{"s":429.59,"e":433.09,"t":"I'm going to start a business next. He said well at your own expense then."},{"s":433.59,"e":436.96,"t":"He refused to support you anymore? That's it, and so..."}]},{"n":2,"title":"Two friends, John and Diane, discussing holiday plans","dur":545.436688,"x":[{"ps":45.88,"en":109.47,"c":"You overhear two friends, John and Diane, discussing holiday plans."},{"ps":215.45,"en":275.23,"c":"You overhear two friends discussing a new film."},{"ps":380.63,"en":449.66,"c":"You hear an interview with the architect Ingrid Chapman. who's talking about an office building she has recently designed."}],"items":[{"q":"John thinks Diane's indecision about the holiday is","qu":"John Dianening ta'til haqidagi ikkilanishini ... deb hisoblaydi","o":["unreasonable in view of her financial position","surprising since her holiday is well overdue","understandable given how much money is involved"],"ou":["moliyaviy ahvolini hisobga olsak, asossiz","ta'tili allaqachon kechikkani uchun ajablanarli","qancha pul ketishini hisobga olsak, tushunarli"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":65.5,"en":75.42,"si":3,"ev":"You told me you'd just been given promotion and a rise, so that can't be an issue, surely.","uz":"Menga yaqinda lavoziming ko'tarilib, maoshing oshganini aytgan eding, demak pul muammo bo'lolmaydi-ku.","why":"John ikkilanishni moliyaviy ahvoliga qarab asossiz deb biladi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"How does Diane feel about the prospect of a break from work?","qu":"Diane ishdan tanaffus olish haqida qanday his qiladi?","o":["nervous that her boss will regret promoting her","worried that staff will take advantage of her absence","doubtful whether she can clear her backlog of work in time"],"ou":["rahbari uni lavozimga ko'targanidan afsuslanishidan xavotirda","xodimlar u yo'qligidan foydalanib qolishidan tashvishda","to'planib qolgan ishlarini vaqtida bitira olishiga shubhali"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":93.82,"en":109.47,"si":7,"ev":"One of my colleagues would probably be only too glad to use my absence to further his own position.","uz":"Hamkasblarimdan biri yo'qligimdan foydalanib, o'z mavqeini mustahkamlashdan juda xursand bo'lardi.","why":"Xodim uning yo'qligidan foydalanishidan xavotir (B). Ishlarni bitirish (C) — \"I could empty my in-tray in time\".","hl":null},{"q":"Why has the film been refused a certificate allowing it to be shown to children?","qu":"Nega filmga bolalarga ko'rsatish ruxsatnomasi berilmadi?","o":["The soundtrack makes it too frightening in places","The plot is too psychologically complex","The opening images are too violent"],"ou":["Musiqasi ba'zi joylarda uni juda qo'rqinchli qiladi","Syujeti psixologik jihatdan juda murakkab","Boshlang'ich kadrlar juda zo'ravonlikka to'la"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":221.94,"en":254.46,"si":10,"ev":"They couldn't take the little bursts of rather tense music. Makes your hair stand on end, apparently.","uz":"Ular ancha keskin musiqaning qisqa parchalariga chiday olishmadi. Odamning sochini tikka qiladi, deyishadi.","why":"Musiqa (soundtrack) qo'rqinchli = A. Zo'ravonlik (C) \"didn't seem to worry the authorities\".","hl":null},{"q":"The friends agree that the original story on which the film is based","qu":"Do'stlar film asoslangan asl hikoya ... degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["is written in a rather unusual style","gives a convincing portrayal of a historical character","manages to keep the reader in suspense until the end"],"ou":["ancha g'ayrioddiy uslubda yozilgan","tarixiy shaxsni ishonarli tasvirlaydi","o'quvchini oxirigacha intizorda ushlab turadi"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":255.19,"en":262.56,"si":12,"ev":"I love the way the author uses dialect all the way through. A bit out of the ordinary.","uz":"Muallifning boshdan-oxir sheva ishlatishi menga yoqadi. Biroz g'ayrioddiy.","why":"\"Out of the ordinary\" = g'ayrioddiy uslub (A). Ikkinchisi rozi: \"decidedly different\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does Ingrid think is the best feature of the new building?","qu":"Ingrid yangi binoning eng yaxshi jihati nima deb hisoblaydi?","o":["the amount of light that comes in","the space she has created for staff interaction","the way each floor has its own facilities"],"ou":["ichkariga tushadigan yorug'lik miqdori","xodimlar muloqoti uchun yaratgan joyi","har bir qavatning o'z qulayliklari borligi"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":395.61,"en":416.86,"si":19,"ev":"The three floors all open onto a cavernous central hall and this is what's crucial for me. There are so many reasons for people to meet there.","uz":"Uch qavat ham katta markaziy zalga ochiladi va men uchun eng muhimi shu. U yerda odamlarning uchrashishi uchun juda ko'p sabab bor.","why":"Xodimlar muloqoti uchun joy (B). Yorug'lik (A) tilga olinadi, lekin \"crucial\" emas.","hl":null},{"q":"What does she suggest companies with outdated office buildings should do?","qu":"U eskirgan ofis binolari bor kompaniyalarga nima qilishni taklif qiladi?","o":["employ her to design a more modern building","ask staff what kind of workplace they would like","use imagination to improve aspects of the offices"],"ou":["zamonaviyroq bino loyihalash uchun uni yollash","xodimlardan qanday ish joyini xohlashlarini so'rash","ofislarning ayrim jihatlarini yaxshilash uchun tasavvurdan foydalanish"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":426.68,"en":441.41,"si":22,"ev":"It doesn't require much. A little creativity, that's all. Under used areas can be refurbished, art hung on the walls.","uz":"Ko'p narsa talab qilinmaydi. Ozgina ijodkorlik, xolos. Kam ishlatiladigan joylarni ta'mirlash, devorlarga rasm osish mumkin.","why":"Ijodkorlik bilan ofisni yaxshilash = C. So'rovnoma (B) — o'zgarishlardan keyin, reaksiyani bilish uchun.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":45.88,"e":45.88,"t":"Extract One — You overhear two friends, John and Diane, discussing holiday plans."},{"s":45.88,"e":59.13,"t":"So Diane, have you finally decided to come to Hong Kong with us for a holiday? Your flight's reserved. We need to confirm by Wednesday. Well John, I've given it some thought, and it's pretty tempting, but it's not that long since I last had a break."},{"s":59.83,"e":65.02,"t":"I don't know. I still haven't come to any definite decision. Oh, come on. What's the problem?"},{"s":65.5,"e":75.42,"t":"I know it may seem extravagant, but you told me you'd just been given promotion and a rise, so that can't be an issue, surely. Well, it's not so much that as my work situation."},{"s":75.99,"e":81.09,"t":"Taking another break so soon after my promotion might send out the wrong message to my team."},{"s":81.56,"e":86.85,"t":"Although I think my line manager would understand. Of course, she knows you're a good worker."},{"s":87.54,"e":93.18,"t":"Well, I guess I could empty my in-tray in time. My workload's not too heavy just now."},{"s":93.82,"e":109.47,"t":"It's just that I haven't had much time to get the office organized. And to be honest, one of my colleagues would probably be only too glad to use my absence to further his own position. Mmm, sounds pretty nasty to me. Are you sure you want to carry on working there?"},{"k":"h","s":215.45,"e":215.45,"t":"Extract Two — You overhear two friends discussing a new film."},{"s":215.45,"e":221.44,"t":"I hear Joe Schultz's new film The System isn't going to be given the 12 certificate he wanted. So youngsters can't see it."},{"s":221.94,"e":236.93,"t":"I'm not surprised. The reviewers say that watching the first few minutes is pretty unpleasant. There's a lot of aggression. That didn't seem to worry the authorities, nor did the strong language, although there's quite a bit of that. But they couldn't take the little bursts of rather tense music."},{"s":237.43,"e":254.46,"t":"Makes your hair stand on end, apparently. Interesting. Anyway, I don't think the storyline's really suitable for young children. Too much delving into people's thoughts and motives. True. You've read the book. Oh yeah, great, Page Turner. I had no idea what the final outcome would be. Oh, I guessed."},{"s":255.19,"e":262.56,"t":"I love the way the author uses dialect all the way through. A bit out of the ordinary. It takes some getting used to, but it's decidedly different."},{"s":263.0,"e":269.69,"t":"You can't really believe the prince is based on a real person from the past though, can you? I thought he did come over well."},{"s":270.2,"e":275.23,"t":"considering how little we know about people from that era. We'll go and see the film, won't we? Definitely."},{"k":"h","s":380.63,"e":380.63,"t":"Extract Three — You hear an interview with the architect Ingrid Chapman. who's talking about an office building she has recently designed."},{"s":380.63,"e":381.53,"t":"Ingrid Chapman"},{"s":382.2,"e":383.74,"t":"Tell us about this new office block."},{"s":384.82,"e":394.91,"t":"It has enormous glass walls because transparency was paramount in the brief I received from my clients. That gives it an airy, spacious feel inside."},{"s":395.61,"e":400.64,"t":"The three floors all open onto a cavernous central hall and this is what's crucial for me."},{"s":401.11,"e":416.86,"t":"There are so many reasons for people to meet there. Have a coffee, gossip, discuss formal matters in an informal setting. I force them to do these things by locating most of the services they need in this area. Toilets, photocopying, cafe, etc."},{"s":417.3,"e":425.89,"t":"forgive me, but there'll be company executives listening who are saying, \"That's all very well if you're able to design a brand new building from scratch.\" What would you say to them?"},{"s":426.68,"e":436.32,"t":"permission me to come up with a scheme for a replacement for example? No, seriously, it doesn't require much. A little creativity, that's all."},{"s":436.92,"e":441.41,"t":"Under used areas can be refurbished, art hung on the walls, that sort of thing."},{"s":441.88,"e":446.97,"t":"and a questionnaire can be sent to all personnel to get their reactions to any changes you've made."},{"s":447.45,"e":449.66,"t":"Good morale facilitates productivity."}]},{"n":3,"title":"Two colleagues, Eva and Colin, talking about a problem at work","dur":538.88,"x":[{"ps":47.83,"en":108.8,"c":"You hear two colleagues, Eva and Colin, talking about a problem at work."},{"ps":212.7,"en":272.41,"c":"You hear an interview with an expert who repairs antique vases."},{"ps":377.5,"en":445.12,"c":"On the radio, you hear a visitor talking to a man about the remote island where he lives."}],"items":[{"q":"What is Colin's opinion of their new boss?","qu":"Colin yangi rahbarlari haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["She fails to consult with colleagues","She is too keen to establish new working practices","She has little understanding of the organisation's history"],"ou":["U hamkasblari bilan maslahatlashmaydi","U yangi ish tartiblarini joriy qilishga haddan tashqari ishtiyoqmand","U tashkilot tarixini yaxshi tushunmaydi"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":53.98,"en":71.45,"si":2,"ev":"John used to get us all involved in the decision-making process. — No chance of that with Sandra? — No way!","uz":"John hammamizni qaror qabul qilish jarayoniga jalb qilardi. — Sandra bilan buning iloji yo'qmi? — Mutlaqo!","why":"Yangi rahbar hamkasblar bilan maslahatlashmaydi (A). Yangi ish tartiblari (B) haqida Colin aksincha: \"we should have had\" — ular kerak edi.","hl":null},{"q":"When talking about the problem, Eva is","qu":"Muammo haqida gapirganda Eva ...","o":["trying to suggest that it is unimportant","comparing alternative ways of solving it","encouraging Colin to take a more positive attitude to it"],"ou":["uni ahamiyatsiz deb ko'rsatishga harakat qilyapti","uni hal qilishning turli yo'llarini solishtiryapti","Colinni unga ijobiyroq qarashga undayapti"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":88.18,"en":96.16,"si":6,"ev":"She's just finding her feet in a new job and she'll soon get the hang of what we're all about. Let's focus on how much she's already achieved.","uz":"U yangi ishga endi ko'nikyapti, tez orada bizning ishimizni tushunib oladi. Keling, u allaqachon nimalarga erishganiga e'tibor beraylik.","why":"Eva Colinni ijobiyroq qarashga undayapti (C). A — tuzoq: \"I wouldn't let anybody tell you it's a trivial issue\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is the expert doing at the start of the interview?","qu":"Intervyu boshida mutaxassis nima qilyapti?","o":["explaining what can ruin a restoration job","comparing various methods of restoration she uses","describing the difficulties of matching colours during restoration"],"ou":["restavratsiya ishini nima buzishi mumkinligini tushuntiryapti","o'zi qo'llaydigan turli restavratsiya usullarini solishtiryapti","restavratsiyada ranglarni moslashtirish qiyinchiliklarini tasvirlayapti"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":234.65,"en":241.73,"si":17,"ev":"We have to lift all the dirt and grease off. If you don't, the pieces won't go back together again. It'll fall apart.","uz":"Barcha kir va yog'ni tozalashimiz kerak. Aks holda bo'laklar qayta birikmaydi — vaza parchalanib ketadi.","why":"U restavratsiyani nima buzishi mumkinligini tushuntiryapti (A). Rang bo'yicha guruhlash (C) — faqat saralash usuli.","hl":null},{"q":"How does the expert feel about leaving visible cracks in the finished vase?","qu":"Mutaxassis tayyor vazada ko'rinadigan yoriqlarni qoldirish haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["They should be avoided if at all possible","They are part of the vase's history and should be seen","They affect the value of the vase rather than its appearance"],"ou":["Iloji boricha ulardan qochish kerak","Ular vaza tarixining bir qismi, ko'rinib turishi kerak","Ular vazaning ko'rinishiga emas, qiymatiga ta'sir qiladi"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":258.32,"en":266.29,"si":23,"ev":"If you cover all the cracks up, you're really making a fake. Being broken is something that's happened to it in its lifetime, which should be recorded.","uz":"Barcha yoriqlarni yopib qo'ysangiz, aslida soxta narsa yasaysiz. Singani — uning hayotida sodir bo'lgan voqea, u qayd etilishi kerak.","why":"Yoriqlar vaza tarixining bir qismi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"The man wants a ferry service between the mainland and the island because","qu":"Erkak materik bilan orol o'rtasida parom qatnovini xohlaydi, chunki","o":["he is keen to develop tourism on the island","he thinks more young people would come to live on the island","he feels the island people should not be isolated from modern life"],"ou":["u oroldagi turizmni rivojlantirishni istaydi","orolga ko'proq yoshlar yashashga keladi deb o'ylaydi","orol aholisi zamonaviy hayotdan uzilib qolmasligi kerak deb hisoblaydi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":398.3,"en":407.01,"si":33,"ev":"There isn't enough work to support our population. If visitors come to the island… catering for them would create employment.","uz":"Aholimizni ta'minlash uchun ish yetarli emas. Agar orolga mehmonlar kelsa… ularga xizmat ko'rsatish ish o'rinlari yaratadi.","why":"Asosiy sabab — turizm orqali ish yaratish (A). Yoshlarning materikka qatnashi (B) qo'shimcha foyda sifatida aytiladi.","hl":null},{"q":"The speakers have different opinions about whether","qu":"So'zlovchilar ... masalasida turlicha fikrda","o":["creating an airport would be advantageous","building houses on the beach would be advisable","commercial development would spoil the island's unique nature"],"ou":["aeroport qurish foydali bo'larmidi","sohilda uylar qurish maqsadga muvofiqmi","tijoriy qurilish orolning o'ziga xos tabiatini buzadimi"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":414.26,"en":445.12,"si":37,"ev":"These beaches could be covered with holiday houses and hotels… No more paradise. — We can build a small airport without impacting on our quality of life… I hope you're right.","uz":"Bu sohillar dam olish uylari va mehmonxonalar bilan qoplanishi mumkin… Jannat qolmaydi. — Hayot sifatimizga ta'sir qilmasdan kichik aeroport qurishimiz mumkin… Umid qilamanki, haqsiz.","why":"Mehmon tijoriy qurilish orolni buzadi deydi, erkak esa yo'q deydi — fikrlari shu masalada farq qiladi (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":47.83,"e":47.83,"t":"Extract One — You hear two colleagues, Eva and Colin, talking about a problem at work."},{"s":47.83,"e":53.53,"t":"So the thing is, you aren't getting on with her new boss then Colin? She's just so different from her predecessor."},{"s":53.98,"e":71.45,"t":"I mean, John used to get us all involved in the decision-making process. No chance of that with Sandra, you think? No way! Okay, I grant you, she's got some good ideas. She moved pretty fast to get us all to agree to individual job descriptions and proper timetable, none of which we've had before, and we should have had."},{"s":72.02,"e":82.24,"t":"And she's done her homework on the staff profile, our qualifications, and past experience and so on. As you'd expect. Yes, but she doesn't seem aware of the atmosphere here."},{"s":82.74,"e":84.77,"t":"It's the way we've always done things."},{"s":85.66,"e":87.29,"t":"I just don't feel I can work with"},{"s":88.18,"e":93.12,"t":"say she's just finding her feet in a new job and she'll soon get the hang of what we're all about."},{"s":93.82,"e":96.16,"t":"Let's focus on how much she's already achieved."},{"s":96.86,"e":99.68,"t":"I wouldn't let anybody tell you it's a trivial issue though."},{"s":100.28,"e":106.17,"t":"If she doesn't settle in soon, and you still have issues with her, I think you should approach her direct."},{"s":107.03,"e":107.52,"t":"Okay."},{"s":108.12,"e":108.8,"t":"Thanks Eva"},{"k":"h","s":212.7,"e":212.7,"t":"Extract Two — You hear an interview with an expert who repairs antique vases."},{"s":212.7,"e":224.86,"t":"Show me how you do it. I see you've got trays and trays of pieces here. Yes. You have to find the bits that match. So I've put all these tiny pieces into colour groups. Red here, blue over there."},{"s":225.69,"e":227.52,"t":"It's a bit like doing a jigsaw really"},{"s":228.02,"e":229.82,"t":"but at least there are no stains to remove."},{"s":230.81,"e":234.17,"t":"All we have to be aware of is the enamel on the surface."},{"s":234.65,"e":237.28,"t":"that we have to lift all the dirt and grease off."},{"s":238.01,"e":241.73,"t":"If you don't, the pieces won't go back together again. It'll fall apart."},{"s":242.74,"e":247.65,"t":"If the cracks are going to show, they've got to be really clean, otherwise they'll look messy."},{"s":248.15,"e":249.79,"t":"You want the cracks to show."},{"s":250.32,"e":254.88,"t":"Some people would say that's terrible for such a valuable vase. Well, yes, they probably would."},{"s":255.31,"e":258.08,"t":"but something that's broken so extensively is this."},{"s":258.32,"e":261.47,"t":"If you cover all the cracks up, you're really making a fake."},{"s":261.84,"e":264.73,"t":"Being broken is something that's happened to it in its lifetime."},{"s":264.97,"e":266.29,"t":"which should be recorded."},{"s":266.68,"e":272.41,"t":"and as long as you can restore it so that aesthetically it still works, it shouldn't matter that the cracks show."},{"k":"h","s":377.5,"e":377.5,"t":"Extract Three — On the radio, you hear a visitor talking to a man about the remote island where he lives."},{"s":377.5,"e":382.27,"t":"This is such an unusual place because there's no public transport to the island."},{"s":382.74,"e":384.73,"t":"I came here in your fishing boat."},{"s":385.3,"e":390.4,"t":"The result is a paradise, rich marine life and spoiled countryside."},{"s":391.03,"e":392.8,"t":"Yet you want to let the world in."},{"s":393.46,"e":396.8,"t":"You've campaigned to start up a ferry service from the mainland."},{"s":398.3,"e":400.93,"t":"Well, there isn't enough work to support our population."},{"s":401.43,"e":407.01,"t":"If visitors come to the island and we have a lot to offer them, catering for them would create employment."},{"s":407.48,"e":410.72,"t":"Also our young people would be able to commute to jobs in the mainland."},{"s":412.25,"e":413.76,"t":"Don't you think it's risky?"},{"s":414.26,"e":424.51,"t":"These beaches could be covered with holiday houses and hotels. Your visitors will complain because there are only a few shops and a ferry service won't be enough."},{"s":424.98,"e":436.16,"t":"People will want to fly here and you'll have to build an airport. No more paradise. We can build a small airport without impacting on our quality of life here and it makes economic sense."},{"s":436.6,"e":440.13,"t":"Our shops can cope with more people on the island, it'll be seasonal anyway."},{"s":440.66,"e":445.12,"t":"And why would we build on the beaches? It'd be crazy. I hope you're right."}]},{"n":4,"title":"Part of a radio discussion about a football team","dur":521.560813,"x":[{"ps":46.1,"en":98.3,"c":"You hear part of a radio discussion about a football team."},{"ps":197.88,"en":270.17,"c":"You hear part of a radio interview with Deena Karakoff. who has just won a prize for her environmental work in South America."},{"ps":385.14,"en":445.92,"c":"You hear part of a radio programme about books and reading."}],"items":[{"q":"What impresses the man about the player called John Elliott?","qu":"John Elliott ismli futbolchining qaysi jihati erkakni hayratga soladi?","o":["He is able to keep calm when he gets near the goal area","He is good at preventing the opponents from scoring","He can score many goals given the right conditions"],"ou":["Darvoza oldiga yetganda xotirjamligini saqlay oladi","Raqiblarga gol urdirmaslikda usta","Sharoit to'g'ri bo'lsa, ko'p gol ura oladi"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":46.1,"en":65.44,"si":1,"ev":"You get a lot of players who get there but then freeze and get erratic. But he's not one of them.","uz":"Ko'p o'yinchilar u yerga yetib, keyin qotib qoladi va xato qila boshlaydi. Lekin u bunday emas.","why":"Darvoza oldida xotirjam qoladi (A). U himoyachi emas (B), o'zi ko'p gol urishi ham aytilmaydi (C) — u boshqalarga uzatadi.","hl":null},{"q":"What do the two speakers disagree about?","qu":"Ikki so'zlovchi nima haqida kelisha olmaydi?","o":["the inflated price paid for the new player","the new player's long-term prospects in the team","the manager's previous mistakes when purchasing players"],"ou":["yangi o'yinchi uchun to'langan oshirilgan narx","yangi o'yinchining jamoadagi uzoq muddatli istiqboli","murabbiyning o'yinchi sotib olishdagi avvalgi xatolari"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":82.52,"en":98.3,"si":4,"ev":"They were overcharged for him. — They probably thought he was a good investment. He's young. They can sell him on if things go wrong.","uz":"Uning uchun ortiqcha pul to'lashgan. — Ehtimol, uni yaxshi sarmoya deb o'ylashgan. U yosh, ishlar yomon ketsa, uni qimmatroqqa sotib yuborishlari mumkin.","why":"Kelishmovchilik — o'yinchining kelajakdagi istiqboli: biri uni ushlab qolish kerak desa, ikkinchisi sotib yuborish mumkin deydi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"Deanna thinks the underlying cause of the ecosystem changes she mentions is","qu":"Deanna o'zi tilga olgan ekotizim o'zgarishlarining asl sababi ... deb hisoblaydi","o":["overfishing by industrial fisheries","increased local sea temperatures","growth of predator populations in the area"],"ou":["sanoat baliqchiligining haddan tashqari ko'p baliq ovlashi","mahalliy dengiz haroratining oshishi","hududda yirtqichlar sonining ko'payishi"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":197.88,"en":220.22,"si":8,"ev":"The local fish population, mainly anchovies, are being forced into colder water because the sea's warming up.","uz":"Mahalliy baliqlar, asosan hamsa, dengiz isib borayotgani sababli sovuqroq suvga ketishga majbur bo'lmoqda.","why":"Asl sabab — dengiz harorati oshishi (B). Sanoat baliqchiligi (A) — qolgan baliqlarga ta'sir qiladi, lekin u asosiy sabab emas.","hl":null},{"q":"How do the local fishermen feel about Deanna's work now?","qu":"Mahalliy baliqchilar hozir Deannaning ishi haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["unhappy about sharing their catch with marine creatures she protects","pleased that she has prevented industrial exploitation of anchovies","optimistic about the prospect of catching better quality fish"],"ou":["ovlarini u himoya qiladigan dengiz jonzotlari bilan bo'lishishdan norozi","u hamsa baliqlarining sanoat miqyosida ovlanishini to'xtatganidan mamnun","sifatliroq baliq ovlash istiqboliga umid bilan qaraydi"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":254.65,"en":270.17,"si":12,"ev":"Now they see me as an ally… the local fishermen can catch more of the large fish that feed on the anchovies.","uz":"Endi ular meni ittifoqchi deb bilishadi… mahalliy baliqchilar hamsa bilan oziqlanadigan yirik baliqlarni ko'proq ovlay oladi.","why":"Ko'proq yirik, sifatli baliq ovlash umidi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"Why did the woman read the book she describes?","qu":"Ayol o'zi ta'riflagan kitobni nega o'qidi?","o":["It was an unexpected gift","She came across it by chance","It was recommended to her"],"ou":["U kutilmagan sovg'a edi","Unga tasodifan duch keldi","Uni unga tavsiya qilishgan"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":409.36,"en":415.94,"si":19,"ev":"I'd heard about it from a friend and I'd got the idea it was something special, and so I asked for it specifically.","uz":"Do'stimdan u haqida eshitgan edim va uni alohida narsa deb o'ylab, aynan shuni so'radim.","why":"Do'sti tavsiya qilgan (C). \"Birthday present\" (A) — tuzoq: u sovg'ani o'zi so'ragan, kutilmagan emas.","hl":null},{"q":"What did the book help her to understand?","qu":"Kitob unga nimani tushunishga yordam berdi?","o":["how strange the world is","how enjoyable stories can be","how she could become a writer"],"ou":["dunyo qanchalik g'alati ekanini","hikoyalar qanchalik maroqli bo'lishi mumkinligini","qanday qilib yozuvchi bo'lishi mumkinligini"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":430.26,"en":442.05,"si":24,"ev":"It just opened me up to what pleasures there are in description, in narrative, you know, in ideas.","uz":"U menga tasvirlash, hikoya qilish va g'oyalarda qanday zavq borligini ochib berdi.","why":"Hikoyalar qanchalik maroqli bo'lishi mumkinligi (B). \"Strangeness\" (A) — kitobning o'zi haqida, dunyo haqida emas.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":46.1,"e":46.1,"t":"Extract One — You hear part of a radio discussion about a football team."},{"s":46.1,"e":65.44,"t":"So is John Elliott a player you like to watch? I'm guessing he is. Yes, he's excellent. Very technical, clever with the ball. He's good at passing the ball to the team's top goal scorers and setting them up to shoot. When he sees that final pass coming as he approaches the goal area, you get a lot of players who get there but then freeze and get erratic. But he's not one of them."},{"s":65.91,"e":69.66,"t":"So if you can get him backing up the strikers, he can be the key player."},{"s":70.55,"e":82.05,"t":"What about their new man Danny Martinez? Seven million they paid for him. Not very cautious given that they've paid up this kind of cash before and it all went wrong, didn't it?"},{"s":82.52,"e":88.0,"t":"I want to hang on to him come what may at that price. Yes, well it hasn't broken the bank but they were overcharged for him."},{"s":88.47,"e":93.6,"t":"They probably thought he was a good investment. He's young. They can sell him on if things go wrong for more money."},{"s":94.2,"e":98.3,"t":"got their fingers burnt once over a similar deal and they won't want it to happen again."},{"k":"h","s":197.88,"e":197.88,"t":"Extract Two — You hear part of a radio interview with Deena Karakoff. who has just won a prize for her environmental work in South America."},{"s":197.88,"e":220.22,"t":"Congratulations, Dina. Thanks very much. Were you surprised to win? Completely. Well, now you're trying to save a wildlife habitat that stretches 3,000 kilometers along the coast of South America. Aren't you daunted by that? It's a huge task, but we're basically getting the message out. The local fish population, mainly anchovies, are being forced into colder water because the sea's warming up."},{"s":220.92,"e":232.25,"t":"Of those left, 85% are being scooped up by industrial fishing trawlers. So predators like seals, penguins, and dolphins, and local fishermen, are left with very little."},{"s":233.34,"e":235.97,"t":"This is the richest ecosystem in the world."},{"s":236.47,"e":254.01,"t":"If it's starting to be affected, you know there must be a tremendous impact on other less robust systems. So what's your relationship like with local fishermen? They used to regard me as an enemy because I used to work for seals, and as you know, fishermen and seals compete for the same fish."},{"s":254.65,"e":270.17,"t":"But now they see me as an ally trying to control industrial fishing. What? Stopping them scooping up anchovies? Not stopping them, but getting them to catch less, which means the local fishermen can catch more of the large fish that feed on the anchovies."},{"k":"h","s":385.14,"e":385.14,"t":"Extract Three — You hear part of a radio programme about books and reading."},{"s":385.14,"e":396.57,"t":"Today we're talking about books that have inspired us, books that have made a difference to our lives. Each of my studio guests has chosen what for them was an important book and first off, we're going to hear about Monica Nairn's choice."},{"s":397.14,"e":397.44,"t":"Monica"},{"s":397.75,"e":398.59,"t":"Thanks, Neil."},{"s":399.0,"e":405.79,"t":"Well, the thing about this book is that when I first discovered it in my late teens, it was a birthday present, if I remember correctly."},{"s":406.07,"e":408.96,"t":"I'd never really read anything like it before."},{"s":409.36,"e":413.63,"t":"I'd heard about it from a friend and I'd got the idea it was something special."},{"s":413.88,"e":415.94,"t":"and so I asked for it specifically."},{"s":416.6,"e":420.96,"t":"I think I was about 17, so I was a fairly late developer as a reader."},{"s":421.27,"e":426.97,"t":"I hadn't been particularly interested up till then, but it suddenly sort of took a grip."},{"s":427.61,"e":429.76,"t":"I think it was the strangeness of that book."},{"s":430.26,"e":442.05,"t":"I mean, it's the one I take with me to a desert island, because it's just got everything in it. And it just opened me up to what pleasures there are in description, in narrative, you know, in ideas."},{"s":442.55,"e":445.92,"t":"Well, we'll discover exactly which book my next guest has chosen."}]},{"n":5,"title":"Two friends, Gordon and Annabelle, discussing a film called A Secret Place,…","dur":525.740375,"x":[{"ps":49.43,"en":105.37,"c":"You overhear two friends, Gordon and Annabelle, discussing a film called A Secret Place, which they have both seen recently."},{"ps":205.85,"en":267.77,"c":"You hear part of a radio interview with an architect called Alan Fassman."},{"ps":375.83,"en":444.03,"c":"You hear part of a radio interview with the ecologist Lorna Hindle about climate change."}],"items":[{"q":"What do Gordon and Annabelle agree about?","qu":"Gordon va Annabelle nima haqida bir fikrda?","o":["The film lacks a coherent storyline","The director was over-ambitious in his aims","The book which the film was based on is far subtler"],"ou":["Filmda izchil syujet yo'q","Rejissyor maqsadlarida haddan tashqari shuhratparast bo'lgan","Film asoslangan kitob ancha nozikroq"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":49.43,"en":74.75,"si":1,"ev":"The action's very patchy. It falls apart here and there. There isn't a thread you can follow all the way through, is there?","uz":"Voqealar juda uzuq-yuluq, u yer-bu yerda bo'linib ketadi. Boshidan oxirigacha kuzatib boradigan ip yo'q, to'g'rimi?","why":"Ikkalasi ham izchil syujet yo'q deb hisoblaydi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"What does Annabelle think about the film's ending?","qu":"Annabelle filmning yakuni haqida nima deb o'ylaydi?","o":["It is greatly enhanced by the musical soundtrack","It strikes a good balance between humour and tragedy","It is a clever way of solving a character's problem"],"ou":["Musiqa uni ancha boyitgan","U hazil va fojia o'rtasida yaxshi muvozanat topgan","Bu qahramon muammosini hal qilishning aqlli usuli"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":81.88,"en":105.37,"si":4,"ev":"I did like the way I was on the verge of laughing, then almost crying for that final two or three minutes.","uz":"Oxirgi ikki-uch daqiqada kulish arafasida, keyin deyarli yig'lash holatida bo'lganim menga juda yoqdi.","why":"Hazil va fojia muvozanati (B). Musiqa (A) — aksincha, unga yoqmagan.","hl":null},{"q":"Alan refers to St Paul's Cathedral in London because","qu":"Alan Londondagi Avliyo Pavel soborini tilga oladi, chunki","o":["it is a building of outstanding beauty","it retains a powerful symbolism","it met with disapproval at first"],"ou":["u favqulodda go'zal bino","u kuchli ramziy ma'nosini saqlab qolgan","dastlab u norozilikka uchragan"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":229.88,"en":241.18,"si":11,"ev":"At the time, people were very antagonistic… Now everyone adores it. It's a landmark, a sort of emblem of the city.","uz":"O'sha paytda odamlar unga juda qarshi edi… Endi hamma uni sevadi. U shaharning ramzi, timsoliga aylangan.","why":"Kuchli ramziy ma'no (B). C ham to'g'ri fakt, lekin u faqat boshlang'ich holat — Alan sobor bugun nimani anglatishini ta'kidlaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"How does Alan account for the success of public architecture in the Netherlands?","qu":"Alan Niderlandiyadagi jamoat arxitekturasining muvaffaqiyatini qanday izohlaydi?","o":["People there are very well-informed about architecture.","Decision-making about architecture is well organised there.","Many of the world's leading architects happen to come from there."],"ou":["U yerdagi odamlar arxitekturani juda yaxshi biladi.","U yerda arxitektura bo'yicha qaror qabul qilish yaxshi tashkil etilgan.","Dunyoning yetakchi arxitektorlarining ko'pi o'sha yerdan chiqqan."],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":255.29,"en":263.74,"si":16,"ev":"A number of the world's leading architects happen to come from there. But the important thing is that the people are very knowledgeable.","uz":"Dunyoning yetakchi arxitektorlarining bir qanchasi o'sha yerdan chiqqan. Lekin muhimi — u yerdagi odamlar arxitekturani juda yaxshi biladi.","why":"\"But the important thing\" dan keyingi gap — javob (A). C — tuzoq.","hl":null},{"q":"What prompted Lorna to begin her latest project?","qu":"Lornani so'nggi loyihasini boshlashga nima undadi?","o":["Dismay over a colleague's behaviour.","Frustration at government inactivity.","Concern about industrial pollution."],"ou":["Hamkasbining xatti-harakatidan hafsalasi pir bo'lgani.","Hukumatning harakatsizligidan g'azablangani.","Sanoat ifloslanishidan xavotiri."],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":379.29,"en":391.29,"si":21,"ev":"I was really upset about some countries' failure to sign up to pollution agreements. It felt like the science wasn't getting through to the politicians.","uz":"Ba'zi davlatlarning ifloslanish bo'yicha kelishuvlarni imzolamaganidan qattiq xafa bo'ldim. Ilm siyosatchilarga yetib bormayotgandek tuyuldi.","why":"Hukumatlarning harakatsizligi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What is Lorna's attitude to climate change?","qu":"Lorna iqlim o'zgarishiga qanday munosabatda?","o":["She believes individuals can help to combat it.","She considers its dangers have been exaggerated.","She places most emphasis on its economic implications."],"ou":["Har bir inson unga qarshi kurashga hissa qo'sha oladi deb hisoblaydi.","Uning xavfi bo'rttirilgan deb hisoblaydi.","Asosiy e'tiborni uning iqtisodiy oqibatlariga qaratadi."],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":417.37,"en":435.9,"si":27,"ev":"She pays attention to little things. Uses low energy light bulbs, doesn't leave the TV on standby, goes in for recycling.","uz":"U mayda narsalarga e'tibor beradi: tejamkor lampochka ishlatadi, televizorni kutish rejimida qoldirmaydi, chiqindini qayta ishlashga topshiradi.","why":"Har bir inson iqlim o'zgarishiga qarshi kurasha oladi (A). Pul tejash (C) — qo'shimcha natija, asosiy urg'u emas.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":49.43,"e":49.43,"t":"Extract One — You overhear two friends, Gordon and Annabelle, discussing a film called A Secret Place, which they have both seen recently."},{"s":49.43,"e":74.75,"t":"You saw a secret place the other day, didn't you? I did. Interesting, but the action's very patchy. It falls apart here and there. There isn't a thread you can follow all the way through, is there? I can see what the director... Yoshiki Mutu. Yeah, I can see what he's trying to do. It's a complex layering of detail, but it just doesn't come off. Well, it's a brave attempt. It works for me, although I have to say I still really prefer the original novel."},{"s":74.94,"e":79.93,"t":"with its very delicate touch."},{"s":80.41,"e":81.44,"t":"But what about the ending?"},{"s":81.88,"e":105.37,"t":"I have enjoyed it more if it hadn't been for that powerful pounding rock music, which was obviously supposed to emphasize what was happening on screen. But I did like the way I was on the verge of laughing, then almost crying for that final two or three minutes. Very well done. Not that it really appeared to sort anything out for our hero. Presumably he'll turn up in a sequel soon with the same old dilemma. Look forward to that then."},{"k":"h","s":205.85,"e":205.85,"t":"Extract Two — You hear part of a radio interview with an architect called Alan Fassman."},{"s":205.85,"e":209.12,"t":"Alan, what's the best way to get good public architecture?"},{"s":209.69,"e":214.81,"t":"Well, people don't want to be challenged by architecture. That's understandable in a way."},{"s":215.42,"e":222.49,"t":"I'm not one for saying necessarily that public buildings are an appropriate area where people should have a vote to say that this building should go ahead or not."},{"s":223.22,"e":226.72,"t":"Many of our greatest and most glorious buildings wouldn't exist if that happened."},{"s":227.51,"e":229.41,"t":"Take St Paul's Cathedral in London"},{"s":229.88,"e":234.14,"t":"At the time, people were very antagonistic and hated its horrid foreign style."},{"s":234.78,"e":241.18,"t":"Now everyone adores it. It's a landmark, a sort of emblem of the city, that wouldn't have existed if public opinion had had its way."},{"s":241.62,"e":249.05,"t":"Do other countries do better than us? Either in terms of imagination or in terms of the kind of decision making we've been talking about."},{"s":249.56,"e":252.35,"t":"Yes, they do. In recent history anyway."},{"s":253.08,"e":254.85,"t":"The Netherlands is a prime example."},{"s":255.29,"e":258.21,"t":"A number of the world's leading architects happen to come from there."},{"s":258.68,"e":263.74,"t":"But the important thing is that the people are very knowledgeable. They learn about architecture in schools."},{"s":264.25,"e":267.77,"t":"They do have a good record for town planning as well, but that's hardly the point."},{"k":"h","s":375.83,"e":375.83,"t":"Extract Three — You hear part of a radio interview with the ecologist Lorna Hindle about climate change."},{"s":375.83,"e":378.78,"t":"Why did you decide to publicise climate change in this way?"},{"s":379.29,"e":391.29,"t":"Well, I was really upset about some countries' failure to sign up to pollution agreements. It felt like the science wasn't getting through to the politicians. So I decided to look into what I personally could do."},{"s":392.44,"e":401.6,"t":"led me to dream up a cartoon character called Mr. Carbon. We all know somebody like him. He's climate ignorant and makes no effort to save energy."},{"s":402.67,"e":404.79,"t":"are the obvious villains, of course."},{"s":405.1,"e":406.68,"t":"But I couldn't do much about them."},{"s":406.96,"e":412.44,"t":"So, are we going to see him in scenes like we get in disaster movies? Oh, that's pretty unlikely."},{"s":412.72,"e":416.76,"t":"You need a lot of alarmist nonsense to make a box office success."},{"s":417.37,"e":435.9,"t":"The reality certainly gives cause for concern. So you came up with the idea of another cartoon character, Mrs. Green. Yes. Now she pays attention to little things. Uses low energy light bulbs, doesn't leave the TV on standby, goes in for recycling, and can you believe it?"},{"s":436.34,"e":444.03,"t":"As well as making a huge difference to her climate impact, she'll save $150,000 over her lifetime. That's incredible."}]},{"n":6,"title":"Part of a conversation between the secretary of a golf club and a visitor to…","dur":497.8155,"x":[{"ps":49.11,"en":108.54,"c":"You overhear part of a conversation between the secretary of a golf club and a visitor to the club."},{"ps":215.19,"en":269.5,"c":"You hear part of a discussion in which the anthropologist Paula Drew and the comedian Mike Morton are talking about their lives."},{"ps":366.58,"en":425.02,"c":"You hear part of a radio discussion about holiday reading."}],"items":[{"q":"What does the visitor feel about installing satellite navigation in her car?","qu":"Mehmon mashinasiga sun'iy yo'ldosh navigatsiyasini o'rnatish haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["worried about its cost","unsure of its usefulness","doubtful about its reliability"],"ou":["narxidan xavotirda","foydasiga ishonchi komil emas","ishonchliligiga shubha qiladi"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":68.5,"en":93.88,"si":4,"ev":"It's not so much the cost… But electronic gadgets aren't my favourite things. Fine when they work, nightmare when they don't.","uz":"Gap narxida emas… Lekin elektron jihozlarni unchalik yoqtirmayman. Ishlasa yaxshi, ishlamasa — dahshat.","why":"U uning foydasiga ishonmaydi (B). Narx (A) — \"It's not so much the cost\" bilan rad etiladi.","hl":null},{"q":"When he talks about in-car satellite navigation systems, the secretary is","qu":"Avtomobil navigatsiya tizimlari haqida gapirganda kotib ...","o":["helping his visitor to choose the best model","providing his visitor with information about them","warning his visitor about the drawbacks of using one"],"ou":["mehmoniga eng yaxshi modelni tanlashga yordam beryapti","mehmoniga ular haqida ma'lumot beryapti","mehmonini undan foydalanishning kamchiliklari haqida ogohlantiryapti"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":95.03,"en":100.19,"si":6,"ev":"Of course, accuracy is down to the mapping companies who do the updating work, but new models come out all the time.","uz":"Albatta, aniqlik xaritalarni yangilaydigan kompaniyalarga bog'liq, lekin yangi modellar doim chiqib turadi.","why":"Kotib qurilma haqida ma'lumot beryapti (B). U aniq model tanlamaydi (A) va kamchiliklar haqida ogohlantirmaydi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What does Mike say about his use of comedy as a child?","qu":"Mike bolaligida hazildan foydalanishi haqida nima deydi?","o":["He appeared to have an instinctive talent for it","His long-term friendships depended on it","It was one of a number of skills he developed"],"ou":["Unda bunga tug'ma iste'dod borga o'xshardi","Uzoq yillik do'stliklari shunga bog'liq edi","Bu u rivojlantirgan bir qancha ko'nikmalardan biri edi"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":215.19,"en":237.24,"si":10,"ev":"If you could run fast or make people laugh, you had a very good chance of surviving… It seemed to come easy and it worked.","uz":"Tez yugura olsangiz yoki odamlarni kuldira olsangiz, omon qolish imkoniyatingiz katta edi… Bu menga oson berildi va ish berdi.","why":"\"It seemed to come easy\" = tug'ma iste'dod (A).","hl":null},{"q":"Both speakers agree that, for a successful life, people need","qu":"Ikkala so'zlovchi muvaffaqiyatli hayot uchun odamlarga ... kerak degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["a belief in themselves","a clearly defined goal","a commitment to hard work"],"ou":["o'ziga ishonch","aniq belgilangan maqsad","mehnatga sadoqat"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":251.35,"en":269.5,"si":15,"ev":"The key to achieving what you want… is the realisation that it's going to be tough, and the sheer persistence that gets you there in the end. — What you have to have is massive self-confidence.","uz":"Xohlaganingizga erishishning kaliti — qiyin bo'lishini anglash va oxir-oqibat maqsadga yetkazadigan sabot. — Sizga juda katta o'ziga ishonch kerak.","why":"Ikkalasi ham aniq maqsad kerakligiga qo'shiladi: \"being specific about what it is you want to do. — Oh well, that goes without saying\" (B). Ishonch (A) — faqat bittasining fikri.","hl":null},{"q":"The man reads books which","qu":"Erkak ... kitoblarni o'qiydi","o":["remind him of people he's met","make a change from his work","are set somewhere he doesn't know"],"ou":["o'zi uchratgan odamlarni eslatadigan","ishidan chalg'itadigan (ishidan farq qiladigan)","voqeasi u bilmaydigan joyda bo'lib o'tadigan"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":378.52,"en":392.06,"si":19,"ev":"This chap who's written books about the criminal underworld of Boston, Massachusetts — hardly culturally or geographically a place that I know. But I find it fascinating.","uz":"Boston (Massachusets) jinoyat olami haqida kitob yozgan bir muallif — madaniy yoki geografik jihatdan men umuman bilmaydigan joy. Lekin men buni juda qiziq deb bilaman.","why":"U bilmaydigan joyda bo'lib o'tadigan kitoblar (C).","hl":null},{"q":"His work involves","qu":"Uning ishi ... ni o'z ichiga oladi","o":["a lot of travel","looking out for new words","studying classical literature"],"ou":["ko'p sayohat qilish","yangi so'zlarni izlash","mumtoz adabiyotni o'rganish"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":392.76,"en":422.65,"si":22,"ev":"If you compile, as I do, dictionaries of slang for a living… one is drawn to someone like this fellow… writing dialogue in almost incomprehensible slang.","uz":"Agar men kabi jargon lug'atlari tuzib kun ko'rsangiz… sizni deyarli tushunarsiz jargonda dialog yozadigan bunday muallif o'ziga tortadi.","why":"Ishi — yangi so'zlarni (jargonni) izlash (B). U mumtoz asarlarda jargon kam deydi (C emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":49.11,"e":49.11,"t":"Extract One — You overhear part of a conversation between the secretary of a golf club and a visitor to the club."},{"s":49.11,"e":61.89,"t":"Sorry to be late. This club's a bit off the beaten track, isn't it? Thought I'd never find it. You don't have an in-car satellite navigation system then? A sat-nav? No, I don't. Though I suppose I should invest in one."},{"s":62.52,"e":66.75,"t":"often have this sort of trouble. Getting to a town's a piece of cake, but after that--"},{"s":67.45,"e":67.97,"t":"Well..."},{"s":68.5,"e":93.88,"t":"It's not so much the cost. My friends all have them and tell me the price is going down all the time. But electronic gadgets aren't my favourite things. Fine when they work, nightmare when they don't. A little black box could hardly have been less useful than my map today though. I wouldn't be without mine now. I won't try and blind you with science, but I do know quite a bit about satellites. The technology is amazing. Position can be pinpointed to within a minute."},{"s":93.98,"e":94.46,"t":"meter."},{"s":95.03,"e":100.19,"t":"Of course, accuracy is down to the mapping companies who do the updating work, but new models come out all the time."},{"s":100.73,"e":106.3,"t":"It's entirely up to you, of course, but imagine never having to ask for directions again. That'll be good."},{"s":106.81,"e":108.54,"t":"I'll certainly give it some thought."},{"k":"h","s":215.19,"e":215.19,"t":"Extract Two — You hear part of a discussion in which the anthropologist Paula Drew and the comedian Mike Morton are talking about their lives."},{"s":215.19,"e":234.65,"t":"We both grew up in a fairly rough part of the city, Mike, so I'm assuming you use comedy to keep yourself safe and popular in the long run. Well, in school, as you know, if you could run fast or make people laugh, you had a very good chance of surviving and emerging unscathed. I wasn't a fast runner, so I exploited comedy to avoid unwelcome attention."},{"s":235.31,"e":237.24,"t":"It seemed to come easy and it worked."},{"s":237.68,"e":241.34,"t":"Your type of comedy is less spontaneous than reflective."},{"s":241.71,"e":246.46,"t":"You see things from your own point of view, don't you? And create a world for other people to see."},{"s":246.7,"e":250.9,"t":"Whereas I explore the world that's already there, which most people don't see."},{"s":251.35,"e":256.54,"t":"Just don't you think that the key to achieving what you want in life is the realisation that it's going to be tough?"},{"s":257.05,"e":269.5,"t":"and the sheer persistence that gets you there in the end. What you have to have is massive self-confidence. With that you can do anything. And being specific about what it is you want to do. Oh well, that goes without saying."},{"k":"h","s":366.58,"e":366.58,"t":"Extract Three — You hear part of a radio discussion about holiday reading."},{"s":366.58,"e":377.89,"t":"If you're English, a nice sad 19th century romance is very useful if you're on holiday and you get attacked by homesickness because it conjures up dripping English autumn days perfectly."},{"s":378.52,"e":385.6,"t":"I always take something by this chap who's written a number of books about the criminal underworld of Boston, Massachusetts."},{"s":386.17,"e":390.11,"t":"is hardly culturally or geographically a place that I know"},{"s":390.68,"e":392.06,"t":"But I find it fascinating."},{"s":392.76,"e":398.88,"t":"There's no doubt about it. If you compile, as I do, dictionaries of slang for a living,"},{"s":399.32,"e":407.17,"t":"One is drawn inevitably, not, alas, to the great classics, who are on the whole rather light-on slang"},{"s":407.77,"e":416.64,"t":"But to someone like this fellow who has this amazing ability, far beyond quoting, of writing 20 or 40 pages of dialogue"},{"s":417.18,"e":422.65,"t":"in almost incomprehensible slang, which I have the most wonderful time going through."},{"s":423.35,"e":425.02,"t":"I find it very alluring."}]},{"n":7,"title":"A man telling a friend about a trip to the theater","dur":489.586938,"x":[{"ps":45.34,"en":97.82,"c":"You overhear a man telling a friend about a trip to the theater."},{"ps":196.44,"en":251.49,"c":"You hear a media interview with a tour operator at a conference on what is called responsible tourism."},{"ps":353.3,"en":414.53,"c":"You hear two local radio presenters, Laura and Steve, talking about a forthcoming rugby match."}],"items":[{"q":"The man says that the theatre","qu":"Erkakning aytishicha, teatr ...","o":["had recently moved","was overcrowded","was unusually small"],"ou":["yaqinda boshqa joyga ko'chgan","odam bilan to'lib ketgan edi","odatdagidan kichik edi"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":67.9,"en":74.11,"si":3,"ev":"When you do get inside, it's really surprisingly intimate. I shouldn't think it holds more than about 40 people.","uz":"Ichkariga kirganingizda, u ajablanarli darajada kichkina va shinam. Menimcha, u 40 kishidan ko'pini sig'dirmaydi.","why":"Teatr odatdagidan kichik (C). Gavjum emas edi (B) — \"only a handful of people turned up\".","hl":null},{"q":"The man criticises the actors for","qu":"Erkak aktyorlarni ... uchun tanqid qiladi","o":["lacking enthusiasm","forgetting their lines","wearing inappropriate make-up"],"ou":["ishtiyoqi yo'qligi","so'zlarini unutib qo'yishgani","nomunosib grim qilishgani"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":87.16,"en":90.65,"si":9,"ev":"They could have done with using at least a bit of makeup and learning their parts better.","uz":"Hech bo'lmasa ozgina grim qilib, rollarini yaxshiroq yodlashsa bo'lardi.","why":"Rollarni yaxshi bilmaslik = so'zlarni unutish (B). Grim nomunosib emas (C), aksincha umuman yo'q edi. Ishtiyoq (A) bor edi: \"throwing themselves into their characters\".","hl":null},{"q":"What distinctive feature of his company is the tour operator keen to stress?","qu":"Turoperator kompaniyasining qaysi o'ziga xos jihatini ta'kidlashga intiladi?","o":["It is responsive to local employment needs","It designs tours for selected groups and special interests","It makes limited use of non-renewable sources of energy"],"ou":["U mahalliy ish o'rinlari ehtiyojiga e'tiborli","U tanlangan guruhlar va maxsus qiziqishlar uchun turlar tuzadi","U qayta tiklanmaydigan energiyadan kam foydalanadi"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":196.44,"en":226.49,"si":12,"ev":"It's the tour organization that really differentiates them… Several of our outdoor staff work only six months of the season but are well paid all year round.","uz":"Ularni boshqalardan aynan turni tashkil qilish ajratib turadi… Ochiq havodagi xodimlarimizning bir qismi mavsumda faqat olti oy ishlaydi, lekin yil bo'yi yaxshi maosh oladi.","why":"Mahalliy ishchilarning ehtiyojiga e'tibor (A). Maxsus guruhlar uchun turlar (B) bor, lekin \"it's the tour organization that really differentiates them\".","hl":null},{"q":"He makes the point that the majority of tourists are now","qu":"U hozir turistlarning aksariyati ... ekanini ta'kidlaydi","o":["conscious of a greater need for social justice","willing to pay additional amounts for responsible tourism","unaware that the choices they make have far-reaching effects"],"ou":["ijtimoiy adolatga ko'proq ehtiyoj borligini anglaydi","mas'uliyatli turizm uchun qo'shimcha pul to'lashga tayyor","o'z tanlovlari keng oqibatlarga olib kelishini bilmaydi"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":227.0,"en":243.17,"si":14,"ev":"Do you believe people are willing to pay more? — Not in the main, but I think they will be once… they become aware of the global consequences of the choices they make.","uz":"Odamlar ko'proq to'lashga tayyor deb o'ylaysizmi? — Asosan yo'q, lekin tanlovlarining global oqibatlarini anglashganda, tayyor bo'lishadi.","why":"Hozir ular tanlovlari oqibatini bilishmaydi (C). B — \"Not in the main\" bilan rad etiladi.","hl":null},{"q":"What do they agree about?","qu":"Ular nima haqida bir fikrda?","o":["The ticket allocation has been unfair","The final result is almost impossible to predict","The absence of certain players will make for a less exciting game"],"ou":["Chiptalar taqsimoti adolatsiz bo'lgan","Yakuniy natijani oldindan aytish deyarli imkonsiz","Ayrim o'yinchilarning yo'qligi o'yinni kamroq qiziqarli qiladi"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":353.3,"en":378.81,"si":17,"ev":"The teams are pretty evenly matched… whether they'll pull it off and by what margin is anybody's guess. A real cliffhanger probably.","uz":"Jamoalar deyarli teng… ular g'alaba qozonadimi va qancha farq bilan — buni hech kim bilmaydi. Juda hayajonli bo'lsa kerak.","why":"Ikkalasi natijani oldindan aytib bo'lmaydi deydi (B). Chiptalar (A) — Steve buni \"eminently reasonable\" deydi.","hl":null},{"q":"Listeners who are planning to go to Australia to see the match should","qu":"O'yinni ko'rish uchun Avstraliyaga borishni rejalashtirgan tinglovchilar ...","o":["organise their accommodation in advance","join the official fan club to reduce their travelling costs","bring their children along to introduce them to the sport"],"ou":["turar joyni oldindan hal qilishlari kerak","yo'l xarajatini kamaytirish uchun rasmiy muxlislar klubiga a'zo bo'lishlari kerak","farzandlarini sport bilan tanishtirish uchun olib borishlari kerak"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":391.86,"en":404.67,"si":20,"ev":"Melbourne's filling up with school groups and junior teams… So better make sure you book somewhere to stay right now.","uz":"Melburn maktab guruhlari va yoshlar jamoalari bilan to'lib bormoqda… Shuning uchun hoziroq turar joy band qiling.","why":"Turar joyni oldindan hal qilish (A). Muxlislar klubining arzon reyslari (B) — \"it's a bit late\".","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":45.34,"e":45.34,"t":"Extract One — You overhear a man telling a friend about a trip to the theater."},{"s":45.34,"e":61.92,"t":"So did you go to that play in the end? I did, and it was an interesting experience. Really? Why's that? Well, for a start the theatre was in Pelham Street. Now I've walked up and down that street many times, but I never realised there was a theatre there. No, nor had I. Has it always been there? Apparently."},{"s":62.36,"e":67.36,"t":"Anyway, it took a bit of finding. You go through a doorway, down a passage, you know the sort of place."},{"s":67.9,"e":71.42,"t":"And when you do get inside, it's really surprisingly intimate."},{"s":71.99,"e":74.11,"t":"I shouldn't think it holds more than about 40 people."},{"s":74.87,"e":75.39,"t":"play"},{"s":75.76,"e":80.03,"t":"Well the show was a big success up in London last year. Huge audiences."},{"s":80.31,"e":83.87,"t":"But unfortunately only a handful of people turned up for last night's performance."},{"s":84.28,"e":86.56,"t":"I'm not surprised though, it was rather amateurish."},{"s":87.16,"e":90.65,"t":"They could have done with using at least a bit of makeup and learning their parts better."},{"s":91.19,"e":97.82,"t":"They just about managed to cover up their mistakes by really throwing themselves into their characters. Yes, I know what you mean."},{"k":"h","s":196.44,"e":196.44,"t":"Extract Two — You hear a media interview with a tour operator at a conference on what is called responsible tourism."},{"s":196.44,"e":221.37,"t":"Excuse me, sir, could you spare a couple of minutes before the conference to answer some questions? Well, if you could make it really brief. You're always identified with responsible tourism. How do you feel it's different from normal tourism? Our trips have unique themes, including culinary spa, angling, indigenous peoples, plus those specially designed for groups with special needs. But it's the tour organization that really differentiates them from others. Take the Himalayas."},{"s":221.72,"e":226.49,"t":"Several of our outdoor staff work only six months of the season but are well paid all year round"},{"s":227.0,"e":243.17,"t":"Then we always use solar-powered equipment and make our environmental commitment known to every tourist. Do you believe people are willing to pay more for your kind of tourism? Not in the main, but I think they will be once their thinking is revolutionized. They just become aware of the global consequences of the choices they make."},{"s":243.67,"e":251.49,"t":"Then I think they'll see that the future of the world depends on justice in commerce and industry and they'll dig deep in their pockets. I must rush now, but come to my session."},{"k":"h","s":353.3,"e":353.3,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two local radio presenters, Laura and Steve, talking about a forthcoming rugby match."},{"s":353.3,"e":378.81,"t":"So Steve, what about next week's all-important match in Melbourne? Australia vs Wales? The teams are pretty evenly matched, aren't they? Australia are certainly the favourites, but whether they'll pull it off and by what margin is anybody's guess. A real cliffhanger probably. And there's huge interest in this match, but I understand the Welsh supporters haven't been allowed enough tickets. As usual, the authorities have given priority to the home fans, but that seems eminently reasonable to me."},{"s":379.45,"e":384.19,"t":"There's concern, isn't there, about two of the Welsh players who are currently recovering from injuries."},{"s":384.66,"e":391.33,"t":"Yes, and there's still doubt about whether they'll play, but even if they don't, I reckon it'll be a gripping match to watch."},{"s":391.86,"e":404.67,"t":"And to anybody listening who's lucky enough to have tickets, Melbourne's filling up with school groups and junior teams because the Australians are very keen to encourage their youngsters to take up rugby. So better make sure you book somewhere to stay right now."},{"s":405.3,"e":414.53,"t":"And of course, you could consider becoming a member of the Welsh team's fan club, although it's a bit late to take advantage of their cheap flight deals. Well, thanks for that, Steve."}]},{"n":8,"title":"Part of an interview with a broadcaster who's talking about a series of…","dur":498.546938,"x":[{"ps":48.34,"en":102.3,"c":"You hear part of an interview with a broadcaster who's talking about a series of programs he presented about landscape painting."},{"ps":201.78,"en":263.55,"c":"You hear an amateur pilot called Gina Nesbitt talking about doing aerobatics in her small plane."},{"ps":370.17,"en":426.78,"c":"You overhear a chef called George talking to a friend about his daily routine."}],"items":[{"q":"Why did he decide to include a picture by a politician?","qu":"U nega siyosatchining rasmini qo'shishga qaror qildi?","o":["to point out how painting helps people in different ways","to show some interesting points about styles of painting","to stress that amateur art can equal professional painting"],"ou":["rassomlik odamlarga turli yo'llar bilan yordam berishini ko'rsatish uchun","rassomlik uslublari haqida qiziqarli jihatlarni ko'rsatish uchun","havaskor san'at professional rassomlikka teng bo'la olishini ta'kidlash uchun"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":48.34,"en":86.04,"si":1,"ev":"I wanted to remind viewers that amateur painting has its own purpose… it helped to give him some respite from the pressures of public life.","uz":"Tomoshabinlarga havaskor rassomlikning ham o'z maqsadi borligini eslatmoqchi edim… bu unga jamoat hayotining bosimidan biroz dam berardi.","why":"Rassomlik odamlarga turli yo'llar bilan yordam berishini ko'rsatish (A). U havaskorni professionalga tenglashtirmaydi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"How does he feel about the process of drawing?","qu":"U rasm chizish jarayoni haqida qanday his qiladi?","o":["The activity relaxes him","He is ashamed of the results","Concentrating on it is exciting"],"ou":["Bu mashg'ulot uni tinchlantiradi","Natijalaridan uyaladi","Unga diqqatni jamlash hayajonli"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":60.63,"en":98.01,"si":2,"ev":"The intensity of drawing is always a great thrill. I can't say it's a relief, which it obviously is for some people.","uz":"Chizishdagi diqqatning jamlanishi har doim katta hayajon beradi. Buni yengillik deya olmayman, garchi ba'zilar uchun shunday bo'lsa ham.","why":"Diqqatni jamlash hayajonli (C). A — tuzoq: \"I can't say it's a relief\". Natijadan uyalmaydi, shunchaki o'zi uchun saqlaydi (B emas).","hl":null},{"q":"What does Gina find hard about learning new aerobatic movements?","qu":"Gina yangi havo akrobatikasi harakatlarini o'rganishda nimani qiyin deb biladi?","o":["It is difficult to practise without any instructions","Trying out some of them makes her feel sick at first","She can get nervous flying the plane unaccompanied"],"ou":["Hech qanday ko'rsatmasiz mashq qilish qiyin","Ba'zilarini sinab ko'rish avvaliga ko'ngilni aynitadi","Samolyotni yolg'iz boshqarganda asabiylashishi mumkin"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":222.81,"en":233.92,"si":9,"ev":"Learning some of the new maneuvers can be quite daunting because this is a single-seater plane. So the first time I do anything new, I'm on my own.","uz":"Ba'zi yangi harakatlarni o'rganish ancha qo'rqinchli, chunki bu bir o'rindiqli samolyot. Biror yangi narsani birinchi marta qilganimda, yolg'iz bo'laman.","why":"Samolyotda yolg'iz bo'lgani uchun asabiylashadi (C). Ko'ngil aynishi (B) — unda bo'lmaydi: \"I'm very fortunate in that I don't\".","hl":null},{"q":"What gives Gina most pleasure when taking part in competitions?","qu":"Musobaqalarda qatnashganda Ginaga eng ko'p nima zavq beradi?","o":["the relief she feels after completing a sequence of actions","the satisfaction of knowing she has performed accurately","the pride she takes in preparing as thoroughly as possible"],"ou":["harakatlar ketma-ketligini tugatgandan keyingi yengillik","aniq bajarganini bilishdan qoniqish","iloji boricha puxta tayyorlanganidan g'urur"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":239.77,"en":252.8,"si":11,"ev":"Ultimately the reward comes from knowing that you've done it with precision.","uz":"Oxir-oqibat mukofot — buni aniq bajarganingizni bilishdan keladi.","why":"Aniq bajarganidan qoniqish (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What does George appreciate most about riding a motorbike?","qu":"George mototsikl haydashning qaysi jihatini eng ko'p qadrlaydi?","o":["It allows him to avoid the traffic jams on the way to work","It reminds him of when he was a teenager","It gives him some time for himself"],"ou":["Ishga ketayotganda tirbandlikdan qochish imkonini beradi","O'smirlik yillarini eslatadi","Unga o'zi uchun biroz vaqt beradi"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":381.05,"en":387.77,"si":15,"ev":"When I put on my helmet, I'm shut away, you know, in my own little world. And that means I arrive feeling quite calm.","uz":"Dubulg'ani kiyganimda o'zimning kichik dunyomga yopilib qolaman. Shuning uchun ishga xotirjam yetib boraman.","why":"O'zi uchun vaqt (C). Tirbandlikdan qochish (A) — \"it is a bit\" quicker, asosiy sabab emas.","hl":null},{"q":"Which is George's favourite object in his house?","qu":"George uyidagi eng sevimli buyumi qaysi?","o":["the kitchen table","the shower","the cooker"],"ou":["oshxona stoli","dush","plita"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":416.73,"en":425.02,"si":20,"ev":"What I long for is a shower when I get home. I feel the stress of the day disappear with the water.","uz":"Uyga kelganda eng ko'p dushni qo'msayman. Kun bo'yi to'plangan stress suv bilan ketganini his qilaman.","why":"Sevimli buyumi — dush (B). Stol (A) — oilasiniki, plita (C) — restorandagisi.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":48.34,"e":48.34,"t":"Extract One — You hear part of an interview with a broadcaster who's talking about a series of programs he presented about landscape painting."},{"s":48.34,"e":59.87,"t":"Why did you decide to include a painting by a famous politician? I wanted to remind viewers that amateur painting has its own purpose, that scores and scores of people paint for themselves as that politician did."},{"s":60.63,"e":86.04,"t":"I liked his daughter's explanation that it helped to give him some respite from the pressures of public life. I thought that was important to focus on so that we weren't just talking about painters as professionals who had really cracked it and who taught us things about their technique. You draw yourself, don't you? Yes, I've always liked it though. I'm afraid my attempts aren't very good so I keep them purely for my own amusement. The intensity of drawing is always a great thrill."},{"s":86.58,"e":98.01,"t":"I can't say it's a relief, which it obviously is for some people. You have to use your eyes to look more carefully at a scene than you would if you were just out for a walk or even if you were taking a photograph as an amateur."},{"s":98.52,"e":102.3,"t":"There's something about drawing that forces you to see things and think about them."},{"k":"h","s":201.78,"e":201.78,"t":"Extract Two — You hear an amateur pilot called Gina Nesbitt talking about doing aerobatics in her small plane."},{"s":201.78,"e":209.37,"t":"I've only ever been up in a plane once where the pilot turned the plane over in an aerobatic display and I've never been more scared or felt sicker."},{"s":209.94,"e":218.56,"t":"Do you get that sinking feeding too Gina? I'm very fortunate in that I don't. This came as a pleasant surprise to me because I do get terribly seasick."},{"s":219.0,"e":222.3,"t":"I find that what's routine and what I'm used to doing isn't frightening."},{"s":222.81,"e":233.92,"t":"Learning some of the new maneuvers, though, can be quite daunting because this is a single-seater plane. So the first time I do anything new, I'm on my own, except for the guidance of my coach who's on the ground."},{"s":234.52,"e":239.26,"t":"What's the real thrill for you of performing these difficult maneuvers in competitions?"},{"s":239.77,"e":252.8,"t":"It's exciting, of course, but ultimately the reward comes from knowing that you've done it with precision. It involves an unusual combination of mental preparation, physical preparation, and skill."},{"s":253.3,"e":263.55,"t":"It's not as difficult as you might first think to fly the sequences of movements. What is difficult is doing it to a high enough standard to avoid the faults the judges are looking out for."},{"k":"h","s":370.17,"e":370.17,"t":"Extract Three — You overhear a chef called George talking to a friend about his daily routine."},{"s":370.17,"e":380.35,"t":"Exhausted! It took an hour to drive 5km You should do what I do and use a motorbike Is it much quicker? It is a bit, because you avoid some cues"},{"s":381.05,"e":387.77,"t":"The great thing is, when I put on my helmet, I'm shut away, you know, in my own little world. And that means I arrive feeling quite calm."},{"s":388.57,"e":394.62,"t":"I started riding a motorbike where I grew up in the country because there weren't any buses. So is that your most prized possession?"},{"s":395.26,"e":406.17,"t":"I was asked recently what my favourite thing at home was. As a chef, I imagine yours is something in the kitchen. Your cooker, perhaps? The one at the restaurant is fantastic because it was specially designed for me."},{"s":407.06,"e":408.48,"t":"It's hard to say here."},{"s":409.08,"e":416.22,"t":"My family love the kitchen table where they chat for hours. Given the late hours I work, I hardly participate in that."},{"s":416.73,"e":421.37,"t":"No, my workplace is so hot and sticky that what I long for is a shower when I get home."},{"s":422.1,"e":425.02,"t":"I feel the stress of the day disappear with the water."},{"s":425.46,"e":426.78,"t":"Odd thing to choose, isn't"}]},{"n":9,"title":"Two people talking about their work as website designers","dur":483.68325,"x":[{"ps":44.25,"en":102.08,"c":"You hear two people talking about their work as website designers."},{"ps":198.58,"en":253.18,"c":"You hear two cyclists talking about their sport."},{"ps":343.06,"en":408.45,"c":"You hear a man called Roy talking about bees on a phonin program."}],"items":[{"q":"How does the man feel about the work?","qu":"Erkak ish haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["He finds the creativity stimulating","He would like to use his academic training more","He gets most satisfaction from being part of a team"],"ou":["Ijodkorlik uni ruhlantiradi","Akademik bilimidan ko'proq foydalanishni xohlardi","Eng katta qoniqishni jamoaning bir qismi bo'lishdan oladi"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":44.25,"en":61.09,"si":1,"ev":"What companies want is people who can come up with ideas. I get a buzz from that side of it, even when it's hard.","uz":"Kompaniyalarga g'oya o'ylab topa oladigan odamlar kerak. Qiyin bo'lsa ham, ishning aynan shu tomonidan zavq olaman.","why":"Ijodkorlik uni ruhlantiradi (A). Diplom \"strictly speaking isn't necessary\" (B emas); u yolg'iz ishlashni yoqtiradi (C emas).","hl":null},{"q":"What do they both think about the job?","qu":"Ikkalasi bu ish haqida nima deb o'ylaydi?","o":["It's a difficult career to get started in","It's important to be able to work flexible hours","It's a poorly paid job for the amount of work involved"],"ou":["Bu sohada ish boshlash qiyin","Moslashuvchan soatlarda ishlay olish muhim","Qilinadigan ish hajmiga nisbatan maoshi past"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":61.59,"en":94.05,"si":2,"ev":"Hours aren't fixed and can be long in relation to the salary… considering what you put in, the job's not the big earner that people assume it is.","uz":"Ish vaqti belgilanmagan va maoshga nisbatan uzoq bo'lishi mumkin… qilgan mehnatingizga qarasangiz, bu ish odamlar o'ylaganchalik daromadli emas.","why":"Ikkalasi ham mehnatga nisbatan maosh past deydi (C). Moslashuvchanlikni faqat ikkinchisi tilga oladi.","hl":null},{"q":"The man thinks his success as a cyclist is due to","qu":"Erkak velosipedchi sifatidagi muvaffaqiyatini ... bilan bog'laydi","o":["his complete dedication","the age at which he started","a series of great role models"],"ou":["to'liq fidoyiligi","qaysi yoshda boshlagani","bir qator ajoyib ibrat namunalari"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":198.58,"en":222.91,"si":8,"ev":"I've always been competitive and I work harder than anyone else. If I don't win, I need to know why… I won't stop till I'm better than them.","uz":"Men doim raqobatchi bo'lganman va hammadan ko'p mehnat qilaman. Yutqazsam, sababini bilishim kerak… ulardan yaxshiroq bo'lmaguncha to'xtamayman.","why":"Muvaffaqiyat — to'liq fidoyilik (A). Olti yoshda boshlagani (B) faqat fakt sifatida aytiladi.","hl":null},{"q":"When talking about cycling in a velodrome, the woman reveals her","qu":"Velotrekda velosiped haydash haqida gapirganda ayol o'zining ... ni oshkor qiladi","o":["fear of dangerous sports","inability to follow instructions","willingness to accept a challenge"],"ou":["xavfli sport turlaridan qo'rquvini","ko'rsatmalarga amal qila olmasligini","sinovni qabul qilishga tayyorligini"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":229.05,"en":251.49,"si":10,"ev":"I jumped at the chance to try it and wow! From the start line that steep slope looks like a mountain.","uz":"Uni sinab ko'rish imkoniyatiga darhol yopishdim — voy! Start chizig'idan o'sha tik qiyalik tog'dek ko'rinadi.","why":"\"Jumped at the chance\" = sinovni qabul qilishga tayyor (C).","hl":null},{"q":"Why has he phoned the programme?","qu":"U nega dasturga qo'ng'iroq qildi?","o":["to raise issues not previously discussed","to challenge the opinions of other contributors","to lend his support to a view that's been expressed"],"ou":["avval muhokama qilinmagan masalalarni ko'tarish uchun","boshqa ishtirokchilarning fikriga e'tiroz bildirish uchun","aytilgan fikrni qo'llab-quvvatlash uchun"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":355.42,"en":363.2,"si":15,"ev":"For what it's worth, my own experience is much like that of other callers who've reported near normal numbers of bumblebees, but virtually no honey bees.","uz":"Aytish joiz bo'lsa, mening tajribam ham boshqa qo'ng'iroq qilganlarnikiga o'xshaydi: tukli arilar soni deyarli normal, lekin asalarilar deyarli yo'q.","why":"U avval aytilgan fikrni qo'llab-quvvatlayapti (C).","hl":null},{"q":"When talking about gardens, he is","qu":"Bog'lar haqida gapirganda u ...","o":["describing what he does in his own","encouraging people to grow certain things","suggesting that people keep bees themselves"],"ou":["o'z bog'ida nima qilishini tasvirlayapti","odamlarni ma'lum o'simliklarni o'stirishga undayapti","odamlarga o'zlari asalari boqishni taklif qilyapti"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":384.73,"en":401.31,"si":21,"ev":"The best thing anyone lucky enough to have a garden can do is provide a bee-friendly area… Choose what you plant carefully.","uz":"Bog'i borlar qila oladigan eng yaxshi ish — arilar uchun qulay joy yaratish… Nima ekishni ehtiyotkorlik bilan tanlang.","why":"Odamlarni ma'lum o'simliklarni o'stirishga undayapti (B). O'z bog'i haqida gapirmaydi (A), asalari boqishni taklif qilmaydi (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":44.25,"e":44.25,"t":"Extract One — You hear two people talking about their work as website designers."},{"s":44.25,"e":61.09,"t":"I was always messing around on computers, so I ended up doing a degree in computer science. Though strictly speaking it isn't necessary for this job, it did mean I could walk straight into it. What companies want is people who can come up with ideas. I get a buzz from that side of it, even when it's hard."},{"s":61.59,"e":74.88,"t":"It's a fluid working environment so hours aren't fixed and can be long in relation to the salary. I generally like to work on my own, but a web designer can't produce stuff in a vacuum because by its very nature it's a collaborative effort."},{"s":75.61,"e":83.71,"t":"Well I didn't go the university route but worked part time with different companies and made loads of contacts so you've come in handy. Got my foot in the door so to speak."},{"s":84.25,"e":86.88,"t":"Then I got a full-time job offer that got me on the ladder"},{"s":87.48,"e":94.05,"t":"It wasn't easy and considering what you put in, the job's not the big earner that people assume it is, or at least not at the beginning."},{"s":94.65,"e":102.08,"t":"I supplement it by writing reviews of other people's sites, but I enjoy the flexibility. I like working with other people, and that's key."},{"k":"h","s":198.58,"e":198.58,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two cyclists talking about their sport."},{"s":198.58,"e":222.91,"t":"Have you been cycling then? I started road cycling when I was six and got hooked immediately I'd practice sprinting between two street lights over and over I've always been competitive and I work harder than anyone else if I don't win I need to know why I copy the person who beat me I won't stop till I'm better than them the stiff competition in the cycling world is what drives me You've been to the velodrome haven't you? Yeah, the track itself is amazing"},{"s":223.45,"e":228.61,"t":"At such a steep angle and the bikes have no brakes, if you stop pedaling it stops."},{"s":229.05,"e":251.49,"t":"Although I'm not such an experienced cyclist as you, I jumped at the chance to try it and wow! From the position of the start line that steep slope looks like a mountain. I was told the faster you go, the safer you are so I pedalled like mad and managed one lap. I kept going and started to enjoy it. So much so I forgot to pedal and immediately fell off. So you'll be going back."},{"s":251.93,"e":253.18,"t":"Can you try stopping me?"},{"k":"h","s":343.06,"e":343.06,"t":"Extract Three — You hear a man called Roy talking about bees on a phonin program."},{"s":343.06,"e":348.8,"t":"So, Rolly, what do you want to talk about on the programme today? I want to talk about bees."},{"s":349.5,"e":354.97,"t":"Bees are a vital part of our ecosystem. They're friendly creatures and they're declining in numbers."},{"s":355.42,"e":363.2,"t":"For what it's worth, my own experience is much like that of other callers who've reported near normal numbers of bumbled bees, but virtually no honey bees."},{"s":363.99,"e":366.17,"t":"I think there's a distinct lack of wasps too."},{"s":366.9,"e":373.82,"t":"I'm at a loss to know why, though I've read interesting articles about the domestication of bees and poor practices of modern beekeepers."},{"s":374.33,"e":378.14,"t":"But it seems clear that we can't discount what others see as the number one culprit."},{"s":378.87,"e":380.83,"t":"The overuse of chemicals by gardener."},{"s":381.82,"e":384.19,"t":"What do you suggest gardeners do, Roy?"},{"s":384.73,"e":390.14,"t":"Well, the best thing anyone lucky enough to have a garden can do is provide a bee-friendly area."},{"s":390.94,"e":395.2,"t":"And the good news is bees prefer lazy gardeners, which I suspect is most of us."},{"s":396.06,"e":398.75,"t":"A wild garden providing a natural habitat is the way forward."},{"s":399.61,"e":401.31,"t":"Choose what you plant carefully."},{"s":401.98,"e":404.67,"t":"It doesn't have to be hard work, but it could make a big difference"},{"s":405.4,"e":408.45,"t":"and buy your honey from local suppliers you know and trust."}]},{"n":10,"title":"Two friends discussing a rock concert they both went to","dur":476.656313,"x":[{"ps":46.49,"en":95.84,"c":"You hear two friends discussing a rock concert they both went to."},{"ps":180.25,"en":244.8,"c":"you hear part of a sports report about a football club manager."},{"ps":343.96,"en":403.39,"c":"You hear two friends discussing an exhibition of modern sculpture."}],"items":[{"q":"How does the boy feel about the main band?","qu":"Bola asosiy guruh haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["disappointed by their performance","confused by all the advanced publicity","unsure whether he got value for money or not"],"ou":["ularning ijrosidan hafsalasi pir bo'lgan","oldindan qilingan reklamalardan chalkashib qolgan","to'lagan puliga arziganmi-yo'qmi, ikkilanadi"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":46.49,"en":71.77,"si":1,"ev":"I went with high hopes of seeing something really spectacular from the headline band, and it just didn't happen.","uz":"Asosiy guruhdan haqiqatan ajoyib narsa ko'rish umidida borgan edim, lekin bunday bo'lmadi.","why":"Ijrodan hafsalasi pir bo'lgan (A). Pul (C) — \"we got a hefty student discount\", reklama (B) — uni chalg'itmagan, aldagan.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the woman doing in her reply?","qu":"Ayol javobida nima qilyapti?","o":["criticising the support band","defending the approach of the media","agreeing with comments about the main band"],"ou":["yordamchi (ochuvchi) guruhni tanqid qilyapti","ommaviy axborot vositalarining yondashuvini himoya qilyapti","asosiy guruh haqidagi fikrlarga qo'shilyapti"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":71.9,"en":95.84,"si":2,"ev":"If you ask me, you're being rather hard on the main band. They were way better than the support act.","uz":"Menimcha, sen asosiy guruhga nisbatan ancha qattiqqo'llik qilyapsan. Ular ochuvchi guruhdan ancha yaxshi edi.","why":"Ayol ochuvchi (support) guruhni tanqid qilyapti (A). U asosiy guruh haqidagi fikrga qo'shilmaydi (C emas).","hl":null},{"q":"What is the male presenter doing?","qu":"Erkak boshlovchi nima qilyapti?","o":["praising changes that the manager has made","suggesting that rumours about the manager are unfounded","describing a growing sense of dissatisfaction with the manager's performance"],"ou":["murabbiy kiritgan o'zgarishlarni maqtayapti","murabbiy haqidagi mish-mishlar asossiz ekanini aytyapti","murabbiy ishidan norozilik kuchayib borayotganini tasvirlayapti"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":189.78,"en":204.03,"si":6,"ev":"I sense that there may actually be little substance to stories that his job's on the line.","uz":"Uning ishi xavf ostida degan gaplarda asos kam bo'lsa kerak deb sezyapman.","why":"Mish-mishlar asossiz (B).","hl":null},{"q":"In the female presenter's opinion","qu":"Ayol boshlovchining fikricha","o":["the manager's strategy is the correct one","the real problem is a lack of talented players","the pressure on the manager is likely to increase"],"ou":["murabbiyning strategiyasi to'g'ri","asl muammo iste'dodli o'yinchilar yetishmasligida","murabbiyga bosim kuchayishi ehtimoli bor"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":212.95,"en":244.8,"si":9,"ev":"Time's running out for him… the results speak for themselves… if a top-flight football team isn't getting points, then something's got to change.","uz":"Uning vaqti tugab bormoqda… natijalar o'zi gapiradi… yuqori ligadagi jamoa ochko olmasa, nimadir o'zgarishi kerak.","why":"Murabbiyga bosim kuchayadi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman particularly admire about the artist?","qu":"Ayol rassomning ayniqsa qaysi jihatiga qoyil qoladi?","o":["the originality of his work","the way his art has developed","the issues that his sculptures raise"],"ou":["ishlarining o'ziga xosligi","san'ati qanday rivojlangani","haykallari ko'taradigan masalalar"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":345.88,"en":361.69,"si":14,"ev":"It really makes you think, you know, about more than just the art, about aspects of life itself.","uz":"U haqiqatan o'ylantiradi — faqat san'at haqida emas, hayotning o'zi haqida ham.","why":"Haykallar ko'taradigan masalalar (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What disappointed them both about the exhibition?","qu":"Ko'rgazmadagi nima ikkalasining ham hafsalasini pir qildi?","o":["the pieces of work that had been chosen","the information provided for visitors","the way it had been laid out"],"ou":["tanlangan asarlar","tashrif buyuruvchilarga berilgan ma'lumot","uning joylashtirilish tartibi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":386.3,"en":390.62,"si":16,"ev":"I'd have been happy to have seen some of his other stuff actually. — Yeah, more of a range.","uz":"Aslida uning boshqa ishlarini ham ko'rsam xursand bo'lardim. — Ha, ko'proq xilma-xillik.","why":"Tanlangan asarlardan norozi (A). Ma'lumot (B) — ular o'qishmaydi; joylashtirish (C) — maqtaladi.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":46.49,"e":46.49,"t":"Extract One — You hear two friends discussing a rock concert they both went to."},{"s":46.49,"e":71.77,"t":"Tom, so what do you think of the concert? Well, I'm not complaining because at the end of the day I had a pretty good night out. But it's just as well that we got a hefty student discount on the tickets. I went with high hopes of seeing something really spectacular from the headline band, and it just didn't happen. I reckon I was taken in by all the hype, you know, the big build-up in the media and everything. I should know better than to take any notice of it, but you just get swept up by it, don't you? Well, you may."},{"s":71.9,"e":83.93,"t":"I hadn't actually read or heard much about the gig at all, so I didn't go with any preconceptions. If you ask me, you're being rather hard on the main band. I mean, they were way better than the support act."},{"s":84.41,"e":95.84,"t":"If the idea was to get us in the mood for what was coming later, then I think they should have been presenting us with something a bit more exciting. Well, who knows? Perhaps they were chosen because they wouldn't upstage the stars."},{"k":"h","s":180.25,"e":180.25,"t":"Extract Two — you hear part of a sports report about a football club manager."},{"s":180.25,"e":189.31,"t":"There's been also speculation in the press this week surrounding the fate of United manager Tony Benson, with some people calling for his resignation after a run of poll results."},{"s":189.78,"e":204.03,"t":"Talking to people at the club this week, I sense that there may actually be little substance to stories that is jobs on the line. Indeed, a number of people I spoke to were keen to defend his record, feeling that he was focusing the players on a more stylish, entertaining brand of football."},{"s":204.66,"e":209.53,"t":"They thought it would only be a matter of time before we begin to see this reflected in the results."},{"s":210.39,"e":212.35,"t":"What's your take on all this, Susie?"},{"s":212.95,"e":224.29,"t":"Well, Gary, the club's invested in promising players. The potential's there, it's just a question of whether Benson's the man to pull it all together and make it work, and time's running out for him."},{"s":224.76,"e":231.04,"t":"I've been talking to some of the players and I'd say there was a groundswell of support in the dressing room for Benson's general approach."},{"s":231.64,"e":244.8,"t":"But I think the results speak for themselves. And these days, if a top-flight football team isn't getting points, then something's got to change. And that comes back to the manager. Because that's his responsibility, getting the results."},{"k":"h","s":343.96,"e":343.96,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two friends discussing an exhibition of modern sculpture."},{"s":343.96,"e":345.02,"t":"So what did you think of"},{"s":345.88,"e":361.69,"t":"I could stand and look at his work all day long. I know it's a strange thing to say about sculpture but it really makes you think, you know, about more than just the art, about aspects of life itself. But this was a strange exhibition. They seem to have gone for quite an eclectic selection."},{"s":362.2,"e":385.57,"t":"Was it meant to be representative of something? I never read the notes they hand out because I prefer to come to my own interpretation. Yes, so do I. Actually, I think the unifying theme was the material. I mean, all these pieces were made out of the same three raw materials, wire, glass and straw. Not all his work is, of course, but I guess it's a phase he went through part of his development as an artist."},{"s":386.3,"e":390.62,"t":"I might have been happy to have seen some of his other stuff actually. Yeah, more of a range."},{"s":391.16,"e":403.39,"t":"Well you can't fault the museum, can you? I mean, any exhibition they put on is worth going to. It's such a brilliant space and you never know how things are going to look because the presentation's so imaginative, isn't it? There's nowhere quite like it, really."}]},{"n":11,"title":"Two friends discussing a TV interview with an actress called Celia Dent","dur":490.266063,"x":[{"ps":8.41,"en":68.67,"c":""},{"ps":171.22,"en":232.83,"c":"You hear two friends discussing a TV interview with an actress called Celia Dent."},{"ps":334.52,"en":408.19,"c":"You hear two freelance journalists talking about their work."}],"items":[{"q":"How does Charles feel about designers who put their names on products?","qu":"Charles mahsulotlarga o'z ismini qo'yadigan dizaynerlar haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["He understands their basic needs.","He is dismissive of their motives.","He admires their business skills."],"ou":["Ularning asosiy ehtiyojlarini tushunadi.","Ularning niyatlarini mensimaydi.","Ularning biznes mahoratiga qoyil qoladi."],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":27.35,"en":45.76,"si":2,"ev":"Nowadays you can find designers' names on products, but it tends to be high profile people seeking attention… A ploy to get you to buy products.","uz":"Hozir mahsulotlarda dizaynerlar ismini ko'rish mumkin, lekin bular odatda e'tibor talab qiladigan mashhur odamlar… Bu sizni xarid qilishga undash uchun hiyla.","why":"U ularning niyatlarini mensimaydi (B): \"seeking attention\", \"a ploy\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does Charles suggest about a good product?","qu":"Charles yaxshi mahsulot haqida nima deydi?","o":["Its appearance should reflect its function.","It should encourage a desire to possess it.","Its ecological impact should be considered."],"ou":["Ko'rinishi vazifasini aks ettirishi kerak.","Unga ega bo'lish istagini uyg'otishi kerak.","Uning ekologik ta'siri hisobga olinishi kerak."],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":46.46,"en":68.67,"si":5,"ev":"I tried to make things appear as if they just belong. They don't need to scream. I don't think a nutcracker needs to look like an elephant.","uz":"Narsalarni o'z joyidagidek ko'rinadigan qilishga harakat qilardim. Ular baqirishi shart emas. Yong'oq chaqqich filga o'xshashi kerak deb o'ylamayman.","why":"Ko'rinish vazifani aks ettirishi kerak (A). Egalik istagini uyg'otish (B) — u buni yoqtirmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"They agree that the interviewer made the mistake of","qu":"Ular intervyu oluvchi ... xatosiga yo'l qo'ygan degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["dominating the discussion.","asking predictable questions.","failing to listen fully to answers."],"ou":["suhbatda hukmronlik qilish","oldindan bilsa bo'ladigan savollar berish","javoblarni oxirigacha tinglamaslik"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":171.22,"en":207.68,"si":9,"ev":"It was the usual tired stuff being put to her… This guy showed no imagination at all, just covering old ground and targeting obvious stuff.","uz":"Unga odatdagi siyqasi chiqqan savollar berildi… Bu odam hech qanday tasavvur ko'rsatmadi, faqat eski, ko'zga tashlanib turgan mavzularni so'radi.","why":"Ikkalasi ham oldindan bilsa bo'ladigan savollarni tanqid qiladi (B). Suhbatda hukmronlik (A) — faqat birinchisi aytadi.","hl":null},{"q":"The man says that certain film stars can be difficult to interview because","qu":"Erkakning aytishicha, ayrim kino yulduzlaridan intervyu olish qiyin, chunki","o":["they generally show a lack of spontaneity.","they're unwilling to reveal their true personality.","they're too anxious to promote their latest work."],"ou":["ular odatda tabiiylikdan yiroq","ular asl qiyofasini ochishni istamaydi","ular so'nggi ishini reklama qilishga juda oshiqadi"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":208.25,"en":226.14,"si":11,"ev":"Some seem afraid to be themselves, like they're desperate to keep up their public image at all costs.","uz":"Ba'zilari o'zligini ko'rsatishdan qo'rqadiganga o'xshaydi, go'yo har qanday holatda ham jamoatchilik oldidagi obro'sini saqlab qolishga intilishadi.","why":"Asl qiyofasini ochishni istamaydi (B). Reklama (C) — \"understandably keen\", lekin muammo deb aytilmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"When talking about how he tackles a creative writing task, the man","qu":"Ijodiy yozish vazifasiga qanday kirishishi haqida gapirganda erkak","o":["points out how easily he can assume the right frame of mind.","tries to justify his antisocial behaviour when working.","admits that frequent breaks can be beneficial."],"ou":["kerakli ruhiy holatga qanchalik oson kira olishini ta'kidlaydi","ishlayotgandagi odamovi xatti-harakatini oqlashga urinadi","tez-tez tanaffus qilish foydali bo'lishi mumkinligini tan oladi"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":354.2,"en":388.22,"si":17,"ev":"I'll shout at anyone who knocks at my study door… I'm certainly not upholding it as a model of good behavior, but… sometimes it's necessary.","uz":"Kabinetim eshigini taqillatgan har kimga baqiraman… Albatta, buni yaxshi xulq namunasi demayman, lekin… ba'zan bu zarur.","why":"U odamovi xatti-harakatini oqlashga urinadi (B). Kayfiyatga kirish oson emas (A emas): \"it can take me a while\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman say about her earlier writing?","qu":"Ayol avvalgi yozganlari haqida nima deydi?","o":["She feels she no longer fully relates to it.","She tends to draw on similar themes in her current work.","She highlights the improvements she's noticed in her work."],"ou":["Endi ular bilan o'zini to'liq bog'lay olmaydi.","Hozirgi ishlarida ham shunga o'xshash mavzulardan foydalanadi.","Ishida sezgan yaxshilanishlarni ta'kidlaydi."],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":388.76,"en":408.19,"si":21,"ev":"I find I can't always recreate the mindset I had during its creation, because inevitably I've since broadened my perspective on it.","uz":"Uni yozgan paytdagi fikrlash tarzimni har doim ham qayta tiklay olmayman, chunki o'shandan beri qarashlarim kengaygan.","why":"U endi eski yozganlari bilan o'zini to'liq bog'lay olmaydi (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":8.41,"e":8.41,"t":"Extract One"},{"s":8.41,"e":26.72,"t":"Charles, you're retired now, but you actually designed some 600 household products, and all of them as an employee of a company. Did it ever frustrate you that you were making products without your name on? It was standard practice. Besides, I needed a weekly paycheck before I needed recognition."},{"s":27.35,"e":33.18,"t":"Nowadays you can find designers' names on products, but it tends to be high profile people seeking attention."},{"s":33.66,"e":36.22,"t":"And then there's celebrity endorsement and all that."},{"s":36.79,"e":45.76,"t":"People think that if they buy a soccer ball that has the name of some famous player on it, they're going to score wonderful goals. A ploy to get you to buy products."},{"s":46.46,"e":60.25,"t":"What advice do you have for young designers? What they do will affect so many people during the lifetime of that product. That's serious stuff. So the product should do what it's supposed to do and be pleasing to have in your environment."},{"s":61.02,"e":65.31,"t":"I tried to make things appear as if they just belong. They don't need to scream."},{"s":65.82,"e":68.67,"t":"I don't think a nutcracker needs to look like an elephant."},{"k":"h","s":171.22,"e":171.22,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two friends discussing a TV interview with an actress called Celia Dent."},{"s":171.22,"e":182.75,"t":"Well, what a one-sided interview that was, and with one of my favourite actresses, she hardly got a look in. No one would have learned anything new about her, especially as it was the usual tired stuff being put to her."},{"s":183.26,"e":207.68,"t":"When she did try to steer things in a different direction, the interviewer just ignored her and kept going on about himself. Hmm, there aren't many really good interviewers, are there? The best ones really take on board what's being said and follow it up. This guy showed no imagination at all, just covering old ground and targeting obvious stuff. No wonder he couldn't get interesting responses. And Celia could have told a few stories. She's had a fascinating life."},{"s":208.25,"e":226.14,"t":"I know some film actors are perhaps a bit tricky, some seem afraid to be themselves, like they're desperate to keep up their public image at all costs, and of course many actors are interviewed just after their last film's been released and are understandably keen to publicise it, but interviewers often concentrate on other superficial stuff."},{"s":226.74,"e":232.83,"t":"I love it when actors are challenged a bit and the interviewer dares to deviate from the set script putting them on the spot."},{"k":"h","s":334.52,"e":334.52,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two freelance journalists talking about their work."},{"s":334.52,"e":335.1,"t":"One"},{"s":335.74,"e":337.41,"t":"You must get down to some work."},{"s":337.91,"e":353.5,"t":"is getting started tricky for you? Well, it can take me a while to enter into a creative state. But once I'm there, I lose awareness of absolutely anything but the ideas flowing. Don't even perceive my fingers typing. Really? Mmm."},{"s":354.2,"e":359.74,"t":"And I'm then extremely resistant to interruption, so I'll shout at anyone who knocks at my study door."},{"s":360.28,"e":365.47,"t":"My defensive reactions are subconscious though, and usually I don't even recall them."},{"s":366.14,"e":371.04,"t":"The family's used to it, and I'm certainly not upholding it as a model of good behavior, but..."},{"s":371.54,"e":388.22,"t":"Sometimes it's necessary. Yeah, once I'm immersed in creating something, I usually maintain that state until I complete the work. And I don't even feel as if I'm working. But if I look at the task ahead of me, all I tend to see is the effort involved. Right."},{"s":388.76,"e":408.19,"t":"And what about stuff you wrote ages back? Do you return to it for inspiration? Well, I find I can't always recreate the mindset I had during its creation, because inevitably I've since broadened my perspective on it. I can see why I use the inspiration I did, but obviously experience changes you. Yes, absolutely."}]},{"n":12,"title":"Two friends talking about online privacy","dur":558.445688,"x":[{"ps":29.88,"en":91.9,"c":"You hear two friends talking about online privacy."},{"ps":194.55,"en":272.28,"c":"You hear two trainee chefs discussing the issue of food waste."},{"ps":391.32,"en":470.01,"c":"You hear two students talking about an experiment into the way people perceive time."}],"items":[{"q":"Why does the man mention his uncle?","qu":"Erkak nega amakisini tilga oladi?","o":["to criticise his attitude to technology","to challenge a recommendation made by the woman","to illustrate the power of the media"],"ou":["uning texnologiyaga munosabatini tanqid qilish uchun","ayolning tavsiyasiga e'tiroz bildirish uchun","ommaviy axborot vositalarining kuchini ko'rsatish uchun"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":45.18,"en":67.13,"si":2,"ev":"I was discussing the whole issue with an uncle of mine… He proudly informed me that there couldn't be any data relating to him on the internet because he'd never used a computer… I was still able to come up with quite a bit of stuff about him.","uz":"Bu masalani 85 yoshli amakim bilan muhokama qilgandim… U kompyuter ishlatmagani uchun internetda u haqida hech qanday ma'lumot yo'q deb faxr bilan aytdi… Lekin bir-ikki daqiqada u haqida ancha ma'lumot topdim.","why":"Amakisi misolida internet (OAV) qanchalik kuchli ekanini ko'rsatadi (C). U amakisining texnologiyaga munosabatini tanqid qilmaydi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"They agree that modern technology","qu":"Ular zamonaviy texnologiya ... degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["makes little difference to the accessibility of personal information.","is less invasive than some people suggest.","will continue to reduce people's privacy."],"ou":["shaxsiy ma'lumotlarning ochiqligiga deyarli ta'sir qilmaydi","ba'zilar aytganchalik shaxsiy hayotga aralashmaydi","odamlarning shaxsiy daxlsizligini kamaytirishda davom etadi"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":86.84,"en":91.9,"si":6,"ev":"And the situation's not going to improve? — No, I guess not. Quite the opposite.","uz":"Vaziyat yaxshilanmaydimi? — Yo'q, menimcha. Aksincha.","why":"Texnologiya shaxsiy daxlsizlikni kamaytirishda davom etadi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman think about her boss's ideas?","qu":"Ayol rahbarining g'oyalari haqida nima deb o'ylaydi?","o":["She's surprised at his forward-looking attitude.","She's dismissive of his attention to detail.","She's concerned about his generosity towards customers."],"ou":["Uning ilg'or qarashidan hayron.","Uning mayda-chuydaga e'tiborini mensimaydi.","Uning mijozlarga saxiyligidan xavotirda."],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":220.7,"en":243.39,"si":9,"ev":"Our place is unrecognisable from what it was like last year. As is my boss. Can't think what's got into him. Thinking ahead for a change.","uz":"Bizning joy o'tgan yilgidan tanib bo'lmas darajada o'zgargan. Rahbarim ham. Unga nima bo'lganini bilmayman — bu safar oldinni o'ylayapti.","why":"Rahbarining ilg'or qarashidan hayron (A).","hl":null},{"q":"In reacting to the woman's comments, the man reveals that he is","qu":"Ayolning gaplariga javob berar ekan, erkak ... ekanini oshkor qiladi","o":["determined to change practices at his own workplace.","unsure about the facts she is presenting to him.","doubtful whether his chef would accept new ideas."],"ou":["o'z ish joyidagi tartiblarni o'zgartirishga qat'iy ahd qilgan","ayol keltirayotgan faktlarga ishonchi yo'q","oshpazi yangi g'oyalarni qabul qilishiga shubhali"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":244.22,"en":272.28,"si":10,"ev":"Okay, maybe I'd better talk to my head chef. Might be fighting an uphill battle though.","uz":"Mayli, bosh oshpazim bilan gaplashib ko'rganim ma'qul. Lekin bu juda qiyin kurash bo'lishi mumkin.","why":"Oshpazi yangi g'oyalarni qabul qilishiga shubha qiladi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman thinks the experiment was important because","qu":"Ayol tajriba muhim bo'lgan deb hisoblaydi, chunki","o":["it provided unexpected results.","it presented a great physical challenge.","it raised public awareness of the subject."],"ou":["u kutilmagan natijalar berdi","u katta jismoniy sinov bo'ldi","u jamoatchilikning mavzu haqidagi xabardorligini oshirdi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":396.82,"en":422.21,"si":14,"ev":"When he came back up, he thought he'd been down there for just 34 days… very revealing for the researchers who'd anticipated it would go the other way.","uz":"Yuqoriga chiqqanda, u yerda atigi 34 kun bo'ldim deb o'ylagan… bu teskarisini kutgan tadqiqotchilar uchun juda ko'p narsani ochib berdi.","why":"Tajriba kutilmagan natija berdi (A). Kaskadyorlar (C emas) faqat shuhrat uchun qiladi.","hl":null},{"q":"She believes celebrating special events","qu":"Uning fikricha, alohida voqealarni nishonlash","o":["convinces people that time passes more quickly.","provides people with pleasant memories.","gives people a sense of structure when recalling the past."],"ou":["odamlarni vaqt tezroq o'tishiga ishontiradi","odamlarga yoqimli xotiralar beradi","o'tmishni eslaganda odamlarga tartib (tayanch nuqtalar) hissini beradi"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":422.65,"en":470.01,"si":16,"ev":"Temporal landmarks… If you build more of them into your life, you will experience time differently… Remember to mark special events like birthdays properly with some sort of celebration.","uz":"Vaqt \"belgilari\"… Ularni hayotingizga ko'proq kiritsangiz, vaqtni boshqacha his qilasiz… Tug'ilgan kun kabi alohida voqealarni munosib nishonlang.","why":"Nishonlash o'tmishni eslashda tayanch nuqtalar (tartib) beradi (C). Vaqt tezroq o'tishiga ishontirmaydi (A) — aksincha.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":29.88,"e":29.88,"t":"Extract One — You hear two friends talking about online privacy."},{"s":29.88,"e":44.57,"t":"You know, I think privacy as we used to understand it is a thing of the past. Why do you say that? Not another scare story in the papers. They're always full of fancy full tales of doom and gloom. You may laugh, but after what happened yesterday... What did happen?"},{"s":45.18,"e":48.89,"t":"I was discussing the whole issue with an uncle of mine who's just turned 85."},{"s":49.78,"e":67.13,"t":"He proudly informed me that there couldn't be any data relating to him on the internet because he'd never used a computer. Well, fair enough, Shirley. Well, I only spent a couple of minutes searching and was still able to come up with quite a bit of stuff about him. Really? That's a bit worrying. I bet he was taken aback, wasn't he? He was stunned."},{"s":67.7,"e":68.41,"t":"speechless."},{"s":68.95,"e":86.37,"t":"asked me to remove it all from cyberspace. But it doesn't work like that, of course. What's there is there. That does seem an erosion of privacy. Mind you, come to think of it, I suppose there's also been some information available on us all for a while, way before the days of the internet. But it wasn't so easy to get at."},{"s":86.84,"e":91.9,"t":"And the situation's not going to improve? No, I guess not. Quite the opposite."},{"k":"h","s":194.55,"e":194.55,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two trainee chefs discussing the issue of food waste."},{"s":194.55,"e":220.12,"t":"Did you know that over 7 million tons of food is thrown away every year in the UK? Really? That's one big garbage mountain. Yeah, and it costs huge amounts to collect, not to mention clogging landfills and producing vast amounts of CO2 emissions. There's not much we can do about it though, is there? Well, actually, restaurants are some of the worst offenders. That's why we adopted responsible practices in our kitchen a while back."},{"s":220.7,"e":243.39,"t":"We've only got one garbage bin now despite having 100 seats but two compost machines for food waste. Oh come on, we've got four or five bins and only 60 seats at our place. Look, anything is possible. Our place is unrecognisable from what it was like last year. As is my boss. Can't think what's got into him. Thinking ahead for a change."},{"s":244.22,"e":272.28,"t":"Okay, maybe I'd better talk to my head chef. Might be fighting an uphill battle though. There are other things you can do too. My chef's obsessive about portion control, keeping an eye on how much food customers leave, and altering dishes accordingly. Don't you get complaints about small servings? Granted, we don't do enormous portions, but if occasionally someone wants a little bit more, we'll give it to them. It works, honest. Hmm, don't suppose we'd go far down that road?"},{"k":"h","s":391.32,"e":391.32,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two students talking about an experiment into the way people perceive time."},{"s":391.32,"e":394.85,"t":"Do you know anything about that experiment the lecturer was referring to?"},{"s":395.38,"e":396.35,"t":"I've looked it up"},{"s":396.82,"e":417.44,"t":"It involved this Frenchman spending two months in a cave under a glacier, in 1962 I think it was. He was 100 metres below ground and because he had nothing to track the time, no clock obviously, no sun either, he got disorientated. When he came back up, he thought he'd been down there for just 34 days."},{"s":417.91,"e":422.21,"t":"very revealing for the researchers who'd anticipated it would go the other way."},{"s":422.65,"e":448.86,"t":"Various stuntmen and entertainers have done similar things to push themselves to extremes, but then of course they've always got an eye on the headlines they'll create. That's fascinating. Yes, it's all about temporal landmarks. They're really important. If you build more of them into your life, you will experience time differently. Days and years won't be one undifferentiated mush. Temporal landmarks help stop the feeling that time's whizzing by."},{"s":449.24,"e":470.01,"t":"I bet for example, you retain memories of events that happen near the beginning or end of term, their kind of landmarks, better than those that happened somewhere in between. So? So establish a few landmarks. Remember to mark special events like birthdays properly with some sort of celebration. That's advice I'm happy to follow."}]},{"n":13,"title":"A trainee teacher called Susanna talking to her tutor","dur":510.798313,"x":[{"ps":46.01,"en":103.93,"c":"You hear a trainee teacher called Susanna talking to her tutor."},{"ps":201.24,"en":264.51,"c":"You hear a student called Sam telling his friend Ella about a concert he's been to."},{"ps":367.29,"en":434.46,"c":"You hear a woman telling her friend about new policies adopted by her company."}],"items":[{"q":"What point does the tutor make about a teacher's attitude?","qu":"Murabbiy (o'qituvchi) o'qituvchining munosabati haqida qanday fikr bildiradi?","o":["A good teacher can put any subject across effectively.","Students will pick up on a teacher's commitment.","There's little point in a teacher trying to fake passion for a subject."],"ou":["Yaxshi o'qituvchi har qanday fanni samarali tushuntira oladi.","Talabalar o'qituvchining fidoyiligini sezadi.","O'qituvchining fanga soxta ishtiyoq ko'rsatishidan foyda yo'q."],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":59.45,"en":83.26,"si":3,"ev":"You can't expect your students to love a subject unless they can see you love it yourself… in the end, your attitude will rub off on them.","uz":"O'zingiz fanni sevayotganingizni ko'rmasalar, talabalardan uni sevishni kuta olmaysiz… oxir-oqibat munosabatingiz ularga ham yuqadi.","why":"Talabalar o'qituvchining fidoyiligini sezadi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What is Susanna doing?","qu":"Susanna nima qilyapti?","o":["complaining about her students' lack of enthusiasm","proposing ways of making her subject more appealing","asking for ideas about exercises her students could do"],"ou":["talabalarining ishtiyoqsizligidan shikoyat qilyapti","fanini qiziqarliroq qilish yo'llarini taklif qilyapti","talabalari bajarishi mumkin bo'lgan mashqlar haqida g'oya so'rayapti"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":84.18,"en":103.93,"si":5,"ev":"I was reading about some techniques I could try in the classroom to keep their interest levels up… trying things out in a practical sense rather than sticking to boring theory.","uz":"Darsda ularning qiziqishini saqlash uchun sinab ko'rsam bo'ladigan usullar haqida o'qidim… zerikarli nazariya o'rniga amaliy narsalarni sinab ko'rish.","why":"Fanni qiziqarliroq qilish yo'llarini taklif qilyapti (B). Ishtiyoq yo'qligidan shikoyat (A) emas.","hl":null},{"q":"Sam is trying to","qu":"Sam ... ga harakat qilyapti","o":["suggest how the visual impact could have been improved.","challenge Ella's preconceptions about the music.","persuade Ella to go to a similar one in the future."],"ou":["vizual ta'sirni qanday yaxshilash mumkin bo'lganini aytish","Ellaning musiqa haqidagi oldindan shakllangan fikrlariga qarshi chiqish","Ellani kelajakda shunga o'xshash tadbirga borishga ko'ndirish"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":201.24,"en":247.84,"si":8,"ev":"I don't really think it's possible to get caught up in the atmosphere when all you see is someone pressing buttons… — But does that matter? If the music's brilliant? And it certainly was.","uz":"Faqat kimdir tugma bosayotganini ko'rsangiz, muhitga berilib ketish mumkin emas deb o'ylayman… — Lekin musiqa ajoyib bo'lsa, buning ahamiyati bormi? U haqiqatan ajoyib edi.","why":"Sam Ellaning elektron musiqa haqidagi oldindan shakllangan fikriga qarshi chiqadi (B). Vizual tomonni u o'zi ham kam deb tan oladi, lekin uni yaxshilashni taklif qilmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"In Sam's opinion, what makes the performer stand out?","qu":"Samning fikricha, ijrochini boshqalardan nima ajratib turadi?","o":["the influence her academic background has on her music","the instinctive way she responds to her audience","the high level of stage presence she displays"],"ou":["akademik bilimining musiqasiga ta'siri","tomoshabinlarga tabiiy, beixtiyor munosabati","sahnada o'zini juda ishonchli tutishi"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":228.28,"en":264.51,"si":11,"ev":"She's a student. Studying comparative literature… That seems to give a bit of substance to her music. Make it thoughtful and rigorous.","uz":"U talaba, qiyosiy adabiyotshunoslikni o'qiydi… Bu uning musiqasiga mazmun beradi — uni o'ylangan va puxta qiladi.","why":"Akademik bilimi musiqasiga ta'sir qiladi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"Staff have been planting trees in order to","qu":"Xodimlar daraxt ekishmoqda, maqsad ...","o":["promote a desirable image.","encourage a spirit of mutual co-operation.","compensate for environmental damage."],"ou":["yaxshi obro' (imij) yaratish","o'zaro hamkorlik ruhini rag'batlantirish","atrof-muhitga yetkazilgan zararni qoplash"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":372.25,"en":399.36,"si":15,"ev":"We're really keen on the idea that the company should be seen to identify with a certain set of values. And I think we were doing just that out there in the woods.","uz":"Kompaniya muayyan qadriyatlarga sodiq ekani ko'rinib turishini juda xohlaymiz. O'rmonda aynan shuni qildik deb o'ylayman.","why":"Yaxshi obro' (imij) yaratish (A). Ichki nizolar unutilgani (B) — qo'shimcha, \"which may not last\".","hl":null},{"q":"The company was surprised that its remote working initiative resulted in","qu":"Kompaniya masofaviy ish tashabbusi ... ga olib kelganidan hayron qoldi","o":["more appreciative customers.","a better standard of new recruits.","a more motivated workforce."],"ou":["mijozlarning ko'proq minnatdor bo'lishi","yangi xodimlar sifatining oshishi","xodimlarning ko'proq ruhlanishi"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":415.32,"en":427.33,"si":18,"ev":"The last bunch of job applicants were a very noticeably higher caliber than previously… though it wasn't part of our original thinking.","uz":"Oxirgi nomzodlar avvalgilaridan sezilarli darajada malakaliroq edi… garchi bu dastlabki rejamizda bo'lmasa ham.","why":"Kutilmagan natija — yangi xodimlar sifati oshdi (B). Mijozlar (A) doim shunday edi.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":46.01,"e":46.01,"t":"Extract One — You hear a trainee teacher called Susanna talking to her tutor."},{"s":46.01,"e":50.75,"t":"How are you finding the teaching course, Uzana? You seem to have been making good progress so far."},{"s":51.29,"e":58.97,"t":"Yeah, I'm feeling more confident in front of my students, but I worry about whether they're inspired by the activities I do with them sometimes."},{"s":59.45,"e":75.61,"t":"I guess this is a wake-up call for me, that it's just too much to expect them to be as excited about maths as I am. I think, when a teacher's motivated, that can't fail to make an impression. You can't expect your students to love a subject unless they can see you love it yourself."},{"s":76.12,"e":83.26,"t":"Sure, your students will think you're crazy if you talk about math as if it were a spectator sport, but in the end, your attitude will rub off on them."},{"s":84.18,"e":89.05,"t":"I was reading about some techniques I could try in the classroom to keep their interest levels up."},{"s":89.82,"e":103.93,"t":"been trying to get some more hands-on stuff into my classes. You know, trying things out in a practical sense rather than sticking to boring theory. Sounds like an excellent idea. Students always appreciate a teacher who goes the extra mile for them."},{"k":"h","s":201.24,"e":201.24,"t":"Extract Two — You hear a student called Sam telling his friend Ella about a concert he's been to."},{"s":201.24,"e":216.57,"t":"So you decided against the concert then? I thought about it, but I don't really think it's possible to get caught up in the atmosphere when all you see is someone pressing buttons on a computer and tinkling the keys on a synthesizer. That's all this electronic music amounts to."},{"s":217.05,"e":221.47,"t":"Admittedly the performer was dressed all in black and she looked like a scene shifter."},{"s":222.26,"e":227.81,"t":"And the visuals were limited. There was a screen, but just with some sober animations on it."},{"s":228.28,"e":247.84,"t":"trees, castles, rippling water, that sort of thing. Yeah, that says it all. But does that matter? If the music's brilliant? And it certainly was, but that's just my opinion. Tell me something about her then. Well, she's a student. Studying comparative literature, I think. That seems to give a bit of substance to her music."},{"s":248.34,"e":264.51,"t":"Make it thoughtful and rigorous. Sounds overly serious. Well, it all paid off. When the audience got more lively towards the end, she kept it steady and didn't change pace to build excitement. And she didn't seem to need the pyrotechnics and lasers that so many techies rely on."},{"k":"h","s":367.29,"e":367.29,"t":"Extract Three — You hear a woman telling her friend about new policies adopted by her company."},{"s":367.29,"e":371.61,"t":"I heard that people from your office were planting trees last week. What's going on?"},{"s":372.25,"e":399.36,"t":"Sustainability is the new watchword these days. Last year we concentrated on cutting down on our use of paper and providing raw material for more. Also seemed a good thing to do. And easier too. Your office is next door to a big forest, isn't it? Yes, very convenient. We're really keen on the idea that the company should be seen to identify with a certain set of values. And I think we were doing just that out there in the woods. So much internal conflict seemed forgotten too."},{"s":399.61,"e":402.46,"t":"Which may not last, of course. What else have you done?"},{"s":403.06,"e":414.72,"t":"It's not just the trees, of course. We've cut down our carbon footprint and reduced staff travel by encouraging remote working and flexible home working. So people have been understandably pleased about that."},{"s":415.32,"e":427.33,"t":"And Word seems to have got round because the last bunch of job applicants were a very noticeably higher caliber than previously, and I'm pretty sure that wasn't just a coincidence, though it wasn't part of our original thinking."},{"s":427.99,"e":434.46,"t":"There are certainly plenty of happy clients, but they've always been keen on the idea of supporting community projects through our efforts."}]},{"n":14,"title":"A sportsman and a businesswoman discussing the issue of being competitive","dur":567.353438,"x":[{"ps":48.18,"en":117.76,"c":"You hear a sportsman and a businesswoman discussing the issue of being competitive."},{"ps":228.82,"en":304.38,"c":"You hear two friends discussing some research into the impact of colour on memory."},{"ps":421.72,"en":488.99,"c":"You hear two people discussing a television programme about music and the effect it has on the brain."}],"items":[{"q":"How does the man feel about the book he's read on competitiveness?","qu":"Erkak raqobatbardoshlik haqida o'qigan kitobi haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["surprised that it contradicts a well-established theory","confused by the wide range of evidence it quotes","unsure about certain aspects of its argument"],"ou":["u mustahkam o'rnashgan nazariyaga zid kelganidan hayron","keltirilgan dalillarning ko'pligidan chalkashgan","uning dalillarining ayrim jihatlariga ishonchi yo'q"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":48.18,"en":78.4,"si":1,"ev":"We've all got used to the belief that competition is a necessary force for good… it was a bit of a shock to read that competition impoverishes people rather than enriching them.","uz":"Hammamiz raqobat zamonaviy dunyoda zarur ezgu kuch degan fikrga ko'nikib qolganmiz… raqobat odamlarni boyitish o'rniga qashshoqlashtiradi, deb o'qish biroz zarba bo'ldi.","why":"Kitob chuqur o'rnashgan nazariyaga zid kelgani uni hayron qoldirdi (A). Dalillar ko'pligi (B) — uni chalkashtirmagan, aksincha \"convincing\".","hl":null},{"q":"The woman feels that in the business world, prioritising competitiveness leads to","qu":"Ayolning fikricha, biznesda raqobatni birinchi o'ringa qo'yish ... ga olib keladi","o":["a demotivating effect on the workforce.","a constant drive towards greater productivity.","an obsession with short-term goals."],"ou":["xodimlarning ruhini tushiradigan ta'sirga","doimiy ravishda ko'proq samaradorlikka intilishga","qisqa muddatli maqsadlarga mukkasidan ketishga"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":79.03,"en":117.76,"si":3,"ev":"The effect is rather to encourage people to focus exclusively on immediate success, not on sustained growth.","uz":"Natijada odamlar barqaror o'sishga emas, faqat darhol erishiladigan muvaffaqiyatga e'tibor beradi.","why":"Qisqa muddatli maqsadlarga berilib ketish (C). Samaradorlik oshishi (B) — \"far from achieving the desired outcome\".","hl":null},{"q":"They both say that","qu":"Ikkalasi ham ... deydi","o":["restaurants use clever tactics to attract new customers.","the research methods used seem valid.","the same colours can affect people in different ways."],"ou":["restoranlar yangi mijozlarni jalb qilish uchun aqlli usullardan foydalanadi","qo'llanilgan tadqiqot usullari asosli ko'rinadi","bir xil ranglar odamlarga turlicha ta'sir qilishi mumkin"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":255.29,"en":304.38,"si":7,"ev":"But it does seem sound… She's followed a thorough process then.","uz":"Lekin bu asosli ko'rinadi… Demak, u puxta jarayonga amal qilgan.","why":"Ikkalasi ham tadqiqot usuli asosli ekaniga qo'shiladi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman feels that the teenager's findings","qu":"Ayolning fikricha, o'smirning topilmalari","o":["could prove significant in the long-term.","need the backing of the scientific establishment.","confirm initial evidence about the way memory is viewed."],"ou":["uzoq muddatda muhim bo'lib chiqishi mumkin","ilmiy doiralarning qo'llab-quvvatlashiga muhtoj","xotira haqidagi dastlabki dalillarni tasdiqlaydi"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":281.78,"en":304.38,"si":8,"ev":"Is there any existing published data that backs up these claims? — Not as such, I grant you, though it sounds like she's onto something to me, but only time will tell.","uz":"Bu da'volarni tasdiqlaydigan chop etilgan ma'lumot bormi? — Rostini aytsam, yo'q, lekin menimcha u nimanidir topgan, faqat vaqt ko'rsatadi.","why":"Topilmalar uzoq muddatda muhim bo'lib chiqishi mumkin (A). Olimlar qo'llab-quvvatlashi (B) haqida gapirilmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"How does the woman feel about the programme?","qu":"Ayol dastur haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["surprised by its conclusion","confused by the approach it took","disappointed by the lack of explanation"],"ou":["uning xulosasidan hayron","tanlagan yondashuvidan chalkashgan","tushuntirish yo'qligidan hafsalasi pir bo'lgan"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":458.26,"en":463.14,"si":14,"ev":"They missed a trick in not clarifying why some people are avid listeners to music and others not.","uz":"Nima uchun ba'zilar musiqani ishtiyoq bilan tinglashi, boshqalar esa yo'qligini tushuntirmay, imkoniyatni boy berishdi.","why":"Tushuntirish yo'qligidan hafsalasi pir bo'lgan (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What do they agree about music?","qu":"Ular musiqa haqida nimada bir fikrga keladi?","o":["It has unexpected benefits.","Its effects on intelligence are obvious.","It's important to study its psychological impact."],"ou":["Uning kutilmagan foydalari bor.","Uning aqlga ta'siri aniq.","Uning psixologik ta'sirini o'rganish muhim."],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":468.15,"en":475.39,"si":16,"ev":"People who've had music training in childhood find long-term positive effects on their verbal memory. Who'd have thought it?","uz":"Bolalikda musiqa ta'limi olganlar og'zaki xotirasida uzoq muddatli ijobiy ta'sirni sezadi. Kim o'ylabdi deysiz?","why":"Musiqaning kutilmagan foydalari bor (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":48.18,"e":48.18,"t":"Extract One — You hear a sportsman and a businesswoman discussing the issue of being competitive."},{"s":48.18,"e":71.07,"t":"You've read this new book on competitiveness. Is it all about striving for success or a defense of the Olympic ideal? You know, taking part is more important than winning? Well, yes. That's a view often ridiculed, certainly, as some sort of excuse for underachievement. I mean, if you run a race, surely it's because you want to win. And we've all got used to the belief that competition is a necessary force for good in the modern world."},{"s":72.12,"e":78.4,"t":"ingrained idea, it was a bit of a shock to read that competition impoverishes people rather than enriching them."},{"s":79.03,"e":108.89,"t":"There's the mind-boggling range of convincing examples you'd expect in support of this theory. And the whole thing is so engagingly written that the most hostile opponents would have trouble refuting it. Well, my experience of competition in the business world is nothing but negative. I'd say that if you put competition at the heart of your strategy, far from achieving the desired outcome of boosting efficiency by pitting staff against each other, the effect is rather to encourage people to focus exclusively on immediate success"},{"s":109.14,"e":117.76,"t":"not on sustained growth. Let's face it, the best businesses are the ones that look ahead instead of limiting their perspective in this way."},{"k":"h","s":228.82,"e":228.82,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two friends discussing some research into the impact of colour on memory."},{"s":228.82,"e":255.1,"t":"You know how colours affect us? Like red and yellow are often used in fast food restaurants? In the decor, I mean? Yeah, yeah. They say they excite the brain, which tells you you're hungry. That was in the papers years back. Well, OK. But now there's a suggestion colours may help us memorise better. Oh, come on. Influence appetites and emotions? Maybe, but... No, really. This teenager did some research. Teenager? Yeah, I know."},{"s":255.29,"e":281.47,"t":"But it does seem sound. She took a page of words and printed them in so-called warm colors. How do you mean? Well, reds, oranges, yellows, etc. and gave people two minutes to memorize the words. She followed that with pretty complicated maths equations to stop them reciting the words in their head. Okay, sounds good so far. And they were given a minute to record how many words they could remember."},{"s":281.78,"e":304.38,"t":"And then the same procedure with words printed in cool colours like green and blue. And? Overall, warm colours were memorised better and cool colours worse. She's followed a thorough process then, but is there any existing published data that backs up or contradicts these claims? Well, not as such, I grant you, though it sounds like she's onto something to me, but only time will tell."},{"k":"h","s":421.72,"e":421.72,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people discussing a television programme about music and the effect it has on the brain."},{"s":421.72,"e":438.62,"t":"I watched How Musical Are You on TV last night. They were saying how listening to music is a really complicated process. The scientists were really going to town on it. I thought so-called musicality meant being able to play a musical instrument, but that seemed to be just one aspect of the whole program."},{"s":439.26,"e":445.57,"t":"It's odd. People who've never set foot inside a music classroom might still have a musical ear without realizing it."},{"s":446.01,"e":452.38,"t":"You mean, everyone has an innate ability to make sense of music? I'm not sure, but it brings an enormous amount of pleasure."},{"s":452.89,"e":457.66,"t":"I really don't know how, but it changes my mood when I'm down, which never ceases to amaze me."},{"s":458.26,"e":463.14,"t":"they missed a trick in not clarifying why some people are avid listeners to music and others not."},{"s":463.54,"e":467.81,"t":"They seem more interested in the possible effect of music on musicians' brains."},{"s":468.15,"e":475.39,"t":"I didn't know that people who've had music training in childhood find long-term positive effects on their verbal memory. Who'd have thought it?"},{"s":475.86,"e":477.95,"t":"I don't remember words whatever I do."},{"s":478.46,"e":488.99,"t":"You know that online quiz they mentioned? That might be worth a go. It's about how engaged you are with music, you know, whether it's part of your identity or not. So you might be more musical than you think."}]},{"n":15,"title":"Two people talking about public speaking","dur":563.121625,"x":[{"ps":46.84,"en":118.26,"c":"You hear two people talking about public speaking."},{"ps":233.72,"en":301.73,"c":"You hear part of a radio program the London Underground."},{"ps":412.54,"en":480.48,"c":"You hear two people discussing the news media."}],"items":[{"q":"Both speakers refer to a feeling of","qu":"Ikkala so'zlovchi ... hissini tilga oladi","o":["over-confidence.","embarrassment.","achievement."],"ou":["haddan tashqari o'ziga ishonch","xijolat","yutuq (muvaffaqiyat)"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":61.5,"en":76.48,"si":5,"ev":"I seem to have forgotten how to speak and I felt my face go red.","uz":"Gapirishni unutib qo'ygandek bo'ldim va yuzim qizarib ketganini his qildim.","why":"Ikkalasi xijolat hissini tilga oladi (B): biri yuzi qizarganini, ikkinchisi \"humiliate yourself\" deydi.","hl":null},{"q":"The two speakers agree that a big problem with speaking in public is","qu":"Ikkala so'zlovchi omma oldida gapirishdagi katta muammo ... degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["losing the audience's attention during a speech.","choosing the wrong content for a speech.","feeling nervous at the thought of giving a speech."],"ou":["nutq paytida tinglovchilar e'tiborini yo'qotish","nutq uchun noto'g'ri mazmun tanlash","nutq so'zlash haqida o'ylashning o'zidan hayajonlanish"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":46.84,"en":55.36,"si":1,"ev":"I dread the experience. It's the anticipation that gets me. Once I start, I'm usually okay, but beforehand I panic.","uz":"Bundan dahshatga tushaman. Meni kutish qiynaydi. Boshlaganimdan keyin odatda yaxshi, lekin oldin vahimaga tushaman.","why":"Muammo — nutq haqida o'ylashning o'zidan hayajonlanish (C). Ikkinchisi: \"pre-presentational anxiety is normal\".","hl":null},{"q":"The poster campaign came at a time when","qu":"Plakat kampaniyasi ... bir paytda boshlandi","o":["various aspects of life in London were changing.","many people were reluctant to travel on the Underground.","the use of posters for advertising was increasing."],"ou":["Londondagi hayotning turli jihatlari o'zgarayotgan","ko'pchilik metroda yurishni istamayotgan","reklamada plakatlardan foydalanish ko'payayotgan"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":258.78,"en":265.76,"si":20,"ev":"They helped to shape people's perceptions and expectations of London… in a period of great change.","uz":"Ular odamlarning London haqidagi tasavvur va kutishlarini shakllantirishga yordam berdi… katta o'zgarishlar davrida.","why":"Londondagi hayot o'zgarayotgan payt (A).","hl":null},{"q":"What does Zoe say about the content of the posters?","qu":"Zoe plakatlarning mazmuni haqida nima deydi?","o":["It only appealed to a certain type of person.","It contrasted with real life for many people.","It influenced the lifestyles of some people."],"ou":["U faqat ma'lum toifadagi odamlarga yoqardi.","U ko'pchilikning haqiqiy hayotidan keskin farq qilardi.","U ba'zi odamlarning turmush tarziga ta'sir qildi."],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":277.72,"en":301.73,"si":22,"ev":"The posters depicted a domestic ideal… the wife would stay at home, even though this was not the case for many families.","uz":"Plakatlar uy hayotining ideal manzarasini ko'rsatardi… xotin uyda qoladi — garchi ko'p oilalarda bunday bo'lmasa ham.","why":"Plakat mazmuni ko'pchilikning haqiqiy hayotidan farq qilardi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What opinion does the man express about the news media?","qu":"Erkak yangiliklar OAV haqida qanday fikr bildiradi?","o":["It doesn't deserve its reputation.","It has become more influential.","Its standards have risen."],"ou":["U o'z obro'siga loyiq emas (yomon nomga loyiq emas).","U ta'sirliroq bo'lib qolgan.","Uning saviyasi oshgan."],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":412.54,"en":436.73,"si":26,"ev":"The cliche is don't believe everything you read in the papers… In many ways that's not backed up by the evidence.","uz":"Mashhur gap: gazetada o'qiganingizning hammasiga ishonmang… Ko'p jihatdan bu dalillar bilan tasdiqlanmaydi.","why":"OAV yomon nomiga loyiq emas (A).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman mentions medical stories","qu":"Ayol tibbiy xabarlarni ... tilga oladi","o":["to explain her attitude to the news media.","to illustrate the importance of the news media.","to describe why people dislike the news media."],"ou":["yangiliklar OAVga munosabatini tushuntirish uchun","yangiliklar OAV muhimligini ko'rsatish uchun","odamlar nega yangiliklar OAVni yoqtirmasligini tasvirlash uchun"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":419.35,"en":447.04,"si":28,"ev":"Personally, I'm always pretty sceptical when it comes to all these revelations. I mean, look at medical stories.","uz":"Shaxsan men bu \"fosh qilishlar\"ga doim shubha bilan qarayman. Masalan, tibbiy xabarlarni oling.","why":"Tibbiy xabarlar — uning OAVga shubhali munosabatini tushuntirish uchun misol (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":46.84,"e":46.84,"t":"Extract One — You hear two people talking about public speaking."},{"s":46.84,"e":50.75,"t":"I dread the experience. It's the anticipation that gets me."},{"s":51.26,"e":55.36,"t":"Once I start, I'm usually okay, but beforehand I panic."},{"s":56.18,"e":59.26,"t":"I think that my mind will go blank and everyone will stare at me."},{"s":59.74,"e":60.96,"t":"This happened once."},{"s":61.5,"e":67.36,"t":"I was trying to speak and listen to my own voice at the same time, but all I could hear was silence."},{"s":67.96,"e":76.48,"t":"I seem to have forgotten how to speak and I felt my face go red. I fumbled for my notes and simply read out the rest of the speech."},{"s":77.14,"e":83.1,"t":"Well, fear of public speaking or what is called pre-presentational anxiety is normal."},{"s":83.99,"e":87.42,"t":"If you think about it, public speaking is not a natural thing to do."},{"s":88.25,"e":90.88,"t":"You don't want to humiliate yourself in front of people."},{"s":92.54,"e":98.27,"t":"and practice, even the most stressed public speakers can conquer their fears."},{"s":99.1,"e":105.31,"t":"There are very few people who are quick, intelligent and extrovert enough to just get up and deliver something spontaneously."},{"s":106.04,"e":107.1,"t":"If you're giving a speech"},{"s":107.6,"e":109.85,"t":"must carefully plan what you're going to say."},{"s":110.28,"e":113.31,"t":"I find it also helps not to think of yourself the whole time."},{"s":113.71,"e":118.26,"t":"Once you shift the focus onto the people you are speaking to, you feel the pressure lift."},{"k":"h","s":233.72,"e":233.72,"t":"Extract Two — You hear part of a radio program the London Underground."},{"s":233.72,"e":245.92,"t":"As part of a huge publicity drive in the 1920s and 1930s, London Transport launched a poster campaign to persuade people to move into the suburbs and make use of the rapidly expanding underground network."},{"s":246.62,"e":247.61,"t":"Tell us about that, Zoe"},{"s":248.54,"e":257.79,"t":"Well, the posters were used to encourage people to live in and enjoy the quiet and domestic life of the suburbs and travel into London for work and leisure."},{"s":258.78,"e":265.76,"t":"They helped to shape people's perceptions and expectations of London and what it meant to live there in a period of great change."},{"s":266.78,"e":277.21,"t":"As well as persuading people to move out to the suburbs, there was a drive for people to make use of the city at a time when the leisure industry was expanding. What kind of things did these posters show?"},{"s":277.72,"e":290.85,"t":"Well, despite the fact that many women worked in the 1920s and 1930s, the Post has depicted a domestic ideal, with pictures of women playing with their children in the park and preparing meals for their husbands return."},{"s":291.67,"e":298.94,"t":"More and more people were becoming middle class and part of this ideal was that the husband would go to work and the wife would stay at home."},{"s":299.38,"e":301.73,"t":"even though this was not the case for many families."},{"k":"h","s":412.54,"e":412.54,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people discussing the news media."},{"s":412.54,"e":416.19,"t":"Of course the cliche is don't believe everything you read in the papers."},{"s":416.7,"e":418.17,"t":"And I guess there's some truth in"},{"s":419.35,"e":436.73,"t":"In many ways that's not backed up by the evidence. Look at all the times when stories would never have come out if it hadn't been for the much maligned news media. I don't know about that. Personally, I'm always pretty sceptical when it comes to all these revelations. I mean, look at medical stories."},{"s":437.27,"e":447.04,"t":"It sometimes seems as if every day brings some new health scare. You mustn't eat that, you should drink that and most of these things you never hear about again."},{"s":447.86,"e":453.73,"t":"I think it'd be really interesting to find out how many of these stories actually turn out to be true."},{"s":454.3,"e":462.05,"t":"I reckon they just write these things to create a stir. I mean, lots of them are in the entertainment industry really, aren't they?"},{"s":463.8,"e":480.48,"t":"Getting the way of a good story is the joke in the trade, isn't it? I think lots of them live by that. I don't think that's really fair. There are lots of investigative journalists who've done the public a great service by exposing things they otherwise would never have known about."}]},{"n":16,"title":"Two people talking about a play that they saw at the theatre","dur":444.290563,"x":[{"ps":15.0,"en":48.86,"c":"You will hear two people talking about a play that they saw at the theatre."},{"ps":110.33,"en":202.49,"c":"You will hear part of a radio interview with a trade and commerce researcher."},{"ps":323.58,"en":377.12,"c":"You'll hear a part of a report about holiday homes in the Mediterranean."}],"items":[{"q":"What do we learn about the writer of the play?","qu":"Pyesa muallifi haqida nimani bilib olamiz?","o":["He died.","He is dying.","He nearly died."],"ou":["U vafot etgan.","U o'lim to'shagida.","U o'limdan qolgan."],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":24.57,"en":38.59,"si":2,"ev":"He'd been seriously ill, hadn't he? Apparently it was touch and go for a while.","uz":"U jiddiy kasal bo'lgan edi-ku? Aytishlaricha, bir muddat hayoti qil ustida turgan.","why":"\"Touch and go\" = o'lim yoqasida edi, lekin tirik qoldi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What do the speakers agree on?","qu":"So'zlovchilar nimada kelishadi?","o":["The writer is quite predictable.","The writer's style has changed direction.","The play wasn't as funny as some of the writer's earlier plays."],"ou":["Muallifni oldindan bilib bo'ladi (kutilgan narsalarni yozadi).","Muallif uslubi yo'nalishini o'zgartirgan.","Pyesa muallifning avvalgi ba'zi pyesalaricha kulgili emas edi."],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":15.0,"en":48.86,"si":1,"ev":"That one was completely different to the others… He really seems to be a different character to when he first started to write.","uz":"Bu pyesa boshqalaridan butunlay farq qiladi… U yozishni boshlagan paytidagidan butunlay boshqacha odamga o'xshaydi.","why":"Ikkalasi ham muallif uslubi o'zgarganini aytadi (B). A — aksincha: \"certainly original\".","hl":null},{"q":"According to Pablo Jenson","qu":"Pablo Jensonning fikricha","o":["a variety of different shops tends to boost sales.","traders that have something in common can boost each other's sales.","butchers are the most successful traders."],"ou":["turli xil do'konlarning bo'lishi savdoni oshiradi","umumiy jihati bor savdogarlar bir-birining savdosini oshira oladi","qassoblar eng muvaffaqiyatli savdogarlar"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":136.76,"en":151.26,"si":9,"ev":"We found that the shops formed clusters, with shops such as butchers and delicatessens in one group… Stores of the same group seem to attract each other.","uz":"Do'konlar to'dalar hosil qilishini aniqladik: qassob va delikates do'konlari bir guruhda… Bir guruhdagi do'konlar bir-birini tortadi.","why":"Umumiy jihati bor savdogarlar bir-birining savdosini oshiradi (B). Turli do'konlar (A) aksincha bir-birini \"itaradi\".","hl":null},{"q":"Jenson's theory","qu":"Jensonning nazariyasi","o":["advertised for similar retailers to open shops in one particular area.","works better for bakers and butchers than for other kinds of retailers.","seems to have been proved to be credible."],"ou":["o'xshash savdogarlarni bitta hududda do'kon ochishga chaqiradi","novvoylar va qassoblar uchun boshqa savdogarlarga qaraganda yaxshiroq ishlaydi","ishonchli ekani isbotlanganga o'xshaydi"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":186.84,"en":202.49,"si":20,"ev":"19 bakeries shut down and their average Q was lower than the average… the Lyon Chamber of Commerce is using the model to help entrepreneurs.","uz":"19 ta nonvoyxona yopildi va ularning o'rtacha Q ko'rsatkichi umumiy o'rtachadan past edi… Lion savdo palatasi bu modeldan tadbirkorlarga yordam berishda foydalanmoqda.","why":"Nazariya ishonchli ekani tasdiqlanganga o'xshaydi (C). Novvoylar faqat sinov uchun olingan (B emas).","hl":null},{"q":"The Costa de la Cruz","qu":"Costa de la Cruz","o":["is being spoiled by developers.","is the cheapest area of Spain in which you can buy a holiday home.","is close to Portugal."],"ou":["quruvchilar tomonidan buzilmoqda","Ispaniyada dam olish uyi sotib olish mumkin bo'lgan eng arzon hudud","Portugaliyaga yaqin"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":330.49,"en":340.89,"si":24,"ev":"…which has earned the nickname the Spanish Algarve, thanks to its charm and proximity to the Portuguese border.","uz":"…jozibasi va Portugaliya chegarasiga yaqinligi tufayli \"Ispaniya Algarvesi\" laqabini olgan.","why":"Portugaliyaga yaqin (C). Eng arzon (B) deyilmagan — faqat Portugaliyadagi uylardan arzon.","hl":null},{"q":"According to Chris Mercer","qu":"Chris Mercerning fikricha","o":["there is a danger that the Costa de la Cruz will lose its appeal.","the Costa de la Cruz can be developed without the area being damaged.","the government has put a stop to the Costa de la Cruz being developed further."],"ou":["Costa de la Cruz o'z jozibasini yo'qotish xavfi bor","Costa de la Cruzni hududga zarar yetkazmasdan rivojlantirish mumkin","hukumat Costa de la Cruzni yanada qurishni to'xtatgan"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":362.84,"en":377.12,"si":28,"ev":"More land will have to be made available for development soon… The government is being careful to preserve the natural beauty and character though.","uz":"Tez orada qurilish uchun ko'proq yer ajratishga to'g'ri keladi… Lekin hukumat tabiiy go'zallik va o'ziga xoslikni ehtiyotkorlik bilan saqlamoqda.","why":"Hududga zarar yetkazmasdan rivojlantirish mumkin (B).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":15.0,"e":15.0,"t":"Extract One — You will hear two people talking about a play that they saw at the theatre."},{"s":15.0,"e":24.13,"t":"Well, that was certainly original. I've seen quite a few of his plays and that one was completely different to the others. Yes, it was quite dark, wasn't it?"},{"s":24.57,"e":38.59,"t":"Maybe it's because he'd become aware of his own mortality when he wrote it. That's right! He'd been seriously ill, hadn't he? Apparently it was touch and go for a while. Mind you, the main character was hilarious in a sick kind of way."},{"s":39.1,"e":48.86,"t":"I think that kind of humour would go right over most people's head. Well, I don't know how he'll follow up that story. He really seems to be a different character to when he first started to write."},{"k":"h","s":110.33,"e":110.33,"t":"Extract Two — You will hear part of a radio interview with a trade and commerce researcher."},{"s":110.33,"e":119.77,"t":"The old mantra about the three most important factors for a shop's success, location, location, location, has been borne out by a new mathematical model."},{"s":120.34,"e":123.49,"t":"It could help retailers pinpoint lucrative sites for their stores."},{"s":124.22,"e":126.72,"t":"Physicist Pablo Jensen is here with us today."},{"s":127.22,"e":136.0,"t":"Good morning Pablo. Good morning. We have analysed location records for more than 8,500 retail outlets in Lyon, France."},{"s":136.76,"e":139.36,"t":"we found that the shops formed clusters."},{"s":139.86,"e":147.81,"t":"with shops such as butchers and delicatessens in one group, for example, and in laundromats and bookstores in another."},{"s":148.76,"e":151.26,"t":"The doors of the same group seem to attract each other."},{"s":151.7,"e":154.72,"t":"while stores from different groups repelled each other."},{"s":155.45,"e":157.44,"t":"You've created a theory, haven't you?"},{"s":157.91,"e":158.53,"t":"Yes, that"},{"s":159.29,"e":164.86,"t":"It's a theory of magnetism to calculate a number Q for shops"},{"s":165.3,"e":170.24,"t":"based on the proximity of attractive and repellent businesses in the area."},{"s":171.45,"e":175.55,"t":"Q represents the suitability of a site for a particular type of shot."},{"s":176.5,"e":179.07,"t":"The higher the number, the better the site."},{"s":179.67,"e":186.01,"t":"We tested this theory with all of the bakeries in Lyon between 2003 and 2005."},{"s":186.84,"e":194.62,"t":"During that period, 19 bakeries shut down and their average Q was lower than the average for all bakeries."},{"s":195.13,"e":202.49,"t":"Actually, the Leon Chamber of Commerce is using the model to help entrepreneurs identify promising new premises."},{"k":"h","s":323.58,"e":323.58,"t":"Extract Three — You'll hear a part of a report about holiday homes in the Mediterranean."},{"s":323.58,"e":329.73,"t":"For a beautiful alternative to the bigger Spanish coasts, try the Costa de la Cruz, the coast of light."},{"s":330.49,"e":340.89,"t":"The government of Andalusia is taking care to protect this little-known region, which has earned the nickname the Spanish Algarve, thanks to its charm and proximity to the Portuguese border."},{"s":341.75,"e":351.2,"t":"A property in the area represents a sound investment because homes are cheaper than their Portuguese equivalents, and land laws mean that it will never become so built up that it's spoiled."},{"s":351.9,"e":355.52,"t":"National parks, farmland and beautiful beaches all abound."},{"s":356.02,"e":361.95,"t":"And Chris Mercer of Spanish property dot co dot UK says that more homes will be built soon."},{"s":362.84,"e":370.14,"t":"More land will have to be made available for development soon because demand is quite simply starting to outstrip supply, he says."},{"s":370.97,"e":377.12,"t":"The government is being careful to preserve the natural beauty and character though, so your investment should stay strong."}]},{"n":17,"title":"Two people talking about a problem at work","dur":339.853063,"x":[{"ps":15.7,"en":57.09,"c":"You will hear two people talking about a problem at work."},{"ps":130.1,"en":174.3,"c":"You will hear two people talking about how the woman got her job."},{"ps":249.72,"en":287.2,"c":"You will hear two people talking about the man's job as a prison officer."}],"items":[{"q":"What is the man's problem?","qu":"Erkakning muammosi nima?","o":["Nobody will listen to his complaints at work.","There is friction between him and a colleague.","He's fallen out with his boss."],"ou":["Ishda hech kim uning shikoyatlarini tinglamaydi.","U bilan bir hamkasbi o'rtasida kelishmovchilik bor.","Rahbari bilan urishib qolgan."],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":15.7,"en":29.82,"si":1,"ev":"One of my colleagues is always complaining about his job, or moaning about our boss… and it's created a very negative atmosphere.","uz":"Hamkasblarimdan biri doim ishidan shikoyat qiladi yoki rahbarimiz ustidan noliydi… bu juda salbiy muhit yaratdi.","why":"Muammo — hamkasb bilan kelishmovchilik (B). Rahbar bilan urishmagan (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman think?","qu":"Ayol nima deb o'ylaydi?","o":["He needs to approach the problem in a different way.","He has to accept that there will be problems in any office.","He is the main cause of all the office problems."],"ou":["U muammoga boshqacha yondashishi kerak.","U har qanday ofisda muammolar bo'lishini qabul qilishi kerak.","Ofisdagi barcha muammolarning asosiy sababi o'zi."],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":32.47,"en":57.09,"si":4,"ev":"I do suspect you've gone about trying to solve it in a way that casts you… as a bit of a self-important bore. Why don't two or three of you put your complaints to your boss in a fair and constructive way?","uz":"Menimcha, sen uni shunday usulda hal qilmoqchi bo'lgansanki, o'zingni kekkaygan zerikarli odamdek ko'rsatib qo'yding. Nega ikki-uchtangiz shikoyatlaringizni rahbarga adolatli va konstruktiv tarzda aytmaysiz?","why":"Muammoga boshqacha yondashish kerak (A). U ofis muammolarining sababchisi deyilmaydi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What were Janet's expectations of the recruitment fair?","qu":"Janet ish yarmarkasidan nimani kutgan edi?","o":["She was hoping to get some ideas for a career.","She was sure that someone would offer her a job in Public Relations.","She had incorrect preconceptions as to what she would gain from it."],"ou":["Kasb tanlash uchun biror g'oya olishga umid qilgan.","Kimdir unga jamoatchilik bilan aloqalar sohasida ish taklif qilishiga ishongan.","Undan nima olishi haqida noto'g'ri tasavvurga ega edi."],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":130.1,"en":149.89,"si":7,"ev":"It was nothing like I thought it would be… I was quite sure that I would become a translator before I went to the fair.","uz":"U men o'ylagandek umuman emas edi… Yarmarkaga borishdan oldin tarjimon bo'lishimga ishonchim komil edi.","why":"Undan nima olishi haqida noto'g'ri tasavvurga ega edi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"How did Paul gain from the recruitment fair?","qu":"Paul ish yarmarkasidan qanday foyda ko'rdi?","o":["He passed an interview there and got a job.","He impressed someone who then recommended him for a job.","He applied for several jobs there and was successful."],"ou":["U yerda suhbatdan o'tib, ishga kirdi.","Kimnidir taassurot qoldirdi, u esa uni ishga tavsiya qildi.","U yerda bir nechta ishga hujjat topshirib, muvaffaqiyatga erishdi."],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":150.52,"en":174.3,"si":8,"ev":"One of the employees I spoke to there passed on my CV to the marketing and business development manager and a week later I was invited for an interview.","uz":"U yerda gaplashgan xodimlardan biri rezyumemni marketing menejeriga uzatdi va bir haftadan so'ng meni suhbatga taklif qilishdi.","why":"Kimnidir taassurot qoldirdi va u uni tavsiya qildi (B). Suhbat yarmarkada bo'lmagan (A emas).","hl":null},{"q":"What does the man say about his job?","qu":"Erkak ishi haqida nima deydi?","o":["You need to have a degree to get a promotion.","If you want a promotion you will have to go into management.","It's a career that offers incentives for industrious people."],"ou":["Lavozim ko'tarilishi uchun diplom kerak.","Lavozim ko'tarilishini xohlasangiz, boshqaruvga o'tishingiz kerak.","Bu mehnatkash odamlarni rag'batlantiradigan kasb."],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":249.72,"en":264.61,"si":10,"ev":"It's a career where you can achieve promotion very quickly… graduates who join can expect… two promotions within the first two years.","uz":"Bu tez lavozim ko'tarilishi mumkin bo'lgan kasb… bitiruvchilar dastlabki ikki yilda ikki marta ko'tarilishi mumkin.","why":"Mehnatkash odamlarni rag'batlantiradi (C). Diplom shart emas (A): \"you can join up straight from school\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is the woman's opinion of the man?","qu":"Ayol erkak haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["He is both courageous and mad.","He must have a cruel side to him.","His desire to get a promotion is more important than anything else."],"ou":["U ham jasur, ham telba.","Unda shafqatsiz tomon bo'lsa kerak.","Uning uchun lavozim ko'tarilishi hamma narsadan muhim."],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":274.42,"en":287.2,"si":14,"ev":"You've got to be out of your mind to want to work with dangerous people like that. Plus, I wouldn't have the courage to face violent criminals.","uz":"Bunaqa xavfli odamlar bilan ishlashni xohlash uchun aqldan ozgan bo'lish kerak. Qolaversa, menda zo'ravon jinoyatchilarga qarshi turishga jasorat yetmasdi.","why":"U ham jasur, ham \"telba\" (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":15.7,"e":15.7,"t":"Extract One — You will hear two people talking about a problem at work."},{"s":15.7,"e":27.23,"t":"One of my colleagues is always complaining about his job, or moaning about our boss, or the company's management. Let's make another team member dissatisfied, because some of his complaints are true."},{"s":27.74,"e":29.82,"t":"and it's created a very negative atmosphere."},{"s":30.39,"e":31.93,"t":"I have tried to speak to him about it"},{"s":32.47,"e":48.35,"t":"But now he just thinks I'm trying to be the boss's favourite. Well, I'm not trying to question your analysis of the problem or your motives for trying to sort it out. But I do suspect you've gone about trying to solve it in a way that casts you, however unjustly, as a bit of a self-important bore."},{"s":49.27,"e":57.09,"t":"Why don't two or three of you put your complaints to your boss in a fair and constructive way? And it might be a good idea to involve your unhappy colleague in that."},{"k":"h","s":130.1,"e":130.1,"t":"Extract Two — You will hear two people talking about how the woman got her job."},{"s":130.1,"e":149.89,"t":"I'm glad you persuaded me to go to the recruitment fair. It was nothing like I thought it would be. Yes, it was really interesting. I was quite sure that I would become a translator before I went to the fair, because I was just about to finish my degree in modern languages. I wandered up to a store that was promoting careers in public relations, just to have a nose, really."},{"s":150.52,"e":174.3,"t":"blown away. It seemed perfect to suit my skills and interests. Well I'd been looking for a job in the papers and in employment agencies and I didn't find anything at the fair. But one of the employees I spoke to there passed on my CV to the marketing and business development manager and a week later I was invited for an interview. I couldn't believe my luck when they offered me the position."},{"k":"h","s":249.72,"e":249.72,"t":"Extract Three — You will hear two people talking about the man's job as a prison officer."},{"s":249.72,"e":254.49,"t":"It's not just a job for men, you know, and it's a career where you can achieve promotion very quickly."},{"s":254.97,"e":256.03,"t":"What's the salary like?"},{"s":256.5,"e":264.61,"t":"Typically, graduates who join can expect to earn £28,000 within a year and achieve two promotions within the first two years."},{"s":265.18,"e":273.95,"t":"Of course, you can join up straight from school, but it will take you longer to get to a higher position such as management. To be honest, I don't think I could ever do your job."},{"s":274.42,"e":287.2,"t":"You've got to be out of your mind to want to work with dangerous people like that. Plus, I wouldn't have the courage to face violent criminals. You never know what they're going to do next. Well, I just wanted to be sure of a career where I could do well without having to wait until I was a lot older."}]},{"n":18,"title":"Two students talking about shopping for clothes","dur":437.6555,"x":[{"ps":26.81,"en":76.93,"c":"You hear two students talking about shopping for clothes."},{"ps":163.16,"en":216.38,"c":"you hear part of an interview with a musician called Max."},{"ps":309.78,"en":369.24,"c":"you hear part of a discussion programme in which two dancers are talking about their careers."}],"items":[{"q":"What do they agree about?","qu":"Ular nima haqida bir fikrda?","o":["Affordable clothing is the better choice.","Purchasing clothes is a bad idea.","People should respect your clothing preferences."],"ou":["Arzon kiyim yaxshiroq tanlov.","Kiyim sotib olish yomon fikr.","Odamlar kiyim tanlovingizni hurmat qilishi kerak."],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":26.81,"en":54.11,"si":1,"ev":"It was the prospect of shopping for new stuff I couldn't face… my trick is to put it off to the last possible moment. So I'll have less chance to waste time on such a pointless activity.","uz":"Yangi narsalar xarid qilishga borish fikriga chiday olmasdim… Men buni oxirgi lahzagacha orqaga suraman, shunda bunday befoyda ishga kamroq vaqt sarflayman.","why":"Ikkalasi ham kiyim xarid qilishni yoqtirmaydi — yomon fikr deb biladi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"The man believes that for many people shopping is","qu":"Erkakning fikricha, ko'pchilik uchun xarid qilish","o":["achieving social status.","commenting on society.","displaying your connection to a social group."],"ou":["ijtimoiy mavqega erishish","jamiyat haqida fikr bildirish","biror ijtimoiy guruhga mansubligini ko'rsatish"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":54.39,"en":76.93,"si":2,"ev":"It's heavily linked to wanting to be the centre of attention… It's basically a way of showing off.","uz":"Bu diqqat markazida bo'lish istagi bilan chambarchas bog'liq… Asosan bu o'zini ko'rsatish usuli.","why":"Xarid — ijtimoiy mavqega erishish yo'li (A). Siyosiy masala emas (B): \"it's not like a political issue for me\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does he say about his music when he was a teen?","qu":"U o'smirlikdagi musiqasi haqida nima deydi?","o":["He didn't feel like sharing it.","He felt quite self-confident about it.","He was unwilling to ask for help with it."],"ou":["Uni boshqalar bilan bo'lishishni xohlamasdi.","Unga nisbatan o'zini ancha ishonchli his qilardi.","U bo'yicha yordam so'rashni istamasdi."],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":163.16,"en":188.25,"si":5,"ev":"I didn't think that being number one was something completely unattainable. I had a cockiness, but I kept it hidden from my peers.","uz":"Birinchi o'rinni butunlay erishib bo'lmas narsa deb o'ylamasdim. Menda o'ziga haddan tashqari ishonch bor edi, lekin uni tengdoshlarimdan yashirardim.","why":"\"Cockiness\" = o'ziga ishonch (B). U yashirgani — ishonchini, musiqani emas (A emas).","hl":null},{"q":"What does he suggest about his recording contract?","qu":"U ovoz yozish shartnomasi haqida nimaga ishora qiladi?","o":["It didn't guarantee him ongoing success.","It didn't allow him to do music full-time.","Its terms and conditions weren't too good."],"ou":["U doimiy muvaffaqiyatni kafolatlamadi.","U musiqa bilan to'liq shug'ullanishga imkon bermadi.","Uning shartlari unchalik yaxshi emas edi."],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":188.47,"en":216.38,"si":6,"ev":"If after my first hit I thought I'd made it, I was soon disabused of that notion… I've had to put in a lot of effort to capitalise on that breakthrough.","uz":"Birinchi xitimdan keyin maqsadga yetdim deb o'ylagan bo'lsam, tez orada bu fikrdan qaytdim… O'sha yutuqdan foydalanish uchun juda ko'p mehnat qilishimga to'g'ri keldi.","why":"Shartnoma doimiy muvaffaqiyatni kafolatlamadi (A). Shartlari yaxshi edi (C emas): \"a good deal in most respects\".","hl":null},{"q":"The man got his inspiration to start dancing from","qu":"Erkak raqsga tushishni boshlash ilhomini ... dan oldi","o":["one reaction to a performance he gave.","getting encouraged by his friends.","the physical effort associated with it."],"ou":["o'z chiqishiga bo'lgan bitta munosabat","do'stlarining rag'batlantirishi","u bilan bog'liq jismoniy harakat"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":326.04,"en":333.79,"si":10,"ev":"One time I danced in a culture show and the dance director at my school asked, \"Are you interested in really training? You seem to have talent.\"","uz":"Bir marta madaniyat ko'rgazmasida raqsga tushdim va maktabimizdagi raqs rahbari: \"Jiddiy shug'ullanishni xohlaysanmi? Senda iste'dod borga o'xshaydi\", deb so'radi.","why":"Uni bitta chiqishiga bo'lgan munosabat ilhomlantirdi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman admits that as a teenager, she","qu":"Ayol o'smirlikda ... ekanini tan oladi","o":["could sometimes behave unreasonably.","resented her parents' ambitions for her.","managed to hide certain feelings."],"ou":["ba'zan o'zini asossiz tutgan","ota-onasining u bilan bog'liq orzularidan norozi bo'lgan","ayrim his-tuyg'ularini yashira olgan"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":344.31,"en":369.24,"si":13,"ev":"I was on the point of rebellion on more than one occasion. Though I'm happy to say that particular storm never actually broke.","uz":"Bir necha marta isyon qilish arafasida edim. Xayriyatki, o'sha bo'ron hech qachon boshlanmadi.","why":"U his-tuyg'ularini ichida saqlay olgan (C). Ota-onasining orzusidan norozi emas edi — \"I wouldn't say I was pressurized\".","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":26.81,"e":26.81,"t":"Extract One — You hear two students talking about shopping for clothes."},{"s":26.81,"e":54.11,"t":"Recently a whole pile of my clothes got chucked out after a flatmate mistook them for rubbish. I was so upset. Oh no. Don't get me wrong, it wasn't that they held any particular significance for me or had any great value. It was the prospect of shopping for new stuff I couldn't face. Tell me about it. Even if there's like something I need to get, my trick is to put it off to the last possible moment. So I'll have less chance to waste time on such a pointless activity. Maybe that's why people think our clothes are rubbish. Yeah."},{"s":54.39,"e":66.21,"t":"But what gets me is that I reckon for a lot of people the clothes aren't the point. It's more about the act of shopping. It's heavily linked to wanting to be the centre of attention, to clothes giving them a strong personal identity or whatever."},{"s":66.78,"e":76.93,"t":"It's basically a way of showing off. Too much importance is placed on clothes and appearance, but it's not like a political issue for me. It's just a game I'm not prepared to play."},{"k":"h","s":163.16,"e":163.16,"t":"Extract Two — you hear part of an interview with a musician called Max."},{"s":163.16,"e":188.25,"t":"So was music in the blood, Max? Do you mean did my mum play the piano? Hardly. But I was well into the charts as a boy. In all honesty, I didn't think that being number one was something completely unattainable. I had a cockiness, but I kept it hidden from my peers. I'd hear a hit record and think, \"I could do that.\" From the age of 14, I fired off loads of demo discs I made in my bedroom. I had a folder where I kept all the rejection letters I got from record labels."},{"s":188.47,"e":216.38,"t":"It might have helped to share that with somebody, but I didn't. I just sulked, then had another go. Then when you did get a contract? I was vindicated. And it was a good deal in most respects too. Funny thing was though, if after my first hit I thought I'd made it, I was soon disabused of that notion. If I was to add up everything I'd done up till that point - school, working in a factory, learning guitar, making the demos - it doesn't compare. I've had to put in a lot of effort to capitalise on that breakthrough, I can tell you."},{"k":"h","s":309.78,"e":309.78,"t":"Extract Three — you hear part of a discussion programme in which two dancers are talking about their careers."},{"s":309.78,"e":319.97,"t":"It's really interesting because I didn't dance when I was in Hong Kong. I didn't pick up dance until I went to high school in the US. And that was probably like when I was 16 years old."},{"s":320.57,"e":325.57,"t":"Again, I didn't do it consciously. It wasn't like something that I was waiting to do."},{"s":326.04,"e":333.79,"t":"One time I danced in a culture show and the dance director at my school, she asked, \"Are you interested in really training? Like, you seem to have talent.\""},{"s":334.39,"e":339.29,"t":"And at that point I was really not interested. I was an athlete, a three-season athlete."},{"s":339.99,"e":343.55,"t":"I was more interested in like hanging with the guys and doing what I was used to."},{"s":344.31,"e":369.24,"t":"When I saw her perform, I was blown away and decided it was for me. And at college, I majored in it. I trained classically. That's so unlike my experience. I mean, I was dancing almost before I could walk. And although I wouldn't say I was pressurized into it, my parents were like behind me every step of the way. So much so that I was on the point of rebellion on more than one occasion. Though I'm happy to say that particular storm never actually broke."}]},{"n":19,"title":"Part of a discussion programme in which two artists are talking about their work","dur":448.992625,"x":[{"ps":31.1,"en":84.7,"c":"You hear part of a discussion programme in which two artists are talking about their work."},{"ps":172.02,"en":226.01,"c":"You hear two club DJs talking about their work."},{"ps":314.78,"en":378.56,"c":"You hear part of an interview with the owner of a new cake shop."}],"items":[{"q":"What do they agree about inspiration?","qu":"Ular ilhom haqida nimada kelishadi?","o":["An artist has to find their own source of it.","Non-artists won't be able to understand it.","It can be difficult to talk about it."],"ou":["Rassom uning manbasini o'zi topishi kerak.","Rassom bo'lmaganlar uni tushuna olmaydi.","U haqida gapirish qiyin bo'lishi mumkin."],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":31.1,"en":52.99,"si":1,"ev":"Getting asked where I get the inspiration for my art, I find that a tough one to answer, don't you? — …whether you think in those terms yourself or not, it's hardly an easy thing to articulate.","uz":"San'atimga ilhomni qayerdan olishimni so'rashsa, javob berish qiyin, shunday emasmi? — …Siz o'zingiz shunday o'ylaysizmi yoki yo'qmi, buni so'z bilan ifodalash oson emas.","why":"Ikkalasi ham ilhom haqida gapirish qiyin deydi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"The man's latest project aims to discover if","qu":"Erkakning so'nggi loyihasi ... ni aniqlashni maqsad qilgan","o":["holiday brochures are actually works of art.","the visual component of holiday brochures is effective.","the image made by holiday brochures is misleading."],"ou":["sayohat bukletlari aslida san'at asarimi","sayohat bukletlarining vizual qismi samaralimi","sayohat bukletlari yaratgan tasavvur chalg'ituvchimi"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":53.46,"en":84.7,"si":2,"ev":"There's a difference between the actual experience and the sanitized reality printed on the page. And that's what I want to look into.","uz":"Haqiqiy taassurot bilan sahifada bosilgan \"silliqlangan\" voqelik o'rtasida farq bor. Men aynan shuni o'rganmoqchiman.","why":"Bukletlar yaratgan tasavvur chalg'ituvchimi — loyiha shuni aniqlamoqchi (C). Faqat rasmlarning jozibasi (B) emas — \"Not just that\".","hl":null},{"q":"What did the man dislike about his last job as a radio DJ?","qu":"Erkakka radio DJ sifatidagi oxirgi ishida nima yoqmagan?","o":["He lacked the knowledge of the industry.","He didn't have one of the necessary skills.","He would often have arguments with the management."],"ou":["Soha haqida bilimi yetishmasdi.","Kerakli ko'nikmalardan biri unda yo'q edi.","Rahbariyat bilan tez-tez tortishib qolardi."],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":184.34,"en":188.19,"si":8,"ev":"It wasn't easy, and I soon discovered that I wasn't really cut out to be an interviewer.","uz":"Oson emas edi, tez orada intervyu olishga yaramasligimni tushundim.","why":"Kerakli ko'nikmalardan biri yo'q edi (B). Sohani yaxshi bilardi (A emas): \"pretty knowledgeable\".","hl":null},{"q":"What do they agree about being a club DJ?","qu":"Ular klub DJ bo'lish haqida nimada kelishadi?","o":["It's not easy to have it as the only job.","You shouldn't play music you don't like personally.","You have to be receptive to what the audience wants."],"ou":["Uni yagona ish sifatida qilish oson emas.","O'zingizga yoqmaydigan musiqani qo'ymasligingiz kerak.","Tomoshabinlar nimani xohlashiga e'tiborli bo'lishingiz kerak."],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":206.49,"en":226.01,"si":13,"ev":"It really depends on the party and the crowd. You've got to give them what they want. — I'm all for being flexible…","uz":"Hammasi bazm va olomonga bog'liq. Ularga xohlaganini berishingiz kerak. — Men moslashuvchanlik tarafdoriman…","why":"Ikkalasi ham tinglovchilar xohishiga e'tiborli bo'lish kerak deydi (C). B — faqat bittasining fikri.","hl":null},{"q":"What does she say about cake making?","qu":"U tort pishirish haqida nima deydi?","o":["It's always been her dream to do it for a living.","She found it interesting as it required different skills.","It was a skill she picked up at her first job."],"ou":["Bu bilan kun ko'rish doim uning orzusi bo'lgan.","Turli ko'nikmalar talab qilgani uchun unga qiziq tuyulgan.","Bu ko'nikmani birinchi ish joyida o'rgangan."],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":334.58,"en":351.52,"si":21,"ev":"I focused on cake making there because it's quite artistic, but also scientific. Getting the right ingredients in the right measures is not something you can leave to chance.","uz":"U yerda tort pishirishga e'tibor berdim, chunki u ham badiiy, ham ilmiy. To'g'ri masalliqlarni to'g'ri miqdorda olish tasodifga qoldirib bo'lmaydigan ish.","why":"Turli ko'nikmalar talab qilgani uchun qiziq (B). Bu uning orzusi bo'lmagan (A) — \"Hardly!\".","hl":null},{"q":"How does she feel about her new business?","qu":"U yangi biznesi haqida qanday his qiladi?","o":["confident in her own judgement.","relieved that she listened to an expert advice.","concerned that the early success might not last."],"ou":["o'z mulohazasiga ishonadi","mutaxassis maslahatiga quloq solganidan yengil tortgan","dastlabki muvaffaqiyat uzoqqa bormasligidan xavotirda"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":365.56,"en":378.56,"si":28,"ev":"I had lots of expert advice… but most of it turned out to be pretty wide of the mark. So I've learnt to follow my instincts.","uz":"Ko'p mutaxassis maslahatlarini oldim… lekin ko'pi noto'g'ri chiqdi. Shuning uchun o'z sezgimga ergashishni o'rgandim.","why":"O'z mulohazasiga ishonadi (A). Mutaxassis maslahati (B) — aksincha, noto'g'ri bo'lgan.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":31.1,"e":31.1,"t":"Extract One — You hear part of a discussion programme in which two artists are talking about their work."},{"s":31.1,"e":52.99,"t":"getting asked where I get the inspiration for my art, I find that a tough one to answer, don't you? Well, I think the answer's got to be there. The real issue is whether you're ready to open up to that extent, because whether you think in those terms yourself or not, it's hardly an easy thing to articulate. You seem to manage. Well, take my most recent work. In that, I've been looking at the idea of the annual holiday."},{"s":53.46,"e":79.55,"t":"I was struck by the thought that it was just another thing that we interact with. In the various brochures and pamphlets, destinations are similarly grouped together in digestible sections, making them objects of desire that we use in our leisure time. You mean the gloss and the allure of the images tempting us to make the visit? Not just that. It's also that from there it's a short step to believing that we're leaving the pressures of the everyday behind us, when in truth there's a difference between the actual experience"},{"s":79.77,"e":84.7,"t":"and the sanitized reality printed on the page. And that's what I want to look into."},{"k":"h","s":172.02,"e":172.02,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two club DJs talking about their work."},{"s":172.02,"e":175.36,"t":"I started out working for a radio station as a studio assistant."},{"s":175.8,"e":179.29,"t":"and because of my love of electronic music I try to push it at the station."},{"s":180.09,"e":183.71,"t":"I pretty soon got my own show because I was pretty knowledgeable about the music scene."},{"s":184.34,"e":188.19,"t":"It wasn't easy, and I soon discovered that I wasn't really cut out to be an interviewer."},{"s":188.73,"e":190.01,"t":"so I wasn't comfortable in the"},{"s":191.13,"e":195.45,"t":"Once I started doing club DJing, I knew I'd found my real niche. Yeah."},{"s":195.9,"e":198.62,"t":"The connection with the crowd can sometimes be incredible, can't it?"},{"s":199.22,"e":205.92,"t":"I'd never have thought that playing records could ever become my life, but here I am, making a living out of it. And not a bad one either."},{"s":206.49,"e":213.98,"t":"I play lots of different styles because I like them all in their own way. But it really depends on the party and the crowd. You've got to give them what they want."},{"s":214.49,"e":217.66,"t":"No two sets are ever the same in that respect, and that's the beauty of it."},{"s":218.14,"e":226.01,"t":"I'm all for being flexible, but I don't play tracks which I don't like myself. I reckon that'd be selling out. Really? I'm happy to go with the flow, actually."},{"k":"h","s":314.78,"e":314.78,"t":"Extract Three — You hear part of an interview with the owner of a new cake shop."},{"s":314.78,"e":321.63,"t":"Now Theresa, you've just opened your own cake shop in town. Was it always your ambition to be a cake maker? Hardly!"},{"s":322.46,"e":325.5,"t":"I left school at 17 with little idea of where I was heading."},{"s":326.23,"e":330.05,"t":"I took a job in an Italian restaurant because there was little else available."},{"s":330.65,"e":334.11,"t":"I had no experience but I found I loved the buzz of working in the kitchen."},{"s":334.58,"e":342.72,"t":"So I decided to go to catering college. Although I've never actually done any before, I focused on cake making there because it's quite artistic."},{"s":343.19,"e":344.57,"t":"but also scientific."},{"s":345.21,"e":351.52,"t":"Getting the right ingredients in the right measures is not something you can leave to chance. I like that idea."},{"s":351.99,"e":353.92,"t":"So how's the cake shop going?"},{"s":354.36,"e":359.55,"t":"Well, after the initial blaze of publicity, you get really worried about whether you've made the right decision."},{"s":360.12,"e":363.26,"t":"People come and try your stuff because you're the new shop on the block."},{"s":363.83,"e":364.8,"t":"But do they come back"},{"s":365.56,"e":369.44,"t":"I had lots of expert advice about pricing and the range of goods to offer."},{"s":369.91,"e":372.25,"t":"but most of it turned out to be pretty wide of the mark."},{"s":372.79,"e":378.56,"t":"So I've learnt to follow my instincts and fortunately, we're beginning to see a firm customer base emerging as a result."}]},{"n":20,"title":"A man talking to a friend who's just arrived at an airport","dur":453.746938,"x":[{"ps":27.83,"en":88.35,"c":"You hear a man talking to a friend who's just arrived at an airport."},{"ps":182.04,"en":240.29,"c":"You hear a science teacher telling a friend about her work."},{"ps":334.49,"en":389.21,"c":"You hear a new album being reviewed on a music radio station."}],"items":[{"q":"They disagree about whether the woman's flight","qu":"Ular ayolning reysi ... masalasida kelisha olmaydi","o":["offered good value for money.","managed to arrive on time.","provided reasonable comfort level."],"ou":["to'langan pulga arzirmidi","o'z vaqtida yetib keldimi","yetarlicha qulaylik berdimi"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":30.2,"en":59.93,"si":3,"ev":"It left half an hour late… — Anyway the pilot obviously made up time. I'd only just turned up and there you were. — I expect you were late too.","uz":"Yarim soat kechikib uchdi… — Har holda uchuvchi vaqtni quvib yetgan. Men endigina kelgan edim, sen ham shu yerda eding. — Sen ham kechikkan bo'lsang kerak.","why":"Ular reys o'z vaqtida yetib kelganmi — shunda kelisha olmaydi (B). Narx (A) haqida erkak ham \"you always pay a bit over the odds\" deydi.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the man's advice for the woman?","qu":"Erkak ayolga nima maslahat beradi?","o":["trying a different air company","choosing a different destination airport","changing the means of transport"],"ou":["boshqa aviakompaniyani sinab ko'rish","boshqa manzil aeroportini tanlash","transport turini o'zgartirish"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":60.41,"en":86.59,"si":5,"ev":"The thing to do next time is steer clear of the big hubs. You could have flown into the little airport down the coast even with this airline.","uz":"Keyingi safar katta aeroportlardan qochgan ma'qul. Shu aviakompaniya bilan sohildagi kichik aeroportga ham ucha olarding.","why":"Boshqa manzil aeroportini tanlash (B). Poyezd (C) — \"it'd still be quicker than the train\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is her opinion of pupils using the Internet to find new information?","qu":"U o'quvchilarning yangi ma'lumot topish uchun internetdan foydalanishi haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["It has altered the teacher's role in the studying process","It has to be supervised by a teacher","It can't substitute a teacher figure in the classroom"],"ou":["U o'qish jarayonida o'qituvchining rolini o'zgartirgan","U o'qituvchi nazoratida bo'lishi kerak","U sinfdagi o'qituvchi o'rnini bosa olmaydi"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":182.04,"en":207.54,"si":8,"ev":"With the internet kids can access information directly, without the mediation of the teacher. What they can't manage to do on their own is question it… That's where the teacher comes in.","uz":"Internet orqali bolalar ma'lumotni o'qituvchi vositachiligisiz to'g'ridan-to'g'ri oladi. Ular o'zlari qila olmaydigan narsa — unga shubha bilan qarash… Mana shu yerda o'qituvchi kerak bo'ladi.","why":"Internet o'qituvchining rolini o'zgartirgan (A): endi u ma'lumot beruvchi emas, tanqidiy fikrlashga o'rgatuvchi.","hl":null},{"q":"What is her opinion of her approach to teaching?","qu":"U o'zining o'qitish yondashuvi haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["She is ready to change it to better suit students' needs","She regrets her colleagues not using the same techniques","She is certain that it has positive results"],"ou":["Uni o'quvchilar ehtiyojiga moslash uchun o'zgartirishga tayyor","Hamkasblari shu usullardan foydalanmasligidan afsuslanadi","Uning ijobiy natija berishiga ishonchi komil"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":227.48,"en":240.29,"si":14,"ev":"Only time will tell if it gets adopted on a wider scale. But we had a meeting last week to see how it was going and nobody wanted to change anything.","uz":"Kengroq qo'llanilishini faqat vaqt ko'rsatadi. Lekin o'tgan hafta qanday ketayotganini ko'rish uchun yig'ilish qildik — hech kim hech narsani o'zgartirishni xohlamadi.","why":"Yondashuvi ijobiy natija berishiga ishonchi komil (C). O'zgartirishga tayyorligi (A) aytilmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"What impressed the woman most about the new album?","qu":"Yangi albomning qaysi jihati ayolni eng ko'p hayratga soldi?","o":["the way it was recorded","the style of the recording","the variety of instruments used"],"ou":["qanday yozib olingani","yozuvning uslubi","ishlatilgan cholg'ularning xilma-xilligi"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":334.49,"en":362.49,"si":17,"ev":"A record that's effectively homemade, not a studio recording… But what really blew me away was the fact that it's unaffected in a way you'd scarcely think possible.","uz":"Amalda uyda yozilgan, studiyada emas… Lekin meni eng ko'p hayratga solgani — uning aql bovar qilmas darajada tabiiyligi.","why":"\"What really blew me away\" — yozuvning uslubi, tabiiyligi (B). Uyda yozilgani (A) — \"incredible in itself\", lekin eng asosiysi emas.","hl":null},{"q":"According to the man, what makes the band stand out?","qu":"Erkakning fikricha, guruhni nima ajratib turadi?","o":["the originality of their sound","the high quality of tracks","the organic combination of various music styles"],"ou":["ovozining o'ziga xosligi","treklarning yuqori sifati","turli musiqa uslublarining tabiiy uyg'unligi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":377.24,"en":389.21,"si":19,"ev":"What makes them kind of unique is that they don't seem to be trying to sound like anyone but themselves.","uz":"Ularni noyob qiladigan narsa — ular hech kimga emas, faqat o'zlariga o'xshab chalishga harakat qiladi.","why":"Ovozining o'ziga xosligi (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":27.83,"e":27.83,"t":"Extract One — You hear a man talking to a friend who's just arrived at an airport."},{"s":27.83,"e":28.48,"t":"Good flight."},{"s":28.98,"e":29.57,"t":"Hardly"},{"s":30.2,"e":56.22,"t":"travel just goes from bad to worse. It wasn't even a particularly cheap flight but there was precious little legroom. It left half an hour late and I wasn't offered as much as a glass of water. Well it was the national airline so you always pay a bit over the odds but there are actually fewer seats so it shouldn't be cramped but since the budget airline started competing nobody's offering free refreshments on these short routes anymore. Anyway the pilot obviously made up time"},{"s":56.57,"e":59.93,"t":"I'd only just turned up and there you were. I expect you were late too."},{"s":60.41,"e":86.59,"t":"But there's an inordinate amount of queuing up and hanging about involved in air travel. I know you're going to say that's because of security and so it's not the airline's fault. I wasn't actually. The thing to do next time is steer clear of the big hubs. You could have flown into the little airport down the coast even with this airline. Lots less hanging about there. There's not the volume of passengers and despite the drive it'd still be quicker than the train. It's not this airport I'm complaining about."},{"s":86.84,"e":88.35,"t":"It's the one I've just come from"},{"k":"h","s":182.04,"e":182.04,"t":"Extract Two — You hear a science teacher telling a friend about her work."},{"s":182.04,"e":198.27,"t":"From what I remember of science at school, it was mostly a case of listen and make notes with the odd set piece experiment. That's not science. I mean, all subjects are knowledge based to a certain extent, but with the internet kids can access information directly, without the mediation of the teacher."},{"s":199.02,"e":201.63,"t":"What they can't manage to do on their own is question it."},{"s":202.16,"e":204.73,"t":"critical view of its accuracy and usefulness."},{"s":205.16,"e":207.54,"t":"That's where the teacher comes in. Right."},{"s":207.99,"e":214.05,"t":"And kids need to know how to use science in real life. So these days it's all about putting information in context."},{"s":214.65,"e":227.01,"t":"Like I did a lesson last week where they worked out how much energy is expended to make, buy and watch a television. I mean there's an immediate relevance there. Should the kids everywhere do that now? Well, it would be good if they could."},{"s":227.48,"e":235.52,"t":"I worked out this scheme of work with some colleagues from other local schools. It had official backing, but only time will tell if it gets adopted on a wider scale."},{"s":236.09,"e":240.29,"t":"But we had a meeting last week to see how it was going and nobody wanted to change anything."},{"k":"h","s":334.49,"e":334.49,"t":"Extract Three — You hear a new album being reviewed on a music radio station."},{"s":334.49,"e":362.49,"t":"And Fiona, you've been listening to the first album from a new band, new to me at least, called The Forerunners. Where did they come from? Well, basically Tom, what you've got here is four young guys from rural England who debut with a record that's effectively homemade, not a studio recording. That's incredible in itself. But what really blew me away was the fact that it's unaffected in a way you'd scarcely think possible. They make a gentle sound and even when doing crescendos they never get harsh."},{"s":362.81,"e":376.7,"t":"never seem to fall in love with their own vibe. Added to that, they seem to use a whole range of instruments without ever drawing your attention to the fact. Yes, I agree, and they keep the interest going from one little jewel to the next. There are almost no duds here."},{"s":377.24,"e":389.21,"t":"And although there are echoes of all sorts of people, it wouldn't be fair to make comparisons. I mean, what makes them kind of unique is that they don't seem to be trying to sound like anyone but themselves. Quite highly recommended."}]},{"n":21,"title":"Two neighbors, Adam and Juliet. talking about living in Montreal, Canada","dur":547.030188,"x":[{"ps":32.12,"en":101.21,"c":"You hear two neighbors, Adam and Juliet. talking about living in Montreal, Canada."},{"ps":214.94,"en":281.92,"c":"You hear two students, a girl called Sariah and a boy called Halim. talking about an essay they have to write on the topic of plastic."},{"ps":391.86,"en":463.13,"c":"You hear a psychologist, Dr. Jane Blake. journalist Ed Riegas discussing the teenage years."}],"items":[{"q":"What attracted Adam to living in Montreal?","qu":"Adamni Monrealda yashashga nima jalb qildi?","o":["the change in weather from winter to summer","the feeling of close community evident there","the value inhabitants place on tradition"],"ou":["qishdan yozga ob-havoning o'zgarishi","u yerda sezilib turadigan ahil jamoa hissi","aholining an'analarga beradigan qadri"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":56.89,"en":68.77,"si":7,"ev":"That sudden shift from biting cold gales to beautifully balmy evenings when you can sit outside in a t-shirt until midnight is what drew me to Montreal.","uz":"Achchiq sovuq shamollardan to yarim tungacha futbolkada tashqarida o'tirsa bo'ladigan iliq oqshomlarga keskin o'tish — meni Monrealga aynan shu jalb qildi.","why":"Qishdan yozga ob-havoning o'zgarishi (A). \"Drew me\" = jalb qildi.","hl":null},{"q":"What do they both say about accommodation in Montreal?","qu":"Ikkalasi Monrealdagi uy-joy haqida nima deydi?","o":["The frequency with which people move house is above average.","Central apartments are rarely available for purchase.","Renting is a comparatively inexpensive option."],"ou":["Odamlarning uy ko'chishi o'rtachadan tez-tez.","Markazdagi kvartiralar kamdan-kam sotuvga chiqadi.","Ijaraga olish nisbatan arzon variant."],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":71.22,"en":91.17,"si":9,"ev":"It makes sense to rent in Montreal. You don't have to fork out a fortune for a place downtown… you can get a deal because there's so much on the market.","uz":"Monrealda ijaraga olish mantiqan to'g'ri. Markazdagi joy uchun katta pul to'lashingiz shart emas… bozorda taklif ko'p bo'lgani uchun arzon topish mumkin.","why":"Ijara nisbatan arzon variant (C). Ko'chish tez-tez bo'lishi (A) — faqat misol, o'rtachadan yuqori deyilmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"What is Soraya doing?","qu":"Soraya nima qilyapti?","o":["acknowledging the benefits of plastic as a material","assessing the accuracy of information written about plastic","clarifying reasons for a change in people's attitudes to plastic"],"ou":["plastikning material sifatidagi foydalarini tan olyapti","plastik haqida yozilgan ma'lumotlarning aniqligini baholayapti","odamlarning plastikka munosabati o'zgarishi sabablarini tushuntiryapti"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":214.94,"en":242.43,"si":14,"ev":"When I read about the 1950s, I get that at that time plastic was seen as revolutionary. You could make anything from it… it was so strong and durable.","uz":"1950-yillar haqida o'qiganimda, o'sha paytda plastik inqilobiy deb hisoblanganini tushunaman. Undan har narsa yasash mumkin edi… u juda mustahkam va chidamli edi.","why":"Soraya plastikning material sifatidagi foydalarini tan olyapti (A).","hl":null},{"q":"What does Halim say about the documentary he saw?","qu":"Halim ko'rgan hujjatli filmi haqida nima deydi?","o":["It failed to offer a balanced argument.","It exaggerated the conclusions it drew.","It omitted some significant points."],"ou":["U muvozanatli fikr bera olmagan.","U chiqargan xulosalarini bo'rttirgan.","U ba'zi muhim jihatlarni tushirib qoldirgan."],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":242.84,"en":281.92,"si":15,"ev":"Wildly overdramatic at the end in my view… But to close with statements like \"most species of fish will be extinct within 10 years\" was way over the top.","uz":"Menimcha, oxiri haddan tashqari dramatik edi… \"Ko'p baliq turlari 10 yil ichida yo'qoladi\" degan gaplar bilan yakunlash mutlaqo oshirib yuborish edi.","why":"Film xulosalarini bo'rttirgan (B). U ijobiy va salbiy tomonlarni ko'rsatgan (A emas), asosiy g'oyalarni qamragan (C emas).","hl":null},{"q":"According to Dr Blake, what mistake do some parents make?","qu":"Doktor Bleykning fikricha, ba'zi ota-onalar qanday xatoga yo'l qo'yadi?","o":["They misinterpret their teenagers' behaviour.","They want to protect their children for too long.","They fail to recognise that their children's needs have changed."],"ou":["O'smir farzandlarining xatti-harakatini noto'g'ri talqin qiladi.","Farzandlarini juda uzoq vaqt himoya qilishni xohlaydi.","Farzandlarining ehtiyojlari o'zgarganini tan olmaydi."],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":391.86,"en":419.07,"si":18,"ev":"Parents are programmed to care for their child, but… the infant must develop, mature and eventually separate from them… If you know when to let go.","uz":"Ota-onalar farzandiga g'amxo'rlik qilishga moslashgan, lekin… bola rivojlanishi, ulg'ayishi va oxir-oqibat ulardan ajralishi kerak… qachon qo'yib yuborishni bilsangiz.","why":"Ba'zi ota-onalar farzandini juda uzoq himoya qilishni xohlaydi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"Which aspect of adolescence particularly interests Ed Regas?","qu":"O'smirlikning qaysi jihati Ed Regasni ayniqsa qiziqtiradi?","o":["the role played by gaming in teenagers' lives","teenagers' abnormal sleep patterns","the influence of peers on teenagers"],"ou":["o'smirlar hayotida kompyuter o'yinlarining o'rni","o'smirlarning g'ayritabiiy uyqu tartibi","tengdoshlarning o'smirlarga ta'siri"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":440.02,"en":454.69,"si":22,"ev":"The good thing is Max and I are both seriously into gaming. And I'm fascinated by how so many games promote universal values.","uz":"Yaxshisi shundaki, Max ikkalamiz ham kompyuter o'yinlariga jiddiy qiziqamiz. Ko'p o'yinlar umuminsoniy qadriyatlarni targ'ib qilishi meni hayratga soladi.","why":"Ed o'yinlarning o'smirlar hayotidagi o'rniga qiziqadi (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":32.12,"e":32.12,"t":"Extract One — You hear two neighbors, Adam and Juliet. talking about living in Montreal, Canada."},{"s":32.12,"e":33.18,"t":"Hi Adam."},{"s":33.82,"e":35.81,"t":"you finding living in Montreal?"},{"s":36.34,"e":43.61,"t":"Hi Juliet, it's a great city and I've got some good buddies now. Guys who live on our street and work colleagues."},{"s":44.12,"e":47.84,"t":"Are you going to the street party to celebrate Canada Day? You bet."},{"s":48.44,"e":54.65,"t":"It's a real important thing for me and my family. Celebrating it is an annual ritual for us."},{"s":55.16,"e":56.38,"t":"I'll see you there then."},{"s":56.89,"e":68.77,"t":"It's gonna be a beautiful day. And that sudden shift from biting cold gales to beautifully balmy evenings when you can sit outside in a t-shirt until midnight is what drew me to Montreal. It's awesome."},{"s":69.37,"e":70.72,"t":"I know what you mean."},{"s":71.22,"e":83.1,"t":"So are you staying on in your apartment? I think you said you only leased it for a year. Yeah, it makes sense to rent in Montreal. You don't have to fork out a fortune for a place downtown."},{"s":83.9,"e":91.17,"t":"you can get a deal because there's so much on the market. And getting a place of my own is, well, financially out of the question."},{"s":91.99,"e":97.21,"t":"Quite a few people on our street are moving out, right? Yeah, like my sister's moving again."},{"s":97.75,"e":101.21,"t":"She wants to be more in the center. Oh, okay."},{"k":"h","s":214.94,"e":214.94,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two students, a girl called Sariah and a boy called Halim. talking about an essay they have to write on the topic of plastic."},{"s":214.94,"e":242.43,"t":"Hi Sariah, how are you getting on with your essay on plastic? Hi Helene, well the background reading is fascinating. Okay, there's been a complete U-turn in the views expressed in journals and even in the popular press in recent years. But actually, when I read about the 1950s, I get that at that time plastic was seen as revolutionary. You could make anything from it, from bottles to roofs, it was so strong and durable."},{"s":242.84,"e":269.4,"t":"was not to like, whereas now it's seen as a real threat to the planet. Yeah, I've read a couple of really thought-provoking articles and I watched the documentary, our tutor recommended, you know, the one called Plastic Madness. Oh yeah, any good. Wildly overdramatic at the end in my view. To be fair, it did go into the pros and cons of the uses of plastic, and it covered the main ideas we'd discussed in class."},{"s":269.88,"e":281.92,"t":"But to close with statements like \"most species of fish will be extinct within 10 years\" was way over the top. And did it go into issues like plastic causing air pollution? It did, yeah."},{"k":"h","s":391.86,"e":391.86,"t":"Extract Three — You hear a psychologist, Dr. Jane Blake. journalist Ed Riegas discussing the teenage years."},{"s":391.86,"e":417.18,"t":"So Jane, I'm the parent of a 16-year-old Max, and my wife and I are constantly wondering if we're doing the right thing. The teenage years are critical in human development Ed. Parents are programmed to care for their child, but in evolutionary terms, the infant must develop, mature and eventually separate from them. And although the majority of parents cope admirably with their child becoming a monosyllabic and at times difficult teenager,"},{"s":417.59,"e":419.07,"t":"If you know when to let go."},{"s":419.58,"e":430.05,"t":"At the same time, parents do generally adapt well to having to provide more emotional support than physical support. With Max, we're going through things like he seems reluctant to wake up before 10."},{"s":430.49,"e":439.45,"t":"Some schools have changed their timetable to take into account the fact that teenagers perform better later in the day. Not his unfortunately."},{"s":440.02,"e":442.91,"t":"The good thing is Max and I are both seriously into gaming."},{"s":443.38,"e":454.69,"t":"And I'm fascinated by how so many games promote universal values like hard work pays off, collaboration works better than confrontation, and thinking things through is to be admired."},{"s":455.58,"e":463.13,"t":"I encourage Max to invite his mates round to our house because I want him to build up a circle of good friends who share common interests."}]},{"n":22,"title":"Nathalie and her brother David talking about thriller movies","dur":579.813875,"x":[{"ps":31.38,"en":100.09,"c":"You hear Nathalie and her brother David talking about thriller movies."},{"ps":210.3,"en":287.71,"c":"You hear two architecture students discussing covered overhead walkways called City Skyways."},{"ps":408.57,"en":488.45,"c":"You hear a radio discussion in which two educationalists, Sophie Lee and Gary Cole, are talking about sport."}],"items":[{"q":"What is Nathalie surprised to read about thriller movies?","qu":"Nathalie triller filmlar haqida nimani o'qib hayron qoladi?","o":["that very logical people tend to prefer them","that families who enjoy watching them together are happiest","that when we watch them, our bodies produce a chemical"],"ou":["juda mantiqli odamlar ularni afzal ko'rishini","ularni birga tomosha qiladigan oilalar eng baxtli ekanini","ularni ko'rganda tanamiz kimyoviy modda ishlab chiqarishini"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":45.62,"en":69.34,"si":2,"ev":"It says that families who like nothing better than sitting together on the sofa in front of a good thriller movie are the most contented. — That's news to me.","uz":"Unda aytilishicha, divanda birga o'tirib yaxshi triller ko'rishni hamma narsadan afzal ko'radigan oilalar eng baxtli ekan. — Buni birinchi eshitishim.","why":"Uni ajablantirgan yangilik — birga triller ko'radigan oilalar eng baxtli (B). Dopamin (C) — \"I'd heard before\", ya'ni yangilik emas.","hl":null},{"q":"David thinks watching horror movies is similar to going on a short holiday because both activities","qu":"David qo'rqinchli film ko'rish qisqa ta'tilga chiqishga o'xshaydi deb hisoblaydi, chunki ikkalasi ham","o":["allow people to escape everyday problems.","make people feel emotionally stronger.","stimulate people's creativity."],"ou":["odamlarga kundalik muammolardan qochish imkonini beradi","odamlarni ruhan kuchliroq his qildiradi","odamlarning ijodkorligini rag'batlantiradi"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":69.78,"en":100.09,"si":3,"ev":"More that it gives me ideas, even about how to solve issues at work… they leave me feeling more excited about possibilities to do with daily life.","uz":"Ko'proq menga g'oyalar beradi, hatto ishdagi muammolarni hal qilish haqida ham… kundalik hayot imkoniyatlariga nisbatan ko'proq ilhom beradi.","why":"Ikkalasi ham ijodkorlikni rag'batlantiradi (C). Xayoliy dunyoga qochish (A) — \"More that it gives me ideas\" bilan rad etiladi.","hl":null},{"q":"What do they agree about trends in shopping?","qu":"Ular xarid qilish tendensiyalari haqida nimada kelishadi?","o":["Skyways have led to a decline in the number of city-centre shops.","Out-of-town shopping malls are less popular nowadays.","Increased deliveries from online shopping will cause problems."],"ou":["Osma yo'laklar shahar markazidagi do'konlar sonining kamayishiga olib kelgan.","Shahar tashqarisidagi savdo markazlari hozir kamroq mashhur.","Onlayn xarid yetkazib berishlarining ko'payishi muammolar tug'diradi."],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":210.3,"en":241.31,"si":7,"ev":"When they link the upper floors of buildings, shops at ground level don't get passing trade anymore. Some even go bust… so many stores are having to close.","uz":"Ular binolarning yuqori qavatlarini bog'laganda, pastki qavatdagi do'konlarga o'tkinchi xaridorlar kelmay qoladi. Ba'zilari hatto sinadi… shuning uchun ko'p do'konlar yopilmoqda.","why":"Osma yo'laklar markazdagi do'konlar sonining kamayishiga olib kelgan (A).","hl":null},{"q":"What does the man think is the greatest advantage of skyways?","qu":"Erkakning fikricha, osma yo'laklarning eng katta afzalligi nima?","o":["They are climate-controlled.","They are safe areas for pedestrians.","They are a solution to overcrowded streets."],"ou":["Ularda harorat nazorat qilinadi.","Ular piyodalar uchun xavfsiz joy.","Ular gavjum ko'chalar muammosining yechimi."],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":263.03,"en":277.98,"si":12,"ev":"Skyways mean pedestrians can enjoy walking through a city in any weather… But to my mind, getting people away from congested roads and sidewalks has to be the winning argument.","uz":"Osma yo'laklar piyodalarga har qanday ob-havoda yurish imkonini beradi… Lekin menimcha, odamlarni gavjum yo'l va trotuarlardan olib chiqish — eng kuchli dalil.","why":"\"But to my mind\" dan keyingi gap — javob (C). Ob-havo (A) va xavfsizlik (B) — \"the arguments\" sifatida sanaladi.","hl":null},{"q":"Gary would like to raise public awareness of how sport contributes to","qu":"Gary sport ... ga qanday hissa qo'shishi haqida jamoatchilik xabardorligini oshirmoqchi","o":["a child's social development.","a child's physical health and growth.","a child's understanding of the need for rules."],"ou":["bolaning ijtimoiy rivojlanishiga","bolaning jismoniy salomatligi va o'sishiga","bolaning qoidalar zarurligini tushunishiga"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":439.26,"en":449.09,"si":20,"ev":"What I want to get across is how sport helps children mature socially by teaching them about teamwork and about fair play.","uz":"Men yetkazmoqchi bo'lgan narsa — sport bolalarga jamoaviy ish va halol o'yinni o'rgatib, ijtimoiy jihatdan ulg'ayishiga qanday yordam berishi.","why":"Bolaning ijtimoiy rivojlanishi (A). Qoidalar (C) — \"I'd rather not focus on the discipline aspect\".","hl":null},{"q":"Sophia says that children who do sport are more likely to","qu":"Sophianing aytishicha, sport bilan shug'ullanadigan bolalar ... ehtimoli yuqoriroq","o":["go on to further education.","have a good school attendance record.","be motivated to succeed academically."],"ou":["o'qishni davom ettirish","maktabga yaxshi qatnash","o'qishda muvaffaqiyatga intilish"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":467.93,"en":488.45,"si":22,"ev":"Those who did sport were much keener to try to get good grades… And did they achieve that? Not always, but the aspiration was there.","uz":"Sport bilan shug'ullanganlar yaxshi baho olishga ancha intilardi… Erishdilarmi? Har doim emas, lekin intilish bor edi.","why":"O'qishda muvaffaqiyatga intilish (C). Davomat (B) kuzatilgan, lekin xulosa u haqda emas.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":31.38,"e":31.38,"t":"Extract One — You hear Nathalie and her brother David talking about thriller movies."},{"s":31.38,"e":45.05,"t":"Have you read this article about watching thriller movies? No, is it good? Yeah, well, I'd heard before that when we're scared our brains pump out the feel-good chemical dopamine like when we're in love with someone."},{"s":45.62,"e":69.34,"t":"But look at this, it says that families who like nothing better than sitting together on the sofa in front of a good thriller movie are the most contented. That's news to me. Most people I know who adore thriller movies appreciate them for the really good plot lines. You know, the stories are so rational in many ways that some otherwise very sensible people are drawn into them."},{"s":69.78,"e":82.37,"t":"For me, when I watch horror movies it's like going on a mini-vacation. Do you mean you can wander off into a fantasy world? More that it gives me ideas, even about how to solve issues at work."},{"s":83.0,"e":95.01,"t":"And I've heard other people say the same. Really? I could understand it if you said something like it's the suspense, the special effects or the thrill you get from watching them. Well, it may sound odd."},{"s":95.61,"e":100.09,"t":"they leave me feeling more excited about possibilities to do with daily life."},{"k":"h","s":210.3,"e":210.3,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two architecture students discussing covered overhead walkways called City Skyways."},{"s":210.3,"e":235.42,"t":"They've just been reading an article about building skyways in cities. Their effect on commerce, particularly shopping, can be considerable because when they link the upper floors of buildings, shops at ground level don't get passing trade anymore. Some even go bust. Absolutely. If people are walking about on the third or fourth floor, they won't make a special trip down to the ground level to buy something."},{"s":235.83,"e":241.31,"t":"And that's why so many stores are having to close, even when they're in prime central locations."},{"s":242.04,"e":249.34,"t":"I read they're also struggling because people are buying online. And with online shopping, deliveries are becoming more efficient."},{"s":249.94,"e":259.42,"t":"Plus centers are suffering because all those large shopping malls on the outskirts of towns were built to attract people by offering a range of activities, like movie theaters."},{"s":259.9,"e":262.37,"t":"I think the two things are different."},{"s":263.03,"e":271.61,"t":"You know the arguments. Skyways mean pedestrians can enjoy walking through a city in any weather, and there is less crime than at street level."},{"s":272.18,"e":277.98,"t":"But to my mind, getting people away from congested roads and sidewalks has to be the winning argument."},{"s":278.42,"e":281.69,"t":"Skyways have the potential to bring life back to city centres."},{"s":282.33,"e":287.71,"t":"After all, the centre is where people not only want to shop and work, but live too."},{"k":"h","s":408.57,"e":408.57,"t":"Extract Three — You hear a radio discussion in which two educationalists, Sophie Lee and Gary Cole, are talking about sport."},{"s":408.57,"e":413.66,"t":"So Gary, you're working on public information campaigns, aren't you? Yes, Sophie."},{"s":414.1,"e":435.9,"t":"I'm actually employed by the government and the thinking behind the public awareness campaigns this year is all about encouraging participation in sports at school. Yes, I saw the very successful TV campaign showing the importance of doing sport for healthy growth in primary age children. But isn't that something that the public already knows? Most people, yes."},{"s":436.34,"e":438.62,"t":"And that's why we started with the health aspect."},{"s":439.26,"e":449.09,"t":"What's less well understood, and what I want to get across, is how sport helps children mature socially by teaching them about teamwork and about fair play."},{"s":449.91,"e":467.39,"t":"I'd rather not focus on the discipline aspect, the idea that sports are all about learning sets of rules and sticking to them. Interesting. I'm looking into the effect of sport on learning performance. My first study followed a group of children from primary school right through to university level."},{"s":467.93,"e":488.45,"t":"I tracked various things like how often they were absent through illness and their grades and what stood out was that those who did sport were much keener to try to get good grades in maths, English, those kinds of subjects. And did they achieve that? Not always, but the aspiration was there and for me that's what really counts."}]},{"n":23,"title":"Two scientists, Peter Cameron and Lisa Mackey discussing generating electricity…","dur":527.595063,"x":[{"ps":33.72,"en":100.19,"c":"You hear two scientists, Peter Cameron and Lisa Mackey discussing generating electricity from the energy in the oceans."},{"ps":208.12,"en":276.73,"c":"You hear two friends discussing the practice of urban foraging, which is picking nuts and fruit from around a city."},{"ps":384.63,"en":450.49,"c":"You hear a husband and wife talking about planning a holiday."}],"items":[{"q":"What does Peter believe is the greatest advantage of generating electricity from the oceans?","qu":"Peter okeanlardan elektr ishlab chiqarishning eng katta afzalligi nima deb hisoblaydi?","o":["The seas provide a reliable energy source.","It will be cost-effective in the long run.","Many countries will be able to create their own energy."],"ou":["Dengizlar ishonchli energiya manbai.","Uzoq muddatda tejamkor bo'ladi.","Ko'p davlatlar o'z energiyasini ishlab chiqara oladi."],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":44.41,"en":67.74,"si":4,"ev":"That's not, as I see it, the main attraction. It's the fact that wherever there's a large body of water, you can generate power. Energy won't need to be imported from abroad.","uz":"Menimcha, asosiy jozibasi bu emas. Gap shundaki, katta suv havzasi bor har qanday joyda energiya ishlab chiqarish mumkin. Energiyani chetdan olib kelish shart bo'lmaydi.","why":"Ko'p davlatlar o'z energiyasini yarata oladi (C). Ishonchli manba (A) — \"that's not the main attraction\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is Lisa doing?","qu":"Lisa nima qilyapti?","o":["correcting the information that Peter gives","suggesting an alternative opinion","predicting future developments"],"ou":["Peter bergan ma'lumotni tuzatyapti","muqobil fikr bildiryapti","kelajakdagi o'zgarishlarni bashorat qilyapti"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":81.37,"en":100.19,"si":11,"ev":"But I'm still a firm believer in land-based wind turbines… the possible damage to marine wildlife… cancels out any benefits.","uz":"Lekin men hamon quruqlikdagi shamol turbinalari tarafdoriman… dengiz jonzotlariga yetishi mumkin bo'lgan zarar har qanday foydani yo'qqa chiqaradi.","why":"Lisa muqobil fikr bildiryapti (B). U Peterning ma'lumotini tuzatmaydi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"Why does the woman think urban foraging is popular?","qu":"Ayol nega shaharda yovvoyi oziq-ovqat terish ommabop deb hisoblaydi?","o":["People seek a strong connection with nature.","Wild food is guaranteed to be organic.","It can save money on grocery bills."],"ou":["Odamlar tabiat bilan mustahkam bog'liqlikka intiladi.","Yovvoyi oziq-ovqat albatta organik bo'ladi.","Bu oziq-ovqat xarajatlarini tejaydi."],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":219.19,"en":233.57,"si":15,"ev":"People are so fed up with mass-produced processed food, they like the idea that it's sure to be natural… free of artificial chemicals.","uz":"Odamlar ommaviy ishlab chiqarilgan qayta ishlangan oziq-ovqatdan shunchalik to'yganki, unda sun'iy kimyoviy moddalar yo'qligi va tabiiyligi g'oyasi ularga yoqadi.","why":"Yovvoyi oziq-ovqat albatta organik (B). Pul tejash (C) — \"it'd barely make a difference\".","hl":null},{"q":"How do they both feel about urban foraging becoming possible in their local park?","qu":"Ikkalasi mahalliy bog'da yovvoyi o'simlik terishga ruxsat berilishi haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["worried that many plants will be destroyed","hopeful that plant identification courses will be held","surprised that local residents weren't consulted about it"],"ou":["ko'p o'simliklar nobud bo'lishidan xavotirda","o'simliklarni aniqlash kurslari o'tkazilishiga umid qiladi","mahalliy aholi bilan maslahatlashilmaganidan hayron"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":255.03,"en":270.43,"si":19,"ev":"As long as they offer classes so that people know what things are… — But good point. You also wouldn't want anyone getting sick.","uz":"Faqat odamlar nima ekanini bilishi uchun darslar tashkil qilinsa… — To'g'ri gap. Hech kim zaharlanib qolishini xohlamaysan.","why":"Ikkalasi ham o'simliklarni aniqlash kurslari o'tkazilishiga umid qiladi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman mentions last year's holiday in an attempt to","qu":"Ayol o'tgan yilgi ta'tilni ... maqsadida tilga oladi","o":["justify increasing their holiday budget this year.","avoid a similar situation occurring this year.","influence their choice of holiday this year."],"ou":["bu yilgi ta'til byudjetini oshirishni oqlash","bu yil shunga o'xshash vaziyat takrorlanishining oldini olish","bu yilgi ta'til tanloviga ta'sir qilish"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":408.89,"en":421.25,"si":25,"ev":"We don't want to book so late this year that we end up in a grotty hotel like last year… But they were all booked.","uz":"Bu yil o'tgan yilgidek iflos mehmonxonaga tushib qolmaslik uchun juda kech band qilmasligimiz kerak… Hammasi band edi.","why":"O'tgan yilgi vaziyat takrorlanmasligi uchun (B). Byudjet (A) — pul bor edi.","hl":null},{"q":"What approach to packing for their holiday do they agree on?","qu":"Ta'tilga narsalarni yig'ish bo'yicha qaysi yondashuvda kelishadi?","o":["It's essential to make a detailed list.","It's a good idea to do it well in advance.","It's better to pack too many items than too few."],"ou":["Batafsil ro'yxat tuzish shart.","Buni ancha oldindan qilgan ma'qul.","Kam narsadan ko'ra ko'p narsa olgan yaxshi."],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":427.0,"en":444.99,"si":28,"ev":"We always seem to take more than we need, but I'd rather it was that way round than be short of things.","uz":"Biz doim keragidan ko'p narsa olamiz, lekin yetishmay qolgandan ko'ra shunisi yaxshi.","why":"Kamdan ko'ra ko'p olgan yaxshi (C). Ro'yxat (A) bor, lekin \"essential\" deyilmaydi.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":33.72,"e":33.72,"t":"Extract One — You hear two scientists, Peter Cameron and Lisa Mackey discussing generating electricity from the energy in the oceans."},{"s":33.72,"e":37.63,"t":"So Peter, how's your work on generating electricity from the oceans going?"},{"s":38.1,"e":39.13,"t":"Good thanks Lisa."},{"s":39.9,"e":43.52,"t":"As you know, my interest is in generating energy from ocean tides."},{"s":44.41,"e":53.92,"t":"it's easy to talk about the obvious benefits to potential investors, like there are always tides twice a day. So as an energy resource, it won't run out."},{"s":54.62,"e":57.73,"t":"But that's not, as I see it, the main attraction."},{"s":58.36,"e":62.37,"t":"It's the fact that wherever there's a large body of water, you can generate power."},{"s":63.16,"e":67.74,"t":"Energy won't need to be imported from abroad. That's a really important point."},{"s":68.22,"e":77.89,"t":"And I think I'm right in saying that a whole range of new devices have been developed to harness energy from the sea, like giant blades and paddles to power turbines."},{"s":78.36,"e":78.94,"t":"Yes."},{"s":79.45,"e":80.48,"t":"They're the next big thing"},{"s":81.37,"e":91.1,"t":"But I'm still a firm believer in land-based wind turbines as a clean renewable energy resource. The company I work for doesn't use offshore wind turbines."},{"s":91.7,"e":100.19,"t":"To me, the possible damage to marine wildlife that can occur with generating energy from the ocean, by whatever means, cancels out any benefits."},{"k":"h","s":208.12,"e":208.12,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two friends discussing the practice of urban foraging, which is picking nuts and fruit from around a city."},{"s":208.12,"e":218.53,"t":"Hey Nancy, you know a lot about plants. What do you think about urban foraging? You mean people going out and picking fruit and things from public areas and cities?"},{"s":219.19,"e":231.45,"t":"And while I can understand the appeal, it'd barely make a difference to your weekly outlay on food, but I think people are so fed up with mass-produced processed food, they like the idea that it's sure to be natural."},{"s":231.9,"e":233.57,"t":"of artificial chemicals."},{"s":234.2,"e":249.05,"t":"But I wonder how many people these days venture out into parks and forests. I mean, loads of city kids have never been into the countryside. Hmm. You know, there's talk of letting people pick the fruit and nuts from the trees in the park on Main Street."},{"s":249.59,"e":254.59,"t":"just in the area where all the trees are, so the flowers and bushes don't get trashed."},{"s":255.03,"e":270.43,"t":"Well, as long as they offer classes so that people know what things are, apparently there are some blueberry bushes in the park. Really? I didn't know that. But good point. You also wouldn't want anyone getting sick because they'd eaten something poisonous."},{"s":271.16,"e":276.73,"t":"It'll be interesting to see how many of my neighbors have heard about foraging and might do it."},{"k":"h","s":384.63,"e":384.63,"t":"Extract Three — You hear a husband and wife talking about planning a holiday."},{"s":384.63,"e":396.32,"t":"Freya, do you think it's about time we did something about booking a summer holiday? Absolutely! It seems age-less since last year's holiday. Are you happy to laze about on a beach again?"},{"s":396.76,"e":397.63,"t":"Perfect."},{"s":398.1,"e":408.19,"t":"living in a city and having hectic jobs, that suits us, I think. And I'd rather not do anything too energetic, like a walking holiday. Remember when we went with your sister?"},{"s":408.89,"e":421.25,"t":"Yeah, exhausting. And we don't want to book so late this year that we end up in a grotty hotel like last year. We'd even saved enough to stay in a four-star hotel. But they were all booked."},{"s":421.82,"e":422.62,"t":"I know."},{"s":423.13,"e":426.53,"t":"Anyway, we've got those new suitcases, so packing will be easy."},{"s":427.0,"e":444.99,"t":"We always seem to take more than we need, but I'd rather it was that way round than be short of things. And you never know exactly what the weather's going to be like, so you've got to cover every eventuality. Have you still got that list you downloaded from the internet so that we don't forget anything? It's saved on my laptop. Do you want to look at it now?"},{"s":445.53,"e":446.33,"t":"Why not?"},{"s":446.81,"e":450.49,"t":"I love planning everything way ahead of time. It's part of the fun."}]},{"n":24,"title":"Two sociologists, Nina Havers and Dan Anandes, discussing praising children","dur":528.58775,"x":[{"ps":34.07,"en":107.01,"c":"You hear two sociologists, Nina Havers and Dan Anandes, discussing praising children."},{"ps":219.51,"en":282.62,"c":"You hear two friends, Martha and Robert, discussing golf."},{"ps":385.5,"en":451.49,"c":"You hear two friends talking about a summer music festival they have just been to."}],"items":[{"q":"Nina compares praising children to rock climbing because in both activities","qu":"Nina bolalarni maqtashni qoyaga tirmashish bilan solishtiradi, chunki ikkalasida ham","o":["time is needed to get it right.","trust plays an important role.","mistakes can have unwanted consequences."],"ou":["to'g'ri bajarish uchun vaqt kerak","ishonch muhim rol o'ynaydi","xatolar istalmagan oqibatlarga olib kelishi mumkin"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":43.64,"en":66.37,"si":3,"ev":"One false move or word can be disastrous… their confidence in themselves and their instructor could be severely damaged.","uz":"Bitta noto'g'ri harakat yoki so'z halokatli bo'lishi mumkin… ularning o'ziga va murabbiyga ishonchi qattiq shikastlanishi mumkin.","why":"Ikkalasida ham xatolar istalmagan oqibatlarga olib keladi (C). Vaqt (A) — aksincha: \"takes only moments to grasp\".","hl":null},{"q":"What advice does Dan give parents about praising children?","qu":"Dan ota-onalarga bolalarni maqtash haqida qanday maslahat beradi?","o":["Focus on praising effort rather than results.","Explain the reason for giving praise.","Include praising personal qualities."],"ou":["Natijani emas, harakatni maqtashga e'tibor bering.","Nima uchun maqtayotganingizni tushuntiring.","Shaxsiy fazilatlarni ham maqtang."],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":74.49,"en":89.28,"si":7,"ev":"Parents look absentmindedly at their child's painting and just say, \"Wonderful.\" It should always be followed up with \"because…\" For example, it's full of detail.","uz":"Ota-onalar farzandining rasmiga beparvo qarab, shunchaki \"Ajoyib\" deyishadi. Har doim \"chunki…\" bilan davom ettirish kerak — masalan, unda tafsilotlar ko'p.","why":"Maqtash sababini tushuntiring (B).","hl":null},{"q":"Robert had been put off taking up golf until now because he believed","qu":"Robert hozirgacha golf bilan shug'ullanishdan qochib kelgan, chunki u ... deb o'ylagan","o":["it was practised only by a privileged few.","it provided relatively little exercise.","it was perceived as old-fashioned."],"ou":["u bilan faqat imtiyozli ozchilik shug'ullanadi","u nisbatan kam jismoniy mashq beradi","u eskicha deb qabul qilinadi"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":236.89,"en":249.05,"si":16,"ev":"But I'd always thought of golf as kind of dated, you know? Not cool.","uz":"Lekin men doim golfni eskicha deb o'ylardim. Zamonaviy emas.","why":"Eskicha deb qabul qilinadi (C). Mashq (B) — aksincha, \"it gives you a good workout\".","hl":null},{"q":"What do they agree they should do next?","qu":"Ular keyin nima qilish kerakligida kelishadi?","o":["take up an opportunity to find out about a venue","get more information about golf from a colleague","look into the expense involved in playing golf"],"ou":["bir maydon haqida bilib olish imkoniyatidan foydalanish","hamkasbidan golf haqida ko'proq ma'lumot olish","golf o'ynash xarajatlarini o'rganib chiqish"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":273.18,"en":282.62,"si":22,"ev":"They're having an open day when potential members can go along… We could check it out then. Interested? — You bet.","uz":"Ular bo'lajak a'zolar uchun ochiq eshiklar kuni o'tkazishmoqda… O'shanda borib ko'rsak bo'ladi. Qiziqasanmi? — Albatta.","why":"Maydon haqida bilib olish imkoniyatidan foydalanish (A). Hamkasbdan so'rash (B) — faqat Robertning fikri.","hl":null},{"q":"According to the man, what element do music festival organisers often overlook?","qu":"Erkakning fikricha, musiqa festivali tashkilotchilari qaysi jihatni ko'pincha e'tibordan chetda qoldiradi?","o":["having good communication between sound engineers and bands","designing the grounds so that the sound is enhanced","ensuring all the equipment is of the highest quality"],"ou":["ovoz muhandislari va guruhlar o'rtasidagi yaxshi aloqa","ovoz yaxshilanishi uchun maydonni loyihalash","barcha jihozlar eng yuqori sifatda bo'lishini ta'minlash"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":408.7,"en":419.52,"si":25,"ev":"What I noticed was the layout of the whole area. That had been landscaped to get the best acoustics. The importance of that often seems to be ignored.","uz":"Men e'tibor bergan narsa — butun hududning joylashuvi. U eng yaxshi akustika uchun landshaftlashtirilgan edi. Buning ahamiyati ko'pincha e'tiborsiz qoldiriladi.","why":"Ovozni yaxshilash uchun maydonni loyihalash (B). Eng yaxshi jihozlar (C) — \"that's a given\".","hl":null},{"q":"How did the woman first find out that a local band was good?","qu":"Ayol mahalliy guruh yaxshi ekanini birinchi marta qanday bildi?","o":["Other musicians were recommending them.","Everyone was talking about them in one of the cafés.","The number of people listening to them was increasing."],"ou":["Boshqa musiqachilar ularni tavsiya qilishardi.","Kafelardan birida hamma ular haqida gapirardi.","Ularni tinglayotganlar soni ortib borardi."],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":420.06,"en":445.47,"si":28,"ev":"I only realised they were worth seeing when I went to the stage where they were playing and a huge crowd was gathering.","uz":"Ular ko'rishga arziydigan guruh ekanini faqat sahnaga borib, katta olomon to'planayotganini ko'rganimda angladim.","why":"Tinglovchilar soni ortib borayotgani (C). Kafedagi suhbat (B) — faqat ular haqida birinchi eshitgan joyi.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":34.07,"e":34.07,"t":"Extract One — You hear two sociologists, Nina Havers and Dan Anandes, discussing praising children."},{"s":34.07,"e":37.5,"t":"My view on giving praise to children is simple."},{"s":37.98,"e":42.97,"t":"approach it in the same way you'd approach rock climbing with great caution."},{"s":43.64,"e":46.65,"t":"One false move or word can be disastrous."},{"s":47.19,"e":52.48,"t":"A child may get the wrong message if you say, for example, that poor homework is wonderful."},{"s":52.98,"e":66.37,"t":"And as for a rock climber, well, if they are led to believe that they are accomplished sports people when they aren't, they may find themselves in difficulty and their confidence in themselves and their instructor could be severely damaged."},{"s":66.9,"e":73.89,"t":"However, unlike rock climbing, how to praise a child in an effective way takes only moments to grasp."},{"s":74.49,"e":86.91,"t":"I agree. And you hear so much what I call empty praise. When parents look absentmindedly at their child's painting and just say, \"Wonderful, it should always be followed up with because...\""},{"s":87.42,"e":89.28,"t":"For example, it's full of detail."},{"s":89.88,"e":98.81,"t":"Children have very different personalities, but I found this sort of praise is always effective, no matter whether the child is naturally self-assured or not."},{"s":99.42,"e":107.01,"t":"And when children have really worked hard at something, it's up to adults to make the praise meaningful. That's very true."},{"k":"h","s":219.51,"e":219.51,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two friends, Martha and Robert, discussing golf."},{"s":219.51,"e":224.89,"t":"Robert are you still thinking about taking up golf? Hi Martha. Yes"},{"s":225.37,"e":228.48,"t":"And the more I think about it, the keener I am on the idea."},{"s":228.98,"e":230.94,"t":"I know it gives you a good workout."},{"s":231.42,"e":236.13,"t":"And I really need that, 'cause in my job I sit in front of a screen all day long."},{"s":236.89,"e":241.34,"t":"But I'd always thought of golf as kind of dated, you know? Not cool."},{"s":242.01,"e":249.05,"t":"My uncle used to play at a very exclusive golf club and had to wear what I thought were ridiculous clothes to play in."},{"s":249.59,"e":256.86,"t":"Perhaps that's where I got my prejudiced ideas from. Probably. Well, I'm up for it if you are."},{"s":257.3,"e":263.13,"t":"I don't have a lot of extra cash to splash out though. You wouldn't need to if we joined the City Golf Club."},{"s":263.96,"e":267.84,"t":"I know what you mean though. Some private golf clubs can be pricey."},{"s":268.57,"e":272.41,"t":"I'll ask a guy I know at work about the city club. He's a golfer."},{"s":273.18,"e":282.62,"t":"Actually they're having an open day when potential members can go along. I saw a poster somewhere. We could check it out then. Interested? You bet."},{"k":"h","s":385.5,"e":385.5,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two friends talking about a summer music festival they have just been to."},{"s":385.5,"e":408.22,"t":"That was the best festival ever! I mean the line up of bands was awesome, sure, but it was the organisation as well that was first class. I've never been to a festival where the sound was so good. Do you think it was because they'd invested in the best sound system? I think that's a given at a music festival. Well, the best they can afford."},{"s":408.7,"e":411.58,"t":"What I noticed was the layout of the whole area."},{"s":412.12,"e":414.91,"t":"That had been landscaped to get the best acoustics."},{"s":415.45,"e":419.52,"t":"The importance of that often seems to be ignored or perhaps forgotten."},{"s":420.06,"e":445.47,"t":"I also liked the way the sound engineers checked everything and wouldn't let the band start until they were happy that everything was okay. That local band held their own against some big international names. Yeah, I didn't know anything about them until I heard someone chatting about them while I was getting coffee. And I only realised they were worth seeing when I went to the stage where they were playing and a huge crowd was gathering."},{"s":445.78,"e":451.49,"t":"I was so pleased for them, especially when one of the big names later said how great they were."}]},{"n":25,"title":"Two friends, Jeanette and David, talking about playing the guitar","dur":555.102,"x":[{"ps":31.74,"en":100.38,"c":"You hear two friends, Jeanette and David, talking about playing the guitar."},{"ps":211.83,"en":284.45,"c":"You hear two engineers who work in the same company talking on the radio about new technology and roads."},{"ps":396.66,"en":470.56,"c":"You hear two sociologists talking about disagreeing."}],"items":[{"q":"What does Jeanette say about being motivated to practise playing the guitar?","qu":"Jeanette gitara chalishni mashq qilishga motivatsiya haqida nima deydi?","o":["Not wanting to practise sometimes is normal.","Studying how to increase motivation is a waste of time.","There is no link between feeling motivated and musical ability."],"ou":["Ba'zan mashq qilgisi kelmasligi normal holat.","Motivatsiyani oshirish yo'llarini o'rganish vaqtni behuda sarflash.","Motivatsiya va musiqiy qobiliyat o'rtasida bog'liqlik yo'q."],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":51.93,"en":67.13,"si":4,"ev":"I looked up on the internet what to do to spur myself into action… But after a few futile hours browsing, I realised just reading about it wasn't the solution.","uz":"Internetdan o'zimni harakatga undash yo'llarini qidirdim… Lekin bir necha soat behuda qidirgandan keyin, faqat o'qishning o'zi yechim emasligini angladim.","why":"Motivatsiyani o'rganish vaqtni behuda sarflash (B). A — u yaxshi-yomon kunlari borligini aytadi, lekin buni \"normal\" deb xulosa qilmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"Why did David take up playing the guitar as a hobby?","qu":"David nega gitara chalishni sevimli mashg'ulot qilib oldi?","o":["to improve his maths skills","to feel less stressed about his college course","to be able to concentrate for longer"],"ou":["matematika ko'nikmalarini yaxshilash uchun","kollejdagi o'qishi tufayli stressni kamaytirish uchun","uzoqroq diqqatini jamlay olish uchun"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":75.51,"en":90.49,"si":7,"ev":"I was finding it hard to keep focused when I was doing these really long calculations, and I heard that learning a musical instrument can help with that.","uz":"Juda uzun hisob-kitoblarni qilayotganda diqqatimni jamlash qiyin edi, cholg'u chalishni o'rganish bunga yordam berishini eshitdim.","why":"Uzoqroq diqqatni jamlay olish uchun (C). Stress (B) — sinfdoshlari haqida.","hl":null},{"q":"At the moment, the man is working on new technology for","qu":"Hozir erkak ... uchun yangi texnologiya ustida ishlayapti","o":["road markings.","electric lights on roads.","a special type of road surface."],"ou":["yo'l chiziqlari","yo'llardagi elektr chiroqlar","maxsus turdagi yo'l qoplamasi"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":234.17,"en":243.07,"si":15,"ev":"I'm involved with harnessing the wind that cars generate as they go along. This can be used to generate the required electricity for street lamps.","uz":"Men mashinalar harakatlanganda hosil qiladigan shamoldan foydalanish ustida ishlayapman. U ko'cha chiroqlari uchun elektr ishlab chiqarishda ishlatilishi mumkin.","why":"Yo'llardagi elektr chiroqlar (B). Yo'l chiziqlari (A) — boshqa bo'lim ishi.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the woman doing when she talks about roads made of glass?","qu":"Shishadan qilingan yo'llar haqida gapirganda ayol nima qilyapti?","o":["reassuring listeners that these roads are safe","clarifying what the man said about these roads","outlining a potential problem with these roads"],"ou":["tinglovchilarni bu yo'llar xavfsiz ekaniga ishontiryapti","erkakning bu yo'llar haqidagi gapini aniqlashtiryapti","bu yo'llardagi ehtimoliy muammoni bayon qilyapti"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":260.95,"en":275.07,"si":19,"ev":"Roads made of glass. But don't worry, they won't be slippery. Drivers can still stop quickly.","uz":"Shishadan yasalgan yo'llar. Lekin xavotir olmang, ular sirpanchiq bo'lmaydi. Haydovchilar baribir tez to'xtay oladi.","why":"Tinglovchilarni bu yo'llar xavfsiz ekaniga ishontiryapti (A).","hl":null},{"q":"Why does the woman think disagreeing is a complex topic?","qu":"Ayol nega kelishmovchilikni murakkab mavzu deb hisoblaydi?","o":["People can feel a range of emotions when others disagree with them.","People express disagreement differently depending on their age.","People's reactions to disagreeing depend on their culture."],"ou":["Boshqalar ular bilan kelishmaganda odamlar turli his-tuyg'ularni boshdan kechirishi mumkin.","Odamlar yoshiga qarab norozilikni turlicha bildiradi.","Odamlarning kelishmovchilikka munosabati madaniyatiga bog'liq."],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":417.24,"en":428.64,"si":23,"ev":"What makes it tricky is that disagreeing stirs up feelings from anger to embarrassment.","uz":"Uni murakkab qiladigan narsa — kelishmovchilik g'azabdan tortib xijolatgacha turli his-tuyg'ularni qo'zg'atadi.","why":"Odamlar turli his-tuyg'ularni boshdan kechiradi (A). Yosh va madaniyat (B, C) — \"that's all quite straightforward\".","hl":null},{"q":"What did the man do when a colleague disagreed with him?","qu":"Hamkasbi u bilan kelishmaganda erkak nima qildi?","o":["asked questions to try to understand the reasons","repeated his opinion politely","attempted to change the subject"],"ou":["sabablarini tushunish uchun savollar berdi","fikrini xushmuomalalik bilan takrorladi","mavzuni o'zgartirishga urindi"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":448.18,"en":470.56,"si":27,"ev":"I almost immediately started steering the conversation to something else… I just kept redirecting the conversation.","uz":"Deyarli darhol suhbatni boshqa mavzuga bura boshladim… Suhbatni boshqa tomonga burib turdim.","why":"Mavzuni o'zgartirishga urindi (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":31.74,"e":31.74,"t":"Extract One — You hear two friends, Jeanette and David, talking about playing the guitar."},{"s":31.74,"e":43.36,"t":"Hi Jeanette, how's your guitar practice going? Hi David! Well, I only started learning to play the guitar about six months ago and I am making progress, although it doesn't always feel like that."},{"s":43.8,"e":45.57,"t":"I have good days and bad days."},{"s":46.65,"e":50.97,"t":"wonder if great famous guitarists have the same problem getting motivated some days."},{"s":51.93,"e":60.54,"t":"My mum keeps telling me to practice more, so I looked up on the internet what to do to spur myself into action, and yes, there's loads of suggestions."},{"s":61.18,"e":67.13,"t":"But after a few futile hours browsing, I realised just reading about it wasn't the solution."},{"s":68.44,"e":75.07,"t":"Still, I really think playing the guitar is a great past time, and it's certainly doing what I hoped it would for me."},{"s":75.51,"e":90.49,"t":"On my college course we were getting into some really complex work. Oh yeah, you're doing maths, right? And I was finding it hard to keep focused when I was doing these really long calculations, and I heard that learning a musical instrument can help with that."},{"s":91.29,"e":97.37,"t":"Does it? Without a doubt. Some of my classmates were getting a bit anxious about college work."},{"s":97.94,"e":100.38,"t":"and I've recommended learning an instrument to them."},{"k":"h","s":211.83,"e":211.83,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two engineers who work in the same company talking on the radio about new technology and roads."},{"s":211.83,"e":216.61,"t":"Our company is working on some exciting new initiatives, all connected with roads."},{"s":217.24,"e":224.96,"t":"For example, making a road surface that contains magnets so that electric cars can be charged as they're driven along the road."},{"s":225.72,"e":231.58,"t":"This means electric car drivers won't have to stop and recharge their cars on long journeys."},{"s":232.6,"e":233.53,"t":"Definitely!"},{"s":234.17,"e":238.46,"t":"I'm involved with harnessing the wind that cars generate as they go along."},{"s":239.13,"e":243.07,"t":"This can be used to generate the required electricity for street lamps."},{"s":243.7,"e":254.01,"t":"A different department is looking at painting road markings with special paint that gets energy from the sun during the day and then the road markings light up at night."},{"s":255.1,"e":260.51,"t":"We've been having some problems with getting the paint to shine to the same brightness along all the roads."},{"s":260.95,"e":275.07,"t":"But what interests me is that we can even put solar panels on roads. Yes, roads made of glass. But don't worry, they won't be slippery. Drivers can still stop quickly, even when traveling at around 125 kilometers an hour."},{"s":275.64,"e":284.45,"t":"These glass roads would also be perfect for countries with cold climates as they can be used to melt snow and ice. That would be a real bonus."},{"k":"h","s":396.66,"e":396.66,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two sociologists talking about disagreeing."},{"s":396.66,"e":416.7,"t":"We teach sociology and this week I've been talking about disagreeing. It's fascinating because I have students from all corners of the world in my classes and we've had some in-depth discussions about who you can express disagreement with and when, you know, what to do if you're talking to someone older than you, for example."},{"s":417.24,"e":428.64,"t":"And actually, that's all quite straightforward. Societies have rules for that. But what makes it tricky is that disagreeing stirs up feelings from anger to embarrassment."},{"s":429.11,"e":437.31,"t":"I think you've hit the nail on the head there. Like you, as a sociologist, I've thought about disagreeing from an academic perspective."},{"s":438.07,"e":443.04,"t":"Interestingly though, when someone at work disagreed with my proposal to introduce flexi-time,"},{"s":443.58,"e":447.52,"t":"I realize there's a great difference between theory and practice."},{"s":448.18,"e":470.56,"t":"I almost immediately started steering the conversation to something else. I didn't do it in a rude way. I just kept redirecting the conversation. Afterwards, I had no idea why I'd done that because I'm sure my colleague and I could have discussed it and come to a practical solution. You were probably worried about being in an awkward situation with a colleague. You're right."}]},{"n":26,"title":"Two friends Lizzie and Raphael talking about playing the keyboard and the drums","dur":487.941188,"x":[{"ps":32.89,"en":96.93,"c":"you hear two friends Lizzie and Raphael talking about playing the keyboard and the drums."},{"ps":199.32,"en":257.28,"c":"You hear two colleagues talking about first impressions."},{"ps":354.68,"en":415.2,"c":"You hear a chef, called Nick, talking to his sister about his work."}],"items":[{"q":"Raphael is thinking of learning the keyboard instead of the drums because","qu":"Raphael baraban o'rniga klavishli cholg'u o'rganishni o'ylayapti, chunki","o":["finding somewhere to practise the keyboard is less problematic.","it's easier to control the volume on a keyboard.","keyboards are much more portable."],"ou":["klavishli cholg'uda mashq qilish uchun joy topish osonroq","klavishli cholg'uda ovoz balandligini boshqarish osonroq","klavishli cholg'ularni olib yurish ancha qulay"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":53.94,"en":66.14,"si":2,"ev":"On keyboards and on an electronic drum kit, there's a knob to adjust the sound level. But the deciding factor might be that I'd struggle to take drums anywhere. I don't have my own car.","uz":"Klavishli cholg'uda ham, elektron barabanda ham ovozni sozlash tugmasi bor. Lekin hal qiluvchi omil — barabanni biror joyga olib borish qiyin. Mening mashinam yo'q.","why":"Klavishli cholg'uni olib yurish oson (C). Ovoz (B) — ikkalasida ham boshqariladi.","hl":null},{"q":"What's Lizzie doing?","qu":"Lizzie nima qilyapti?","o":["trying to persuade Raphael to make up his mind","questioning whether he has made the right decision","suggesting he takes more time to choose which instrument to play"],"ou":["Raphaelni qaror qabul qilishga ko'ndirmoqchi","u to'g'ri qaror qilganiga shubha bildiryapti","qaysi cholg'uni tanlashga ko'proq vaqt ajratishni taklif qilyapti"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":73.18,"en":96.93,"si":7,"ev":"If you went for the drums, we'd be able to practice together at your place… he'd be happy to give us and our kit a lift. What do you think?","uz":"Agar baraban tanlasang, sizlarnikida birga mashq qila olardik… u bizni jihozlarimiz bilan olib borishga tayyor. Nima deysan?","why":"Lizzie uni qaror qabul qilishga (barabanga) ko'ndirmoqchi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman say about meeting clients for the first time?","qu":"Ayol mijozlar bilan birinchi marta uchrashish haqida nima deydi?","o":["She doesn't feel comfortable wearing formal clothes.","She isn't as open as she usually is.","She tries not to be influenced by the surroundings."],"ou":["Rasmiy kiyimda o'zini noqulay his qiladi.","Odatdagidek ochiq bo'lmaydi.","Atrof-muhit ta'siriga berilmaslikka harakat qiladi."],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":199.32,"en":237.15,"si":10,"ev":"I always feel a bit tense when I meet clients for the first time… I always feel as though I've got to watch what I say, and I end up not being my usual candid self.","uz":"Mijozlar bilan birinchi marta uchrashganda doim biroz hayajonlanaman… Doim gapimni o'ylab gapirishim kerakdek tuyuladi va odatdagidek ochiq bo'lmay qolaman.","why":"Odatdagidek ochiq bo'lmaydi (B). Rasmiy kiyim (A) — \"even when I don't need to put my best business suit on\".","hl":null},{"q":"What do they agree about long-term business relationships?","qu":"Ular uzoq muddatli ish munosabatlari haqida nimada kelishadi?","o":["First impressions can turn out to be right.","Friendship can develop over time.","Promotion can change the way a person behaves."],"ou":["Birinchi taassurot to'g'ri bo'lib chiqishi mumkin.","Vaqt o'tib do'stlik paydo bo'lishi mumkin.","Lavozim ko'tarilishi insonning xulqini o'zgartirishi mumkin."],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":241.05,"en":248.51,"si":13,"ev":"But when she became the chief accountant, she became very distant. — Absolutely, to the point where she was almost unfriendly.","uz":"Lekin bosh hisobchi bo'lgach, u juda uzoqlashib ketdi. — Albatta, deyarli do'stona bo'lmay qoldi.","why":"Lavozim insonning xulqini o'zgartirishi mumkin (C).","hl":null},{"q":"How did Nick feel when he made a dish he used to love as a child?","qu":"Nick bolaligida yaxshi ko'rgan taomni tayyorlaganda qanday his qildi?","o":["disappointed that it was less sweet than he remembered","frustrated that it took a long time to make","embarrassed that it tasted so unpleasant"],"ou":["eslaganidan kamroq shirin bo'lganidan hafsalasi pir bo'ldi","tayyorlash uzoq vaqt olganidan asabiylashdi","ta'mi juda yoqimsiz bo'lganidan xijolat bo'ldi"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":376.31,"en":395.07,"si":22,"ev":"It was heavy, sticky and sickly… I didn't even dare tell the other chefs… I just very quietly got rid of it and hoped no one would notice that I'd made something so foul.","uz":"U og'ir, yopishqoq va ko'ngilni aynitadigan edi… Boshqa oshpazlarga aytishga ham jur'at etmadim… Uni jimgina tashlab yubordim va bunday jirkanch narsa qilganimni hech kim sezmasligiga umid qildim.","why":"Ta'mi yoqimsizligidan xijolat (C). Murakkab bo'lgan (B), lekin u uddalagan.","hl":null},{"q":"What aspect of Nick's job is his sister interested in?","qu":"Nickning singlisi (opasi) uning ishining qaysi jihatiga qiziqadi?","o":["how competitive it is","how unpredictable it is","how technical it is"],"ou":["qanchalik raqobatli ekaniga","qanchalik oldindan aytib bo'lmasligiga","qanchalik texnik ekaniga"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":395.51,"en":408.77,"si":26,"ev":"I'm intrigued about that sense of rivalry that seems to go through everything you do at the restaurant.","uz":"Restoranda qiladigan har bir ishingizda sezilib turadigan raqobat hissi meni qiziqtiradi.","why":"Uning ishi qanchalik raqobatli ekani (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":32.89,"e":32.89,"t":"Extract One — you hear two friends Lizzie and Raphael talking about playing the keyboard and the drums."},{"s":32.89,"e":53.47,"t":"So have you come to a decision about taking up the keyboard or the drums? I have and I've bought a great keyboard. I'm still not 100% sure to be honest. We've got a huge garage at home that'd be easy to soundproof so my parents don't think the noise will be a problem whether I go for a keyboard or drums. Are they sure about that?"},{"s":53.94,"e":60.25,"t":"Well, anyway, on keyboards and on an electronic drum kit, there's a knob to adjust the sound level."},{"s":60.7,"e":64.19,"t":"But the deciding factor might be that I'd struggle to take drums anywhere."},{"s":64.86,"e":66.14,"t":"I don't have my own car"},{"s":66.84,"e":68.45,"t":"We're going back to what I was seeing"},{"s":68.89,"e":72.61,"t":"Our garage would make a great rehearsal space for any instrument."},{"s":73.18,"e":81.5,"t":"Why don't you come over to see it? Sounds fantastic! Listen, if you went for the drums, we'd be able to practice together at your place."},{"s":81.94,"e":96.93,"t":"And my brother's got a van, so if we got to the point where we played in a group, he'd be happy to give us and our kit a lift. What do you think? Oh, I don't know. I want to make sure I decide what's best for me, because neither instrument's cheap to buy."},{"k":"h","s":199.32,"e":199.32,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two colleagues talking about first impressions."},{"s":199.32,"e":224.92,"t":"Hi, are you meeting our new Mexican clients next week? Yes, I've booked the main boardroom for the meeting and I'm taking them out to the Clayton restaurant for lunch. Wow, that'll make a great first impression. The atmosphere's perfect for a formal lunch. Yes, I always feel a bit tense when I meet clients for the first time. Even when I don't need to put my best business suit on and I just meet them in my office, you know? A much more informal meeting."},{"s":225.46,"e":237.15,"t":"I always feel as though I've got to watch what I say, and I end up not being my usual candid self. But it's interesting how relationships change over the years. Do you remember Lily Douglas?"},{"s":237.59,"e":240.35,"t":"We all thought she was wonderful when we first met her."},{"s":241.05,"e":244.29,"t":"But when she became the chief accountant, she became very distant."},{"s":244.76,"e":248.51,"t":"Absolutely, to the point where she was almost unfriendly."},{"s":249.24,"e":257.28,"t":"can happen, it just goes to show that there's a very clear line between business relationships and the genuine closeness you get with your friends."},{"k":"h","s":354.68,"e":354.68,"t":"Extract Three — You hear a chef, called Nick, talking to his sister about his work."},{"s":354.68,"e":360.93,"t":"Nick, did you put that chocolate dessert on the menu of your restaurant? The one we often had when we were kids? Oh, yeah."},{"s":361.5,"e":364.61,"t":"We've been talking about that, haven't we? And I thought, why not?"},{"s":365.37,"e":368.35,"t":"I found the recipe and did a trial run to see what it was like."},{"s":369.21,"e":373.02,"t":"The recipe is quite complicated because there are several stages you have to go through."},{"s":373.66,"e":375.68,"t":"But anyway, I managed it. And?"},{"s":376.31,"e":382.24,"t":"Well, the honey flavor came across well, but apart from that, it was heavy, sticky and sickly."},{"s":382.94,"e":384.96,"t":"After a couple of spoonfuls I bend it."},{"s":385.4,"e":388.51,"t":"I didn't even dare tell the other chefs that have been a family favourite."},{"s":389.05,"e":395.07,"t":"I just very quietly got rid of it and hoped no one would notice that I'd made something so foul. Oh no!"},{"s":395.51,"e":408.77,"t":"But it's great that you have a job where you can do that, just decide to try something out. And I think it's funny that you didn't want the others to know about it. I'm intrigued about that sense of rivalry that seems to go through everything you do at the restaurant."},{"s":409.21,"e":415.2,"t":"And I think good chefs need that drive so that they keep experimenting with new techniques and ingredients."}]},{"n":27,"title":"You'll hear part of a radio interview","dur":401.86775,"x":[{"ps":16.76,"en":75.93,"c":"You'll hear part of a radio interview."},{"ps":164.57,"en":214.3,"c":"You will hear two friends talking about a trip one of them went on."},{"ps":293.98,"en":341.66,"c":"You will hear two people talking about digital cameras."}],"items":[{"q":"What does Bob Aldridge do currently?","qu":"Bob Aldridge hozir nima ish qiladi?","o":["He's an executive","He's a politician","He's probably retired"],"ou":["U rahbar (ijrochi direktor)","U siyosatchi","U nafaqaga chiqqan bo'lsa kerak"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":23.48,"en":44.99,"si":2,"ev":"A study by Bob Aldridge, a former British Airways chief executive…","uz":"Bob Aldridge — \"British Airways\"ning sobiq bosh direktori — tadqiqotiga ko'ra…","why":"\"Former\" = sobiq; demak hozir u nafaqada bo'lsa kerak (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What does Bob think about air travel?","qu":"Bob havo qatnovi haqida nima deb o'ylaydi?","o":["It can be justified but travellers should pay more tax","Airports are big enough to cope with the number of air travellers","Rail travel could eventually replace air travel"],"ou":["Uni oqlash mumkin, lekin yo'lovchilar ko'proq soliq to'lashi kerak","Aeroportlar yo'lovchilar soniga yetarlicha katta","Oxir-oqibat temir yo'l havo qatnovining o'rnini bosishi mumkin"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":58.17,"en":67.49,"si":4,"ev":"Air travellers should pay the full environmental costs of their journey… But I think there is still a case for expanding airport capacity.","uz":"Havo yo'lovchilari safarining to'liq ekologik xarajatlarini to'lashi kerak… Lekin aeroportlar sig'imini kengaytirish uchun hali ham asos bor.","why":"Havo qatnovini oqlash mumkin, lekin yo'lovchilar ko'proq to'lashi kerak (A). Kitob kalitida C berilgan, lekin audio A ni tasdiqlaydi: u yangi tezyurar temir yo'llarga ishonmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman feel about travelling alone?","qu":"Ayol yolg'iz sayohat qilish haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["She gets a thrill out of taking big risks abroad","She believes that positive common sense keeps most out of trouble","She believes that being abroad is bound to be more dangerous than being at home"],"ou":["Chet elda katta tavakkal qilishdan zavq oladi","Sog'lom aql ko'pchilikni muammodan saqlaydi deb hisoblaydi","Chet elda bo'lish uydagidan albatta xavfliroq deb hisoblaydi"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":179.13,"en":205.15,"si":10,"ev":"Plus it seems that believing the best about a place and its people is often the very thing that helps keep you safe.","uz":"Qolaversa, joy va uning odamlari haqida yaxshi o'ylash ko'pincha sizni xavfsiz saqlaydigan narsaning o'zi.","why":"Sog'lom fikrlash ko'pchilikni muammodan saqlaydi (B). Kitob kalitida A berilgan, lekin u tavakkal qilmaganini aytadi: \"I never felt that I was taking any extra risks… I was always extremely careful\".","hl":null},{"q":"When the woman was in Thailand, she","qu":"Ayol Tailandda bo'lganida","o":["thought her life was in danger","was too interested in the coup to be frightened","realised immediately that there was nothing to be afraid of"],"ou":["hayoti xavf ostida deb o'yladi","to'ntarishga shunchalik qiziqdiki, qo'rqmadi ham","qo'rqadigan hech narsa yo'qligini darhol angladi"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":207.58,"en":211.42,"si":12,"ev":"I was fascinated by the whole event so I didn't really have time to freak out.","uz":"Butun voqea meni shunchalik qiziqtirdiki, qo'rqishga vaqtim ham bo'lmadi.","why":"To'ntarishga qiziqqani uchun qo'rqmadi (B). Kitob kalitida C berilgan, lekin u xavfsizlikni faqat ertasi kuni bilgan: \"by the following morning it became clear\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman want a new camera for?","qu":"Ayolga yangi fotoapparat nima uchun kerak?","o":["To take holiday snaps to show her friends and family when she returns","To take photographs to sell as cards in an art gallery","To try to create an original impression of the countries she visits"],"ou":["Qaytganda do'stlari va oilasiga ko'rsatish uchun ta'til suratlarini olish","San'at galereyasida otkritka sifatida sotish uchun suratga olish","Borgan mamlakatlari haqida o'ziga xos taassurot yaratishga urinish"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":310.2,"en":318.21,"si":16,"ev":"It's more important to me that I have images to keep that reflect my own personal experience of the places. I'm not interested in taking typical pretty tourist shots.","uz":"Men uchun muhimi — joylar haqidagi shaxsiy taassurotimni aks ettiradigan suratlar. Odatiy chiroyli turistik suratlar meni qiziqtirmaydi.","why":"O'ziga xos taassurot yaratish (C). Otkritkalar (B) — \"I'm not bothered about creating the greetings cards\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does the man say about digital cameras?","qu":"Erkak raqamli fotoapparatlar haqida nima deydi?","o":["Compact cameras are convenient for the casual photographer","More creative photography demands a film camera","The bigger the camera, the better the quality of picture"],"ou":["Ixcham fotoapparatlar havaskor suratkash uchun qulay","Ijodiyroq suratga olish uchun plyonkali fotoapparat kerak","Fotoapparat qancha katta bo'lsa, surat sifati shuncha yaxshi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":328.09,"en":332.8,"si":19,"ev":"If you just wanted to take snaps, you'd only need one of the smaller size digital cameras.","uz":"Agar shunchaki suratga olmoqchi bo'lsangiz, kichik raqamli fotoapparat kifoya.","why":"Ixcham fotoapparat havaskor uchun qulay (A). Plyonkali kerak emas (B) — \"You don't need a big bulky film camera\".","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":16.76,"e":16.76,"t":"Extract One — You'll hear part of a radio interview."},{"s":16.76,"e":22.88,"t":"Drivers will soon have to pay tolls to use Britain's roads or face sitting in endless traffic jams, it has been claimed."},{"s":23.48,"e":44.99,"t":"A study by Bob Aldridge, a former British Airways chief executive, has suggested that the move would cut congestion in half. Bob, is this true? Yes. Unless steps are taken, Britain will soon grind to a halt, with 13% of traffic reduced to stop-start conditions by 2025, and there will certainly be more overcrowding on trains."},{"s":45.43,"e":57.73,"t":"So are you in favour of road pricing? Yes, good transport has a direct effect on the economy. But money raised in any road pricing scheme must be ploughed back into transport network improvements."},{"s":58.17,"e":63.87,"t":"Air travellers should pay the full environmental costs of their journey to make the industry sustainable."},{"s":64.31,"e":67.49,"t":"But I think there is still a case for expanding airport capacity."},{"s":68.12,"e":75.93,"t":"I don't, however, believe there is much evidence in favour of building new high-speed rail lines. Longer trains would be more cost-efficient."},{"k":"h","s":164.57,"e":164.57,"t":"Extract Two — You will hear two friends talking about a trip one of them went on."},{"s":164.57,"e":171.81,"t":"Don't you worry about travelling on your own abroad? I lost count of the number of people who told me it was dangerous for a woman to be travelling on her own."},{"s":172.25,"e":178.59,"t":"As someone whose only experience of crime was being mugged outside my own home in London, I never felt that I was taking any extra risks."},{"s":179.13,"e":205.15,"t":"Then again I was always extremely careful. Plus it seems that believing the best about a place and its people is often the very thing that helps keep you safe. But what about what happened to you in Thailand with the military coup? That must have been terrifying. Well, I know the media showed chaotic scenes with both tourists and locals looking frightened and bewildered. But by the following morning it became clear that the coup had been bloodless and well organized and as coups went..."},{"s":205.34,"e":207.01,"t":"It almost wasn't exciting enough."},{"s":207.58,"e":211.42,"t":"I was fascinated by the whole event so I didn't really have time to freak out."},{"s":211.96,"e":214.3,"t":"You have to go to Thailand. It's a wonderful place."},{"k":"h","s":293.98,"e":293.98,"t":"Extract Three — You will hear two people talking about digital cameras."},{"s":293.98,"e":309.63,"t":"You're the camera expert. What kind of camera should I buy for my trip to Africa? Well, that depends why you're taking photographs. But it's not simply to have something to laugh over in the pub after, and I'm not bothered about creating the greetings cards that I used to do, although I suppose I might show them somewhere one day."},{"s":310.2,"e":318.21,"t":"It's more important to me that I have images to keep that reflect my own personal experience of the places. I'm not interested in taking typical pretty tourist shots."},{"s":318.9,"e":322.4,"t":"Well, you probably need a good quality camera for what you want to do."},{"s":323.03,"e":327.52,"t":"There are so many on the market now, it can be difficult to choose the most appropriate one."},{"s":328.09,"e":332.8,"t":"If you just wanted to take snaps, you'd only need one of the smaller size digital cameras."},{"s":333.27,"e":341.66,"t":"On the other hand, a good digital camera with all the extras will satisfy your requirements. You don't need a big bulky film camera these days to get a professional image."}]},{"n":28,"title":"Two students discussing a part-time design course they're doing","dur":463.777938,"x":[{"ps":28.41,"en":87.2,"c":"You hear two students discussing a part-time design course they're doing."},{"ps":181.3,"en":242.94,"c":"You hear part of an interview with a young man who has been travelling in many remote parts of the world."},{"ps":338.23,"en":397.34,"c":"you hear part of an interview with the lead singer in a rock band."}],"items":[{"q":"What do they like about the course most?","qu":"Ularga kursning qaysi jihati eng ko'p yoqadi?","o":["the way the course is delivered","the teacher's attitude to the students","the content of the sessions"],"ou":["kursning o'tkazilish usuli","o'qituvchining talabalarga munosabati","mashg'ulotlarning mazmuni"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":28.41,"en":55.29,"si":1,"ev":"This mixture of classes with the group and one-to-one sessions online with the tutors… I've come round to thinking it's the real strength of the course. — Undoubtedly.","uz":"Guruh darslari va o'qituvchilar bilan onlayn yakkama-yakka mashg'ulotlarning aralashmasi… bu kursning asl kuchli tomoni degan fikrga keldim. — Shubhasiz.","why":"Ikkalasiga kursning o'tkazilish usuli yoqadi (A). O'qituvchilar (B) — \"some of the staff are more helpful than others\".","hl":null},{"q":"According to the woman, how could the course be improved?","qu":"Ayolning fikricha, kursni qanday yaxshilash mumkin?","o":["give assignment feedback","allow unlimited access to certain resources","give pre-course information for students"],"ou":["topshiriqlar bo'yicha fikr-mulohaza berish","ayrim manbalardan cheklovsiz foydalanishga ruxsat berish","talabalarga kurs boshlanishidan oldin ma'lumot berish"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":72.12,"en":87.2,"si":3,"ev":"The sessions are the only chance we get to use some of the more sophisticated software… I still think it's a shame we can't come in and use it out of class time.","uz":"Bu mashg'ulotlar murakkabroq dasturlardan foydalanishning yagona imkoniyati… Darsdan tashqari vaqtda kelib undan foydalana olmasligimiz baribir afsuslanarli.","why":"Ayrim manbalardan cheklovsiz foydalanishga ruxsat berish (B). Kursdan oldin ma'lumot (C) — allaqachon berilgan edi.","hl":null},{"q":"What does he say about his luggage?","qu":"U yuki haqida nima deydi?","o":["He hasn't found the perfect bag yet.","He's learnt to leave out unnecessary pieces of equipment.","He's become very good at packing the absolute minimum."],"ou":["Hali ideal sumkani topmagan.","Keraksiz jihozlarni olmaslikni o'rgangan.","Eng kerakli minimumni yig'ishda juda usta bo'lib qolgan."],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":201.5,"en":204.96,"si":10,"ev":"I'm still looking for the ideal rucksack, or carry on actually.","uz":"Hali ham ideal ryukzakni, aniqrog'i qo'l yukini qidiryapman.","why":"U hali ideal sumkani topmagan (A). Ko'p narsa olib yuradi (B, C emas).","hl":null},{"q":"When asked what he's learnt from travelling, he says that","qu":"Sayohatdan nima o'rganganini so'rashganda, u ... deydi","o":["he would now like to settle down somewhere.","he realises that his opportunity to travel is quite rare.","he feels bad about living in poor countries."],"ou":["endi biror joyda o'rnashib qolishni xohlashini","sayohat qilish imkoniyati ancha kamyob ekanini anglashini","kambag'al mamlakatlarda yashashdan o'zini yomon his qilishini"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":224.63,"en":241.18,"si":14,"ev":"I've got the opportunity to travel… because I've got folks back home in a wealthy Western culture to pick up the tab if things go wrong… a lot of people you meet don't have that.","uz":"Men sayohat qilish imkoniyatiga egaman… chunki uyda, boy G'arb madaniyatida, ishlar yomon ketsa, xarajatni to'laydigan yaqinlarim bor… siz uchratadigan ko'p odamlarda bu yo'q.","why":"Sayohat qilish imkoniyati kamyob ekanini anglagan (B).","hl":null},{"q":"How does he feel about the criticism of his band's latest album cover?","qu":"U guruhining so'nggi albom muqovasiga bo'lgan tanqid haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["He thinks it's been exaggerated.","He admits it's the reaction he was going for.","He resents the suggestion that the cover was unoriginal."],"ou":["U bo'rttirilgan deb hisoblaydi.","Aynan shunday munosabatni ko'zlaganini tan oladi.","Muqova o'ziga xos emas degan gapdan ranjiydi."],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":344.66,"en":365.02,"si":20,"ev":"We knew it might cause some controversy, but I didn't think it was that outrageous… we got all these irate bloggers going overboard.","uz":"Bu biroz shov-shuv chiqarishini bilardik, lekin uni unchalik dahshatli deb o'ylamagandim… g'azablangan blogerlar haddan oshib ketishdi.","why":"U tanqidni bo'rttirilgan deb hisoblaydi (A). \"Going overboard\" = haddan oshish.","hl":null},{"q":"He thinks much of the criticism was due to","qu":"Uning fikricha, tanqidning ko'p qismi ... tufayli bo'lgan","o":["a lack of respect for his band in the music business.","a foolish comment he made to a journalist.","a misunderstanding of his real intentions."],"ou":["musiqa sohasida guruhiga hurmat yetishmasligi","jurnalistga aytgan ahmoqona gapi","asl niyatining noto'g'ri tushunilishi"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":380.25,"en":394.24,"si":27,"ev":"The problem stemmed from the fact that we were misquoted… It said that I wanted to kill album artwork, which is just so far off the mark.","uz":"Muammo bizning gapimiz noto'g'ri keltirilganidan kelib chiqdi… Yozilishicha, men albom bezagini yo'q qilmoqchi ekanman — bu mutlaqo noto'g'ri.","why":"Asl niyati noto'g'ri tushunilgan (C). Hurmat yetishmasligi (A) — \"I don't think that's what lies behind it\".","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":28.41,"e":28.41,"t":"Extract One — You hear two students discussing a part-time design course they're doing."},{"s":28.41,"e":55.29,"t":"So is the course living up to your expectations? Yes, I have no real issues with it really. I wasn't sure initially whether I'd like the fact that there's this mixture of classes with the group and one-to-one sessions online with the tutors. But actually, I've come round to thinking it's the real strength of the course, don't you agree? Undoubtedly. I mean, that's why I went for it in the first place. It's nice to meet the staff and other students, but it's the personal attention by email that you want."},{"s":55.9,"e":71.52,"t":"Although I must say, some of the staff are more helpful than others. But the group lessons are useful too. Oh yes. Some people complained about the fact that you get face-to-face feedback on project work in them, that it wastes class time. But I have no problem with that."},{"s":72.12,"e":76.64,"t":"But the sessions are the only chance we get to use some of the more sophisticated software."},{"s":77.08,"e":82.01,"t":"I mean, they did make it clear in the pre-course information that we'd only have limited access to that."},{"s":82.46,"e":87.2,"t":"But I still think it's a shame we can't come in and use it out of class time. Yes, I agree."},{"k":"h","s":181.3,"e":181.3,"t":"Extract Two — You hear part of an interview with a young man who has been travelling in many remote parts of the world."},{"s":181.3,"e":183.74,"t":"So basically as a seasoned traveller"},{"s":184.22,"e":194.01,"t":"He must have got packing off to a fine art. I'm not that great at travelling light, simply because anything can and often does happen, and I like to feel fully prepared."},{"s":194.55,"e":200.7,"t":"So I'm a complete sucker for gadgets and gizmos and I have a bag load of stuff that I take with me."},{"s":201.5,"e":204.96,"t":"I'm still looking for the ideal rucksack, or carry on actually."},{"s":205.53,"e":212.22,"t":"And of course I've always got my iPod for those long days on the road when you don't know how long you might be hanging around waiting for transport."},{"s":213.18,"e":220.67,"t":"So what have you learnt from travelling? Well, I guess it's a cliche, but the more you see of other cultures, the more you come to appreciate your own."},{"s":221.18,"e":224.03,"t":"I don't mean that I miss the comforts of home or anything like that."},{"s":224.63,"e":231.36,"t":"More that I've got the opportunity to travel and see the world because I've got forks back home in a wealthy Western culture."},{"s":231.8,"e":233.5,"t":"Pick up the tab if things go wrong."},{"s":234.1,"e":241.18,"t":"I mean, without that, and a lot of people you meet don't have that, would I ever have had the courage to do half the things I've done?"},{"s":242.14,"e":242.94,"t":"I doubt it somehow"},{"k":"h","s":338.23,"e":338.23,"t":"Extract Three — you hear part of an interview with the lead singer in a rock band."},{"s":338.23,"e":344.16,"t":"Now, you've come in for a lot of stick, haven't you, in response to your latest album? Everyone went nuts about the cover."},{"s":344.66,"e":347.87,"t":"We knew it might cause some controversy, but I didn't think it was that outrageous."},{"s":348.47,"e":353.41,"t":"We just had this slogan which read 'No cover art' like the Beatles did the White Album all those years ago."},{"s":353.88,"e":355.42,"t":"The first one with no picture on the cover"},{"s":356.57,"e":365.02,"t":"But, predictably, I guess, we got all these irate bloggers going overboard and dismissing it, and one newspaper included it in a list of the worst album covers ever."},{"s":365.69,"e":367.97,"t":"Actually I reckon it's quite endearing the way it was done"},{"s":368.63,"e":376.45,"t":"But is this because these people don't like the music? Well, there is a certain snobbery out there, and I reckon these are people who don't regard us as cool or whatever."},{"s":376.98,"e":379.2,"t":"But I don't think that's what lies behind it actually."},{"s":380.25,"e":385.44,"t":"I reckon the problem stemmed from the fact that we were misquoted in the first piece written about it."},{"s":386.23,"e":390.69,"t":"It said that I wanted to kill album artwork, which is just so far off the mark."},{"s":391.38,"e":394.24,"t":"What we actually wanted to do was draw people's attention to it."},{"s":394.81,"e":397.34,"t":"for them to have a look round and see that it's mostly rubbish."}]},{"n":29,"title":"Part of a radio program about a famous London hotel","dur":531.800813,"x":[{"ps":33.21,"en":104.77,"c":"You hear part of a radio program about a famous London hotel."},{"ps":219.38,"en":281.5,"c":"You hear two presenters talking on a science programme."},{"ps":387.83,"en":452.32,"c":"You hear two people talking about popular music."}],"items":[{"q":"In the beginning, the presenter tries to","qu":"Boshida boshlovchi ... ga harakat qiladi","o":["dispel a common misconception about the hotel.","briefly describe what the hotel is like.","make the hotel sound attractive."],"ou":["mehmonxona haqidagi keng tarqalgan noto'g'ri tasavvurni yo'qotish","mehmonxona qandayligini qisqacha tasvirlash","mehmonxonani jozibali qilib ko'rsatish"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":33.21,"en":71.68,"si":1,"ev":"The tea at the Grand Hotel in London is served in the green room, a light airy space… There are four sittings for tea… There are 12 types of tea on offer.","uz":"Londondagi \"Grand\" mehmonxonasida choy yashil zalda — yorug', keng xonada beriladi… Choy to'rt mahal tortiladi… 12 xil choy taklif etiladi.","why":"Boshlovchi mehmonxona qandayligini qisqacha tasvirlaydi (B) — faktlar bilan, reklama qilmasdan.","hl":null},{"q":"How does the manager approach hotel visitors?","qu":"Menejer mehmonxona mehmonlariga qanday yondashadi?","o":["He would rather have fewer rich people attending.","He treats everyone equally well.","He has an eye for what kind of visitor is in front of him."],"ou":["Boy mehmonlar kamroq bo'lishini afzal ko'radi.","Hammaga birdek yaxshi munosabatda bo'ladi.","Qarshisida qanday mehmon turganini darrov ilg'aydi."],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":80.92,"en":99.39,"si":10,"ev":"I can tell as soon as someone walks in what type of person they are, where they are from, why they are here.","uz":"Kimdir kirib kelishi bilanoq uning qanday odam ekani, qayerdan va nima uchun kelganini bilaman.","why":"U qarshisida qanday mehmon turganini darrov ilg'aydi (C). Hammaga bir xil emas (B) — tejab kelganlarga alohida e'tibor beradi.","hl":null},{"q":"The man states that the data produced as a result of the research established","qu":"Erkakning aytishicha, tadqiqot natijasida olingan ma'lumotlar ... ni aniqladi","o":["how much time it took to find the teaspoons.","how long it took for teaspoons to disappear.","the place where lost teaspoons were found."],"ou":["choy qoshiqlarini topish qancha vaqt olganini","choy qoshiqlari qancha vaqtda yo'qolishini","yo'qolgan choy qoshiqlari topilgan joyni"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":249.53,"en":265.5,"si":17,"ev":"It was calculated that they had a half-life, that is, the length of time it took for half of the teaspoons to disappear, of 81 days.","uz":"Ularning \"yarim yemirilish davri\" — ya'ni qoshiqlarning yarmi yo'qolishi uchun ketgan vaqt — 81 kun ekani hisoblandi.","why":"Qoshiqlar qancha vaqtda yo'qolishi aniqlandi (B). Ular qayerga ketgani (C) — noma'lum.","hl":null},{"q":"The woman believes that the topic of this research","qu":"Ayolning fikricha, bu tadqiqot mavzusi","o":["led to new interesting discoveries.","touches upon a problematic matter.","is not particularly interesting."],"ou":["yangi qiziqarli kashfiyotlarga olib keldi","muammoli masalaga daxl qiladi","unchalik qiziq emas"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":219.38,"en":226.72,"si":13,"ev":"Possibly one of the most talked about pieces of research recently published has surprisingly little to do with anything of particular importance.","uz":"Yaqinda chop etilgan eng ko'p muhokama qilingan tadqiqotlardan biri ajablanarli darajada hech qanday muhim narsaga aloqasi yo'q.","why":"Mavzu unchalik qiziq (muhim) emas (C).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman believes that","qu":"Ayolning fikricha","o":["it is challenging to come up with something original nowadays.","modern pop songs are inferior to older ones.","pop music is a poor imitation of other music genres."],"ou":["hozirgi kunda biror o'ziga xos narsa o'ylab topish qiyin","zamonaviy pop qo'shiqlar eskilaridan past","pop musiqa boshqa janrlarning sayoz taqlidi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":387.83,"en":440.44,"si":21,"ev":"Most of the innovations that took place in it had happened by the end of the 1970s and after that it's all been copies… it's all been done before.","uz":"Undagi yangiliklarning aksariyati 1970-yillar oxirigacha sodir bo'lgan, keyin hammasi takrorlash… hammasi avval qilingan.","why":"Hozir o'ziga xos narsa yaratish qiyin (A). U yangi musiqani yomon demaydi: \"they sometimes do that very well\" (B emas).","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman say about modern performers?","qu":"Ayol zamonaviy ijrochilar haqida nima deydi?","o":["They ignore the older audience.","They are using their fans to make money.","They imitate older performers without even noticing it."],"ou":["Ular kattaroq yoshdagi tinglovchilarni e'tiborsiz qoldiradi.","Ular muxlislaridan pul ishlash uchun foydalanadi.","Ular o'zlari sezmagan holda eski ijrochilarga taqlid qiladi."],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":441.27,"en":452.32,"si":23,"ev":"Influences pass from one generation to another and it's not always a conscious thing.","uz":"Ta'sirlar avloddan avlodga o'tadi va bu har doim ham ongli ravishda bo'lmaydi.","why":"Zamonaviy ijrochilar o'zlari sezmagan holda taqlid qiladi (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":33.21,"e":33.21,"t":"Extract One — You hear part of a radio program about a famous London hotel."},{"s":33.21,"e":43.07,"t":"The tea at the Grand Hotel in London is served in the green room, a light airy space with luxuriant plants, fountains, and a panoramic view over the city."},{"s":43.8,"e":45.85,"t":"Dress is strictly smart casual."},{"s":46.46,"e":48.19,"t":"There are four sittings for tea."},{"s":48.66,"e":53.47,"t":"the first at 1130 in the morning and the last at 630 in the evening."},{"s":54.26,"e":58.53,"t":"Despite the high price tag, tables are booked up months in advance."},{"s":59.06,"e":65.28,"t":"He includes a selection of sandwiches, crustless of course, scones, cakes and pastries."},{"s":65.91,"e":71.68,"t":"There are 12 types of tea on offer, including the Grand's own Superior Afternoon Brew."},{"s":72.34,"e":75.84,"t":"David James has been manager of the Green Room for 15 years."},{"s":76.44,"e":80.41,"t":"David, Tea at the Ground is very popular, isn't it? Yes, indeed."},{"s":80.92,"e":99.39,"t":"When I first started, we had 80 to 100 people a day. Now it's twice that number. And are they all wealthy people? Not at all. I can tell as soon as someone walks in what type of person they are, where they are from, why they are here. Some people who come here have lots of money and some don't."},{"s":99.93,"e":104.77,"t":"someone has saved to come here as a treat, I like to make a special effort to make them feel comfortable."},{"k":"h","s":219.38,"e":219.38,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two presenters talking on a science programme."},{"s":219.38,"e":226.72,"t":"Possibly one of the most talked about pieces of research recently published has surprisingly little to do with anything of particular importance."},{"s":227.26,"e":242.72,"t":"Entitled 'The Case of the Disappearing Teaspoons', the study proves that this is a naturally occurring phenomenon with no apparent explanation. Yes, a research team in Australia placed 70 numbered teaspoons in various tea rooms at their institute."},{"s":243.16,"e":245.98,"t":"and tracked them over a period of five months."},{"s":246.55,"e":249.02,"t":"80% disappeared for good."},{"s":249.53,"e":265.5,"t":"It was calculated that they had a half-life, that is, the length of time it took for half of the teaspoons to disappear, of 81 days. If this is a global phenomenon, then 600,000 teaspoons are disappearing each year. So, where have they all gone?"},{"s":266.26,"e":272.8,"t":"Practical and mundane explanations include people taking them home or losing them under piles of work."},{"s":273.59,"e":281.5,"t":"However, with such a large quantity of teaspoons being lost each year, many people feel these explanations are simply not sufficient."},{"k":"h","s":387.83,"e":387.83,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people talking about popular music."},{"s":387.83,"e":408.48,"t":"One thing that's quite interesting about popular music is how derivative and imitative it is. You see, most of the innovations that took place in it had happened by the end of the 1970s and after that it's all been copies of what had already been and gone. That's just not true. There's lots of really innovative new music going on now and there always will be."},{"s":408.95,"e":440.44,"t":"Every new generation develops its own styles and sounds that are unique to it. No, they just think that's what they're doing. Actually, they're just recycling old things. Granted, they sometimes do that very well, but it's all been done before. The truth is, it's new for them, but it's not actually new. But the fans, the public, they don't see it that way, do they? No, they buy the music and they go to concerts by the latest successful or fashionable bands and singers and they think..."},{"s":441.27,"e":445.66,"t":"It's only older people like me who spot the similarities with music from the past."},{"s":446.23,"e":452.32,"t":"Like a lot of things, influences pass from one generation to another and it's not always a conscious thing."}]},{"n":30,"title":"Two people talking about reading books aloud for children","dur":498.494688,"x":[{"ps":32.02,"en":85.41,"c":"You hear two people talking about reading books aloud for children."},{"ps":180.15,"en":242.65,"c":"you hear a part of a radio programme."},{"ps":349.85,"en":416.57,"c":"You hear two people on a radio program talking about running."}],"items":[{"q":"The woman states that","qu":"Ayolning aytishicha","o":["her children enjoy the stories read to them.","other parents are likely to read these stories.","more parents should do this reading."],"ou":["farzandlari ularga o'qib berilgan hikoyalarni yaxshi ko'radi","boshqa ota-onalar ham bu hikoyalarni o'qishi ehtimoli bor","ko'proq ota-onalar shunday o'qib berishi kerak"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":75.99,"en":85.41,"si":7,"ev":"And I bet I'm not the only parent who, having turned out the light… sits down on the stairs and reads on to find out what happens next.","uz":"Ishonamanki, chiroqni o'chirib, xayrli tun degandan keyin, zinaga o'tirib, keyin nima bo'lishini bilish uchun o'qishda davom etadigan yagona ota-ona men emasman.","why":"Boshqa ota-onalar ham bu hikoyalarni o'qishi ehtimoli bor (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What similar idea do the posters express?","qu":"Xabar qoldiruvchilar (post yozganlar) qanday o'xshash fikr bildiradi?","o":["how their children react to story reading","personal reasons to do reading","the artistic approach they use when reading"],"ou":["farzandlarining hikoya o'qishga munosabati","o'qib berishning shaxsiy sabablari","o'qiyotganda foydalanadigan badiiy yondashuvi"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":41.59,"en":75.36,"si":3,"ev":"My kids are totally unimpressed… — I always claim that I read aloud to our three children for their benefit… But it is, of course, for me.","uz":"Bolalarim umuman ta'sirlanmaydi… — Men doim uch farzandimizga ular uchun o'qib beraman deyman… Lekin, albatta, bu o'zim uchun.","why":"Ikkalasi ham o'qib berishning shaxsiy sabablarini aytadi (B). Bolalar munosabati (A) — faqat biri tilga oladi.","hl":null},{"q":"The presenter states that some choose to set up a business with a friend because","qu":"Boshlovchining aytishicha, ba'zilar do'sti bilan biznes ochishni tanlaydi, chunki","o":["they have a history of working together fruitfully.","the friend might have skills you don't.","you can be too scared to do it on your own."],"ou":["ular ilgari birga samarali ishlagan","do'stingizda sizda yo'q ko'nikmalar bo'lishi mumkin","buni yolg'iz qilishdan qo'rqishingiz mumkin"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":188.22,"en":205.12,"si":10,"ev":"The reasons for this often aren't purely practical, for example because of complementary skills and experience. It often comes down to fear… a daunting prospect.","uz":"Buning sabablari ko'pincha faqat amaliy emas — masalan, bir-birini to'ldiruvchi ko'nikmalar. Ko'pincha gap qo'rquvda… bu qo'rqinchli istiqbol.","why":"Yolg'iz qilishdan qo'rqish (C). Ko'nikmalar (B) — \"aren't purely practical\".","hl":null},{"q":"What difficulties did Dean have in his partnership?","qu":"Dean sherikchiligida qanday qiyinchiliklarga duch keldi?","o":["He would refuse to take part in an important process.","He was too lazy.","His personality changed over time."],"ou":["U muhim bir jarayonda qatnashishdan bosh tortardi.","U juda dangasa edi.","Vaqt o'tib uning xarakteri o'zgardi."],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":218.65,"en":242.65,"si":16,"ev":"He just wasn't prepared to take responsibility for any decisions at all… I felt as if I was making all the big decisions on my own.","uz":"U hech qanday qarorga mas'uliyat olishga tayyor emas edi… Barcha muhim qarorlarni yolg'iz qabul qilayotgandek edim.","why":"Muhim jarayonda (qaror qabul qilishda) qatnashishdan bosh tortardi (A). Xarakteri o'zgarmagan (C) — \"I'd had no reason to notice that aspect before\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is the occupation of the speakers?","qu":"So'zlovchilarning kasbi nima?","o":["professional athletes","health and fitness specialists","journalists"],"ou":["professional sportchilar","salomatlik va fitnes mutaxassislari","jurnalistlar"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":354.62,"en":372.06,"si":22,"ev":"You're missing out on lots of fitness attributes that could contribute to improving your technique, your running economy… and your injury resistance.","uz":"Siz texnikangiz, yugurish samaradorligi… va jarohatga chidamliligingizni yaxshilashi mumkin bo'lgan ko'plab jismoniy sifatlarni boy beryapsiz.","why":"Ular salomatlik va fitnes mutaxassislari (B) — mashq usullari haqida mutaxassis sifatida gapiradi.","hl":null},{"q":"Both speakers agree that a successful runner should train","qu":"Ikkala so'zlovchi muvaffaqiyatli yuguruvchi ... mashq qilishi kerak degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["a specific group of muscles.","using a personalised, tailor-made method.","change the focus of training from time to time."],"ou":["muayyan mushaklar guruhini","shaxsga moslashtirilgan usul bilan","vaqti-vaqti bilan mashg'ulot yo'nalishini o'zgartirib"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":387.06,"en":408.48,"si":24,"ev":"If running is all you do, some muscle groups get flabby… If you can strengthen the neglected muscles, stretch the tight ones… you'll be on the way to a more balanced body.","uz":"Agar faqat yugursangiz, ba'zi mushaklar bo'shashib qoladi… E'tiborsiz mushaklarni kuchaytirsangiz, tarang mushaklarni cho'zsangiz… tanangiz muvozanatliroq bo'ladi.","why":"Mashg'ulot yo'nalishini o'zgartirib turish (C). Bitta mushaklar guruhi (A) — aksincha.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":32.02,"e":32.02,"t":"Extract One — You hear two people talking about reading books aloud for children."},{"s":32.02,"e":34.97,"t":"I'm a terrible ham when it comes to reading to my kids."},{"s":35.51,"e":40.99,"t":"I like to do all the voices so I look for books with lots of dialogue and different characters."},{"s":41.59,"e":46.08,"t":"My kids are totally unimpressed and probably prefer having their mother read to them."},{"s":46.55,"e":50.65,"t":"She reads in a very soothing voice and she's not trying to act or show off."},{"s":51.35,"e":54.49,"t":"It reminds me of listening to my own mother read when I was a kid."},{"s":55.1,"e":75.36,"t":"Yes, I always claim that I read aloud to our three children for their benefit, that it's good for their educational development to sit and listen last thing at night, that somehow through hearing a story their creative juices will be stirred. But it is, of course, for me. Nothing can beat the delight of disappearing into a new thrilling chapter."},{"s":75.99,"e":85.41,"t":"And I bet I'm not the only parent who, having turned out the light and said goodnight to their grateful offspring, sits down on the stairs and reads on to find out what happens next."},{"k":"h","s":180.15,"e":180.15,"t":"Extract Two — you hear a part of a radio programme."},{"s":180.15,"e":187.49,"t":"Lots of people set up their own businesses, and in many cases they do so in partnership with a friend rather than going it alone."},{"s":188.22,"e":196.64,"t":"The reasons for this often aren't purely practical, for example because of complementary skills and experience. It often comes down to fear."},{"s":197.3,"e":201.37,"t":"Starting and running a business on your own can be a daunting prospect."},{"s":201.85,"e":205.12,"t":"It's no wonder people often prefer to share the burden with a friend."},{"s":205.69,"e":211.77,"t":"It doesn't always go according to plan though, as Dean Ransom discovered when he started a business with a friend."},{"s":212.31,"e":213.47,"t":"What went wrong Dean?"},{"s":213.94,"e":218.08,"t":"Well, I'd known my partner for years and I felt we had a lot in common."},{"s":218.65,"e":226.59,"t":"What I hadn't realized about him was how indecisive he was, but I'd had no reason to notice that aspect of his personality before."},{"s":227.13,"e":230.85,"t":"He just wasn't prepared to take responsibility for any decisions at all."},{"s":231.32,"e":233.63,"t":"He just sat back and expected me to do it all."},{"s":234.2,"e":242.65,"t":"I didn't want to carry that burden alone. I wanted some sense of shared responsibility, but instead I felt as if I was making all the big decisions on my own."},{"k":"h","s":349.85,"e":349.85,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people on a radio program talking about running."},{"s":349.85,"e":353.79,"t":"Some people think there's only one way to become a better runner and that's to run."},{"s":354.62,"e":372.06,"t":"I'd argue that by confining your sessions purely to running, you're missing out on lots of fitness attributes that could contribute to improving your technique, your running economy - that's your ability to run faster without using up more energy - and your injury resistance. Absolutely."},{"s":372.76,"e":386.53,"t":"Running is a perfectly natural activity, but the body was designed to move in all directions, using a variety of muscle groups, not just in a forward direction, using only the lower body, often on unforgiving hard surfaces."},{"s":387.06,"e":395.42,"t":"If running is all you do, some muscle groups get flabby and lazy through underuse, while others become tight and short through overuse."},{"s":396.12,"e":408.48,"t":"If you can strengthen the neglected muscles, stretch the tight ones and make the most heavily used ones more resilient, you'll be on the way to a more balanced body and this will translate into better running."},{"s":409.02,"e":416.57,"t":"And by better, I don't just mean faster, I mean more comfortable, less strained and altogether more enjoyable."}]},{"n":31,"title":"Two people talking","dur":483.186938,"x":[{"ps":32.76,"en":91.74,"c":"You hear two people talking."},{"ps":194.65,"en":236.8,"c":"You hear two people on the radio discussing a letter from a listener."},{"ps":325.08,"en":397.41,"c":"You hear two people talking about jokes and comedy."}],"items":[{"q":"What is the situation?","qu":"Vaziyat qanday?","o":["They let their friend down","They had an argument with their friend","Their opinion of their friend has changed"],"ou":["Ular do'stining ishonchini oqlamadi","Ular do'sti bilan janjallashib qoldi","Ularning do'sti haqidagi fikri o'zgardi"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":64.89,"en":84.83,"si":3,"ev":"The minute we confronted him about this latest dreadful piece of behaviour, he just totally lost it.","uz":"Uning so'nggi dahshatli qilmishi haqida yuziga aytganimiz zahoti u butunlay o'zini yo'qotdi.","why":"Ular do'sti bilan janjallashib qolgan (B). Ular do'stini yo'lda qoldirmagan (A) — aksincha, u ularga yomon munosabatda bo'lgan.","hl":null},{"q":"How do the speakers feel about the situation?","qu":"So'zlovchilar vaziyat haqida qanday his qiladi?","o":["resigned","upset","uncertain"],"ou":["taqdirga tan bergan","xafa","ikkilangan"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":64.89,"en":91.74,"si":3,"ev":"Well, it was inevitable that it would come to this… So that's that. Yeah, let's forget all about it now.","uz":"Bunga kelishi muqarrar edi… Xullas, shu. Ha, endi hammasini unutaylik.","why":"Ular taqdirga tan bergan, xotirjam (A). Xafa emas (B): \"I'm glad to see the back of him\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is the man doing as he speaks?","qu":"Erkak gapirayotganda nima qilyapti?","o":["justifying somebody's hobby","showing concern for somebody's problem","describing a problem in detail"],"ou":["kimningdir sevimli mashg'ulotini oqlayapti","kimningdir muammosiga hamdardlik bildiryapti","muammoni batafsil tasvirlayapti"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":194.65,"en":216.93,"si":6,"ev":"He's a train spotter. He likes looking at trains and reading about them and collecting the numbers… and his friends make fun of him for it. He's worried…","uz":"U poyezd ishqibozi: poyezdlarni tomosha qilish, ular haqida o'qish va raqamlarini yig'ishni yaxshi ko'radi… do'stlari esa uni masxara qilishadi. U xavotirda…","why":"Boshlovchi muammoni batafsil tasvirlayapti (C). U hobbini oqlamaydi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman believes that the author of the letter should","qu":"Ayolning fikricha, xat muallifi ...","o":["face the fact that people can be cruel.","reassess his attitude to certain people.","discuss the situation with his friends."],"ou":["odamlar shafqatsiz bo'lishi mumkinligini tan olishi kerak","ayrim odamlarga munosabatini qayta ko'rib chiqishi kerak","vaziyatni do'stlari bilan muhokama qilishi kerak"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":223.0,"en":236.8,"si":9,"ev":"Perhaps he needs to look at why he wants to be friendly with these people when they make fun of what he's interested in.","uz":"Balki u qiziqishini masxara qiladigan bu odamlar bilan nega do'st bo'lishni xohlashi haqida o'ylab ko'rishi kerakdir.","why":"Ayrim odamlarga munosabatini qayta ko'rib chiqishi kerak (B).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman believes that punchlines","qu":"Ayolning fikricha, latifalarning kulgili yakunlari (punchline)","o":["can be found in jokes that follow a certain structure.","are usually more funny than catchphrases.","are more accessible than inside jokes."],"ou":["ma'lum tuzilishga ega hazillarda uchraydi","odatda mashhur iboralardan kulgiliroq","faqat tanishlar tushunadigan hazillardan ko'ra tushunarliroq"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":335.45,"en":343.74,"si":13,"ev":"Many jokes are written backwards with the punchline, the funny line at the end that gets the laugh, sorted out first.","uz":"Ko'p hazillar teskari yoziladi: kulgi chiqaradigan oxirgi jumla — \"punchline\" birinchi o'ylab topiladi.","why":"Punchline'lar ma'lum tuzilishdagi hazillarda bo'ladi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"The man says that many professional comedians","qu":"Erkakning aytishicha, ko'plab professional komiklar","o":["attempt to create context they can make jokes about.","make events sound more exciting than they really were.","find it difficult to tell made-up experiences from real ones."],"ou":["hazil qilish mumkin bo'lgan vaziyatlarni o'zlari yaratishga urinadi","voqealarni aslidagidan qiziqroq qilib aytadi","to'qilgan voqealarni haqiqiysidan ajratishda qiynaladi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":383.67,"en":397.41,"si":20,"ev":"That's why most comics are outrageous liars. It's also why some comics may even begin to provoke hilarious episodes by deliberately forgetting their wedding anniversaries.","uz":"Shuning uchun ko'p komiklar ashaddiy yolg'onchilar. Shu sababli ba'zilari to'y yilligini ataylab unutib, kulgili vaziyatlarni o'zlari keltirib chiqaradi.","why":"Hazil qilish mumkin bo'lgan vaziyatni o'zlari yaratadi (A). \"Liars\" (B) — bu ham aytiladi, lekin savol \"attempt to create context\" ga mos keladi.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":32.76,"e":32.76,"t":"Extract One — You hear two people talking."},{"s":32.76,"e":58.72,"t":"Well, I suppose it had to happen some time. I mean, however good-natured you are, there's only so much bad behavior you can take. Yeah. I mean, we've known him all these years and we've put up with all sorts of terrible scenes with him. And times when he's been awful to both of us. I'm just amazed neither of us has had the guts to say anything to him before. I'm not sure it was a lack of courage on my part. I think it was more a misplaced sense of loyalty."},{"s":58.97,"e":64.41,"t":"I mean, we go back a long way. I know, but it's hard to come up with many good memories."},{"s":64.89,"e":84.83,"t":"Anyway, I guess it's over now and that's the last we'll see of him. Yeah, his reaction was typical. The minute we confronted him about this latest dreadful piece of behaviour, he just totally lost it. He's obviously never had any idea of the effect he has on people. Even people who were supposed to be his friends. Well, it was inevitable that it would come to this."},{"s":85.37,"e":91.74,"t":"We've said our piece and frankly I'm glad to see the back of him. So that's that. Yeah, let's forget all about it now."},{"k":"h","s":194.65,"e":194.65,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two people on the radio discussing a letter from a listener."},{"s":194.65,"e":211.42,"t":"Okay, we've had a letter here from Paul who says that his friends are into all the latest trendy hobbies and fashions, whereas he really likes trains. He's a train spotter. He likes looking at trains and reading about them and collecting the numbers of ones he's seen, and his friends make fun of him for it."},{"s":211.99,"e":216.93,"t":"He's worried that they'll stop being his friends if he carries on with his hobby. What will you tell him, Esther?"},{"s":218.1,"e":222.17,"t":"Well, we usually end up choosing friends because we have something in common with them."},{"s":223.0,"e":236.8,"t":"Perhaps he needs to look at why he wants to be friendly with these people when they make fun of what he's interested in. I'm sure there are plenty of potential friends out there who share his interest. With them, he could enjoy that interest rather than having it used against him."},{"k":"h","s":325.08,"e":325.08,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people talking about jokes and comedy."},{"s":325.08,"e":329.98,"t":"Well, of course no single theory has yet been able to explain how jokes work."},{"s":330.52,"e":334.69,"t":"Even the great comedians have been stuck for a proper analysis."},{"s":335.45,"e":343.74,"t":"Of course, many jokes are written backwards with the punchline, the funny line at the end that gets the laugh sorted out first."},{"s":344.25,"e":349.82,"t":"However, a line or a phrase doesn't necessarily need a narrative set up to make us laugh."},{"s":350.46,"e":355.77,"t":"Witness comedy shows in which characters get laughs simply from saying catch phrases."},{"s":356.38,"e":360.03,"t":"This is also how an in-joke works among a group of friends."},{"s":360.6,"e":369.66,"t":"Life itself provides the setup and a word or two, sometimes just a knowing look between two people who are in on the joke, provides the punchline."},{"s":370.49,"e":377.28,"t":"Another thing about jokes is that a professional comedian's routine may be based on personal experience."},{"s":377.78,"e":383.04,"t":"but real experience doesn't tend to come conveniently complete with a punch line."},{"s":383.67,"e":386.88,"t":"That's why most comics are outrageous liars."},{"s":387.35,"e":397.41,"t":"It's also why some comics may even begin to provoke hilarious episodes by deliberately forgetting their wedding anniversaries or leaving their children in the supermarket."}]},{"n":32,"title":"Two people on the radio discussing an item in the news","dur":468.3755,"x":[{"ps":29.11,"en":86.91,"c":"You hear two people on the radio discussing an item in the news."},{"ps":186.14,"en":243.23,"c":"You hear two people discussing a meeting they attended."},{"ps":342.49,"en":398.08,"c":"You hear an actress called Marina Kay talking to a photographer."}],"items":[{"q":"What are the people discussing?","qu":"Odamlar nimani muhokama qilyapti?","o":["a fire","floods","an earthquake"],"ou":["yong'in","suv toshqinlari","zilzila"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":47.54,"en":56.93,"si":4,"ev":"A couple of key roads are impassable because of the River Teal breaking its banks.","uz":"Teal daryosi qirg'oqlaridan toshib ketgani sababli bir nechta asosiy yo'llar o'tib bo'lmaydigan holatda.","why":"Suv toshqini (B). Yong'in (A) — tuzoq: \"fire service\" faqat qutqaruv xizmati sifatida aytiladi.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the purpose of the discussion?","qu":"Muhokamaning maqsadi nima?","o":["to prevent listeners from going to the place","to get donations for the people affected by the situation","to provide factual information about the current state of emergency"],"ou":["tinglovchilarni u joyga borishdan qaytarish","vaziyatdan zarar ko'rganlar uchun xayriya yig'ish","hozirgi favqulodda holat haqida aniq ma'lumot berish"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":38.1,"en":61.63,"si":3,"ev":"Many people are still trapped in their homes… There's still considerable uncertainty as to the numbers of people affected.","uz":"Ko'p odamlar hali ham uylarida qamalib qolgan… Zarar ko'rganlar soni hali ham aniq emas.","why":"Favqulodda holat haqida aniq ma'lumot berish (C). Xayriya (B) — \"Not much at the moment\".","hl":null},{"q":"Both speakers agree that","qu":"Ikkala so'zlovchi ... degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["the leaving colleague will cause lower profits for the company.","their colleague's decision to leave came as a surprise","working without the leaving colleague is going to be less enjoyable"],"ou":["ketayotgan hamkasb kompaniya foydasining kamayishiga sabab bo'ladi","hamkasbining ketish qarori kutilmagan bo'ldi","ketayotgan hamkasbsiz ishlash kamroq maroqli bo'ladi"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":209.91,"en":226.01,"si":14,"ev":"He's got such a great sense of humor… He always really brightens the place up. What on earth will we do now to keep ourselves going?","uz":"Uning hazilkashligi ajoyib… U doim muhitni yoritib turadi. Endi o'zimizni qanday qilib ruhlantiramiz?","why":"Ketayotgan hamkasbsiz ishlash kamroq maroqli bo'ladi (C). Kutilmagan bo'ldi (B) — faqat birinchisi uchun; ikkinchisi bilgan edi.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the speakers' attitude towards their work?","qu":"So'zlovchilar o'z ishiga qanday munosabatda?","o":["It lacks variety.","It is too physically taxing.","It can cause emotional strain."],"ou":["Unda xilma-xillik yetishmaydi.","U jismonan juda charchatadi.","U ruhiy zo'riqishga sabab bo'lishi mumkin."],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":237.3,"en":243.23,"si":17,"ev":"Much as I'd like to do something a bit more exciting at times, at least life here is not too demanding.","uz":"Ba'zan qiziqroq ish qilishni qanchalik xohlamay, hech bo'lmasa bu yerda ish unchalik og'ir emas.","why":"Ishda xilma-xillik yetishmaydi (A). Jismonan og'ir emas (B) — \"not too demanding\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is the aim of the man?","qu":"Erkakning maqsadi nima?","o":["to apologise","to convince","to clarify"],"ou":["kechirim so'rash","ishontirish","aniqlashtirish"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":342.49,"en":398.08,"si":19,"ev":"Would you mind if I just quickly took your picture?… You'd look stunning against the backdrop of the marble pillars… Oh, it won't take a moment, I promise.","uz":"Tezgina suratingizni olsam maylimi?… Marmar ustunlar fonida ajoyib ko'rinasiz… Bir lahza ham ketmaydi, va'da beraman.","why":"Fotograf aktrisani ishontirmoqchi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What is the actress's attitude to the conversation?","qu":"Aktrisaning suhbatga munosabati qanday?","o":["embarrassment","surprise","impatience"],"ou":["xijolat","hayrat","sabrsizlik"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":369.59,"en":398.08,"si":20,"ev":"I'm actually in rather a hurry. I've got to be somewhere in half an hour and I'm already behind time… No, look, my driver's beckoning to me.","uz":"Aslida ancha shoshib turibman. Yarim soatdan keyin bir joyda bo'lishim kerak, allaqachon kechikyapman… Yo'q, qarang, haydovchim chaqiryapti.","why":"Aktrisa sabrsizlik bilan javob beradi (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":29.11,"e":29.11,"t":"Extract One — You hear two people on the radio discussing an item in the news."},{"s":29.11,"e":33.28,"t":"So now we're going over to Joanna, who's there, where it's all been happening."},{"s":33.78,"e":37.09,"t":"Joanna, how are the police and other services coping?"},{"s":38.1,"e":46.97,"t":"Well, things are difficult. Many people are still trapped in their homes, unable to escape and hoping that things will not get any worse."},{"s":47.54,"e":56.93,"t":"The fire service has been able to rescue some people from the roofs of their homes, but a couple of key roads are impassable because of the River Teal breaking its banks."},{"s":57.62,"e":61.63,"t":"There's still considerable uncertainty as to the numbers of people affected."},{"s":62.36,"e":67.52,"t":"A number of listeners have contacted us about how to provide financial or other help."},{"s":68.02,"e":69.66,"t":"What can you tell us about that, Jo"},{"s":70.23,"e":76.57,"t":"Not much at the moment, I'm afraid, but I've been assured that something will be in place by the end of the day."},{"s":77.5,"e":86.91,"t":"been asked to emphasise however that although things are dramatic now, the ground should soon dry out if Metopu's predictions of hot weather are accurate."},{"k":"h","s":186.14,"e":186.14,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two people discussing a meeting they attended."},{"s":186.14,"e":199.26,"t":"Well, that was something of a change from the usual boredom of a Friday afternoon meeting, wasn't it? Absolutely. I was dumbfounded when Pete announced his resignation. He'll be a great loss to the company. That's right."},{"s":199.96,"e":205.6,"t":"I knew he was planning to leave, but he'd asked me to keep it under my hat till he made a public announcement."},{"s":206.3,"e":208.83,"t":"He said I was the only person he'd spoken to."},{"s":209.91,"e":217.69,"t":"I'm gonna miss him loads. He's got such a great sense of humor, and he's really good at his job, too. Mmm, I couldn't agree more."},{"s":218.26,"e":226.01,"t":"He always really brightens the place up. What on earth will we do now to keep ourselves going? I'm sure you'll think of something."},{"s":226.78,"e":236.61,"t":"I'll be relying on you. Oh, well, it'll be a challenge. Yes, but don't stress out. I couldn't cope if you decided to leave too. I don't think there's much hope of that."},{"s":237.3,"e":243.23,"t":"Such as I'd like to do something a bit more exciting at times, at least life here is not too demanding."},{"k":"h","s":342.49,"e":342.49,"t":"Extract Three — You hear an actress called Marina Kay talking to a photographer."},{"s":342.49,"e":369.15,"t":"It's Marina Kay, isn't it? What a pleasure to see you. Our paths crossed in Hollywood once, but I don't suppose you remember that. You're here for the premiere of Love in Hawaii, I presume? You're looking beautiful as always. Thank you, you flatter me. But I don't really- I'm sorry, but would you mind if I just quickly took your picture? Nothing formal, but just you as you are now, walking across the Hotel Foyer."},{"s":369.59,"e":377.79,"t":"You'd look stunning against the backdrop of the marble pillars here. We can have this vase of lilies in the foreground. I'm actually in rather a hurry."},{"s":378.52,"e":398.08,"t":"It's got to be somewhere in half an hour and I'm already behind time. Oh, it won't take a moment, I promise. I've got all my equipment here and I can set it up in a flash. If you'll pardon the expression. No, look, my driver's beckoning to me. Call my agent if you want to arrange something for later. I'll give you his card. You can talk terms with him."}]},{"n":33,"title":"A man and a woman discussing a news item about the Oxford English Dictionary","dur":539.428563,"x":[{"ps":29.75,"en":114.81,"c":"You overhear a man and a woman discussing a news item about the Oxford English Dictionary."},{"ps":240.79,"en":298.08,"c":"You hear two people discussing a journey."},{"ps":396.66,"en":461.63,"c":"You hear two people discussing a report."}],"items":[{"q":"What is the new information about the dictionary?","qu":"Lug'at haqidagi yangi ma'lumot nima?","o":["They have discontinued work on the new edition.","The digital version has much higher sales figures.","The printed version might not get released."],"ou":["Yangi nashr ustidagi ish to'xtatilgan.","Raqamli versiyasi ancha ko'p sotilmoqda.","Bosma versiyasi chiqmasligi mumkin."],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":29.75,"en":36.7,"si":1,"ev":"The Oxford English Dictionary may never again be published as a set of books.","uz":"Oksford ingliz tili lug'ati endi hech qachon kitoblar to'plami sifatida nashr etilmasligi mumkin.","why":"Bosma versiyasi chiqmasligi mumkin (C). Ish to'xtatilmagan (A) — hali 10 yillik ish bor.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the woman's opinion of the change?","qu":"Ayol bu o'zgarish haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["it indicates that people lose interest in the language.","it is nothing to worry about.","it means that the books are getting less popular."],"ou":["bu odamlarning tilga qiziqishi yo'qolayotganini ko'rsatadi","bundan xavotirlanishga asos yo'q","bu kitoblarning ommabopligi kamayayotganini anglatadi"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":78.65,"en":110.21,"si":9,"ev":"Someone else said he thought it's better to see the change as a good thing and to celebrate it… — I go along with that.","uz":"Boshqa birov bu o'zgarishni yaxshi narsa sifatida ko'rish va nishonlash kerak, dedi… — Men bunga qo'shilaman.","why":"Ayol fikricha, xavotirlanishga asos yo'q (B). \"Decline of culture\" (A) — radiodagi boshqa odamning fikri.","hl":null},{"q":"What distressed the man most?","qu":"Erkakni eng ko'p nima bezovta qildi?","o":["looking for a parking spot","backing up down a narrow street","finding the right address"],"ou":["mashina qo'yish uchun joy qidirish","tor ko'chada orqaga yurish","to'g'ri manzilni topish"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":268.86,"en":280.03,"si":21,"ev":"The worst thing was when I came to leave. The street turned out to be a dead end… so I had to back all the way out.","uz":"Eng yomoni — ketayotganimda bo'ldi. Ko'cha boshi berk ekan… shuning uchun butun yo'l orqaga yurishimga to'g'ri keldi.","why":"Tor ko'chada orqaga yurish (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What is the woman's reaction to the man's story?","qu":"Ayol erkakning hikoyasiga qanday munosabat bildiradi?","o":["She is angry because he didn't listen to her.","She is sorry she couldn't help him.","She is impressed with the way he managed to deal with the problem."],"ou":["U uning gapiga quloq solmagani uchun jahli chiqqan.","Unga yordam bera olmaganidan afsuslanadi.","Muammoni qanday hal qilganiga qoyil qoladi."],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":280.73,"en":298.08,"si":23,"ev":"Anyway, I really wondered if I was going to be able to make it. — Well, good for you. I hate having to reverse like that.","uz":"Har holda, uddalay olamanmi deb rosa o'yladim. — Barakalla. Men bunaqa orqaga yurishni yomon ko'raman.","why":"U muammoni hal qilganiga qoyil qoladi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"How are the speakers related?","qu":"So'zlovchilar o'rtasida qanday munosabat bor?","o":["They are two colleagues","They are a client and a freelancer","They are a boss and a subordinate"],"ou":["Ular ikki hamkasb","Ular mijoz va frilanser","Ular rahbar va qo'l ostidagi xodim"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":398.49,"en":445.92,"si":26,"ev":"Yes, it was just to talk about that report you did for me… You do what you can on it for the rest of this week and over the weekend.","uz":"Ha, men uchun tayyorlagan hisobotingiz haqida gaplashmoqchi edim… Haftaning qolgan qismida va dam olish kunlari unga qo'lingizdan kelganini qiling.","why":"Rahbar va qo'l ostidagi xodim (C): biri vazifa beradi, ikkinchisi bajaradi.","hl":null},{"q":"According to the woman, what is the problem with the paper?","qu":"Ayolning fikricha, maqoladagi muammo nima?","o":["different kind of work has to be done.","it has been done too quickly.","it has not been proof-read."],"ou":["boshqacha turdagi ish qilinishi kerak","u juda shoshilib qilingan","u tekshirib (korrektura qilib) chiqilmagan"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":414.52,"en":441.44,"si":29,"ev":"The client has now come back to us with some changes to the specs… there do seem to be one or two significant points.","uz":"Mijoz endi texnik talablarga ba'zi o'zgarishlar bilan qaytdi… bir-ikkita muhim jihat borga o'xshaydi.","why":"Endi boshqacha ish qilinishi kerak (A). Shoshilib qilingani (B) — u buni tushunadi va maqtaydi.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":29.75,"e":29.75,"t":"Extract One — You overhear a man and a woman discussing a news item about the Oxford English Dictionary."},{"s":29.75,"e":36.7,"t":"Did you see that article in the paper, saying that the Oxford English Dictionary may never again be published as a set of books?"},{"s":37.62,"e":50.53,"t":"They were saying that since 1989 a large team of lexicographers have been working away on the new edition trying to map what the article called the 'endlessly flowing river of the English language'."},{"s":51.38,"e":53.98,"t":"only about a third of the work's been done so far."},{"s":54.42,"e":58.05,"t":"And it's estimated there's at least 10 years' work still to do."},{"s":59.03,"e":65.15,"t":"I wonder how the researchers felt when they were told their work might never actually appear in its traditional book form."},{"s":65.82,"e":67.29,"t":"I didn't read the article."},{"s":67.77,"e":73.21,"t":"But I heard someone on the radio saying it's a typical reflection of the decline of culture."},{"s":73.72,"e":77.98,"t":"and increasing sloppiness with regard to words, all the usual stuff."},{"s":78.65,"e":84.89,"t":"But then someone else said he thought it's better to see the change as a good thing and to celebrate it."},{"s":85.59,"e":96.35,"t":"He argued that the Oxford English Dictionary had no choice but to be published as a set of heavy and expensive volumes first because no better technology was available."},{"s":97.05,"e":103.04,"t":"Now, at last, we're able to have it in a much more beautiful and accessible form."},{"s":103.64,"e":107.74,"t":"and don't have to put up with old inconveniences like books anymore."},{"s":109.08,"e":110.21,"t":"Go along with that."},{"s":110.81,"e":114.81,"t":"I'm sure there'll be a tendency for lots of other books to go the same way soon."},{"k":"h","s":240.79,"e":240.79,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two people discussing a journey."},{"s":240.79,"e":246.75,"t":"So how did it go then? Was the traffic as dire as you'd expected? Worse if anything."},{"s":247.19,"e":250.08,"t":"but at least it made it easier to find where I had to get to."},{"s":250.65,"e":256.13,"t":"It was off a tiny little side street and I could easily have missed it if I'd been going a bit faster."},{"s":256.57,"e":263.65,"t":"Oh well, at least you saw it. Yeah, but the street was so narrow with cars parked on either side."},{"s":264.18,"e":268.03,"t":"I only just managed to squeeze into a really tight spot at the end."},{"s":268.86,"e":271.13,"t":"The worst thing was when I came to leave."},{"s":271.61,"e":280.03,"t":"The street turned out to be a dead end. There wasn't enough room for a car the size of ours to turn, so I had to back all the way out."},{"s":280.73,"e":298.08,"t":"I wish you'd been there to help guide me. Well, I don't suppose you'd have listened to me if I had been there. I get flustered and you get cross. No, I don't. Anyway, I really wondered if I was going to be able to make it. Well, good for you. I hate having to reverse like that."},{"k":"h","s":396.66,"e":396.66,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people discussing a report."},{"s":396.66,"e":397.89,"t":"You wanted to see me?"},{"s":398.49,"e":403.23,"t":"Yes, it was just to talk about that report you did for me. Was it alright?"},{"s":403.7,"e":408.89,"t":"I didn't have as much time to work through all the issues as I'd have liked. No, I appreciate that."},{"s":409.46,"e":413.57,"t":"It was very good considering the constraints you were under. Thank you."},{"s":414.52,"e":423.1,"t":"So... The thing is, the client has now come back to us with some changes to the specs. Oh, right. Anything major? Well..."},{"s":423.83,"e":427.2,"t":"You're going to have to go away and study the fine print pretty thoroughly."},{"s":427.9,"e":432.51,"t":"I've only skimmed his document as I've been so busy with that university project."},{"s":433.21,"e":441.44,"t":"there do seem to be one or two significant points. So I'll need to start again from scratch. I don't think that'll be necessary."},{"s":442.23,"e":442.85,"t":"Anyway."},{"s":443.38,"e":445.92,"t":"You do what you can on it for the rest of this week."},{"s":446.49,"e":451.13,"t":"and over the weekend and then we can get together again on Monday and check it through carefully."},{"s":452.25,"e":453.18,"t":"Oh, um..."},{"s":453.66,"e":457.37,"t":"If you have any questions about it before then, feel free to email."},{"s":458.17,"e":461.63,"t":"I'll be working from home for the next few days. Oh, OK. Thank you."}]},{"n":34,"title":"A man and a woman talking about a radio series","dur":503.222813,"x":[{"ps":31.67,"en":97.28,"c":"You hear a man and a woman talking about a radio series."},{"ps":203.26,"en":265.82,"c":"You hear two lecturers discussing selecting students for university courses."},{"ps":367.06,"en":428.48,"c":"You hear two people talking about some work they are having done."}],"items":[{"q":"What do the people have different opinions about?","qu":"Odamlar nima haqida turlicha fikrda?","o":["how interesting the programme is","the website design","the choice of the objects in the collection"],"ou":["dastur qanchalik qiziqligi","veb-sayt dizayni","kolleksiyadagi buyumlarning tanlanishi"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":58.71,"en":77.92,"si":8,"ev":"I caught up with what it had been about on the website of the museum… — That's good too, though I'm not so keen on their constantly dancing graphics. — I rather liked those.","uz":"Muzey veb-saytidan nima haqida bo'lganini bilib olardim… — Bu ham yaxshi, lekin doim \"raqsga tushib turadigan\" grafikalari menga yoqmaydi. — Menga esa ancha yoqdi.","why":"Fikrlar veb-sayt dizayni bo'yicha farq qiladi (B). Buyumlar tanlovi (C) — ikkalasi ham maqtaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman like about the programme?","qu":"Ayolga dasturning nimasi yoqadi?","o":["the consistency of quality in the interviews","the fact that it is educational","the way they talk about history"],"ou":["intervyular sifatining doimo bir xil yuqoriligi","uning ma'rifiy ekani","tarix haqida qanday gapirishlari"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":78.46,"en":94.88,"si":11,"ev":"Informative of course, but entertaining as well… But generally, I learnt so much from the programmes.","uz":"Albatta ma'lumotli, lekin qiziqarli ham… Umuman olganda, dasturlardan juda ko'p narsa o'rgandim.","why":"Ayolga dasturning ma'rifiy ekani yoqadi (B). Intervyular sifati (A) — \"some of those were much better than others\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman say about the procedure in her department?","qu":"Ayol o'z bo'limidagi tartib haqida nima deydi?","o":["it could have been more efficient.","it does not necessarily help admit the best students.","going through the application forms is very tedious."],"ou":["u samaraliroq bo'lishi mumkin edi","u eng yaxshi talabalarni qabul qilishga har doim ham yordam bermaydi","ariza shakllarini ko'rib chiqish juda zerikarli"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":203.26,"en":232.35,"si":16,"ev":"We sort all the application forms into two piles… It seems to work pretty well for us, though of course it's quite time consuming.","uz":"Barcha arizalarni ikki qismga ajratamiz… Bu bizda yaxshi ishlaydi, garchi ko'p vaqt olsa ham.","why":"U jarayon samaraliroq bo'lishi mumkin edi deb biladi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"What part of the man's suggestion worries the woman?","qu":"Erkak taklifining qaysi qismi ayolni xavotirga soladi?","o":["if it would be any better than the current approach","if her colleagues would like it","if the procedure would be secure"],"ou":["u hozirgi yondashuvdan yaxshiroq bo'ladimi","hamkasblariga yoqadimi","jarayon xavfsiz bo'ladimi"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":246.46,"en":265.82,"si":20,"ev":"But how could you be sure that the essays were all their own work? — Unless you could somehow make them do it under exam conditions.","uz":"Lekin insholarni o'zlari yozganiga qanday ishonch hosil qilasiz? — Agar ularni imtihon sharoitida yozdirmasangiz.","why":"Jarayon xavfsiz (ishonchli) bo'ladimi — shu tashvishlantiradi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What is the project?","qu":"Loyiha nima?","o":["putting up decorations in a room","building an extension to a house","renovating a room"],"ou":["xonani bezash","uyga qo'shimcha qurish","xonani ta'mirlash"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":367.06,"en":405.08,"si":23,"ev":"They rang me today about the kitchen… they think they'll start work on Thursday… I've still got to empty the old cupboards, take all the curtains down.","uz":"Bugun oshxona bo'yicha qo'ng'iroq qilishdi… ishni payshanba kuni boshlashmoqchi… Hali eski shkaflarni bo'shatishim, pardalarni olishim kerak.","why":"Loyiha — oshxonani ta'mirlash (C).","hl":null},{"q":"Both speakers agree that","qu":"Ikkala so'zlovchi ... degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["they could learn something from this work.","it is a relief that the work will start soon.","the process will cause certain discomfort."],"ou":["bu ishdan nimadir o'rganishlari mumkin","ish tez orada boshlanishi yengillik","jarayon ma'lum noqulaylik tug'diradi"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":405.78,"en":428.48,"si":28,"ev":"We're going to have to eat out while work's in progress anyway. That's a nuisance, isn't it?… — Absolutely.","uz":"Ish davomida baribir tashqarida ovqatlanishga to'g'ri keladi. Bu noqulay, shunday emasmi? — Albatta.","why":"Ikkalasi jarayon noqulaylik tug'dirishiga qo'shiladi (C). Yengillik (B) — biri tezroq boshlanishini xohlaydi, boshqasi emas.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":31.67,"e":31.67,"t":"Extract One — You hear a man and a woman talking about a radio series."},{"s":31.67,"e":33.28,"t":"Here's a good quiz question for you."},{"s":34.1,"e":38.62,"t":"began with a mummy of hornedgetev and a Tanzanian chopping tool"},{"s":39.06,"e":42.37,"t":"and ended with a credit card and a solar-powered lamp."},{"s":43.13,"e":44.25,"t":"I can answer that."},{"s":44.92,"e":49.18,"t":"It was that amazing radio series on the history of the world in a hundred objects."},{"s":49.69,"e":53.73,"t":"I didn't hear all the programmes but I thought those I did catch were fantastic."},{"s":54.33,"e":58.08,"t":"They chose such interesting things to talk about. Yes, didn't they just?"},{"s":58.71,"e":67.71,"t":"I did try to listen to most of the programs, and if I missed one then I caught up with what it had been about on the website of the museum that all the selected objects came from."},{"s":68.41,"e":73.21,"t":"That's good too, though I'm not so keen on their constantly dancing graphics."},{"s":73.98,"e":77.92,"t":"rather liked those. They make it nice and light-hearted, I thought."},{"s":78.46,"e":81.09,"t":"Well, the series wasn't heavy in any way, was it?"},{"s":81.56,"e":84.13,"t":"informative of course, but entertaining as well."},{"s":84.82,"e":94.88,"t":"I thought they interviewed some really interesting people. Actually, I thought some of those were much better than others. But generally, I learnt so much from the programmes. I hope they repeat them soon."},{"s":95.51,"e":97.28,"t":"Yes, they were fun, weren't they?"},{"k":"h","s":203.26,"e":203.26,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two lecturers discussing selecting students for university courses."},{"s":203.26,"e":222.94,"t":"How many applicants do you tend to have for your undergraduate courses? We've got three applicants for every place this year and it's going to be very hard to pick who we should accept. Yeah, we have that problem too. We sort all the application forms into two piles, a \"no's\" and \"maybes.\" Then we invite the \"maybes\" for interview."},{"s":223.45,"e":232.35,"t":"It seems to work pretty well for us, though of course it's quite time consuming. We interviewed too, but it's hard to be confident we're picking the right people."},{"s":233.05,"e":237.12,"t":"Some people really don't show themselves at their best in an interview situation."},{"s":237.66,"e":245.5,"t":"And we wondered whether it might not be better just to set the most promising applicants an essay to write and see how they get along with that."},{"s":246.46,"e":256.35,"t":"It'd surely be better for everyone if we didn't have to spend time on interviews. Yes, I'm sure my colleagues might welcome that. But how could you be sure that the essays were all their own work?"},{"s":256.82,"e":265.82,"t":"unless you could somehow make them do it under exam conditions, of course. I suppose you're right, but I still think it'd be fairer than the system we currently operate."},{"k":"h","s":367.06,"e":367.06,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people talking about some work they are having done."},{"s":367.06,"e":369.37,"t":"They rang me today about the kitchen."},{"s":369.85,"e":374.88,"t":"Someone's going to pop round tomorrow to discuss it and they think they'll start work on Thursday."},{"s":375.45,"e":376.7,"t":"As soon as that?"},{"s":377.3,"e":378.59,"t":"Do you think we'll be ready"},{"s":379.19,"e":405.08,"t":"I've still got to empty the old cupboards, take all the curtains down, all that sort of thing, and I'd like to have done a bit of decorating before they get going. Well, it'd certainly be better to do it before rather than after and risk getting paint on the new surfaces. Perhaps I could ask them to extend the schedule a bit and start next week. No, let's leave things as they are. The sooner they start, the sooner they finish after all."},{"s":405.78,"e":428.48,"t":"And I'm quite looking forward to seeing how they do things. Are you really? I'm going to try to be out most of the time. We're going to have to eat out while work's in progress anyway. That's a nuisance, isn't it? I'm so busy at the moment. I'd really prefer to be spending the evenings quietly at home. Absolutely. Still, it'll be great when all the work's done. I hope so."}]},{"n":35,"title":"A man and a woman discussing an international sports event","dur":533.18525,"x":[{"ps":29.72,"en":104.16,"c":"You hear a man and a woman discussing an international sports event."},{"ps":217.69,"en":284.8,"c":"You hear two students discussing a piece of group coursework they are doing."},{"ps":391.13,"en":455.81,"c":"You hear a man and a woman discussing a film they have recently seen."}],"items":[{"q":"What was the woman's initial reaction to the news of the planned event?","qu":"Rejalashtirilgan tadbir haqidagi xabarga ayolning dastlabki munosabati qanday bo'ldi?","o":["looking forward to attending it","worried about feeling discomfort because of it","happy with the potential benefits it could bring"],"ou":["unda qatnashishni intiqlik bilan kutdi","u sababli noqulaylik sezishidan xavotirlandi","u keltirishi mumkin bo'lgan foydadan xursand bo'ldi"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":59.1,"en":71.9,"si":5,"ev":"But I don't feel sorry it's coming here though. Right from the start I thought it would be really positive for the local economy.","uz":"Lekin uning bu yerga kelayotganidan afsuslanmayman. Boshidanoq bu mahalliy iqtisodiyot uchun juda foydali bo'ladi deb o'ylaganman.","why":"Keltirishi mumkin bo'lgan foydadan xursand (C). U qatnashmaydi (A emas), uyda bo'lmaydi (B emas).","hl":null},{"q":"What is the reason the man is unhappy about the upcoming event?","qu":"Erkak bo'lajak tadbirdan nega norozi?","o":["He believes that it is a very wasteful operation.","He is concerned that the main venue may not get finished on time.","He thinks that the people in charge should be replaced."],"ou":["U buni juda isrofgarchilik deb hisoblaydi.","Asosiy maydon o'z vaqtida qurib bitkazilmasligidan xavotirda.","Mas'ul shaxslarni almashtirish kerak deb hisoblaydi."],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":72.6,"en":104.16,"si":7,"ev":"Now they've run into other problems with the foundations for the new stadium… beginning to feel like a real possibility that it won't be [ready].","uz":"Endi yangi stadion poydevori bilan boshqa muammolar chiqdi… u tayyor bo'lmasligi real ehtimolga aylanmoqda.","why":"Asosiy maydon o'z vaqtida tugamasligidan xavotirda (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What has caused the man most annoyance?","qu":"Erkakni eng ko'p nima jahlini chiqargan?","o":["unclear instructions from the tutor","the fact that the project deadline has been moved","how much help he received from the group"],"ou":["o'qituvchining tushunarsiz ko'rsatmalari","loyiha muddati ko'chirilgani","guruhdan qancha yordam olgani"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":223.61,"en":244.61,"si":14,"ev":"Mark said it'd be easy, and there was no need to start it till Saturday… Then he decided to go away for the weekend, leaving it all to Amy and me.","uz":"Mark bu oson, shanbagacha boshlash shart emas dedi… Keyin dam olish kunlari ketib qoldi va hammasini Emi bilan menga qoldirdi.","why":"Guruhdan qancha yordam olgani (C). Muddat ko'chirilgani (B) — u buni yaxshi deb biladi.","hl":null},{"q":"How does the woman react to the man's problem?","qu":"Ayol erkakning muammosiga qanday munosabat bildiradi?","o":["She expresses her sympathy.","She believes that he is exaggerating.","She thinks he will learn from the experience."],"ou":["Hamdardlik bildiradi.","U bo'rttirayotgan deb o'ylaydi.","U bu tajribadan saboq oladi deb o'ylaydi."],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":270.74,"en":281.09,"si":22,"ev":"You poor thing.","uz":"Bechora-ya.","why":"Ayol hamdardlik bildiradi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"Both people believe that","qu":"Ikkalasi ham ... deb hisoblaydi","o":["the story was believable.","the actors were chosen poorly.","the movie made you think."],"ou":["voqea ishonarli edi","aktyorlar yomon tanlangan","film o'ylantiradi"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":423.03,"en":442.33,"si":31,"ev":"Even though I wasn't too impressed when I saw it, it has kept coming into my mind since then… It's certainly not the kind of film you see and then instantly forget.","uz":"Ko'rganimda unchalik ta'sirlanmagan bo'lsam ham, o'shandan beri tez-tez esimga tushadi… Bu ko'rib, darrov unutib yuboradigan film emas.","why":"Film o'ylantiradi (C). Voqea ishonarli emas (A) — \"totally inauthentic\".","hl":null},{"q":"According to the woman, what was the best thing about the film?","qu":"Ayolning fikricha, filmning eng yaxshi tomoni nima edi?","o":["the camerawork","the soundtrack","the cast"],"ou":["operatorlik ishi","musiqasi","aktyorlar tarkibi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":443.06,"en":452.8,"si":34,"ev":"The one thing that made it a bit special for me was the way it was very visually interesting. Plenty of unusual and beautiful shots.","uz":"Men uchun uni alohida qilgan narsa — vizual jihatdan juda qiziqligi. Ko'plab g'ayrioddiy va chiroyli kadrlar.","why":"Eng yaxshi tomoni — operatorlik ishi (A). Aktyorlar (C) — \"the wrong people were cast\".","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":29.72,"e":29.72,"t":"Extract One — You hear a man and a woman discussing an international sports event."},{"s":29.72,"e":33.85,"t":"There's more in the papers about next year's International Athletics Competition."},{"s":34.46,"e":40.38,"t":"It seems they're running into more problems. I'm beginning to wish they hadn't decided to hold it in our area."},{"s":41.27,"e":49.98,"t":"It seems to be causing endless problems. I know. Not that it bothers me personally that much. I certainly know intention of going along to anything."},{"s":50.49,"e":58.49,"t":"I realised at once that I'd be away while it was on, and I feel quite relieved about that now. The town will probably be horribly crowded."},{"s":59.1,"e":61.18,"t":"But I don't feel sorry it's coming here though."},{"s":61.69,"e":71.9,"t":"Right from the start I thought it would be really positive for the local economy, and you can already see that happening. I guess so, but I wish I could feel more confident it'd all be worth it in the end."},{"s":72.6,"e":78.37,"t":"It's just one thing after another. Now they've run into other problems with the foundations for the new stadium."},{"s":79.16,"e":82.37,"t":"They're still adamant it'll be ready well before the due date."},{"s":83.19,"e":84.51,"t":"I believe it when I see it"},{"s":85.05,"e":104.16,"t":"beginning to feel like a real possibility that it won't be. And how awful would that be? You'd think that with all that experience on the planning committee and the huge budget they've been given, they'd be able to do things properly. I know what you mean, but there's no point in getting too worked up about it. There's nothing we can do to help, is there?"},{"k":"h","s":217.69,"e":217.69,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two students discussing a piece of group coursework they are doing."},{"s":217.69,"e":219.55,"t":"your coursework coming along, Rick?"},{"s":220.28,"e":223.1,"t":"groups meeting to finish Azov this afternoon then."},{"s":223.61,"e":239.45,"t":"We've been finding it really hard, but I think I've probably learnt a lot from the experience of doing it. We've still got messes to do on ours. Mark said it'd be easy, and there was no need to start it till Saturday, even though we thought it was due in first thing on Monday morning."},{"s":239.93,"e":244.61,"t":"Then he decided to go away for the weekend, leaving it all to Amy and me."},{"s":245.11,"e":254.21,"t":"Sounds like it's a good job the tutor extended the deadline till 5 o'clock tomorrow afternoon then. I suppose so. Though I'd rather have had it done by now."},{"s":254.71,"e":257.47,"t":"I've got another piece of work due in later this week."},{"s":258.04,"e":260.83,"t":"Anyway, I'm afraid it's going to be an all-nighter for"},{"s":261.43,"e":262.72,"t":"Amy's not much help."},{"s":263.26,"e":265.44,"t":"She said she'd do one part of it."},{"s":266.07,"e":270.14,"t":"but she misunderstood the tutor's instructions and has done the wrong thing."},{"s":270.74,"e":281.09,"t":"I must admit, he didn't explain things all that clearly, but even so. You poor thing. I always thought people were exaggerating when they complained about this course."},{"s":281.53,"e":284.8,"t":"But now I'm beginning to feel they had a point. Absolutely."},{"k":"h","s":391.13,"e":391.13,"t":"Extract Three — You hear a man and a woman discussing a film they have recently seen."},{"s":391.13,"e":393.25,"t":"So what did you think of silent laughter?"},{"s":393.85,"e":395.01,"t":"I was a bit disappointed."},{"s":395.45,"e":405.31,"t":"I didn't think it was as good as it's been hyped up to be. Yeah, I thought it was weird, bordering on the pretentious. But I suppose that might be how things really are in the world of fashion."},{"s":406.46,"e":407.23,"t":"so sure"},{"s":407.74,"e":412.89,"t":"My cousin knows someone who's a model and she says the storyline was totally inauthentic."},{"s":413.59,"e":422.53,"t":"And my cousin and I both thought that absolutely the wrong people were cast in the main roles. Yeah, though some of the supporting actors were okay, I suppose. Maybe."},{"s":423.03,"e":428.73,"t":"Mind you, even though I wasn't too impressed when I saw it, it has kept coming into my mind since then."},{"s":429.53,"e":433.73,"t":"I start wondering just how much was the model's dream and how much was reality."},{"s":434.3,"e":442.33,"t":"or about the relationship between the supermodel and the designer. I know what you mean. It's certainly not the kind of film you see and then instantly forget."},{"s":443.06,"e":452.8,"t":"I think the one thing that made it a bit special for me was the way it was very visually interesting. Plenty of unusual and beautiful shots, particularly of the main characters."},{"s":453.56,"e":455.81,"t":"Enjoy the music too. Absolutely."}]},{"n":36,"title":"A man and a woman discussing a work colleague","dur":431.490563,"x":[{"ps":29.4,"en":74.49,"c":"You hear a man and a woman discussing a work colleague."},{"ps":158.87,"en":211.26,"c":"You hear two people discussing an article from a local newspaper."},{"ps":302.17,"en":360.96,"c":"You'll hear two students discussing a course they're doing."}],"items":[{"q":"What is the problem the colleague causes?","qu":"Hamkasb qanday muammo tug'diradi?","o":["others have to do more work because of them","clients are not happy with the service","other members of staff are dissatisfied with them"],"ou":["uning sababli boshqalar ko'proq ishlashga majbur","mijozlar xizmatdan norozi","boshqa xodimlar undan norozi"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":33.24,"en":46.81,"si":2,"ev":"I've heard mutterings from several members of staff already. — I know. And it used to be such a happy team.","uz":"Bir nechta xodimlarning g'o'ldirashini allaqachon eshitdim. — Bilaman. Ilgari jamoa juda baxtli edi.","why":"Boshqa xodimlar undan norozi (C). Mijozlar (B) — \"everything seems fine\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman suggest as a solution?","qu":"Ayol yechim sifatida nimani taklif qiladi?","o":["talk about it with the colleague","get the management involved","give the situation more time"],"ou":["bu haqda hamkasb bilan gaplashish","rahbariyatni aralashtirish","vaziyatga ko'proq vaqt berish"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":61.91,"en":74.49,"si":7,"ev":"I think I'd be more in favour of hanging on for a bit. It might just be a matter of him getting used to our way of working.","uz":"Menimcha, biroz kutib turgan ma'qul. Balki u shunchaki bizning ish uslubimizga ko'nikishi kerakdir.","why":"Vaziyatga ko'proq vaqt berish (C). Rahbariyat (B) — \"no reason to take it up with our line manager\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is the newspaper article about?","qu":"Gazeta maqolasi nima haqida?","o":["poor results of a football match","club management changes","a sports club involved in a lawsuit"],"ou":["futbol o'yinining yomon natijalari","klub rahbariyatidagi o'zgarishlar","sud ishiga aralashgan sport klubi"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":158.87,"en":177.18,"si":11,"ev":"They've gone and sacked their manager… and they've terminated the coach's contract too.","uz":"Ular menejerini ishdan bo'shatishdi… murabbiyning shartnomasini ham bekor qilishdi.","why":"Klub rahbariyatidagi o'zgarishlar (B). Natijalar (A) — aksincha, jamoa yaxshilanish arafasida edi.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the man's reaction to the news?","qu":"Erkak yangilikka qanday munosabat bildiradi?","o":["He is unhappy because the situation is very unfortunate","He feels relief that they avoided a difficult situation","He is puzzled by the timing of the event"],"ou":["Vaziyat juda achinarli bo'lgani uchun xafa","Qiyin vaziyatdan qutulganlaridan yengil tortgan","Voqeaning vaqtidan hayron"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":190.68,"en":209.25,"si":17,"ev":"But it's still an odd time to do it… I wonder if there's more to it than meets the eye.","uz":"Lekin baribir buni qilish uchun g'alati vaqt… Buning ortida ko'rinmaydigan boshqa narsa bormikan.","why":"Voqea vaqtidan hayron (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What do they agree about?","qu":"Ular nima haqida bir fikrda?","o":["The teacher manages to arouse interest in the difficult subject.","The course got off to a bad start.","Their future careers will benefit from this course."],"ou":["O'qituvchi qiyin fanga qiziqish uyg'ota oladi.","Kurs yomon boshlandi.","Bu kurs kelajakdagi kasbiga foyda beradi."],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":307.1,"en":319.68,"si":24,"ev":"I thought it was going to be tedious at first, but it seems to get a bit better each time. — Yes, I thought I might end up dropping it after the first week.","uz":"Avvaliga zerikarli bo'ladi deb o'ylagandim, lekin har safar biroz yaxshilanyapti. — Ha, birinchi haftadan keyin tashlab ketsam kerak deb o'ylagandim.","why":"Ikkalasi ham kurs yomon boshlangan deydi (B). Kelajakdagi kasb (C) — \"I'm not so sure about that\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman like about the lectures?","qu":"Ayolga ma'ruzalarning nimasi yoqadi?","o":["the voice of the lecturer","the lecturer's humorous approach","the lecturer's visual presentation of the material"],"ou":["ma'ruzachining ovozi","ma'ruzachining hazilomuz yondashuvi","ma'ruzachining materialni vizual taqdim etishi"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":320.12,"en":344.48,"si":25,"ev":"He's got quite a dry sense of humour… If he wasn't so witty, I don't think I'd make the effort.","uz":"Uning hazili ancha \"quruq\" (nozik)… Agar u shunchalik zukko-hazilkash bo'lmaganida, men harakat qilmasdim.","why":"Ma'ruzachining hazilomuz yondashuvi (B). Ovozi (A) — juda past, slaydlar (C) — juda to'la.","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":29.4,"e":29.4,"t":"Extract One — You hear a man and a woman discussing a work colleague."},{"s":29.4,"e":32.57,"t":"Jeremy's gonna turn out okay as the new store supervisor."},{"s":33.24,"e":46.81,"t":"beginning to have my doubts. Well, he's bound to take some time to settle into the role, I guess, but things aren't looking that promising. I've heard mutterings from several members of staff already. I know. And it used to be such a happy team."},{"s":47.48,"e":50.17,"t":"At least everything seems fine as far as customers are concerned."},{"s":51.03,"e":54.4,"t":"I guess there's no reason to take it up with our line manager at this stage."},{"s":55.03,"e":57.18,"t":"Perhaps we should have a quiet word with him."},{"s":57.91,"e":61.09,"t":"You're good at that sort of thing? Well, I wouldn't mind but..."},{"s":61.91,"e":68.51,"t":"I think I'd be more in favour of hanging on for a bit. It might just be a matter of him getting used to our way of working with each other."},{"s":68.98,"e":71.9,"t":"He might just have been used to a less collaborative atmosphere."},{"s":72.41,"e":74.49,"t":"Okay, let's give that a try then."},{"k":"h","s":158.87,"e":158.87,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two people discussing an article from a local newspaper."},{"s":158.87,"e":164.25,"t":"Look at this, they've gone and sacked their manager. He's only been in the post for a couple of years."},{"s":164.73,"e":168.09,"t":"Is that because they've had such poor results recently?"},{"s":168.66,"e":173.82,"t":"when everyone had said the team was on the verge of doing so much better than before. Oh, it must be."},{"s":174.33,"e":177.18,"t":"and they've terminated the coaches contract too."},{"s":177.69,"e":184.13,"t":"But he's no loss. I never thought he was much good. And you never thought much of the manager either, did you?"},{"s":184.57,"e":190.05,"t":"You were always saying he was in out of his depth. Yes, in the long term it might be a good thing."},{"s":190.68,"e":192.54,"t":"but it's still an odd time to do it."},{"s":193.11,"e":195.77,"t":"It's going to be pretty unsettling for the players."},{"s":196.5,"e":201.47,"t":"I wonder if there's more to it than meets the eye. Some legal issue perhaps. Maybe."},{"s":201.94,"e":209.25,"t":"But perhaps it's a relief to see the back of them if something like that's involved. I'd agree with you if it had happened at the beginning of the season."},{"s":209.69,"e":211.26,"t":"But now I'm not so sh..."},{"k":"h","s":302.17,"e":302.17,"t":"Extract Three — You'll hear two students discussing a course they're doing."},{"s":302.17,"e":306.49,"t":"The Monday afternoon optional course seems to be turning out okay, don't you think?"},{"s":307.1,"e":319.68,"t":"I thought it was going to be tedious at first, but it seems to get a bit better each time. Yes, I thought I might end up dropping it after the first week, but I'm getting more used to the lecturer, and I think I quite like his style now."},{"s":320.12,"e":330.91,"t":"He's got quite a dry sense of humour, and I suppose vibrations could be an important topic if we're going to become hands-on engineers. I'm not so sure about that."},{"s":331.42,"e":334.56,"t":"Anyway, I've decided to stick with it for a bit longer."},{"s":335.13,"e":340.89,"t":"I wish he didn't speak so softly though. It's hard to hear his voice from the back of that huge lecture hall."},{"s":341.5,"e":344.48,"t":"If he wasn't so witty, I don't think I'd make the effort."},{"s":345.21,"e":347.26,"t":"and the slides have far too much on them."},{"s":347.86,"e":360.96,"t":"I can't read them when I'm sitting at the back. It's a good job he puts them up online for us. I know. And did you see he's also put up a coursework assignment for us? We've got to get it done by the end of next week."}]},{"n":37,"title":"You'll hear a husband and wife discussing their plans for the weekend","dur":473.0775,"x":[{"ps":29.46,"en":90.27,"c":"You'll hear a husband and wife discussing their plans for the weekend."},{"ps":188.89,"en":246.49,"c":"You'll hear two people discussing an opinion poll."},{"ps":341.94,"en":401.63,"c":"You'll hear two people talking about a website."}],"items":[{"q":"What is the woman's reaction to the man's idea?","qu":"Ayol erkakning g'oyasiga qanday munosabat bildiradi?","o":["She has some reservations about it.","She feels quite scared.","She is excited by the idea."],"ou":["Unga nisbatan ba'zi shubhalari bor.","Ancha qo'rqib ketadi.","G'oyadan hayajonlanadi."],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":50.1,"en":64.89,"si":7,"ev":"[I've never been a] passenger on a motorbike in my life… — That's okay. I've got a spare one and some leathers you could borrow… — Well, I did say I wanted something challenging, I suppose.","uz":"Hayotimda hech qachon mototsiklda yo'lovchi bo'lmaganman… — Hechqisi yo'q. Menda zaxira dubulg'a va charm kiyim bor. — Mayli, o'zim qiyinroq narsa xohlayman degandim-ku.","why":"Ayolda biroz ikkilanish bor, lekin rozi bo'ladi (A). U qo'rqib ketmaydi (B), hayajonlanmaydi ham (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What do they agree to do in the evening?","qu":"Ular kechqurun nima qilishga kelishadi?","o":["to eat out","to go listen to some live music","to stay at home"],"ou":["tashqarida ovqatlanish","jonli musiqa tinglashga borish","uyda qolish"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":71.64,"en":90.27,"si":15,"ev":"Why don't we just eat out?… we can just flake out in front of the telly with a takeaway if we're really that worn out. — Sounds good to me.","uz":"Nega shunchaki tashqarida ovqatlanmaymiz?… Juda charchagan bo'lsak, uyda televizor oldida tayyor ovqat bilan dam olamiz. — Menga ma'qul.","why":"Ular uyda qolishga kelishadi (C). Jonli musiqa (B) — bolalar boradi.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the survey about?","qu":"So'rovnoma nima haqida?","o":["people's reaction to social problems","people's TV show preferences","people's attitude to suggested infrastructure development"],"ou":["odamlarning ijtimoiy muammolarga munosabati","odamlarning teleko'rsatuvlar bo'yicha afzalliklari","odamlarning taklif qilingan infratuzilma loyihasiga munosabati"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":201.98,"en":220.22,"si":19,"ev":"He wanted to know what I felt about the new shopping centre they're thinking about building near the railway station.","uz":"U vokzal yonida qurilishi rejalashtirilayotgan yangi savdo markazi haqida nima deb o'ylashimni bilmoqchi edi.","why":"Taklif qilingan infratuzilma loyihasiga munosabat (C). TV (B) — boshqa so'rovnoma edi.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the woman's attitude to the survey?","qu":"Ayolning so'rovnomaga munosabati qanday?","o":["it did not pose questions correctly","it is only a publicity stunt","it was a waste of time"],"ou":["unda savollar to'g'ri qo'yilmagan","bu shunchaki reklama nayrangi","bu vaqtni behuda sarflash bo'ldi"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":222.81,"en":238.56,"si":22,"ev":"I don't think he really had any interest in what I had to say. Feeling the authorities just want to be able to tick a few boxes, saying that consultation with residents has taken place.","uz":"Menimcha, uni aytganlarim umuman qiziqtirmadi. Rasmiylar shunchaki \"aholi bilan maslahatlashildi\" deb belgi qo'yib qo'yishni xohlaydi.","why":"So'rovnoma — shunchaki ko'z-ko'z uchun nayrang (B). Vaqt behuda ketmadi (C) — u uni yana ruhlantirdi.","hl":null},{"q":"What does the man want from the woman?","qu":"Erkak ayoldan nima istaydi?","o":["ask for tips on how to make the website better","talk about some development ideas that he has","come up with some new website pages"],"ou":["veb-saytni yaxshilash bo'yicha maslahat so'rash","o'zidagi rivojlantirish g'oyalari haqida gaplashish","yangi veb-sahifalar o'ylab topish"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":362.74,"en":392.86,"si":33,"ev":"I wondered if you could take a look at what's online already and tell me how user friendly it is… My idea is that it should be totally straightforward to navigate.","uz":"Hozir saytda bor narsaga qarab, qanchalik qulayligini aytib bera olasanmi deb o'yladim… Fikrim — undan foydalanish juda oson bo'lishi kerak.","why":"Erkak saytni yaxshilash bo'yicha maslahat so'raydi (A). Yangi sahifalar (C) yaratish so'ralmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"What problems might the woman have helping the man?","qu":"Erkakka yordam berishda ayolda qanday muammo bo'lishi mumkin?","o":["She is too busy to do it on time","Her computer has been malfunctioning","She needs more information about the project"],"ou":["Uni o'z vaqtida qilishga juda band","Kompyuteri buzilib turibdi","Loyiha haqida ko'proq ma'lumot kerak"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":396.7,"en":401.63,"si":36,"ev":"My laptop's been playing up a bit recently but hopefully it won't let me down.","uz":"Noutbukim keyingi paytda biroz injiqlik qilyapti, lekin umid qilamanki, pand bermaydi.","why":"Kompyuteri nosozligi muammo bo'lishi mumkin (B). Shoshilinch emas (A emas): \"It's not too urgent\".","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":29.46,"e":29.46,"t":"Extract One — You'll hear a husband and wife discussing their plans for the weekend."},{"s":29.46,"e":32.06,"t":"I'd like to do something different this weekend."},{"s":32.98,"e":36.19,"t":"I feel as if I'm stuck in a rut. I need a break."},{"s":36.63,"e":39.77,"t":"bit of a challenge. Well, here's a suggestion for you."},{"s":40.25,"e":44.73,"t":"I was planning to take my bike down to the south coast to see a veteran car race."},{"s":45.24,"e":46.33,"t":"Why don't you come with"},{"s":46.84,"e":48.32,"t":"On your motorbike."},{"s":50.1,"e":52.45,"t":"passenger on a motorbike in my life."},{"s":53.98,"e":54.81,"t":"or anything."},{"s":55.26,"e":58.46,"t":"That's okay. I've got a spare one and some leathers you could borrow."},{"s":58.94,"e":59.87,"t":"It'd be fun."},{"s":61.02,"e":64.89,"t":"Well, I did say I wanted something challenging, I suppose."},{"s":66.1,"e":67.07,"t":"Let's go for it"},{"s":68.09,"e":68.89,"t":"then when we get"},{"s":69.46,"e":71.1,"t":"I'll make something special for dinner."},{"s":71.64,"e":78.65,"t":"I've got a great new Thai recipe. Oh, I think you'll be tired. Why don't we just eat out? No, it'll be fine."},{"s":79.29,"e":90.27,"t":"Kids are going out to a gig. Their friend's band is playing at the college club this weekend, so we can just flake out in front of the telly with a takeaway if we're really that worn out. Sounds good to me."},{"k":"h","s":188.89,"e":188.89,"t":"Extract Two — You'll hear two people discussing an opinion poll."},{"s":188.89,"e":201.12,"t":"stopped in the street and asked some questions by some man doing an opinion poll today. Did you? Was it about what you watched on TV last night? I got asked about that by someone in the street a few days ago."},{"s":201.98,"e":207.71,"t":"Actually he wanted to know what I felt about the new shopping centre they're thinking about building near the railway station."},{"s":208.31,"e":220.22,"t":"Whether I felt it would solve some of the town's problems or actually just cause more. Well, you've certainly got strong opinions about that. You're always telling me what a rubbish idea you think it is. True."},{"s":220.76,"e":222.08,"t":"and I told him what I thought"},{"s":222.81,"e":226.21,"t":"but I don't think he really had any interest in what I had to say."},{"s":227.26,"e":234.78,"t":"Feeling the authorities just want to be able to tick a few boxes, saying that consultation with residents has taken place."},{"s":235.45,"e":238.56,"t":"I don't think he wrote down my answers to any of his questions."},{"s":239.51,"e":243.33,"t":"would at least it serve the useful purpose of firing me up about it again."},{"s":243.99,"e":246.49,"t":"I'm going to sit down and write a letter to the local paper now"},{"k":"h","s":341.94,"e":341.94,"t":"Extract Three — You'll hear two people talking about a website."},{"s":341.94,"e":344.25,"t":"Hi Mel, I'm glad I bumped into you."},{"s":344.73,"e":346.59,"t":"Now I've been wanting to ask you a favour."},{"s":347.28,"e":350.94,"t":"Right. As you know, I've been working on this website idea of mine."},{"s":351.31,"e":356.54,"t":"It's a portal for people interested in this part of the country with lots of pages relating to its history."},{"s":356.88,"e":362.27,"t":"landscape, wildlife, local businesses, study opportunities here, all that sort of thing."},{"s":362.74,"e":379.36,"t":"Sounds interesting, but I'm not sure how I can help. I'm pretty new to the area and don't know much about it. Well, you do know a lot about websites. I wondered if you could take a look at what's online already and tell me how user friendly it is, that sort of thing."},{"s":379.8,"e":392.86,"t":"My idea is that it should be totally straightforward to navigate. Sounds interesting, certainly. But when do you want it done for? I'm pretty busy at the moment. It's not too urgent, in fact. OK, then."},{"s":393.46,"e":396.22,"t":"Email me the URL and I'll do what I can."},{"s":396.7,"e":401.63,"t":"My laptop's been playing up a bit recently but hopefully it won't let me down. Thanks."}]},{"n":38,"title":"Part of a radio program about a famous London hotel","dur":530.6775,"x":[{"ps":33.5,"en":105.05,"c":"You hear part of a radio program about a famous London hotel."},{"ps":220.41,"en":282.59,"c":"You hear two presenters talking on a science programme."},{"ps":388.34,"en":452.86,"c":"You hear two people talking about popular music."}],"items":[{"q":"The presenter's aim in her introduction is to","qu":"Boshlovchining kirish so'zidagi maqsadi ...","o":["correct misunderstandings about the Grand","provide factual information about the Grand","encourage listeners to go to the Grand"],"ou":["\"Grand\" haqidagi noto'g'ri tasavvurlarni tuzatish","\"Grand\" haqida aniq ma'lumot berish","tinglovchilarni \"Grand\"ga borishga undash"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":33.5,"en":71.97,"si":1,"ev":"The tea at the Grand Hotel in London is served in the green room… There are four sittings for tea… There are 12 types of tea on offer.","uz":"Londondagi \"Grand\" mehmonxonasida choy yashil zalda beriladi… Choy to'rt mahal tortiladi… 12 xil choy taklif etiladi.","why":"Boshlovchi \"Grand\" haqida aniq faktlarni beradi (B). U tinglovchilarni borishga undamaydi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What is the manager's attitude towards the customers?","qu":"Menejerning mijozlarga munosabati qanday?","o":["He wishes that more of them were not rich people.","He treats them all in the same way, regardless of who they are.","He always knows instantly what category they belong to."],"ou":["Ularning ko'prog'i boy bo'lmasligini xohlaydi.","Kim bo'lishidan qat'i nazar, hammaga bir xil munosabatda bo'ladi.","Ular qaysi toifaga kirishini doim darhol biladi."],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":89.78,"en":99.71,"si":11,"ev":"I can tell as soon as someone walks in what type of person they are, where they are from, why they are here.","uz":"Kimdir kirib kelishi bilanoq uning qanday odam ekani, qayerdan va nima uchun kelganini bilaman.","why":"Mijoz qaysi toifaga kirishini darhol biladi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"The male presenter says that the research produced data on","qu":"Erkak boshlovchining aytishicha, tadqiqot ... haqida ma'lumot berdi","o":["the period of time that some teaspoons were missing","how quickly a certain number of teaspoons disappeared","where disappearing teaspoons had gone"],"ou":["ba'zi choy qoshiqlari qancha vaqt yo'q bo'lgani","ma'lum miqdordagi choy qoshiqlari qanchalik tez yo'qolgani","yo'qolgan choy qoshiqlari qayerga ketgani"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":250.58,"en":266.56,"si":18,"ev":"It was calculated that they had a half-life, that is, the length of time it took for half of the teaspoons to disappear, of 81 days.","uz":"Qoshiqlarning yarmi yo'qolishi uchun ketgan vaqt 81 kun ekani hisoblandi.","why":"Ma'lum miqdordagi qoshiqlar qanchalik tez yo'qolgani (B).","hl":null},{"q":"The female presenter says that disappearing teaspoons is a topic which","qu":"Ayol boshlovchining aytishicha, choy qoshiqlarining yo'qolishi ... mavzu","o":["has produced some interesting theories.","concerns a growing phenomenon.","has no great significance."],"ou":["qiziqarli nazariyalarni yuzaga keltirgan","kuchayib borayotgan hodisaga oid","unchalik ahamiyatga ega bo'lmagan"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":220.41,"en":227.77,"si":14,"ev":"Possibly one of the most talked about pieces of research recently published has surprisingly little to do with anything of particular importance.","uz":"Yaqinda chop etilgan eng ko'p muhokama qilingan tadqiqotlardan biri ajablanarli darajada hech qanday muhim narsaga aloqasi yo'q.","why":"Mavzu unchalik ahamiyatli emas (C).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman's point is that","qu":"Ayolning fikri shuki","o":["it is no longer possible to create genuinely original popular music.","all modern popular music is a poor imitation of older music.","popular music has always been an overrated form of music."],"ou":["endi chinakam o'ziga xos pop musiqa yaratish mumkin emas","barcha zamonaviy pop musiqa eski musiqaning sayoz taqlidi","pop musiqa doim ortiqcha baholangan janr bo'lib kelgan"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":388.34,"en":430.24,"si":22,"ev":"Most of the innovations… had happened by the end of the 1970s and after that it's all been copies… it's all been done before.","uz":"Yangiliklarning aksariyati 1970-yillar oxirigacha sodir bo'lgan, keyin hammasi takror… hammasi avval qilingan.","why":"Chinakam o'ziga xos pop musiqa yaratish endi mumkin emas (A). Barchasi sayoz taqlid (B) emas — \"they sometimes do that very well\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman say about modern performers?","qu":"Ayol zamonaviy ijrochilar haqida nima deydi?","o":["They are not interested in the views of older people","They are taking advantage of their audience","They are influenced without realizing it."],"ou":["Ularni kattalarning fikri qiziqtirmaydi","Ular tinglovchilaridan foydalanmoqda","Ular o'zlari sezmagan holda ta'sirlanadi."],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":441.82,"en":452.86,"si":25,"ev":"Influences pass from one generation to another and it's not always a conscious thing.","uz":"Ta'sirlar avloddan avlodga o'tadi va bu har doim ham ongli bo'lmaydi.","why":"Ular o'zlari sezmagan holda ta'sirlanadi (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":33.5,"e":33.5,"t":"Extract One — You hear part of a radio program about a famous London hotel."},{"s":33.5,"e":43.39,"t":"The tea at the Grand Hotel in London is served in the green room, a light airy space with luxuriant plants, fountains, and a panoramic view over the city."},{"s":44.12,"e":46.14,"t":"The dress is strictly smart casual."},{"s":46.74,"e":48.51,"t":"There are four sittings for tea."},{"s":48.95,"e":53.76,"t":"the first at 1130 in the morning and the last at 630 in the evening."},{"s":54.55,"e":58.81,"t":"Despite the high price tag, tables are booked up months in advance."},{"s":59.35,"e":65.6,"t":"He includes a selection of sandwiches, crustless of course, scones, cakes and pastries."},{"s":66.2,"e":71.97,"t":"There are 12 types of tea on offer, including the Grand's own Superior Afternoon Brew."},{"s":72.66,"e":76.13,"t":"David James has been manager of the green room for 15 years."},{"s":76.76,"e":80.73,"t":"David, Tea at the Ground is very popular, isn't it? Yes, indeed."},{"s":81.24,"e":89.34,"t":"When I first started, we had 80 to 100 people a day. Now it's twice that number. And are they all wealthy people? Not at all."},{"s":89.78,"e":99.71,"t":"I can tell as soon as someone walks in what type of person they are, where they are from, why they are here. Some people who come here have lots of money and some don't."},{"s":100.22,"e":105.05,"t":"When someone has saved to come here as a treat, I like to make a special effort to make them feel comfortable."},{"k":"h","s":220.41,"e":220.41,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two presenters talking on a science programme."},{"s":220.41,"e":227.77,"t":"Possibly one of the most talked about pieces of research recently published has surprisingly little to do with anything of particular importance."},{"s":228.31,"e":243.77,"t":"Entitled 'The Case of the Disappearing Teaspoons', the study proves that this is a naturally occurring phenomenon with no apparent explanation. Yes, a research team in Australia placed 70 numbered teaspoons in various tea rooms at their institute."},{"s":244.25,"e":247.04,"t":"and tracked them over a period of five months."},{"s":247.64,"e":250.08,"t":"80% disappeared for good."},{"s":250.58,"e":266.56,"t":"It was calculated that they had a half-life, that is, the length of time it took for half of the teaspoons to disappear, of 81 days. If this is a global phenomenon, then 600,000 teaspoons are disappearing each year. So, where have they all gone?"},{"s":267.54,"e":273.85,"t":"The practical and mundane explanations include people taking them home or losing them under piles of work."},{"s":274.65,"e":282.59,"t":"However, with such a large quantity of teaspoons being lost each year, many people feel these explanations are simply not sufficient."},{"k":"h","s":388.34,"e":388.34,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people talking about popular music."},{"s":388.34,"e":409.02,"t":"One thing that's quite interesting about popular music is how derivative and imitative it is. You see, most of the innovations that took place in it had happened by the end of the 1970s and after that it's all been copies of what had already been and gone. That's just not true. There's lots of really innovative new music going on now and there always will be."},{"s":409.5,"e":430.24,"t":"Every new generation develops its own styles and sounds that are unique to it. No, they just think that's what they're doing. Actually, they're just recycling old things. Granted, they sometimes do that very well, but it's all been done before. The truth is, it's new for them, but it's not actually new. But the fans, the public..."},{"s":430.68,"e":441.02,"t":"They don't see it that way, do they? No, they buy the music and they go to concerts by the latest successful or fashionable bands and singers and they think it's all being done for the first time."},{"s":441.82,"e":446.21,"t":"It's only older people like me who spot the similarities with music from the past."},{"s":446.78,"e":452.86,"t":"Like a lot of things, influences pass from one generation to another and it's not always a conscious thing."}]},{"n":39,"title":"Two people talking about reading books aloud for children","dur":499.356688,"x":[{"ps":33.37,"en":86.78,"c":"You hear two people talking about reading books aloud for children."},{"ps":182.07,"en":244.22,"c":"you hear a part of a radio programme."},{"ps":351.42,"en":418.14,"c":"You hear two people on a radio program talking about running."}],"items":[{"q":"The second speaker says that she believes that","qu":"Ikkinchi so'zlovchining aytishicha, u ... deb hisoblaydi","o":["Her children enjoy listening to her read aloud","She shares a reading habit with other parents","Parents should read aloud to children"],"ou":["farzandlari uning ovoz chiqarib o'qishini tinglashni yoqtiradi","u boshqa ota-onalar bilan bir xil o'qish odatiga ega","ota-onalar bolalarga ovoz chiqarib o'qib berishi kerak"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":77.34,"en":86.78,"si":7,"ev":"I bet I'm not the only parent who… sits down on the stairs and reads on to find out what happens next.","uz":"Ishonamanki, zinaga o'tirib, keyin nima bo'lishini bilish uchun o'qishda davom etadigan yagona ota-ona men emasman.","why":"U boshqa ota-onalar bilan bir xil odatga ega (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What do both speakers talk about?","qu":"Ikkala so'zlovchi nima haqida gapiradi?","o":["their children's reactions when they read aloud to them","their selfish motives for reading aloud to their children","their dramatic approach to reading aloud to their children"],"ou":["ovoz chiqarib o'qib berganda farzandlarining munosabati","farzandlariga o'qib berishning xudbinona sabablari","farzandlariga o'qib berishdagi ta'sirchan (aktyorona) yondashuvi"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":33.37,"en":76.67,"si":1,"ev":"I like to do all the voices… — I always claim that I read aloud to our three children for their benefit… But it is, of course, for me.","uz":"Barcha qahramonlar ovozini qilishni yaxshi ko'raman… — Doim farzandlarimiz uchun o'qib beraman deyman… Lekin, albatta, bu o'zim uchun.","why":"Ikkalasi ham o'qib berishning xudbinona sabablarini aytadi (B). Ta'sirchan o'qish (C) — faqat birinchisi.","hl":null},{"q":"The presenter says that some people start a business with a friend because","qu":"Boshlovchining aytishicha, ba'zilar do'sti bilan biznes boshlaydi, chunki","o":["they have worked well together in the past","their friend persuades them to do it","they lack the courage to do it alone"],"ou":["ular ilgari birga yaxshi ishlagan","do'sti ularni bunga ko'ndiradi","ularda buni yolg'iz qilishga jasorat yetishmaydi"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":189.94,"en":206.72,"si":10,"ev":"It often comes down to fear. Starting and running a business on your own can be a daunting prospect.","uz":"Ko'pincha gap qo'rquvda. Biznesni yolg'iz boshlash va yuritish qo'rqinchli bo'lishi mumkin.","why":"Ularda yolg'iz qilishga jasorat yetishmaydi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What was Dean's problem with his partner?","qu":"Deanning sherigi bilan muammosi nima edi?","o":["He refused to take part in an important aspect of the business","His personality changed after they started the business","He often criticized the business decisions Dean made"],"ou":["U biznesning muhim bir qismida qatnashishdan bosh tortdi","Biznes boshlangandan keyin uning xarakteri o'zgardi","U Deanning qarorlarini tez-tez tanqid qilardi"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":220.25,"en":244.22,"si":16,"ev":"He just wasn't prepared to take responsibility for any decisions at all… I felt as if I was making all the big decisions on my own.","uz":"U hech qanday qaror uchun mas'uliyat olishga tayyor emas edi… Barcha muhim qarorlarni yolg'iz qabul qilayotgandek edim.","why":"Biznesning muhim jihati — qaror qabul qilishda qatnashishdan bosh tortdi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"Who are the two speakers?","qu":"Ikki so'zlovchi kim?","o":["successful athletes","fitness experts","sports journalists"],"ou":["muvaffaqiyatli sportchilar","fitnes mutaxassislari","sport jurnalistlari"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":356.18,"en":373.63,"si":22,"ev":"You're missing out on lots of fitness attributes that could contribute to improving your technique, your running economy… and your injury resistance.","uz":"Texnikangiz, yugurish samaradorligi… va jarohatga chidamliligingizni yaxshilashi mumkin bo'lgan sifatlarni boy beryapsiz.","why":"Ular fitnes mutaxassislari (B).","hl":null},{"q":"Both speakers agree that, to improve as a runner, runners should","qu":"Ikkala so'zlovchi yuguruvchi sifatida rivojlanish uchun ... kerak degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["limit the amount of training they do","develop their own personal training methods","vary the focus of their training"],"ou":["mashg'ulot hajmini cheklash","o'zining shaxsiy mashg'ulot usullarini ishlab chiqish","mashg'ulot yo'nalishini o'zgartirib turish"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":388.63,"en":410.01,"si":24,"ev":"If running is all you do, some muscle groups get flabby… If you can strengthen the neglected muscles, stretch the tight ones… you'll be on the way to a more balanced body.","uz":"Faqat yugursangiz, ba'zi mushaklar bo'shashadi… E'tiborsiz mushaklarni kuchaytirib, taranglarini cho'zsangiz… tanangiz muvozanatliroq bo'ladi.","why":"Mashg'ulot yo'nalishini o'zgartirib turish (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":33.37,"e":33.37,"t":"Extract One — You hear two people talking about reading books aloud for children."},{"s":33.37,"e":36.32,"t":"I'm a terrible ham when it comes to reading to my kids."},{"s":36.89,"e":42.33,"t":"I like to do all the voices so I look for books with lots of dialogue and different characters."},{"s":42.94,"e":47.45,"t":"My kids are totally unimpressed and probably prefer having their mother read to them."},{"s":47.93,"e":52.03,"t":"She reads in a very soothing voice and she's not trying to act or show off."},{"s":52.7,"e":55.84,"t":"It reminds me of listening to my own mother read when I was a kid."},{"s":56.44,"e":76.67,"t":"Yes, I always claim that I read aloud to our three children for their benefit, that it's good for their educational development to sit and listen last thing at night, that somehow through hearing a story their creative juices will be stirred. But it is, of course, for me. Nothing can beat the delight of disappearing into a new thrilling chapter."},{"s":77.34,"e":86.78,"t":"And I bet I'm not the only parent who, having turned out the light and said goodnight to their grateful offspring, sits down on the stairs and reads on to find out what happens next."},{"k":"h","s":182.07,"e":182.07,"t":"Extract Two — you hear a part of a radio programme."},{"s":182.07,"e":189.15,"t":"People set up their own businesses and in many cases they do so in partnership with a friend rather than going it alone."},{"s":189.94,"e":198.24,"t":"Reasons for this often aren't purely practical, for example because of complementary skills and experience. It often comes down to fear."},{"s":198.9,"e":202.97,"t":"Starting and running a business on your own can be a daunting prospect."},{"s":203.45,"e":206.72,"t":"No wonder people often prefer to share the burden with a friend."},{"s":207.29,"e":213.37,"t":"It doesn't always go according to plan though, as Dean Ransom discovered when he started a business with a friend."},{"s":213.94,"e":215.07,"t":"What went wrong Dean?"},{"s":215.54,"e":219.68,"t":"Well, I'd known my partner for years and I felt we had a lot in common."},{"s":220.25,"e":228.19,"t":"What I hadn't realized about him was how indecisive he was, but I'd had no reason to notice that aspect of his personality before."},{"s":228.76,"e":232.48,"t":"He just wasn't prepared to take responsibility for any decisions at all."},{"s":232.95,"e":235.23,"t":"He just sat back and expected me to do it all."},{"s":235.8,"e":244.22,"t":"I didn't want to carry that burden alone. I wanted some sense of shared responsibility, but instead I felt as if I was making all the big decisions on my own."},{"k":"h","s":351.42,"e":351.42,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people on a radio program talking about running."},{"s":351.42,"e":355.36,"t":"Some people think there's only one way to become a better runner and that's to run."},{"s":356.18,"e":373.63,"t":"I'd argue that by confining your sessions purely to running, you're missing out on lots of fitness attributes that could contribute to improving your technique, your running economy - that's your ability to run faster without using up more energy - and your injury resistance. Absolutely."},{"s":374.33,"e":388.09,"t":"Running is a perfectly natural activity, but the body was designed to move in all directions, using a variety of muscle groups, not just in a forward direction, using only the lower body, often on unforgiving hard surfaces."},{"s":388.63,"e":396.99,"t":"If running is all you do, some muscle groups get flabby and lazy through underuse, while others become tight and short through overuse."},{"s":397.69,"e":410.01,"t":"If you can strengthen the neglected muscles, stretch the tight ones and make the most heavily used ones more resilient, you'll be on the way to a more balanced body and this will translate into better running."},{"s":410.58,"e":418.14,"t":"And by better, I don't just mean faster, I mean more comfortable, less strained and altogether more enjoyable."}]},{"n":40,"title":"Two people talking","dur":479.973875,"x":[{"ps":29.3,"en":88.32,"c":"You hear two people talking."},{"ps":191.77,"en":233.89,"c":"You hear two people on the radio discussing a letter from a listener."},{"ps":322.42,"en":394.75,"c":"You hear two people talking about jokes and comedy."}],"items":[{"q":"What is the situation?","qu":"Vaziyat qanday?","o":["They have treated someone unfairly","They have fallen out with someone","They have changed their view of someone"],"ou":["Ular kimgadir adolatsiz munosabatda bo'lgan","Ular kim bilandir urishib qolgan","Ular kimdir haqidagi fikrini o'zgartirgan"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":61.46,"en":81.37,"si":3,"ev":"The minute we confronted him about this latest dreadful piece of behaviour, he just totally lost it.","uz":"Uning so'nggi dahshatli qilmishi haqida yuziga aytganimiz zahoti u butunlay o'zini yo'qotdi.","why":"Ular kim bilandir urishib qolgan (B).","hl":null},{"q":"How do the speakers feel about the situation?","qu":"So'zlovchilar vaziyat haqida qanday his qiladi?","o":["resigned","distressed","puzzled"],"ou":["taqdirga tan bergan","qattiq xafa","hayron"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":61.46,"en":88.32,"si":3,"ev":"It was inevitable that it would come to this… So that's that. Yeah, let's forget all about it now.","uz":"Bunga kelishi muqarrar edi… Xullas, shu. Ha, endi hammasini unutaylik.","why":"Taqdirga tan bergan (A). Qattiq xafa emas (B): \"I'm glad to see the back of him\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is the first speaker doing when he speaks?","qu":"Birinchi so'zlovchi gapirayotganda nima qilyapti?","o":["suggesting that a problem is common","expressing sympathy about someone's problem","giving an objective account of a problem"],"ou":["muammo keng tarqalganini aytyapti","kimningdir muammosiga hamdardlik bildiryapti","muammoni xolis bayon qilyapti"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":191.77,"en":214.05,"si":6,"ev":"He's a train spotter. He likes looking at trains and reading about them… and his friends make fun of him for it. He's worried that they'll stop being his friends.","uz":"U poyezd ishqibozi… do'stlari esa uni masxara qilishadi. Ular do'stligini to'xtatishidan xavotirda.","why":"Birinchi so'zlovchi muammoni xolis bayon qiladi (C). Hamdardlik (B) bildirmaydi, muammo keng tarqalgan ham demaydi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"The second speaker suggests that Paul should","qu":"Ikkinchi so'zlovchi Paulga ... ni taklif qiladi","o":["accept that some people are unkind to others","change his own attitude towards certain people","confront the people who have upset him"],"ou":["ba'zi odamlar boshqalarga mehrsiz bo'lishini qabul qilish","ayrim odamlarga o'z munosabatini o'zgartirish","uni xafa qilgan odamlarga qarshi chiqish"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":220.12,"en":233.89,"si":9,"ev":"Perhaps he needs to look at why he wants to be friendly with these people when they make fun of what he's interested in.","uz":"Balki u qiziqishini masxara qiladigan odamlar bilan nega do'st bo'lishni xohlashi haqida o'ylashi kerakdir.","why":"Ayrim odamlarga munosabatini o'zgartirishi kerak (B). Ularga qarshi chiqish (C) taklif qilinmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"The first speaker says that punchlines","qu":"Birinchi so'zlovchining aytishicha, hazillarning kulgili yakunlari","o":["come in jokes that have formal structures","tend to be funnier than catchphrases","are easier to understand than in-jokes"],"ou":["aniq tuzilishga ega hazillarda bo'ladi","odatda mashhur iboralardan kulgiliroq","faqat tanishlar tushunadigan hazillardan osonroq tushuniladi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":332.98,"en":341.09,"si":13,"ev":"Many jokes are written backwards with the punchline, the funny line at the end that gets the laugh, sorted out first.","uz":"Ko'p hazillar teskari yoziladi: kulgili oxirgi jumla birinchi o'ylab topiladi.","why":"Punchline'lar aniq tuzilishga ega hazillarda bo'ladi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"The second speaker says that many professional comedians","qu":"Ikkinchi so'zlovchining aytishicha, ko'plab professional komiklar","o":["try to cause events that they can make jokes about","exaggerate events that have actually happened to them","become confused about what is fact and what is fiction"],"ou":["hazil qilish mumkin bo'lgan voqealarni ataylab keltirib chiqarishga urinadi","boshlaridan haqiqatan o'tgan voqealarni bo'rttiradi","nima haqiqat, nima to'qima ekanini chalkashtirib yuboradi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":381.02,"en":394.75,"si":20,"ev":"That's why most comics are outrageous liars. It's also why some comics may even begin to provoke hilarious episodes by deliberately forgetting their wedding anniversaries.","uz":"Shuning uchun ko'p komiklar ashaddiy yolg'onchilar. Shu sababli ba'zilari to'y yilligini ataylab unutib, kulgili vaziyatlarni keltirib chiqaradi.","why":"Hazil qilish uchun voqealarni ataylab keltirib chiqaradi (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":29.3,"e":29.3,"t":"Extract One — You hear two people talking."},{"s":29.3,"e":55.29,"t":"Well, I suppose it had to happen sometime. I mean, however good-natured you are, there's only so much bad behavior you can take. Yeah. I mean, we've known him all these years and we've put up with all sorts of terrible scenes with him. And times when he's been awful to both of us. I'm just amazed neither of us has had the guts to say anything to him before. I'm not sure it was a lack of courage on my part. I think it was more a misplaced sense of loyalty."},{"s":55.54,"e":60.96,"t":"I mean, we go back a long way. I know, but it's hard to come up with many good memories."},{"s":61.46,"e":81.37,"t":"Anyway, I guess it's over now and that's the last we'll see of him. Yeah, his reaction was typical. The minute we confronted him about this latest dreadful piece of behaviour, he just totally lost it. He's obviously never had any idea of the effect he has on people. Even people who were supposed to be his friends. Well, it was inevitable that it would come to this."},{"s":81.94,"e":88.32,"t":"We've said our piece and frankly I'm glad to see the back of him. So that's that. Yeah, let's forget all about it now."},{"k":"h","s":191.77,"e":191.77,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two people on the radio discussing a letter from a listener."},{"s":191.77,"e":208.54,"t":"OK, we've had a letter here from Paul who says that his friends are into all the latest trendy hobbies and fashions, whereas he really likes trains. He's a train spotter. He likes looking at trains and reading about them and collecting the numbers of ones he's seen, and his friends make fun of him for it."},{"s":209.11,"e":214.05,"t":"He's worried that they'll stop being his friends if he carries on with his hobby. What will you tell him, Esther?"},{"s":215.26,"e":219.29,"t":"Well, we usually end up choosing friends because we have something in common with them."},{"s":220.12,"e":233.89,"t":"Perhaps he needs to look at why he wants to be friendly with these people when they make fun of what he's interested in. I'm sure there are plenty of potential friends out there who share his interest. With them, he could enjoy that interest rather than having it used against him."},{"k":"h","s":322.42,"e":322.42,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people talking about jokes and comedy."},{"s":322.42,"e":327.33,"t":"Well, of course no single theory has yet been able to explain how jokes work."},{"s":327.86,"e":332.03,"t":"Even the great comedians have been stuck for a proper analysis."},{"s":332.98,"e":341.09,"t":"Of course, many jokes are written backwards with the punchline, the funny line at the end that gets the laugh sorted out first."},{"s":341.59,"e":347.13,"t":"However, a line or a phrase doesn't necessarily need a narrative set up to make us laugh."},{"s":347.8,"e":353.15,"t":"Witness comedy shows in which characters get laughs simply from saying catch phrases."},{"s":353.72,"e":357.37,"t":"This is also how an in-joke works among a group of friends."},{"s":357.91,"e":367.01,"t":"Life itself provides the setup and a word or two, sometimes just a knowing look between two people who are in on the joke, provides the punchline."},{"s":367.83,"e":374.62,"t":"Another thing about jokes is that a professional comedian's routine may be based on personal experience."},{"s":375.13,"e":380.38,"t":"but real experience doesn't tend to come conveniently complete with a punchline."},{"s":381.02,"e":384.22,"t":"That's why most comics are outrageous liars."},{"s":384.7,"e":394.75,"t":"It's also why some comics may even begin to provoke hilarious episodes by deliberately forgetting their wedding anniversaries or leaving their children in the supermarket."}]},{"n":41,"title":"Two students talking about shopping for clothes","dur":193.410563,"x":[{"ps":2.6,"en":52.0,"c":"You hear two students talking about shopping for clothes."},{"ps":60.02,"en":113.24,"c":"You hear part of an interview with a musician called Max."},{"ps":121.18,"en":180.54,"c":"You hear part of a discussion programme in which two dancers are talking about their careers."}],"items":[{"q":"What do they agree about?","qu":"Ular nima haqida bir fikrda?","o":["It's better to buy inexpensive clothes.","Shopping for clothes is to be avoided.","People should respect your taste in clothes."],"ou":["Arzon kiyim sotib olgan yaxshi.","Kiyim xarid qilishdan qochish kerak.","Odamlar kiyimdagi didingizni hurmat qilishi kerak."],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":13.75,"en":24.6,"si":3,"ev":"It was the prospect of shopping for new stuff I couldn't face… my trick is to put it off to the last possible moment… such a pointless activity.","uz":"Yangi narsalar xarid qilish fikriga chiday olmasdim… Men buni oxirgi lahzagacha orqaga suraman… bunday befoyda mashg'ulot.","why":"Ikkalasi ham kiyim xarid qilishdan qochish kerak deb biladi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"According to the man, many people see shopping as a way of","qu":"Erkakning fikricha, ko'pchilik xarid qilishni ... usuli deb biladi","o":["achieving social status.","making a comment on society.","identifying with a particular social group."],"ou":["ijtimoiy mavqega erishish","jamiyat haqida fikr bildirish","o'zini muayyan ijtimoiy guruhga mansub qilib ko'rsatish"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":26.3,"en":52.0,"si":5,"ev":"It's heavily linked to wanting to be the centre of attention… it's basically a way of showing off.","uz":"Bu diqqat markazida bo'lish istagi bilan bog'liq… asosan bu o'zini ko'rsatish usuli.","why":"Ijtimoiy mavqega erishish yo'li (A). Jamiyat haqida fikr (B) — \"it's not like a political issue for me\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does he say about his music in his teenage years?","qu":"U o'smirlik yillaridagi musiqasi haqida nima deydi?","o":["He wanted to keep it to himself.","He felt quite self-confident about it.","He was reluctant to ask for help with it."],"ou":["Uni o'zigagina saqlashni xohlagan.","Unga nisbatan o'zini ancha ishonchli his qilgan.","U bo'yicha yordam so'rashni istamagan."],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":60.02,"en":85.12,"si":8,"ev":"I didn't think that being number one was something completely unattainable. I had a cockiness, but I kept it hidden from my peers.","uz":"Birinchi o'rinni erishib bo'lmas narsa deb o'ylamasdim. Menda o'ziga haddan tashqari ishonch bor edi, lekin uni tengdoshlarimdan yashirardim.","why":"O'ziga ishonchi bor edi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What does he suggest about his recording contract?","qu":"U ovoz yozish shartnomasi haqida nimaga ishora qiladi?","o":["It didn't guarantee him ongoing success.","It didn't mean he could give up other work.","It didn't have very good terms and conditions."],"ou":["U doimiy muvaffaqiyatni kafolatlamadi.","U boshqa ishlarni tashlab yuborishi mumkinligini anglatmasdi.","Uning shartlari unchalik yaxshi emas edi."],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":85.37,"en":113.24,"si":9,"ev":"If after my first hit I thought I'd made it, I was soon disabused of that notion… I've had to put in a lot of effort to capitalise on that breakthrough.","uz":"Birinchi xitdan keyin maqsadga yetdim deb o'ylagan bo'lsam, tez orada bu fikrdan qaytdim… O'sha yutuqdan foydalanish uchun ko'p mehnat qildim.","why":"Shartnoma doimiy muvaffaqiyatni kafolatlamadi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"The man was inspired to train as a dancer by","qu":"Erkakni raqqos bo'lib tayyorlanishga ... ilhomlantirdi","o":["one reaction to a performance he gave.","some encouragement from his friends.","the athletic nature of the activity."],"ou":["o'z chiqishiga bo'lgan bitta munosabat","do'stlarining dalda berishi","bu mashg'ulotning sportga xos tabiati"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":137.5,"en":145.21,"si":13,"ev":"One time I danced in a culture show and the dance director at my school asked, \"Are you interested in really training? You seem to have talent.\"","uz":"Bir marta ko'rgazmada raqsga tushdim va maktabdagi raqs rahbari: \"Jiddiy shug'ullanishni xohlaysanmi? Senda iste'dod bor\", dedi.","why":"Uni bitta chiqishiga bo'lgan munosabat ilhomlantirdi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman admits that as a teenager, she","qu":"Ayol o'smirlikda ... ekanini tan oladi","o":["behaved unreasonably at times.","resented her parents' ambitions for her.","managed to keep certain feelings to herself."],"ou":["ba'zan o'zini asossiz tutgan","ota-onasining u bilan bog'liq orzularidan norozi bo'lgan","ayrim his-tuyg'ularini ichida saqlay olgan"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":155.61,"en":180.54,"si":16,"ev":"I was on the point of rebellion on more than one occasion. Though I'm happy to say that particular storm never actually broke.","uz":"Bir necha marta isyon arafasida edim. Xayriyatki, o'sha bo'ron hech qachon boshlanmadi.","why":"U ayrim his-tuyg'ularini ichida saqlagan (C).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":2.6,"e":2.6,"t":"Extract One — You hear two students talking about shopping for clothes."},{"s":2.6,"e":11.67,"t":"Recently a whole pile of my clothes got chucked out after a flatmate mistook them for rubbish. I was so upset. Oh no. Don't get me wrong, it wasn't that they held any particular significance for me"},{"s":11.83,"e":13.44,"t":"or had any great value."},{"s":13.75,"e":24.6,"t":"It was the prospect of shopping for new stuff I couldn't face. Tell me about it. Even if there's like something I need to get, my trick is to put it off to the last possible moment. So I'll have less chance to waste time on such a-"},{"s":24.75,"e":26.11,"t":"pointless activity."},{"s":26.3,"e":41.28,"t":"Maybe that's why people think our clothes are rubbish. Yeah, but what gets me is that I reckon for a lot of people the clothes aren't the point. It's more about the act of shopping. It's heavily linked to wanting to be the centre of attention to clothes giving them a strong personal identity or whatever."},{"s":41.88,"e":52.0,"t":"it's basically a way of showing off. Too much importance is placed on clothes and appearance, but it's not like a political issue for me, it's just a game I'm not prepared to play."},{"k":"h","s":60.02,"e":60.02,"t":"Extract Two — You hear part of an interview with a musician called Max."},{"s":60.02,"e":85.12,"t":"So was music in the blood, Max? Do you mean, did my mum play the piano? Hardly. But I was well into the charts as a boy. In all honesty, I didn't think that being number one was something completely unattainable. I had a cockiness, but I kept it hidden from my peers. I'd hear a hit record and think, \"I could do that.\" From the age of 14, I fired off loads of demo discs I made in my bedroom. I had a folder where I kept all the rejection letters I got from record labels."},{"s":85.37,"e":113.24,"t":"It might have helped to share that with somebody, but I didn't. I just sulked, then had another go. Then when you did get a contract? I was vindicated. And it was a good deal in most respects too. Funny thing was though, if after my first hit I thought I'd made it, I was soon disabused of that notion. If I was to add up everything I'd done up till that point - school, working in a factory, learning guitar, making the demos - it doesn't compare. I've had to put in a lot of effort to capitalise on that breakthrough, I can tell you."},{"k":"h","s":121.18,"e":121.18,"t":"Extract Three — You hear part of a discussion programme in which two dancers are talking about their careers."},{"s":121.18,"e":131.39,"t":"It's really interesting because I didn't dance when I was in Hong Kong. I didn't pick up dance until I went to high school in the US. And that was probably like when I was 16 years old."},{"s":132.02,"e":137.05,"t":"Again, I didn't do it consciously. It wasn't like something that I was waiting to do."},{"s":137.5,"e":145.21,"t":"One time I danced in a culture show and the dance director at my school, she asked, \"Are you interested in really training? Like, you seem to have talent.\""},{"s":145.85,"e":150.81,"t":"And at that point I was really not interested. I was an athlete, a three-season athlete."},{"s":151.42,"e":154.97,"t":"I was more interested in like hanging with the guys and doing what I was used to."},{"s":155.61,"e":180.54,"t":"But when I saw her perform, I was blown away and decided it was for me. And at college, I majored in it. I trained classically. That's so unlike my experience. I mean, I was dancing almost before I could walk. And although I wouldn't say I was pressurized into it, my parents were like behind me every step of the way. So much so that I was on the point of rebellion on more than one occasion. Though I'm happy to say that particular storm never actually broke."}]},{"n":42,"title":"Part of an interview with an author called Marian Bly","dur":552.90775,"x":[{"ps":31.58,"en":90.14,"c":"You hear part of an interview with an author called Marian Bly."},{"ps":183.74,"en":250.46,"c":"You hear two people on a radio program Talking about consumerism."},{"ps":357.43,"en":451.42,"c":"You hear part of an interview with Kizaya Tavola. the organiser of an exhibition of TAPA. kind of decorated cloth."}],"items":[{"q":"Marian mentions the woman in Brighton in order to show how people","qu":"Marian Braytondagi ayolni odamlar qanday ... ekanini ko'rsatish uchun tilga oladi","o":["seem to find tragedy in fiction very appealing","tend to forget that they are reading fiction, not fact","want something in common with the writer they read"],"ou":["badiiy asardagi fojiani juda jozibali deb bilishini","haqiqatni emas, to'qimani o'qiyotganlarini unutib qo'yishini","o'qiyotgan yozuvchisi bilan umumiy jihat bo'lishini xohlashini"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":42.3,"en":64.41,"si":5,"ev":"A woman came up to me recently… and asked if I'd ever tried to make contact with the child I've given away for adoption… she'd wanted to exchange stories… and thought I was someone who could relate to her.","uz":"Yaqinda bir ayol oldimga kelib, asrandi qilib bergan farzandim bilan bog'lanishga harakat qilganmisiz deb so'radi… u o'z hikoyasini bo'lishmoqchi va meni uni tushunadigan odam deb o'ylagan ekan.","why":"Odamlar o'qigan yozuvchisi bilan umumiy jihat bo'lishini xohlaydi (C). B — tuzoq: ayol badiiy asarni haqiqat deb o'ylagan bo'lsa ham, Marian maqsadi bu emas.","hl":null},{"q":"What does Marian say about the increasing public interest in stories about suffering?","qu":"Marian iztirob haqidagi hikoyalarga jamoatchilik qiziqishining ortishi haqida nima deydi?","o":["it is probably a temporary trend","it shows that people are generally unhappy","publishing companies are responsible for it"],"ou":["bu, ehtimol, vaqtinchalik moda","bu odamlarning umuman baxtsizligini ko'rsatadi","bunga nashriyotlar sababchi"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":74.52,"en":85.69,"si":9,"ev":"I think the world's become a rather depressing place for many people and it's comforting for them to read about the misfortunes of others… probably not a trend that's likely to go away.","uz":"Menimcha, ko'pchilik uchun dunyo ancha tushkun joyga aylangan va boshqalarning baxtsizligi haqida o'qish ularga taskin beradi… bu moda tez o'tib ketmasa kerak.","why":"Bu odamlarning umuman baxtsizligini ko'rsatadi (B). Vaqtinchalik moda emas (A); nashriyotlar aybdor emas (C).","hl":null},{"q":"What does the man imply when he describes his shopping trip?","qu":"Erkak xarid qilishga borganini tasvirlaganda nimaga ishora qiladi?","o":["children expect to receive more material things nowadays","parents are buying gifts instead of spending time with children","packaging has become far more sophisticated than it used to be"],"ou":["hozir bolalar ko'proq moddiy narsalar olishni kutadi","ota-onalar bolalar bilan vaqt o'tkazish o'rniga sovg'a sotib olmoqda","qadoqlash avvalgidan ancha murakkablashgan"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":185.4,"en":209.63,"si":14,"ev":"Now I looked at toys when I was a kid, but I never thought my mum would actually buy anything… he's gonna scream if he doesn't get it.","uz":"Bolaligimda men ham o'yinchoqlarga qarardim, lekin onam sotib oladi deb o'ylamasdim… u esa olmasa, qichqirib yuboradi.","why":"Hozir bolalar ko'proq moddiy narsalar olishni kutadi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"The woman says that people do not return goods to stores because they","qu":"Ayolning aytishicha, odamlar mollarni do'konga qaytarmaydi, chunki ular","o":["forget to keep their receipts","doubt they will get their money back","did not pay much for them"],"ou":["cheklarini saqlashni unutadi","pulini qaytarib olishiga shubha qiladi","ular uchun ko'p pul to'lamagan"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":236.22,"en":246.94,"si":20,"ev":"The simple fact of the matter is that we can't be bothered. We can now buy a lot for little money.","uz":"Gap shundaki, biz bunga erinamiz. Endi oz pulga ko'p narsa sotib olishimiz mumkin.","why":"Ular buyum uchun ko'p pul to'lamagan (C). Chek (A) — \"as long as they've got proof of payment\", lekin sabab bu emas.","hl":null},{"q":"According to Kesaia, what led to the decline of tapa-making in Hawaii?","qu":"Kesaianing fikricha, Gavayida tapa (daraxt po'stlog'idan mato) tayyorlash nega so'ndi?","o":["the availability of other material","the migration of Hawaiian communities","the preference amongst native Hawaiians for European fashion"],"ou":["boshqa materiallarning paydo bo'lishi","Gavayi jamoalarining ko'chib ketishi","mahalliy gavayiliklarning Yevropa modasini afzal ko'rishi"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":376.12,"en":403.58,"si":29,"ev":"The craft of tapa making nearly died out… They brought cotton with them, and this was welcomed with a great deal of enthusiasm. It was much easier to work with.","uz":"Tapa tayyorlash hunari deyarli yo'qolib ketdi… Ular o'zlari bilan paxta olib kelishdi va u katta ishtiyoq bilan kutib olindi. U bilan ishlash ancha oson edi.","why":"Boshqa materialning paydo bo'lishi (A). Missionerlar (C emas) — kiyimni emas, marosimdagi foydalanishni yoqtirishmagan.","hl":null},{"q":"What does Kesaia say is behind the resumed interest in tapa-making?","qu":"Kesaianing aytishicha, tapa tayyorlashga qiziqishning qayta tiklanishi ortida nima turibdi?","o":["a sense of cultural pride","the need for financial security","increased demand from tourists."],"ou":["madaniy g'urur hissi","moliyaviy barqarorlikka ehtiyoj","sayyohlar talabining ortishi"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":433.21,"en":440.32,"si":37,"ev":"They rely on it for survival. I mean, the income it brings in. It can support a whole family.","uz":"Ular undan tirikchilik uchun foydalanadi — keltiradigan daromadi bilan butun oilani boqsa bo'ladi.","why":"Moliyaviy barqarorlik zarurati (B). Sayyohlar (C) — \"it's sold to local people rather than holiday makers\".","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":31.58,"e":31.58,"t":"Extract One — You hear part of an interview with an author called Marian Bly."},{"s":31.58,"e":32.09,"t":"Marion"},{"s":32.57,"e":35.65,"t":"Is there ever an autobiographical element to your work?"},{"s":36.12,"e":37.12,"t":"Definitely not."},{"s":37.56,"e":41.69,"t":"But people seem desperate to believe it and look for anything that can connect you to them."},{"s":42.3,"e":48.86,"t":"A woman came up to me recently while I was in Brighton and asked if I'd ever tried to make contact with the child I've given away for adoption."},{"s":49.46,"e":56.45,"t":"I had to tell her I'd never had a child, and she looked at first astounded and then rather angry with me as if I'd lied to her."},{"s":57.02,"e":64.41,"t":"And I realised she'd wanted to exchange stories that she'd given away a child and thought I was someone who could relate to her."},{"s":65.91,"e":74.05,"t":"There seems to be a growing interest in autobiographies of people who've had absolutely terrible lives. True. And many of them are best sellers."},{"s":74.52,"e":80.86,"t":"I think the world's become a rather depressing place for many people and it's comforting for them to read about the misfortunes of others."},{"s":81.37,"e":85.69,"t":"Not that that's a good thing, mind you, but it's probably not a trend that's likely to go away."},{"s":86.36,"e":90.14,"t":"For once I don't blame the publishers, they're only responding to a demand."},{"k":"h","s":183.74,"e":183.74,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two people on a radio program Talking about consumerism."},{"s":183.74,"e":184.89,"t":"you'll laugh at this"},{"s":185.4,"e":201.34,"t":"I was shopping with my five year old. We were in a rush as always, but of course he insisted on looking at the toys. Now I looked at toys when I was a kid, but I never thought my mum would actually buy anything. It was look, don't touch and wait for your birthday."},{"s":202.07,"e":209.63,"t":"Anyway, I can see my son pointing at this plastic truck in its big bright box and he's gonna scream if he doesn't get it."},{"s":210.14,"e":212.64,"t":"He's not the only one I've seen using that trick."},{"s":213.18,"e":225.21,"t":"Anyway, you know what? We get home and it's broken after 10 minutes. Yes, that sounds familiar. And I'm pretty sure, like most consumers, you didn't bother going back to the store. You're right."},{"s":225.69,"e":229.15,"t":"Why do people put up with substandard products nowadays?"},{"s":229.88,"e":235.61,"t":"people are usually entitled to a refund if they want one as long as they've got proof of payment"},{"s":236.22,"e":239.39,"t":"The simple fact of the matter is that we can't be bothered."},{"s":240.18,"e":246.94,"t":"We can now buy a lot for little money. We've got used to buying inexpensive, easily replaceable things."},{"s":247.77,"e":250.46,"t":"That's an expensive way to do things in the long run."},{"k":"h","s":357.43,"e":357.43,"t":"Extract Three — You hear part of an interview with Kizaya Tavola. the organiser of an exhibition of TAPA. kind of decorated cloth."},{"s":357.43,"e":358.11,"t":"Asaya"},{"s":358.62,"e":361.02,"t":"Where do these beautiful cloths come from?"},{"s":361.46,"e":363.87,"t":"These here from Hawaii."},{"s":364.44,"e":371.07,"t":"These from Fiji and here these ones from Tonga and Samoa."},{"s":371.99,"e":375.23,"t":"The pieces are quite old, but nicely preserved."},{"s":376.12,"e":393.63,"t":"One of the reasons why we don't see so many examples from the more recent past is that the craft of tapa making nearly died out in some of these places, especially in Hawaii, what with the arrival of the Europeans and their effect on society."},{"s":394.17,"e":400.25,"t":"You see, they brought cotton with them, and this was welcomed with a great deal of enthusiasm."},{"s":400.86,"e":403.58,"t":"It was much easier to work with C."},{"s":404.12,"e":412.09,"t":"And, of course, the European missionaries did not like the way tapa cloth was worn in religious ceremonies."},{"s":412.6,"e":417.89,"t":"Not at all. But I believe there's a bit of a revival of this craft going on."},{"s":418.74,"e":420.8,"t":"That's true to an extent."},{"s":421.34,"e":426.11,"t":"In Fiji, for example, some women I know are making tapir again."},{"s":426.74,"e":432.64,"t":"They learnt the skill from their grandmothers and now they're teaching their daughters."},{"s":433.21,"e":440.32,"t":"They rely on it for survival. I mean, the income it brings in. It can support a whole family."},{"s":440.89,"e":446.05,"t":"in the main, it's sold to local people rather than holiday makers."},{"s":446.55,"e":451.42,"t":"I'm glad that it's one cultural tradition that isn't going to die out."}]},{"n":43,"title":"Part of an interview with an environmental campaigner called Richard Frost","dur":587.728938,"x":[{"ps":31.8,"en":117.69,"c":"You hear part of an interview with an environmental campaigner called Richard Frost."},{"ps":239.83,"en":311.1,"c":"You hear two people on a radio programme talking about the subject of hypnotherapy."},{"ps":420.5,"en":499.13,"c":"you hear part of an interview with a woman called Fiona, who works as a zoo tour guide."}],"items":[{"q":"Why did businessman Kwabena Osei Bonsu set up Trashy Bags?","qu":"Tadbirkor Kwabena Osei Bonsu nega \"Trashy Bags\"ni tashkil qildi?","o":["He wanted to solve a problem.","He had seen a similar project overseas.","He was given government funding."],"ou":["U bir muammoni hal qilmoqchi edi.","U chet elda shunga o'xshash loyihani ko'rgan edi.","Unga davlat mablag'i ajratilgan edi."],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":69.69,"en":93.89,"si":6,"ev":"Kwabena had decided he wasn't going to wait around. He says he wanted to come up with an idea that would sort out this awful situation in his lifetime.","uz":"Kvabena kutib o'tirmaslikka qaror qildi. U bu dahshatli vaziyatni o'z umrida hal qiladigan g'oya topmoqchi bo'lganini aytadi.","why":"U bir muammoni hal qilmoqchi edi (A). Davlat mablag'i (C) — \"should be sponsored\", lekin berilmagan.","hl":null},{"q":"What does Richard Frost say about the use of plastic bags in supermarkets?","qu":"Richard Frost supermarketlarda plastik paketlardan foydalanish haqida nima deydi?","o":["Customers should be made to pay for them.","The government will eventually have to disallow it.","Supermarkets should offer other kinds of bag instead."],"ou":["Mijozlarni ular uchun pul to'lashga majbur qilish kerak.","Oxir-oqibat hukumat uni taqiqlashga majbur bo'ladi.","Supermarketlar o'rniga boshqa turdagi sumkalarni taklif qilishi kerak."],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":73.3,"en":117.69,"si":7,"ev":"I can't see our government going as far as banning them… such a small charge doesn't put most people off… it's up to the supermarkets to start promoting [other bags] a bit more actively.","uz":"Hukumatimiz ularni taqiqlashgacha boradi deb o'ylamayman… bunday kichik to'lov ko'pchilikni to'xtatmaydi… boshqa sumkalarni faolroq taklif qilish supermarketlarning vazifasi.","why":"Supermarketlar boshqa sumkalarni taklif qilishi kerak (C). Taqiq (B) — \"I can't see our government going as far as banning them\".","hl":null},{"q":"What did the woman think about hypnotism before she visited a hypnotherapist?","qu":"Gipnoterapevtga borishdan oldin ayol gipnoz haqida nima deb o'ylagan?","o":["She doubted it would permanently stop a bad habit","She believed it could treat psychological issues","She thought it might work for people who believed in it"],"ou":["U yomon odatni butunlay to'xtatishiga shubha qilgan","U ruhiy muammolarni davolay oladi deb hisoblagan","U faqat unga ishonganlarga ta'sir qilishi mumkin deb o'ylagan"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":249.82,"en":268.0,"si":13,"ev":"I've always been fairly open-minded when it comes to hypnotherapy, at least when it came to dealing with psychological problems… I didn't think it would work for actual physical symptoms.","uz":"Gipnoterapiyaga, hech bo'lmaganda ruhiy muammolarda, doim ochiq qaraganman… Jismoniy alomatlarga ta'sir qiladi deb o'ylamagandim.","why":"Ruhiy muammolarni davolay oladi deb hisoblagan (B).","hl":null},{"q":"The two speakers agree that many people","qu":"Ikki so'zlovchi ko'p odamlar ... degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["have a negative image of hypnotists.","are not in control of themselves during hypnosis.","are disappointed with the results of hypnotherapy."],"ou":["gipnozchilar haqida salbiy tasavvurga ega","gipnoz paytida o'zini nazorat qila olmaydi","gipnoterapiya natijalaridan hafsalasi pir bo'ladi"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":268.82,"en":300.89,"si":16,"ev":"A lot of people see celebrity hypnotists on TV embarrassing people… people are put off going to see genuine hypnotherapists because they think anyone who practices hypnotism is not trustworthy. — I think you're right.","uz":"Ko'pchilik televizorda mashhur gipnozchilarning odamlarni sharmanda qilishini ko'radi… shu sababli ular haqiqiy gipnoterapevtlarga bormaydi — gipnozchilarga ishonib bo'lmaydi deb o'ylashadi. — Haqsiz.","why":"Ko'pchilik gipnozchilar haqida salbiy tasavvurga ega (A). B — \"I can tell you it's not like that\".","hl":null},{"q":"What does Fiona say about visitors who go on zoo tours?","qu":"Fiona hayvonot bog'i sayohatiga boradiganlar haqida nima deydi?","o":["They encounter some animals for the first time","They have strong preferences about which animals to see","They are unaware of the potential danger"],"ou":["Ular ba'zi hayvonlarni birinchi marta ko'radi","Qaysi hayvonlarni ko'rish bo'yicha aniq xohishlari bor","Ehtimoliy xavfdan bexabar"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":449.94,"en":476.7,"si":25,"ev":"Even though you do warn people about them, they just don't realise what could happen. I mean, even the cheetahs look so docile and so cuddly.","uz":"Ogohlantirsangiz ham, ular nima bo'lishi mumkinligini anglamaydi. Hatto gepardlar ham juda yuvosh va yoqimtoy ko'rinadi.","why":"Mehmonlar xavfdan bexabar (C). Hayvonlarni yaxshi bilishadi (A emas) — \"they've been going to the zoo for years\".","hl":null},{"q":"How did Fiona feel after the incident with the chimpanzee?","qu":"Shimpanze bilan bo'lgan voqeadan keyin Fiona qanday his qildi?","o":["She was reluctant to work with chimpanzees again.","She realized that she needed to be more careful at work","She was uncertain why the incident had occurred"],"ou":["Shimpanzelar bilan qayta ishlashni istamadi.","Ishda ehtiyotkorroq bo'lishi kerakligini angladi","Voqea nega sodir bo'lganini aniq bilmadi"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":484.38,"en":494.43,"si":27,"ev":"From that moment on I've always been doubly aware of how close I am to an animal and what tools it has to get to me.","uz":"O'sha paytdan beri hayvonga qanchalik yaqin ekanim va u menga yetish uchun qanday vositalarga ega ekaniga ikki baravar e'tiborliman.","why":"Ishda ehtiyotkorroq bo'lishi kerakligini angladi (B).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":31.8,"e":31.8,"t":"Extract One — You hear part of an interview with an environmental campaigner called Richard Frost."},{"s":31.8,"e":32.51,"t":"Richard"},{"s":32.98,"e":47.55,"t":"Can you give us an example of what people in other countries are doing in terms of recycling? Absolutely. Well, 60 tons of plastic packaging are dumped on the streets of Accra, the capital city of Ghana, every day."},{"s":47.99,"e":55.26,"t":"But recently, a businessman called Kwabena Osei Bonsu set up a company called Trashy Bags to do something about it."},{"s":56.02,"e":61.02,"t":"pays people to collect plastic bags and these are stitched together to make new ones."},{"s":61.53,"e":68.99,"t":"This kind of venture should be sponsored by governments and there are plenty of similar projects occurring in other countries if they need ideas."},{"s":69.69,"e":72.83,"t":"Cuabena had decided he wasn't going to wait around."},{"s":73.3,"e":93.89,"t":"He says he wanted to come up with an idea that would sort out this awful situation in his lifetime. That's fantastic. What about here though? I suppose you'd like to stop the use of plastic bags in supermarkets completely. Well, yes. They are an absolute environmental disaster, but I can't see our government going as far as banning them."},{"s":94.58,"e":103.01,"t":"I know that some supermarkets are charging customers 5 or 10 pence per bag, but such a small charge doesn't put most people off."},{"s":103.51,"e":117.69,"t":"Actually, you can get bags made of bamboo or other fabrics, but only a minority of people are using them. So I'd say it's up to the supermarkets to start promoting them a bit more actively, so that customers know they're available to buy instead."},{"k":"h","s":239.83,"e":239.83,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two people on a radio programme talking about the subject of hypnotherapy."},{"s":239.83,"e":243.04,"t":"You've just had a few sessions of hypnotherapy, haven't you?"},{"s":243.7,"e":249.37,"t":"I have to say, I didn't think you were into that kind of thing. Mmm, you thought I was the skeptical type."},{"s":249.82,"e":260.96,"t":"Well, I've never been a believer in most alternative therapies, but I've always been fairly open-minded when it comes to hypnotherapy, at least when it came to dealing with psychological problems."},{"s":261.5,"e":261.92,"t":"I mean"},{"s":262.39,"e":268.0,"t":"Before I experienced hypnotism for myself, I didn't think it would work for actual physical symptoms."},{"s":268.82,"e":284.67,"t":"I went along because I wanted to quit smoking, but Dr Gray helped me overcome my back pain too. I guess a lot of people see celebrity hypnotists on TV embarrassing people they've hypnotised making them do ridiculous things."},{"s":285.21,"e":300.89,"t":"And I think the result of that is that people are put off going to see genuine hypnotherapists because they think anyone who practices hypnotism is not trustworthy. Mm-hmm. I think you're right. But people should know that hypnotherapy is a serious profession."},{"s":301.46,"e":306.08,"t":"And if the idea of being under someone else's control makes you nervous..."},{"s":306.55,"e":308.41,"t":"I can tell you it's not like that."},{"s":309.08,"e":311.1,"t":"always aware of what's going on."},{"k":"h","s":420.5,"e":420.5,"t":"Extract Three — you hear part of an interview with a woman called Fiona, who works as a zoo tour guide."},{"s":420.5,"e":426.75,"t":"Fiona, how is it working with visitors to the zoo? The public? Generally they're fantastic."},{"s":427.35,"e":441.73,"t":"Maybe they're a little bit quiet to start with because they're not sure what they're going to do but soon after we've met the rhinos or we've started doing the monkeys they normally open up and they're all, oh this is fantastic."},{"s":442.23,"e":449.28,"t":"They start asking questions and they know a lot about the animals anyway because they've been going to the zoo for years."},{"s":449.94,"e":476.7,"t":"But the hardest thing for me is being constantly alert to the risks because even though you do warn people about them, they just don't realise what could happen. I mean, even the cheetahs look so docile and so cuddly. Have you ever had an incident yourself? No, not exactly. But I did get a bit too close to the bars of the chimpanzee enclosure once. And the chimps had branches with them to try and get food from beyond the bars."},{"s":477.11,"e":483.84,"t":"and one of the male chimps basically just reaped through the bars with his branch and poked me in the ribs and it was basically a \"get f***ing out!\""},{"s":484.38,"e":494.43,"t":"my food! And from that moment on I've always been doubly aware of how close I am to an animal and what tools it has to get to me as well."},{"s":495.38,"e":499.13,"t":"He could have been a lot nastier than he was, it was just a warning."}]},{"n":44,"title":"Part of an interview with James Finn, a young musician","dur":573.884063,"x":[{"ps":49.05,"en":129.21,"c":"You hear part of an interview with James Finn, a young musician."},{"ps":247.03,"en":310.56,"c":"You hear part of an interview with Martin Greenwood, an education specialist."},{"ps":412.86,"en":486.37,"c":"You hear part of an interview with a woman called Shelly Sumner. appeared on a TV reality show."}],"items":[{"q":"James no longer owns a television because he","qu":"James endi televizor saqlamaydi, chunki u","o":["dislikes the immoral content of some of the programmes","is irritated by the frequency of the advertisements","feels that he becomes too easily absorbed in watching it"],"ou":["ba'zi dasturlarning axloqsiz mazmunini yoqtirmaydi","reklamalarning tez-tez chiqishidan jahli chiqadi","uni ko'rishga haddan tashqari oson berilib ketishini sezadi"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":85.59,"en":97.41,"si":9,"ev":"Not having one lets me appreciate how addictive I did find it. Like, if I went to a house and the TV was on, I'd find myself drawn to that and drawn out of the conversation.","uz":"Televizorsiz yashash unga qanchalik bog'lanib qolganimni anglashga yordam berdi. Biror uyga borsam va televizor yoniq bo'lsa, o'zimni unga tortilib, suhbatdan chiqib qolganimni sezardim.","why":"U televizorga osonlikcha berilib ketadi (C). Axloqiy sabab (A) — \"I haven't taken a particularly moral step\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is James' opinion about the future of television?","qu":"James televideniyening kelajagi haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["it will be replaced by the Internet","it will become increasingly commercial","it will show more and more poor quality programmes"],"ou":["uning o'rnini internet egallaydi","u tobora tijoratlashib boradi","u tobora ko'proq sifatsiz dasturlar ko'rsatadi"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":106.17,"en":118.56,"si":12,"ev":"I'd be willing to bet that TV is coming to the end of its lifespan… Eventually, all digital media will go onto the internet.","uz":"Garov o'ynashga tayyorman: televideniyening umri tugab bormoqda… Oxir-oqibat barcha raqamli media internetga o'tadi.","why":"Uning o'rnini internet egallaydi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"What does Martin blame for the lack of male teachers in secondary education?","qu":"Martin o'rta ta'limda erkak o'qituvchilar kamligini nimaga to'nkaydi?","o":["the low salary","the lack of status","the perception that it is a female job"],"ou":["past maosh","obro' yetishmasligi","bu ayollar ishi degan tasavvur"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":270.94,"en":284.25,"si":22,"ev":"I think the image of the teaching profession in our society is pretty poor. No one wants to go to work and be disrespected.","uz":"Menimcha, jamiyatimizda o'qituvchilik kasbining obro'si ancha past. Hech kim ishga borib, hurmatsizlikka uchrashni istamaydi.","why":"Obro' yetishmasligi (B). Maosh (A) — hukumat buni yaxshilagan.","hl":null},{"q":"Martin mentions the argument in the playground to illustrate","qu":"Martin maydonchadagi janjalni ... ni ko'rsatish uchun tilga oladi","o":["the lack of control some female teachers have over male students","the different ways men and women handle conflict","the fact that boys need to be taught how to manage aggression"],"ou":["ba'zi ayol o'qituvchilar o'g'il bolalarni nazorat qila olmasligini","erkaklar va ayollar nizoni turlicha hal qilishini","o'g'il bolalarga tajovuzkorlikni boshqarishni o'rgatish kerakligini"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":299.0,"en":310.56,"si":27,"ev":"One of the female staff went running over and told them both off for being violent. But a male teacher would have known they had to sort things out for themselves.","uz":"Ayol xodimlardan biri yugurib borib, ikkalasini zo'ravonlik uchun koyidi. Lekin erkak o'qituvchi ular masalani o'zlari hal qilishi kerakligini bilardi.","why":"Erkaklar va ayollar nizoni turlicha hal qiladi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"Shelley says she decided to take part in the reality show because she","qu":"Shelley realiti-shouda qatnashishga qaror qilganini aytadi, chunki u","o":["needed the prize money that was offered","was attracted by the idea of fame","felt pressured into it by her friends"],"ou":["taklif qilingan mukofot puliga muhtoj edi","shuhrat g'oyasi uni o'ziga tortdi","do'stlari bosim o'tkazganini his qildi"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":424.5,"en":452.0,"si":33,"ev":"It was actually for a dare. I said I'd have a go at getting in if my friends Sandra and Jasmine did… they wouldn't let me quit.","uz":"Aslida bu bahs uchun edi. Do'stlarim Sandra va Jasmin ham qatnashsa, men ham urinib ko'raman dedim… ular menga voz kechishga qo'yishmadi.","why":"Do'stlari bosim o'tkazgan (C). Pul (A) — \"That's not why I did it\".","hl":null},{"q":"Why does Shelley compare herself to a new member of royalty?","qu":"Shelley nega o'zini qirollik oilasining yangi a'zosiga o'xshatadi?","o":["to show how she has lost her privacy","to show how relationships with former friends have changed","to show the advantages she has gained from celebrity"],"ou":["shaxsiy hayotini qanday yo'qotganini ko'rsatish uchun","eski do'stlari bilan munosabati qanday o'zgarganini ko'rsatish uchun","mashhurlikdan olgan afzalliklarini ko'rsatish uchun"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":464.09,"en":486.37,"si":38,"ev":"It's the tabloids that get on my nerves. I could be out doing the shopping and suddenly there's someone across the road taking your photo.","uz":"Asabimga tegadigani — sariq matbuot. Xarid qilib yurganimda, birdan ko'chaning narigi tomonida kimdir suratimni olayotgan bo'ladi.","why":"Shaxsiy hayotini yo'qotgani (A). Do'stlari o'zgarmagan (B emas): \"nothing's changed there\".","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":49.05,"e":49.05,"t":"Extract One — You hear part of an interview with James Finn, a young musician."},{"s":49.05,"e":52.38,"t":"I recently heard you say that you never watch TV."},{"s":52.82,"e":54.3,"t":"Is that right? Yep."},{"s":54.78,"e":56.29,"t":"I threw it out a while back."},{"s":57.02,"e":64.35,"t":"I'm not saying there aren't any good things about it, but the negatives outweigh the positives in terms of what it does to society."},{"s":65.18,"e":72.29,"t":"It encourages us to be passive. So although I haven't taken a particularly moral step to not have a TV,"},{"s":72.73,"e":73.95,"t":"I'm happy to do without it"},{"s":74.81,"e":80.22,"t":"TV's all about programming people to buy certain things, far more so than it used to be."},{"s":80.86,"e":85.05,"t":"And it makes us become more materialistic. Not a great value, I think."},{"s":85.59,"e":89.89,"t":"and not having one lets me appreciate how addictive I did find it."},{"s":90.42,"e":97.41,"t":"Like, if I went to a house and the TV was on, I'd find myself drawn to that and drawn out of the conversation."},{"s":98.1,"e":105.37,"t":"Don't your friends find your lack of a television set a bit... weird? Honestly, a lot of my mates don't have one either."},{"s":106.17,"e":111.97,"t":"I'd be willing to bet that TV is coming to the end of its lifespan as the major form of entertainment."},{"s":112.54,"e":118.56,"t":"Eventually, all digital media will go onto the internet. So what will be the point of having a TV?"},{"s":119.19,"e":125.85,"t":"But that's not to say that everything on the net is or will be of superior quality to what we get now on the TV."},{"s":126.46,"e":129.21,"t":"But at least you can ignore the advertising on the net."},{"k":"h","s":247.03,"e":247.03,"t":"Extract Two — You hear part of an interview with Martin Greenwood, an education specialist."},{"s":247.03,"e":252.64,"t":"Martin Greenwood, why do we need this campaign to get more male teachers into secondary schools?"},{"s":253.18,"e":254.24,"t":"Look at the ratios."},{"s":254.74,"e":259.33,"t":"For every 10 female teachers there's one male and that's been the case for too long."},{"s":259.99,"e":264.03,"t":"The government has made progress in offering better financial incentives."},{"s":264.47,"e":269.85,"t":"But the number of young men currently enrolled on teacher training courses is still depressingly low."},{"s":270.94,"e":277.53,"t":"I think the image of the teaching profession in our society is pretty poor. No one wants to go to work and be disrespected."},{"s":278.42,"e":284.25,"t":"Past and still in some cultures people look up to teachers but not here in the UK not anymore"},{"s":284.76,"e":288.57,"t":"But surely it's the quality of the teacher that counts, not the gender."},{"s":289.59,"e":290.59,"t":"Let me give you an example"},{"s":291.13,"e":298.11,"t":"I was observing a playground recently and a couple of young boys got into a bit of a fight. Not too serious, just some pushing around."},{"s":299.0,"e":303.13,"t":"One of the female staff went running over and told them both off for being violent."},{"s":303.74,"e":307.29,"t":"But a male teacher would have known they had to sort things out for themselves."},{"s":307.74,"e":310.56,"t":"They know that boys fight and then get on with things."},{"k":"h","s":412.86,"e":412.86,"t":"Extract Three — You hear part of an interview with a woman called Shelly Sumner. appeared on a TV reality show."},{"s":412.86,"e":416.8,"t":"It's been what, two months since you won the show, Shelley?"},{"s":417.4,"e":424.06,"t":"Have you spent all the prize money yet? Yeah, that soon went. It wasn't a lot in the first place."},{"s":424.5,"e":427.87,"t":"That's not why I did it. It was actually for a dare."},{"s":428.38,"e":433.18,"t":"I said I'd have a go at getting in if my friends Sandra and Jasmine did."},{"s":434.2,"e":441.44,"t":"You know, you have to send in a video, you talking about yourself, that kind of thing, but I never thought I'd hear back."},{"s":442.17,"e":452.0,"t":"And then someone from the show rang me up and I'd got an interview. And when the others found out, even though they hadn't got onto the show, they wouldn't let me quit."},{"s":452.47,"e":463.01,"t":"They like the idea of having a famous mate. And are you still seeing those same people or have you moved up in the world? No, nothing's changed there. We still hang out together."},{"s":464.09,"e":476.06,"t":"I do feel like a new member of the royal family sometimes. Well, it's not like I'm getting into exclusive restaurants for free, but it's the tabloids that get on my nerves."},{"s":476.54,"e":481.85,"t":"I could be out doing the shopping and suddenly there's someone across the road taking your photo."},{"s":482.39,"e":486.37,"t":"Basically, it's quite intrusive, but I guess that's what happens."}]},{"n":45,"title":"Two people on a radio program discussing the effect of price on consumers","dur":640.208938,"x":[{"ps":32.89,"en":129.89,"c":"you hear two people on a radio program discussing the effect of price on consumers."},{"ps":265.94,"en":348.13,"c":"You hear part of an interview with a woman called Petra Davies who is training for a marathon"},{"ps":470.97,"en":551.39,"c":"You hear two people on a radio program Thinking about the idea of educating children at home."}],"items":[{"q":"If the woman had known the real cost of her hotel room, she says she would have","qu":"Ayolning aytishicha, mehmonxona xonasining asl narxini bilganida u ...","o":["chosen another hotel.","appreciated her stay more.","hidden the price from her husband."],"ou":["boshqa mehmonxonani tanlagan bo'lardi","u yerda bo'lishini ko'proq qadrlagan bo'lardi","narxni eridan yashirgan bo'lardi"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":68.6,"en":84.22,"si":8,"ev":"I actually felt cheated out of a better experience. My husband had been enjoying a really expensive weekend, and I hadn't.","uz":"Aslida o'zimni yaxshiroq taassurotdan mahrum qilingandek his qildim. Erim haqiqatan qimmat dam olish kunlaridan zavqlangan, men esa yo'q.","why":"Narxni bilganida, dam olishni ko'proq qadrlagan bo'lardi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What do the two speakers agree about?","qu":"Ikki so'zlovchi nima haqida bir fikrda?","o":["expensive wine is worth the money for the effect it creates.","people tend to trust scientific researchers too easily.","it is usually luxury items that people are happy to pay high prices for."],"ou":["qimmat vino beradigan taassuroti uchun pulga arziydi","odamlar olimlarga juda oson ishonib qoladi","odamlar odatda hashamatli buyumlar uchun yuqori narx to'lashdan xursand bo'ladi"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":99.1,"en":123.68,"si":13,"ev":"In a sense, I suppose people should buy expensive wine if it really gives them additional pleasure… And if paying $45 for wine makes you happy, why not?","uz":"Ma'lum ma'noda, agar qimmat vino haqiqatan qo'shimcha zavq bersa, odamlar uni sotib olishi kerak… Agar 45 dollar to'lash sizni xursand qilsa, nega yo'q?","why":"Ikkalasi qimmat vino beradigan taassuroti uchun arziydi deydi (A). C — u \"anything\" deydi, faqat hashamatli buyumlar emas.","hl":null},{"q":"Petra was reluctant to do much running in her training because she","qu":"Petra mashg'ulotlarida ko'p yugurishni istamagan, chunki u","o":["found it had not been an effective strategy before.","was still suffering from an injury.","did not want to put in the effort it required."],"ou":["bu avval samarali usul bo'lmaganini ko'rgan","hali ham jarohatdan aziyat chekayotgan edi","u talab qiladigan kuchni sarflashni istamagan"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":294.74,"en":312.03,"si":21,"ev":"I'm basically lazy and the idea of running five or six times a week doesn't actually appeal… I suppose I wanted a shortcut.","uz":"Men asosan dangasaman, haftada besh-olti marta yugurish g'oyasi menga yoqmaydi… Qisqa yo'l izlagan bo'lsam kerak.","why":"U kerakli kuchni sarflashni istamagan (C). Jarohat (B) aytilmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"According to Petra, what is Sean Deacon's attitude to preparing for a marathon?","qu":"Petraning aytishicha, Sean Deacon marafonga tayyorgarlikka qanday qaraydi?","o":["he rejects the idea of there being one correct way to train successfully.","he is insistent that athletes do long runs soon after training has started.","he believes in the importance of strength training over long-distance running."],"ou":["muvaffaqiyatli mashq qilishning yagona to'g'ri yo'li bor degan g'oyani rad etadi","sportchilar mashg'ulot boshlanishi bilanoq uzoq masofaga yugurishini talab qiladi","kuch mashqlari uzoq masofaga yugurishdan muhimroq deb hisoblaydi"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":312.57,"en":339.42,"si":24,"ev":"He encourages people to work on improving their overall strength before they go anywhere near an actual long run.","uz":"U odamlarni uzoq masofaga yugurishdan oldin umumiy kuchini oshirishga undaydi.","why":"Kuch mashqlari uzoq masofaga yugurishdan muhimroq (C). A — boshqa yuguruvchilarning fikri.","hl":null},{"q":"What is the woman's opinion of traditional school education?","qu":"Ayol an'anaviy maktab ta'limi haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["it is essential as it demonstrates school leavers' academic ability.","it is not a suitable form of education for all children.","it does not encourage children's imagination to develop."],"ou":["u bitiruvchilarning akademik qobiliyatini ko'rsatgani uchun zarur","u hamma bolalar uchun mos ta'lim shakli emas","u bolalar tasavvurining rivojlanishiga yordam bermaydi"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":502.26,"en":508.09,"si":34,"ev":"Of course, there are children who shouldn't be there. It just doesn't suit their learning style.","uz":"Albatta, u yerda bo'lmasligi kerak bo'lgan bolalar ham bor. Bu ularning o'rganish uslubiga mos kelmaydi.","why":"An'anaviy ta'lim hamma bolalar uchun mos emas (B). C — aksincha, unda ijodkorlik imkoni bo'lgan.","hl":null},{"q":"What does the man conclude about 'unschooling'?","qu":"Erkak \"maktabsiz ta'lim\" (unschooling) haqida qanday xulosaga keladi?","o":["it is unproven whether 'unschooling' is better than schooling.","'unschooling' will become an increasingly popular form of education.","Being educated at home may cause children to lack social skills."],"ou":["\"maktabsiz ta'lim\" maktabdan yaxshiroq ekani isbotlanmagan","\"maktabsiz ta'lim\" tobora ommalashib boradi","Uyda ta'lim olish bolalarda ijtimoiy ko'nikmalar yetishmasligiga olib kelishi mumkin"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":534.81,"en":548.0,"si":39,"ev":"There's not been a proper study into how successful it actually is. Also, I can't imagine it'll really catch on with many parents.","uz":"U qanchalik muvaffaqiyatli ekani haqida jiddiy tadqiqot o'tkazilmagan. Qolaversa, ko'p ota-onalar buni qabul qilishini tasavvur qila olmayman.","why":"Maktabdan yaxshiroq ekani isbotlanmagan (A). B — aksincha: \"can't imagine it'll really catch on\".","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":32.89,"e":32.89,"t":"Extract One — you hear two people on a radio program discussing the effect of price on consumers."},{"s":32.89,"e":34.97,"t":"How did your anniversary weekend go, Jennifer?"},{"s":36.09,"e":39.97,"t":"You know, Tom and I went to a hotel I found on the internet."},{"s":40.54,"e":42.91,"t":"And we had a perfectly nice time there."},{"s":43.86,"e":49.41,"t":"When it was over and I went to pay, I realized I hadn't looked closely enough at the price."},{"s":50.2,"e":53.5,"t":"It wasn't for the two of us, it was per person."},{"s":54.36,"e":60.32,"t":"I went back to our suddenly twice as expensive room and I had to confess to my husband."},{"s":61.43,"e":67.07,"t":"Actually, he'd known the price all along and said not to worry and that we could afford it."},{"s":68.6,"e":73.98,"t":"wasn't the point. I actually felt cheated out of a better experience."},{"s":74.58,"e":78.27,"t":"My husband had been enjoying a really expensive weekend"},{"s":78.71,"e":84.22,"t":"And I hadn't. Well, researchers at Stanford University wouldn't be surprised at that."},{"s":84.86,"e":94.69,"t":"They asked people to try a wine marked with a five dollar price tag and then one with a forty-five dollar price tag. And, of course, they preferred the more expensive one."},{"s":95.19,"e":98.46,"t":"even though the wine came from the same five dollar bottle."},{"s":99.1,"e":104.64,"t":"In a sense, I suppose people should buy expensive wine if it really gives them additional pleasure."},{"s":105.3,"e":118.94,"t":"And they did the same experiment with painkillers with the same results. Yes, I'd say people will pay more for anything, whether it's a fast car or a packet of potato chips, if they think it's better quality."},{"s":119.58,"e":123.68,"t":"And if paying $45 for wine makes you happy, why not?"},{"s":124.5,"e":127.68,"t":"Don't you think some of these experiments are misleading, though?"},{"s":128.28,"e":129.89,"t":"I mean the way they're set up."},{"k":"h","s":265.94,"e":265.94,"t":"Extract Two — You hear part of an interview with a woman called Petra Davies who is training for a marathon"},{"s":265.94,"e":280.25,"t":"Um Petra, you've been in training for the marathon for 12 weeks now. What advice would you give would be runners? Well for a start, if you've never done a race before, like me, you have to go and get yourself a good fitness trainer."},{"s":280.89,"e":294.08,"t":"It helps keep up the motivation and if you want to avoid painful blisters and swollen ankles and that kind of thing, you're best off finding someone who knows what they're doing and can work out the right training plan for you."},{"s":294.74,"e":303.84,"t":"look, I'm the first to admit that I'm basically lazy and that the idea of running five or six times a week doesn't actually appeal."},{"s":304.34,"e":307.9,"t":"So I was more than pleased when I found out I didn't have to."},{"s":308.57,"e":312.03,"t":"I suppose I wanted a shortcut to being a marathon runner."},{"s":312.57,"e":323.39,"t":"Can you explain what you mean by that? Yes. My fitness trainer, Sean Deacon. He's very much against people wearing themselves out before they even get to the day of the marathon."},{"s":323.93,"e":339.42,"t":"He encourages people to work on improving their overall strength before they go anywhere near an actual long run. So I was doing tons of sit-ups and press-ups and weightlifting, that kind of thing, before I did any kind of practice running at all."},{"s":340.22,"e":345.89,"t":"I've heard other runners say you've got to train the way you feel best, by instinct almost."},{"s":346.58,"e":348.13,"t":"That wouldn't have worked for me."},{"k":"h","s":470.97,"e":470.97,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people on a radio program Thinking about the idea of educating children at home."},{"s":470.97,"e":476.22,"t":"What do you think of the idea of being educated at home, or unschooling as it's been called?"},{"s":476.73,"e":482.69,"t":"Yes, I think unschooling was first used by the American educator John Holt."},{"s":483.45,"e":489.53,"t":"He rather saw schools as prisons where children were bored and weren't in charge of their own development."},{"s":490.26,"e":491.87,"t":"Personally, I loved school."},{"s":492.34,"e":501.41,"t":"It was a traditional education, but we had the chance to be creative through drama and story writing. And for me, it was beneficial."},{"s":502.26,"e":508.09,"t":"I mean, of course, there are children who shouldn't be there. It just doesn't suit their learning style."},{"s":508.73,"e":515.49,"t":"And I think employers are often just as impressed with personal skills as with actual qualifications nowadays."},{"s":515.93,"e":521.85,"t":"So you don't need a formal education as much as you used to, but... I can see the benefits."},{"s":522.33,"e":528.67,"t":"You get lots of individual attention and you get to interact with your family members or others in the community."},{"s":529.27,"e":533.98,"t":"I believe things like museum trips and studying things in your environment play a big part."},{"s":534.81,"e":542.88,"t":"But it's a relatively recent trend as far as educational theory goes, and there's not been a proper study into how successful it actually is."},{"s":543.51,"e":548.0,"t":"Also, I can't imagine it'll really catch on with many parents. No."},{"s":548.54,"e":551.39,"t":"A lot of us like some time away from the kids.\""}]},{"n":46,"title":"A football fan talking to a friend about a new stadium he's just been to","dur":445.910188,"x":[{"ps":32.12,"en":91.01,"c":"You overhear a football fan talking to a friend about a new stadium he's just been to."},{"ps":189.02,"en":239.55,"c":"You hear part of an interview with a presenter of a breakfast radio program."},{"ps":333.27,"en":384.25,"c":"You overhear two friends, Greg and Tamsin, discussing a newspaper article about something called a seed bank."}],"items":[{"q":"He thinks the architect's decision not to use strong colours was good because","qu":"Uning fikricha, arxitektorning yorqin ranglardan foydalanmaslik qarori to'g'ri bo'lgan, chunki","o":["the stadium has to blend in with its surroundings","it gives the stadium a more sophisticated atmosphere","the matches and crowds will provide a feeling of energy"],"ou":["stadion atrofiga moslashib ketishi kerak","bu stadionga nafisroq muhit beradi","o'yinlar va olomon o'zi g'ayrat hissini beradi"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":36.09,"en":51.97,"si":3,"ev":"It's really impressive, though surprisingly subdued when it comes to colour. The architect deliberately worked with neutral tones because he reckons that the events themselves will provide enough life and excitement.","uz":"Juda ta'sirli, lekin ranglar bo'yicha ajablanarli darajada vazmin. Arxitektor ataylab neytral ranglardan foydalangan, chunki tadbirlarning o'zi yetarlicha hayot va hayajon beradi deb hisoblaydi.","why":"O'yinlar va olomon g'ayrat hissini beradi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"He compares the new stadium to a modern airport in order to","qu":"U yangi stadionni zamonaviy aeroportga ... uchun o'xshatadi","o":["praise the quality of the facilities","emphasise the size of the building","explain how many people it can hold"],"ou":["qulayliklar sifatini maqtash","binoning kattaligini ta'kidlash","u qancha odamni sig'dira olishini tushuntirish"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":75.38,"en":84.83,"si":7,"ev":"It's got the feel of an airport, not so much because of all those lofty interiors, but because absolutely no expense has been spared in the choice of seating, washrooms and refreshment areas.","uz":"Unda aeroportdagidek tuyg'u bor — baland ichki makon tufayli emas, balki o'rindiqlar, hojatxonalar va ovqatlanish joylari uchun hech qanday xarajat ayalmagani uchun.","why":"Qulayliklar sifatini maqtash (A). Bino kattaligi (B) — \"not so much because of all those lofty interiors\".","hl":null},{"q":"How does she feel about her job?","qu":"U o'z ishi haqida qanday his qiladi?","o":["keen to continue as long as she can","fearful that she will soon be replaced","reluctant to go into work on some occasions"],"ou":["iloji boricha uzoq davom ettirishni xohlaydi","tez orada o'rniga boshqasini olishlaridan qo'rqadi","ba'zan ishga borishni istamaydi"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":189.02,"en":215.23,"si":10,"ev":"So, provided I'm healthy enough to do it, I'll carry on.","uz":"Sog'ligim yetarli bo'lsa, davom etaveraman.","why":"Iloji boricha davom ettirishni xohlaydi (A). Almashtirilishidan qo'rqmaydi (B) — \"I have no illusions about that\", bu xotirjam qabul qilish.","hl":null},{"q":"When talking about her colleague, she reveals","qu":"Hamkasbi haqida gapirganda u ... ni oshkor qiladi","o":["her amusement at his choice of language","her admiration of what he can get away with","her wish that she could be as popular as him"],"ou":["uning so'z tanlovidan kulgisi kelishini","uning nimalarni jazosiz qila olishiga qoyil qolishini","u kabi mashhur bo'lishni xohlashini"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":215.61,"en":239.55,"si":11,"ev":"He's brave enough to open his mouth without knowing what he's going to say. Yet… people rarely take offence… I've heard him do stuff that I certainly wouldn't attempt.","uz":"U nima deyishini bilmay turib og'iz ochishga jur'at qiladi. Lekin… odamlar kamdan-kam xafa bo'ladi… Men aslo urinmaydigan narsalarni qilganini eshitganman.","why":"U hamkasbi nimalarni \"jazosiz\" qila olishiga qoyil qoladi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"According to Tamsin, what is the purpose of the seed bank?","qu":"Tamsinning fikricha, urug' bankining maqsadi nima?","o":["to encourage farmers to sow older crop varieties","to ensure replacement of species which may be lost","to enable experts to produce disease-resistant plants"],"ou":["fermerlarni eski ekin navlarini ekishga undash","yo'qolishi mumkin bo'lgan turlarni qayta tiklashni ta'minlash","mutaxassislarga kasallikka chidamli o'simliklar yetishtirish imkonini berish"],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":346.2,"en":358.88,"si":14,"ev":"Farmers these days prefer modern, higher yield, disease-resistant species, so the more traditional varieties might disappear completely one day.","uz":"Hozir fermerlar zamonaviy, hosildor, kasallikka chidamli navlarni afzal ko'radi, shuning uchun an'anaviy navlar bir kun butunlay yo'qolishi mumkin.","why":"Yo'qolishi mumkin bo'lgan turlarni saqlab qolish (B). Kasallikka chidamli o'simliklar (C) — tuzoq.","hl":null},{"q":"Greg thinks that the organisers of the seed bank","qu":"Gregning fikricha, urug' banki tashkilotchilari","o":["are underestimating the security issues.","will have difficulty finding the right personnel.","have not adequately specified the procedures involved."],"ou":["xavfsizlik masalalarini kam baholamoqda","kerakli xodimlarni topishda qiynaladi","tegishli tartiblarni yetarlicha aniq belgilamagan"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":359.32,"en":376.38,"si":15,"ev":"People in charge are just going to find someone to keep an eye on the place, pass by once a week or so. I reckon they'll get caught out there.","uz":"Mas'ullar shunchaki joyga qarab turadigan, haftada bir marta kelib ketadigan kishini topishmoqchi. Menimcha, ular bunda pand yeyishadi.","why":"Greg xavfsizlik masalasi kam baholanmoqda deb o'ylaydi (A). Qorovul topish qiyin emas (B emas).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":32.12,"e":32.12,"t":"Extract One — You overhear a football fan talking to a friend about a new stadium he's just been to."},{"s":32.12,"e":34.21,"t":"So what did you think of the new stadium?"},{"s":34.65,"e":35.58,"t":"You should go."},{"s":36.09,"e":44.25,"t":"I mean it's a stadium of sporting dreams. The design is obviously very high-tech. It's really impressive, though surprisingly subdued when it comes to colour."},{"s":44.98,"e":51.97,"t":"The architects deliberately worked with neutral tones because he reckons that the events themselves will provide enough life and excitement."},{"s":52.63,"e":64.09,"t":"At night, a central tower lights up like a beacon so everyone can see not just where it is, but also how important it is, both to the local community and to the sport of football itself."},{"s":64.54,"e":74.85,"t":"And what's it like inside? It's like a kind of swooping, smooth, concrete arena, wrapped around with five levels of atrium's, walkways, cafes, shops."},{"s":75.38,"e":84.83,"t":"It's got the feel of an airport, not so much because of all those lofty interiors, but because absolutely no expense has been spared in the choice of seating, washrooms and refreshment areas."},{"s":85.4,"e":91.01,"t":"And they've got to be good because they'll have to stand up to the wear and tear that 90,000 people will impose."},{"k":"h","s":189.02,"e":189.02,"t":"Extract Two — You hear part of an interview with a presenter of a breakfast radio program."},{"s":189.02,"e":215.23,"t":"What amazes me about your radio programme is that after all these years you sound so cheerful and up for it at 6.30 in the morning. And surely there must be mornings when you think, \"I don't want to do this.\" Well, I'm a performer, aren't I? I get a buzz out of it. I mean, on dark winter mornings it can be a bit hard, but I still come in with a spring in my step. So, provided I'm healthy enough to do it, I'll carry on. But I know they'll eventually find someone younger to do the job. I have no illusions about that."},{"s":215.61,"e":239.55,"t":"one of my colleagues maybe. Well, if your colleague John took over that would be a huge change. You don't swear like he does for one thing. I rather thought you disapproved of that. Well, he's an incredible risk taker. He's brave enough to open his mouth without knowing what he's going to say. Yet, funnily enough, people rarely take offence at what comes out. You'd think they would, but in fact they like him all the more for it. I've heard him do stuff that I certainly wouldn't attempt."},{"k":"h","s":333.27,"e":333.27,"t":"Extract Three — You overhear two friends, Greg and Tamsin, discussing a newspaper article about something called a seed bank."},{"s":333.27,"e":345.76,"t":"Have you read this article, Greg, about the three million seed varieties they've stored in a vault near the North Pole? I only glanced at it, really. What's the seed bank for, then? Do you know? Back up the whole genetic diversity thing."},{"s":346.2,"e":358.88,"t":"The article says that farmers these days prefer modern, higher yield, disease-resistant species, so the more traditional varieties might disappear completely one day. I see. Sounds like a pretty valuable resource."},{"s":359.32,"e":376.38,"t":"It'll probably have loads of cameras and barbed wire and stuff to protect it. Nothing about that here. It says that people in charge are just going to find someone to keep an eye on the place, pass by once a week or so. I reckon they'll get caught out there. Not that it'll be hard to find a suitable caretaker if that's all you have to do."},{"s":376.82,"e":384.25,"t":"So have they decided actually how and when they'll supply the seeds? There's a whole paragraph on that. Here, you can read it. Alright, thanks."}]},{"n":47,"title":"Two people on a radio programme discussing music education for children","dur":471.7975,"x":[{"ps":25.59,"en":94.17,"c":"You hear two people on a radio programme discussing music education for children."},{"ps":177.02,"en":239.2,"c":"You hear part of an interview with a rock climber called Ben."},{"ps":316.7,"en":390.08,"c":"You hear part of an interview with a restaurant critic called Amanda Downing."}],"items":[{"q":"They agree that young children should","qu":"Ular kichik bolalar ... kerak degan fikrga qo'shiladi","o":["learn an instrument that requires a lot of concentration.","be started on instruction at an early age.","focus largely on music theory."],"ou":["ko'p diqqat talab qiladigan cholg'uni o'rganishi","erta yoshdan o'qitila boshlanishi","asosan musiqa nazariyasiga e'tibor berishi"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":25.59,"en":70.3,"si":1,"ev":"The optimum time to start music education is between the ages of three and four… — Starting early is vital.","uz":"Musiqa ta'limini boshlashning eng maqbul vaqti — uch-to'rt yosh… — Erta boshlash juda muhim.","why":"Ikkalasi ham erta yoshdan o'qitishni boshlash kerak deydi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What does the woman say about the piano?","qu":"Ayol pianino haqida nima deydi?","o":["It is not possible to play simple tunes on it.","Playing it can discourage children from learning another instrument.","Most young children are not mature enough to learn it."],"ou":["Unda oddiy kuylarni chalib bo'lmaydi.","Uni chalish bolalarni boshqa cholg'u o'rganishdan sovutishi mumkin.","Ko'p kichik bolalar uni o'rganishga yetarlicha ulg'aymagan."],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":43.06,"en":88.7,"si":2,"ev":"Children have to show the mental, physical and emotional readiness to learn an instrument like the piano… very few children under six are able to take on that kind of challenge.","uz":"Bolalar pianino kabi cholg'uni o'rganishga aqliy, jismoniy va hissiy tayyorlik ko'rsatishi kerak… olti yoshgacha bo'lgan juda kam bola bunday sinovni uddalay oladi.","why":"Ko'p kichik bolalar uni o'rganishga yetarlicha ulg'aymagan (C).","hl":null},{"q":"In Ben's view, what is the best way to improve as a climber?","qu":"Benning fikricha, alpinist sifatida rivojlanishning eng yaxshi yo'li qaysi?","o":["take the advice of other climbers","learn from the mistakes you make","watch more experienced climbers"],"ou":["boshqa alpinistlarning maslahatiga amal qilish","o'z xatolaringizdan saboq olish","tajribaliroq alpinistlarni kuzatish"],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":187.58,"en":198.49,"si":7,"ev":"At the end of the day, you've got to learn independently through trial and error.","uz":"Oxir-oqibat, mustaqil ravishda, sinov va xatolar orqali o'rganishingiz kerak.","why":"O'z xatolaringizdan o'rganish (B). Boshqalarni kuzatish (C) — \"different things work best for different people\".","hl":null},{"q":"Why does Ben prefer not to climb alone in icy conditions?","qu":"Ben nega muzli sharoitda yolg'iz chiqmaslikni afzal ko'radi?","o":["He can learn new techniques from other people.","He gets nervous when rocks have ice on them.","He lacks experience of climbing on ice."],"ou":["Boshqalardan yangi usullarni o'rganishi mumkin.","Qoyalarda muz bo'lsa, asabiylashadi.","Muzda chiqish tajribasi yetishmaydi."],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":210.52,"en":229.02,"si":10,"ev":"I haven't done much winter climbing. So I still feel out of my depth climbing alone on rock faces covered in ice.","uz":"Qishda ko'p chiqmaganman. Shuning uchun muz qoplagan qoyalarda yolg'iz chiqishda o'zimni hali ham ishonchsiz his qilaman.","why":"Muzda chiqish tajribasi yetishmaydi (C).","hl":null},{"q":"How do most waiters react when they realise who Amanda is?","qu":"Ko'pchilik ofitsiantlar Amanda kimligini bilib qolganda qanday munosabat bildiradi?","o":["They give her special attention.","They are overcome with nerves.","They provide her with free food."],"ou":["Unga alohida e'tibor berishadi.","Ularni hayajon bosib ketadi.","Unga bepul ovqat berishadi."],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":330.17,"en":340.7,"si":16,"ev":"When that happens it's inevitable, I suppose, that they take a bit more care over serving the food and some seem a bit nervous.","uz":"Bunday bo'lganda, ular ovqat tortishga biroz ko'proq e'tibor berishi muqarrar, ba'zilari esa biroz asabiylashadi.","why":"Ko'pchilik unga alohida e'tibor beradi (A). Asabiylashish (B) — faqat \"some\", bepul ovqat (C) — \"I've never been given\".","hl":null},{"q":"In what way, according to Amanda, are most restaurant owners completely wrong?","qu":"Amandaning fikricha, ko'pchilik restoran egalari qaysi jihatdan butunlay xato qiladi?","o":["They think customers choose a restaurant only for its quality of service.","They don't understand customers' motivation for eating in restaurants.","They think their priorities are different to those of their customers."],"ou":["Mijozlar restoranni faqat xizmat sifati uchun tanlaydi deb o'ylashadi.","Mijozlar nega restoranda ovqatlanishini tushunishmaydi.","O'z ustuvorliklari mijozlarnikidan farq qiladi deb o'ylashadi."],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":360.66,"en":371.97,"si":18,"ev":"Most restaurant owners believe that the main reason people go to restaurants is for the food… that's completely wrong. The main reason people go to restaurants is to have a good time.","uz":"Ko'pchilik restoran egalari odamlar asosan ovqat uchun keladi deb o'ylaydi… bu butunlay noto'g'ri. Asosiy sabab — yaxshi vaqt o'tkazish.","why":"Ular mijozlarning restoranga kelish sababini tushunmaydi (B).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":25.59,"e":25.59,"t":"Extract One — You hear two people on a radio programme discussing music education for children."},{"s":25.59,"e":42.53,"t":"Research shows that the optimum time to start music education is between the ages of three and four. As well as improving manual dexterity and concentration, it seems that it may help emotional development too. And starting young on understanding musical notation lays down an excellent foundation for later on."},{"s":43.06,"e":70.3,"t":"The piano is the instrument that many parents want their children to start learning, and I think three years old is the right time to start. Starting early is vital, but less demanding instruments would be my choice. Things like the recorder or a half-size guitar. Personally, I don't think the piano is the best instrument to start with so early. Children have to show the mental, physical and emotional readiness to learn an instrument like the piano, which obviously takes a lot of effort and commitment."},{"s":70.81,"e":88.7,"t":"In my experience, very few children under six are able to take on that kind of challenge. Well, I think children of that age can learn to play simple tunes on the piano when they soon progress to more complicated pieces if they can read music. But a rather academic approach will turn children off for life if they're not ready for it."},{"s":89.14,"e":94.17,"t":"enjoyment has got to be the priority. Well, enjoyment is certainly important, but if you..."},{"k":"h","s":177.02,"e":177.02,"t":"Extract Two — You hear part of an interview with a rock climber called Ben."},{"s":177.02,"e":187.13,"t":"So, Ben, you're well known in the climbing world as a bit of a loner. You prefer climbing without other people, is that true? Well, to some extent."},{"s":187.58,"e":198.49,"t":"I've always talked to other climbers about the technical side of things, training, equipment and things like that. But at the end of the day, you've got to learn independently through trial and error."},{"s":198.97,"e":204.54,"t":"If you're climbing in a group, you'll always compare yourself to others, and that doesn't always help you to improve."},{"s":205.08,"e":209.98,"t":"It's good to admire other climbers, but different things work best for different people."},{"s":210.52,"e":229.02,"t":"So you never climb with other people? As far as possible, I climb alone. But occasionally I look to others for support. When I was younger, I used to do most of my climbing during the summer holidays. And I haven't done much winter climbing. So I still feel out of my depth climbing alone on rock faces covered in ice."},{"s":229.53,"e":232.89,"t":"When it's dangerous like that, you need people who've been brought up with it."},{"s":233.34,"e":239.2,"t":"It's good to have people around to advise you on what's a safe manoeuvre to make in the circumstances."},{"k":"h","s":316.7,"e":316.7,"t":"Extract Three — You hear part of an interview with a restaurant critic called Amanda Downing."},{"s":316.7,"e":322.3,"t":"You're such a household name, it must be terrifying for staff when you go into a restaurant. How do they react?"},{"s":322.74,"e":329.6,"t":"It's true that a lot of people know me, at least in the restaurant world, so I always eat with a friend and they'll make the booking."},{"s":330.17,"e":340.7,"t":"Often though, I get recognised and when that happens it's inevitable, I suppose, that they take a bit more care over serving the food and some seem a bit nervous."},{"s":341.21,"e":360.09,"t":"I've never been given a complimentary meal though, or anything like that. That would be just too obvious. And of course it could be considered unethical to accept a gift like that. And what makes a good restaurant? A good restaurant is one where the management and waiting staff have given some thought to why their customers are there."},{"s":360.66,"e":366.59,"t":"Most restaurant owners believe that the main reason people go to restaurants is for the food, for that's completely wrong."},{"s":367.22,"e":371.97,"t":"The main reason people go to restaurants is to have a good time, not because they're hungry."},{"s":372.54,"e":377.6,"t":"So there might be a big difference between the priorities of a restaurant and the priorities of diners."},{"s":378.04,"e":390.08,"t":"For example, one thing that a restaurant gets judged on is the quality of service. What restaurant owners think is good is service that is efficient, but what customers have as their priority is friendly service."}]},{"n":48,"title":"Two friends talking about doing team sports in the schools they went to","dur":454.24325,"x":[{"ps":10.26,"en":80.73,"c":"You hear two friends talking about doing team sports in the schools they went to."},{"ps":164.79,"en":237.28,"c":"You hear two friends talking about reading."},{"ps":325.59,"en":385.85,"c":"You hear two people talking about receiving marketing texts on mobile phones."}],"items":[{"q":"Which aspect of participating in team sports do the friends disagree about?","qu":"Do'stlar jamoaviy sportda qatnashishning qaysi jihati haqida kelisha olmaydi?","o":["that it kept them fit","that they made good friends as a result","that competition in team sports is positive"],"ou":["ularni sog'lom (chaqqon) saqlagani","natijada yaxshi do'stlar orttirgani","jamoaviy sportdagi raqobat ijobiy ekani"],"a":"C","x":0,"ps":53.27,"en":80.73,"si":9,"ev":"I also hated the competitive side, the constant pressure to win… — I suppose I'm a naturally competitive person and I got a lot of fun out of playing against teams from other schools.","uz":"Raqobat tomonini, doimiy g'alaba bosimini ham yomon ko'rardim… — Men tabiatan raqobatchi odamman, boshqa maktab jamoalariga qarshi o'ynashdan katta zavq olardim.","why":"Fikrlar raqobat ijobiymi — shu masalada farq qiladi (C). Sog'lom bo'lish (A) va do'stlar (B) — ikkalasi ham rozi.","hl":null},{"q":"In the man's opinion, team sports at his school","qu":"Erkakning fikricha, maktabidagi jamoaviy sport","o":["helped him to avoid failure in later life.","distracted him from his academic studies.","encouraged him to do sport as an adult."],"ou":["keyingi hayotida muvaffaqiyatsizlikdan qochishga yordam berdi","uni o'qishdan chalg'itdi","uni katta bo'lganda ham sport bilan shug'ullanishga undadi"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":39.1,"en":52.61,"si":7,"ev":"What I disliked most was having to spend so much time on it after school. All I really wanted to do was get on with homework… but the rugby practice got in the way.","uz":"Eng yomon ko'rganim — darsdan keyin unga juda ko'p vaqt sarflash. Men faqat uy vazifasini qilishni xohlardim… lekin regbi mashg'uloti xalaqit berardi.","why":"Jamoaviy sport uni o'qishdan chalg'itgan (B).","hl":null},{"q":"What is the woman doing during the conversation?","qu":"Suhbat davomida ayol nima qilyapti?","o":["persuading the man to use his e-reader","complaining about paperback books","encouraging the man to read more"],"ou":["erkakni elektron kitobidan foydalanishga ko'ndiryapti","yumshoq muqovali kitoblardan shikoyat qilyapti","erkakni ko'proq o'qishga undayapti"],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":176.44,"en":188.96,"si":15,"ev":"Oh, but e-readers are so convenient. You should really try it more.","uz":"E-reader juda qulay-ku. Undan ko'proq foydalanib ko'rishing kerak.","why":"Ayol erkakni e-readerdan foydalanishga ko'ndiryapti (A).","hl":null},{"q":"What reason does the man give for preferring printed books to e-readers?","qu":"Erkak bosma kitoblarni elektron kitoblardan afzal ko'rishiga qanday sabab keltiradi?","o":["They are easier to read.","They display a person's interests.","They can be shared with friends."],"ou":["Ularni o'qish osonroq.","Ular insonning qiziqishlarini ko'rsatib turadi.","Ularni do'stlar bilan bo'lishish mumkin."],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":223.99,"en":234.14,"si":23,"ev":"I like having them on my bookshelves to remind me what I've read… and also to show people who visit what I've read so they can learn something about me.","uz":"Ularni javonlarimda saqlashni yaxshi ko'raman — nima o'qiganimni eslatadi… mehmonlarga ham nima o'qiganimni ko'rsatadi, ular men haqimda nimadir bilib oladi.","why":"Kitoblar insonning qiziqishlarini ko'rsatadi (B).","hl":null},{"q":"Why doesn't the man like marketing texts?","qu":"Erkak nega reklama SMS-xabarlarini yoqtirmaydi?","o":["They are not interesting.","They are not effective.","They are usually unwanted."],"ou":["Ular qiziq emas.","Ular samarali emas.","Ular odatda keraksiz (so'ralmagan)."],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":328.28,"en":346.88,"si":28,"ev":"They tend to come from companies I know nothing about trying to sell me things I've no wish to own.","uz":"Ular odatda men bilmaydigan kompaniyalardan keladi va menga keragi yo'q narsalarni sotmoqchi bo'ladi.","why":"Xabarlar so'ralmagan, keraksiz (C). Samarasiz (B) emas — \"It's a really efficient way\".","hl":null},{"q":"How does the woman respond to the man's criticism of marketing texts?","qu":"Ayol erkakning reklama xabarlarini tanqid qilishiga qanday javob beradi?","o":["She says people are interested in receiving them.","She says she sends them to people who have agreed to receive them.","She says it can be difficult to prevent companies breaking the rules."],"ou":["Odamlar ularni olishga qiziqadi, deydi.","U ularni faqat rozilik bergan odamlarga yuborishini aytadi.","Kompaniyalarning qoidani buzishining oldini olish qiyin bo'lishi mumkinligini aytadi."],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":347.42,"en":375.71,"si":29,"ev":"Our company just sends texts to people who we think would want to find out more about our products… They'll have given us permission to send them details as well.","uz":"Bizning kompaniya faqat mahsulotlarimiz haqida ko'proq bilishni xohlaydi deb hisoblaganlarga yozadi… Ular bizga ma'lumot yuborishga ruxsat ham bergan bo'ladi.","why":"U faqat rozilik berganlarga yuboradi (B).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":10.26,"e":10.26,"t":"Extract One — You hear two friends talking about doing team sports in the schools they went to."},{"s":10.26,"e":13.47,"t":"You did a lot of team sports at school, didn't you?"},{"s":13.91,"e":18.72,"t":"Yes, mainly football and volleyball. I was in the school team for both of them."},{"s":19.45,"e":24.0,"t":"I always felt really healthy from it and it was a great way of getting to know people well."},{"s":24.66,"e":28.29,"t":"some of the people I played with are still people I meet up with regularly."},{"s":29.14,"e":31.33,"t":"You were good at sport too, weren't you?"},{"s":31.9,"e":38.49,"t":"Didn't you enjoy it? To be honest, I really didn't like team sports at school. Although I did play rugby."},{"s":39.1,"e":45.6,"t":"It certainly kept me in good shape, but what I disliked most was having to spend so much time on it after school."},{"s":46.1,"e":52.61,"t":"All I really wanted to do was get on with homework, which I actually enjoyed, but the rugby practice got in the way."},{"s":53.27,"e":57.15,"t":"I also hated the competitive side, the constant pressure to win."},{"s":57.78,"e":73.89,"t":"I've spoken to some team mates since then, still people I keep in touch with, and many of them felt the same way. Well, I suppose the pressure is sometimes a bit intense. But overall, I think doing team sports can really help you develop skills that are useful in later life."},{"s":74.52,"e":80.73,"t":"I suppose I'm a naturally competitive person and I got a lot of fun out of playing against teams from other schools."},{"k":"h","s":164.79,"e":164.79,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two friends talking about reading."},{"s":164.79,"e":173.05,"t":"I noticed one of your friends gave you an e-reader for your birthday, but I haven't seen you use it yet. No, I've hardly used it at all."},{"s":173.59,"e":175.71,"t":"I still prefer reading printed books."},{"s":176.44,"e":179.13,"t":"Oh, but e-readers are so convenient."},{"s":179.67,"e":188.96,"t":"You should really try it more. I use mine all the time. On the train, on the way to work, on holiday, reading in bed before I go to sleep."},{"s":189.56,"e":197.31,"t":"You read a lot, don't you? You'd be able to carry a load of reading material around with you in something that's the size of a single paperback."},{"s":197.82,"e":202.01,"t":"And it's not just books. You can get newspapers and magazines as well."},{"s":202.62,"e":210.3,"t":"What I particularly like is being able to change the font size so easily. I hate reading books with very small print."},{"s":210.97,"e":211.58,"t":"a go"},{"s":212.09,"e":214.27,"t":"Yes, that's all very true, but..."},{"s":214.94,"e":223.55,"t":"just like holding real books, there's something about how they feel and sometimes even how they smell that really appeals."},{"s":223.99,"e":228.8,"t":"And I like having them on my bookshelves to remind me what I've read as I walk past them."},{"s":229.59,"e":234.14,"t":"and also to show people who visit what I've read so they can learn something about me."},{"s":234.71,"e":237.28,"t":"You can't do that if what you've read is on an e-"},{"k":"h","s":325.59,"e":325.59,"t":"Extract Three — You hear two people talking about receiving marketing texts on mobile phones."},{"s":325.59,"e":327.71,"t":"You've got a new job in your company haven't you"},{"s":328.28,"e":346.88,"t":"Yes, I transferred to the marketing department just a couple of weeks ago. My job's to send text to people about new offers and new products. Oh, I get marketing texts all the time and I must say that I find it pretty irritating. They tend to come from companies I know nothing about trying to sell me things I've no wish to own."},{"s":347.42,"e":372.7,"t":"Although I sometimes text back telling them to stop contacting me, the texts just keep coming. I mean, I can understand why companies do it. It's a really efficient way of keeping people informed, but I wish I could stop it somehow. Well, our company just sends texts to people who we think would want to find out more about our products. Perhaps they've already bought something from us online, so we know they might be interested in hearing from us."},{"s":373.27,"e":375.71,"t":"They'll have given us permission to send them details as well."},{"s":376.22,"e":385.85,"t":"And if people tell us to stop contacting them, we always delete their details from our database. Of course, not all companies follow the regulations that have been agreed about marketing texts."}]},{"n":49,"title":"A woman asking her friend about a change in his transport habits","dur":445.44,"x":[{"ps":10.2,"en":72.32,"c":"You hear a woman asking her friend about a change in his transport habits."},{"ps":148.6,"en":210.88,"c":"You hear two people talking about flying."},{"ps":289.24,"en":363.26,"c":"You hear part of an interview with a man who is talking about travelling on the London Underground."}],"items":[{"q":"On what occasions does he say he used to travel by taxi?","qu":"U qanday hollarda taksida yurganini aytadi?","o":["when he couldn't get a lift","when he was on a short journey","when he missed the last bus or train"],"ou":["hech kim mashinada olib keta olmaganda","qisqa masofaga borganda","oxirgi avtobus yoki poyezdga ulgurmaganda"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":10.2,"en":28.38,"si":1,"ev":"You always used to get us to drive you everywhere… Yeah, well, a couple of weeks ago, just about everyone seemed to be away and I had to get taxis every day.","uz":"Doim bizni hamma joyga olib borishga majbur qilarding… Ha, bir-ikki hafta oldin deyarli hamma ketib qoldi va har kuni taksiga o'tirishimga to'g'ri keldi.","why":"Uni hech kim olib keta olmaganda taksiga o'tirgan (A).","hl":null},{"q":"What is the main reason he started walking more?","qu":"U ko'proq piyoda yura boshlashining asosiy sababi nima?","o":["He was spending too much money on taxis.","He became tired of waiting for taxis.","He realised that walking was beneficial for him."],"ou":["Taksiga juda ko'p pul sarflardi.","Taksi kutishdan charchadi.","Piyoda yurish o'ziga foydali ekanini angladi."],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":28.95,"en":59.84,"si":2,"ev":"It was costing me an absolute fortune… I realised that there were a lot of better things I could be doing with my cash than blowing it on taxis.","uz":"Bu menga juda qimmatga tushayotgan edi… Pulimni taksiga sovurish o'rniga undan yaxshiroq foydalanish mumkinligini angladim.","why":"Asosiy sabab — taksiga juda ko'p pul sarflagani (A). Taksi kutishdan charchash (B) — faqat bir kechadagi voqea.","hl":null},{"q":"What did the woman think when the pilot started speaking?","qu":"Uchuvchi gapira boshlaganda ayol nima deb o'yladi?","o":["She was determined not to lose control of herself.","She was afraid that the plane was in real danger.","She thought the plane was going to turn back because of bad weather."],"ou":["O'zini yo'qotmaslikka qat'iy qaror qildi.","Samolyot haqiqiy xavf ostida deb qo'rqdi.","Yomon ob-havo tufayli samolyot orqaga qaytadi deb o'yladi."],"a":"B","x":1,"ps":151.0,"en":178.24,"si":10,"ev":"When the pilot started speaking I thought he was going to tell us to prepare for an emergency landing and I started to panic.","uz":"Uchuvchi gapira boshlaganda, u bizga favqulodda qo'nishga tayyorlanishni aytadi deb o'yladim va vahimaga tushdim.","why":"Samolyot haqiqiy xavf ostida deb qo'rqdi (B). Ob-havo tufayli qaytish (C) aytilmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"Which is the worst part of flying for the woman?","qu":"Ayol uchun parvozning eng yomon qismi qaysi?","o":["the last few moments of the flight","the time she spends waiting to board the plane","when the plane is about to leave the ground"],"ou":["parvozning so'nggi daqiqalari","samolyotga chiqishni kutib o'tkazadigan vaqti","samolyot yerdan ko'tarilish oldidagi payt"],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":178.42,"en":210.88,"si":11,"ev":"I guarantee you, on the plane I'll feel absolutely sick when the engine starts up. But landing is a massive relief to me.","uz":"Kafolat beraman, samolyotda dvigatel ishga tushganda ko'nglim aynib ketadi. Lekin qo'nish men uchun katta yengillik.","why":"Eng yomoni — samolyot ko'tarilish oldidagi payt (C). Oxirgi daqiqalar (A) — aksincha, yengillik.","hl":null},{"q":"How did he feel about travelling when he first used the Underground?","qu":"Metrodan birinchi marta foydalanganda yo'l yurish haqida qanday his qildi?","o":["He was terrified.","He was overexcited.","He found it very funny."],"ou":["Juda qo'rqib ketdi.","Haddan tashqari hayajonlandi.","Buni juda kulgili deb bildi."],"a":"B","x":2,"ps":289.24,"en":318.11,"si":14,"ev":"I couldn't believe it when we stepped on the escalator and started going down into the ground. That was so thrilling for a little kid… At one point I got so carried away that I almost toppled.","uz":"Eskalatorga chiqib, yer ostiga tusha boshlaganimizda ishonolmadim. Kichkina bola uchun bu juda hayajonli edi… Bir payt shunchalik berilib ketdimki, yiqilishimga sal qoldi.","why":"U haddan tashqari hayajonlangan (B). Faqat bir narsa biroz qo'rqinchli edi (A emas).","hl":null},{"q":"What does he think of the Underground as an adult?","qu":"Katta bo'lgach u metro haqida qanday fikrda?","o":["It doesn't inspire any particular feelings in him.","It is surrounded by unnecessary marketing hype.","It is an important part of London's cultural heritage."],"ou":["U unda alohida his-tuyg'u uyg'otmaydi.","Uning atrofida keraksiz reklama shov-shuvi ko'p.","U London madaniy merosining muhim qismi."],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":327.77,"en":363.26,"si":17,"ev":"It's still awe-inspiring though… It's one of the great London institutions… The London Underground has become an icon.","uz":"Bu hanuz hayratlanarli… Bu Londonning buyuk ramzlaridan biri… London metrosi timsolga aylangan.","why":"U London madaniy merosining muhim qismi (C). A — tuzoq: \"I'm pretty blasé now\", lekin \"still awe-inspiring\".","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":10.2,"e":10.2,"t":"Extract One — You hear a woman asking her friend about a change in his transport habits."},{"s":10.2,"e":28.38,"t":"What's happened to you? You never used to walk anywhere. I know, but now I've turned over a new leaf. I don't believe it. You always used to get us to drive you everywhere, even when you could have caught a bus or a train. Yeah, well, a couple of weeks ago, just about everyone seemed to be away and I had to get taxis every day."},{"s":28.95,"e":37.89,"t":"You know, I have no idea about public transport. Even though I was often just travelling very short distances, it was costing me an absolute fortune."},{"s":38.39,"e":43.45,"t":"One night it was really late and I got fed up of waiting for a taxi. So I walked home"},{"s":43.96,"e":51.36,"t":"It only took me about 10 minutes longer than it would have taken me by taxi. I really felt quite pleased with myself because I'd saved the price of a pizza."},{"s":52.02,"e":59.84,"t":"I realised that there were a lot of better things I could be doing with my cash than blowing it on taxis. Why don't you buy yourself a car? Yeah, you're right."},{"s":60.28,"e":68.03,"t":"Actually, I've started taking driving lessons and I'm saving what I would have spent on taxi fares. Eventually, I'll be able to afford my own car."},{"s":68.6,"e":72.32,"t":"In the meantime, I'm enjoying walking. It's really good exercise."},{"k":"h","s":148.6,"e":148.6,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two people talking about flying."},{"s":148.6,"e":150.37,"t":"So how did it all start?"},{"s":151.0,"e":178.24,"t":"Well, it got really bad after a flight to France. It was a small plane and the weather wasn't wonderful, but it was only a 55 minute flight. And what happened? Well, take off was a bit wobbly and as we got higher it started to get really bumpy. When the pilot started speaking I thought he was going to tell us to prepare for an emergency landing and I started to panic. As it turned out all he said was that the flight was going to be a bit rough because of turbulence. But that didn't help?"},{"s":178.42,"e":205.69,"t":"No, not really. I thought he was just saying that to stop everyone panicking. But nobody else was panicking. They were taking the whole incident very calmly. It was then that I realised I had a problem. Hmm. And you always get like this in the airport? Well, I just feel a bit apprehensive now. That's natural, isn't it? My hands are a bit sweaty, I suppose. I guarantee you, on the plane I'll feel absolutely sick when air-ups when the engine starts up."},{"s":206.3,"e":210.88,"t":"But landing is a massive relief to me, which is the bit most people find scary."},{"k":"h","s":289.24,"e":289.24,"t":"Extract Three — You hear part of an interview with a man who is talking about travelling on the London Underground."},{"s":289.24,"e":307.55,"t":"Do you remember the first time you went on an underground train? Yeah, I was about five I think. I remember it was my first time in London. I didn't have the faintest idea what the tube was. I couldn't believe it when we stepped on the escalator and started going down into the ground. That was so thrilling for a little kid."},{"s":308.15,"e":318.11,"t":"I remember giggling and waving at the people on the up escalator. At one point I got so carried away that I almost toppled, but luckily my dad was holding my hand."},{"s":318.74,"e":327.13,"t":"On the platform I remember staring at the black tunnel. Then there was a whooshing noise, a warm wind and suddenly there was the train."},{"s":327.77,"e":340.96,"t":"doors slid open and hundreds of people spilled out. That was the only thing that was a bit scary. Do you still get like that? No, I'm pretty blasé now. It's still awe-inspiring though when you think about it."},{"s":341.46,"e":363.26,"t":"all the business types, tourists, clubbers and buskers rushing about in those hot airless tunnels because it's simply the best way to get from A to B. It's one of the great London institutions. No wonder you see all the merchandise covered in logos and maps on sale everywhere these days. The London Underground has become an icon."}]},{"n":50,"title":"Two friends discussing the topic of marketing","dur":475.951,"x":[{"ps":30.84,"en":91.23,"c":"You hear two friends discussing the topic of marketing."},{"ps":190.07,"en":248.57,"c":"You hear two friends talking about ways of keeping fit."},{"ps":347.92,"en":406.91,"c":"You hear a woman telling a friend about living in her capital city as a student."}],"items":[{"q":"Which aspect of college publicity material do the friends disagree about?","qu":"Do'stlar kollej reklama materiallarining qaysi jihati haqida kelisha olmaydi?","o":["how useful the environmental rating system is","how well the different courses are described","how visually attractive the brochures are"],"ou":["ekologik reyting tizimi qanchalik foydaliligi","turli kurslar qanchalik yaxshi tasvirlangani","bukletlar ko'rinishdan qanchalik jozibaliligi"],"a":"A","x":0,"ps":43.8,"en":63.29,"si":2,"ev":"They've got a star rating system for this one… though I'm not sure that would have much impact on my choice. — Well, yes, but if I was torn between two courses, the new rating could decide it.","uz":"Bunga yulduzli reyting tizimi ham bor… lekin bu tanlovimga unchalik ta'sir qilmasa kerak. — Ha, lekin ikki kurs orasida ikkilansam, yangi reyting hal qilishi mumkin.","why":"Ekologik reyting tizimi qanchalik foydaliligi bo'yicha fikr farq qiladi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"In the woman's opinion, companies link themselves with charities in order to","qu":"Ayolning fikricha, kompaniyalar o'zini xayriya tashkilotlari bilan bog'laydi, maqsad ...","o":["boost their profits","improve their image in society","distract attention away from other issues"],"ou":["foydasini oshirish","jamiyatdagi obro'sini yaxshilash","e'tiborni boshqa muammolardan chalg'itish"],"a":"B","x":0,"ps":81.53,"en":91.23,"si":9,"ev":"The cynic in me reckons many companies just want to appear softer in the public eye, so they make a lot of noise about their charitable credentials.","uz":"Ichimdagi shubhachi aytadiki, ko'p kompaniyalar jamoatchilik oldida yumshoqroq ko'rinishni xohlaydi, shuning uchun xayriyalari haqida ko'p shov-shuv qiladi.","why":"Jamiyatdagi obro'sini yaxshilash (B). Foyda (A) — \"I don't know if it increases sales\".","hl":null},{"q":"What is the woman's criticism of exercising in gyms?","qu":"Ayol sport zallarida shug'ullanishni qanday tanqid qiladi?","o":["Members get limited access to the facilities.","The membership cost is too high for the services offered.","It encourages exercise habits that lead to unhealthy lifestyles."],"ou":["A'zolar jihozlardan cheklangan foydalanadi.","A'zolik narxi taklif qilinadigan xizmatlarga nisbatan juda qimmat.","U nosog'lom turmush tarziga olib keladigan mashq odatlarini shakllantiradi."],"a":"C","x":1,"ps":218.81,"en":242.49,"si":14,"ev":"People tend to think that a 60-minute workout entitles them to laze around for the rest of the day, or eat a lot and then undo all the good they might have done.","uz":"Odamlar 60 daqiqalik mashg'ulotdan keyin kunning qolgan qismida yotib dam olish yoki ko'p ovqat yeyish huquqi bor deb o'ylashadi va foydasini yo'qqa chiqaradi.","why":"Sport zali nosog'lom odatlarga olib keladi (C). Narx (B) — faqat tilga olinadi.","hl":null},{"q":"How does the man respond to his friend's criticism?","qu":"Erkak do'stining tanqidiga qanday javob beradi?","o":["He objects to her making sweeping generalisations about gyms.","He questions the value of excessive gym attendance.","He suspects she'd enjoy a different type of gym."],"ou":["U sport zallari haqida shoshilinch umumlashtirishlar qilishiga e'tiroz bildiradi.","Sport zaliga haddan tashqari ko'p qatnashning foydasiga shubha qiladi.","Unga boshqa turdagi sport zali yoqishi mumkin deb o'ylaydi."],"a":"A","x":1,"ps":218.81,"en":248.57,"si":14,"ev":"That's all very well, Mary. But what about the people who don't give up on the gym and who actually feel the benefit… Each to his own.","uz":"Bu yaxshi gap, Meri. Lekin sport zalini tashlamaydigan va haqiqatan foydasini ko'radiganlar-chi… Har kimning o'z yo'li bor.","why":"U sport zallari haqida shoshilinch umumlashtirishga e'tiroz bildiradi (A).","hl":null},{"q":"What is she doing during the conversation?","qu":"Suhbat davomida u nima qilyapti?","o":["admitting to regrets about her choice of place to study","complaining about challenges she's had to face","expressing her admiration for people in the city"],"ou":["o'qish joyi tanlovidan afsuslanishini tan olyapti","duch kelgan qiyinchiliklaridan shikoyat qilyapti","shahar odamlariga qoyil qolishini bildiryapti"],"a":"C","x":2,"ps":357.08,"en":382.56,"si":21,"ev":"Folks in the city are just determined to grow stuff on rooftops, balconies, wherever… It was a reminder of the strong spirit of gardeners.","uz":"Shahar aholisi tomlarda, balkonlarda — qayerda bo'lmasin, nimadir o'stirishga qat'iy ahd qilgan… Bu bog'bonlarning kuchli ruhini eslatardi.","why":"U shahar odamlariga qoyil qolishini bildiradi (C). Iqlim qattiq (B), lekin u shikoyat qilmaydi.","hl":null},{"q":"Why does the man give the example of trees?","qu":"Erkak nega daraxtlarni misol qilib keltiradi?","o":["to support her main point","to present a counter-argument to hers","to express a reservation about her interpretation"],"ou":["ayolning asosiy fikrini qo'llab-quvvatlash uchun","uning fikriga qarshi dalil keltirish uchun","uning talqiniga nisbatan shubhasini bildirish uchun"],"a":"A","x":2,"ps":382.97,"en":406.91,"si":22,"ev":"Instead of bare bits of ground around urban trees, they seemed to take great pride in filling the earth around them with flowers. — Ah, and all that's done by the residents themselves.","uz":"Shahar daraxtlari atrofidagi yalang'och yer o'rniga, ular atrofini gullar bilan to'ldirishdan faxrlanishardi. — Ha, bularning hammasini aholining o'zi qiladi.","why":"Erkak ayolning asosiy fikrini qo'llab-quvvatlash uchun daraxtlarni misol qiladi (A).","hl":null}],"segs":[{"k":"h","s":30.84,"e":30.84,"t":"Extract One — You hear two friends discussing the topic of marketing."},{"s":30.84,"e":43.33,"t":"Daniel, how are things? Have you applied for college yet? Well, I can't decide which one to go for. Lots of colleges have sent me their glossy brochures, and I see they now go on about how environmentally friendly they are."},{"s":43.8,"e":50.59,"t":"In fact, they've got a star rating system for this one. They're trying to attract as much interest as possible."},{"s":51.03,"e":53.92,"t":"though I'm not sure that would have much impact on my choice."},{"s":54.46,"e":63.29,"t":"Ultimately the course has to be the right one, though I can see they need to compete. Well, yes, but if I was torn between two courses, the new rating could decide it."},{"s":64.18,"e":65.92,"t":"they're thinking about these issues."},{"s":66.19,"e":68.67,"t":"and the marketing people are certainly shouting about it."},{"s":69.04,"e":74.21,"t":"It's getting like the commercial sector. Those companies who sponsor a charity for example."},{"s":74.61,"e":81.14,"t":"trying to persuade consumers that just by buying their products they're doing their bit for charity and can ignore other causes."},{"s":81.53,"e":91.23,"t":"I don't know if it increases sales, but the cynic in me reckons many companies just want to appear softer in the public eye, so they make a lot of noise about their charitable credentials."},{"k":"h","s":190.07,"e":190.07,"t":"Extract Two — You hear two friends talking about ways of keeping fit."},{"s":190.07,"e":195.84,"t":"Are you still going to the gym, Frank? Yes, but not as often as I should be. That's the problem, isn't it?"},{"s":196.31,"e":202.75,"t":"I've heard that the dropout rate among gym members is very high even in those really expensive luxury health centers."},{"s":203.42,"e":218.05,"t":"Anyway, gyms aren't the answer. I'm sure the real key is to build exercise into your daily routine by doing something simple like walking to the mall or taking the stairs rather than the elevator or doing sport."},{"s":218.81,"e":242.49,"t":"And another thing, people tend to think that a 60-minute workout entitles them to laze around for the rest of the day, or eat a lot and then undo all the good they might have done. But people who exercise little and often don't fall into the same trap. That's all very well, Mary. But what about the people who don't give up on the gym and who actually feel the benefit and quite enjoy the comradeship?"},{"s":243.1,"e":244.32,"t":"Each to his own, you know"},{"s":245.08,"e":248.57,"t":"If you just give it another shot, you might find it suited you too."},{"k":"h","s":347.92,"e":347.92,"t":"Extract Three — You hear a woman telling a friend about living in her capital city as a student."},{"s":347.92,"e":350.39,"t":"Can you study at university, Alicia?"},{"s":350.7,"e":352.57,"t":"horticulture, plants and things."},{"s":352.97,"e":356.79,"t":"I was based at a regional one, but I also spent time studying in the capital."},{"s":357.08,"e":382.56,"t":"Seems a strange place to go if you want to grow things the middle of a huge city. That's what my fellow student said. I mean, I know it wasn't ideal. It's a harsh climate, winters are bitterly cold and the summer's sweltering with little rain. But folks in the city are just determined to grow stuff on rooftops, balconies, wherever. They'll just garden anywhere they can. It was a reminder of the strong spirit of gardeners."},{"s":382.97,"e":406.91,"t":"Come to think of it, I do remember noticing the way some of the trees were looked after there. Instead of bare bits of ground around urban trees, they seemed to take great pride in filling the earth around them with flowers. Ah, and all that's done by the residents themselves. It's as if every tree is to be celebrated. I wouldn't go that far. Not all parts of the city are like that."}]}];
